window.TWG_I18N=window.TWG_I18N||{};TWG_I18N["zh-hant"]=Object.assign(TWG_I18N["zh-hant"]||{},{"I'll build you a tailor-made path to pass your Level 1 exam. It takes 5 quick questions.":"我會為你量身打造一條通過 Level 1 考試的學習路線，只需要回答 5 個簡短的問題。","Level 1 exam":"Level 1 考試","Lessons, quizzes and flashcards on the Level 1 grapes and regions.":"Level 1 葡萄品種與產區的課程、測驗與字卡。","All of Level 1":"Level 1 全部內容","Lessons, flashcards and mistakes: only the Level 1 syllabus.":"課程、字卡與錯題：只涵蓋 Level 1 的考試範圍。","Level 1 games":"Level 1 遊戲","Short games on Level 1 questions and terms.":"以 Level 1 題目與術語設計的小遊戲。","Grapes, vines and climate":"葡萄、葡萄樹與氣候","How wine is made":"葡萄酒如何釀造","Types and styles of wine":"葡萄酒的類型與風格","The four key white grapes":"四大白葡萄品種","The four key black grapes":"四大黑葡萄品種","Famous wines from the key grapes":"以主要品種釀造的知名葡萄酒","Other wines to know":"其他必須認識的葡萄酒","Storing and serving wine":"葡萄酒的保存與侍酒","Tasting: first steps":"品飲入門","From vine to wine":"從葡萄樹到葡萄酒","Types, styles and grapes":"類型、風格與品種","Store, serve, pair":"保存、侍酒與搭配","Which definition best describes wine?":"下列哪一項最能說明葡萄酒的定義？","Fermented grape juice":"發酵的葡萄汁","Distilled grape juice":"蒸餾的葡萄汁","Concentrated grape juice":"濃縮的葡萄汁","Pasteurised grape juice":"經巴氏殺菌的葡萄汁","Wine is made by fermenting the sweet juice of grapes.":"葡萄酒是由葡萄的甜汁發酵而成。","To make wine, grapes are crushed to release their sweet juice. Alcoholic fermentation, carried out by yeast, then turns the sugar in that juice into alcohol. Without fermentation you would simply have grape juice; distilling or concentrating the juice is not part of the basic definition of wine.":"釀造葡萄酒時，先將葡萄破皮，釋出甜美的汁液，再由酵母進行酒精發酵，把汁液中的糖轉化為酒精。沒有發酵，就只是葡萄汁；蒸餾或濃縮葡萄汁都不屬於葡萄酒的基本定義。","Which part of a black grape contains tannins?":"黑葡萄的哪個部位含有單寧？","The juice":"果汁","The flower":"花","Black grape skins hold both the colour and the tannins.":"黑葡萄的果皮同時含有顏色與單寧。","The skin is what really sets black grapes apart from white ones: it is deeply coloured and contains tannins, which leave the mouth feeling dry. The pulp, by contrast, holds the juice, made of water, sugar and acid, and it is the same colour in all grapes.":"黑葡萄與白葡萄真正的差別在果皮：黑葡萄的果皮顏色深，並含有單寧，會讓口腔感到乾澀。果肉則含有由水、糖和酸組成的果汁，而且所有葡萄的果肉顏色都一樣。","What is the juice in the pulp mainly made of?":"果肉中的果汁主要由什麼組成？","Water, sugar and acid":"水、糖和酸","Water, tannin and colour":"水、單寧和顏色","Alcohol, sugar and yeast":"酒精、糖和酵母","Water, alcohol and carbon dioxide":"水、酒精和二氧化碳","Grape juice is mostly water, sugar and acid.":"葡萄汁的主要成分是水、糖和酸。","The pulp is the soft part of the grape and holds the juice, which is mostly water, sugar and acid. Tannin and colour are found in the skin instead. Alcohol and carbon dioxide only appear later, when yeast ferments the sugar in the juice.":"果肉是葡萄柔軟的部分，裡面的果汁主要是水、糖和酸。單寧和顏色則存在於果皮中。酒精和二氧化碳要到後來酵母發酵果汁中的糖時才會出現。","What do tannins do to your mouth?":"單寧會讓口腔有什麼感覺？","Make it feel dry":"感到乾澀","Make it water":"分泌唾液","Make it feel hot":"感到灼熱","Make it feel sweet":"感到甜味","Tannins from the skins leave the mouth feeling dry.":"來自果皮的單寧會讓口腔感到乾澀。","Tannins come from black grape skins and are felt more than tasted: they dry out the mouth. When tasting, they should not be confused with acidity, which makes your mouth water instead; these are two opposite sensations worth learning to tell apart.":"單寧來自黑葡萄的果皮，與其說是嚐到，不如說是感覺到：它會讓口腔變得乾澀。品飲時別把它和酸度混淆，酸度反而會讓你分泌唾液；這是兩種相反的感覺，值得學會分辨。","What colour is the pulp of a black grape?":"黑葡萄的果肉是什麼顏色？","The same as in a white grape":"和白葡萄的果肉一樣","Deep red, like the skin":"深紅色，和果皮一樣","Purple, but only when fully ripe":"紫色，但要完全成熟才是","Pink, paler than the skin":"粉紅色，比果皮淺","Pulp is the same colour in all grapes; the colour is in the skin.":"所有葡萄的果肉顏色都一樣；顏色在果皮裡。","Inside, white and black grapes look very alike: the pulp is the same colour whatever the colour of the skin. This is exactly why a red wine gets its colour from the skins, and why a white wine can even be made from black grapes if the juice is separated from the skins straight away.":"從內部看，白葡萄和黑葡萄非常相似：不論果皮是什麼顏色，果肉的顏色都相同。正因如此，紅酒的顏色來自果皮；只要立刻把果汁與果皮分開，甚至可以用黑葡萄釀出白酒。","In which season does the grape vine flower?":"葡萄樹在哪個季節開花？","Spring":"春季","Summer":"夏季","Autumn":"秋季","Winter":"冬季","Vines flower in spring; the grapes then ripen in summer.":"葡萄樹在春季開花，葡萄則在夏季成熟。","The vine's yearly cycle follows the seasons. In spring the clusters of flowers appear, and each flower will become a grape. During summer the grapes ripen, and they are picked towards the end of summer. In winter the vine rests, and it needs enough cold to do so.":"葡萄樹的年度週期跟著四季走。春季長出花序，每一朵花都會變成一顆葡萄。夏季葡萄逐漸成熟，並在夏末採收。冬季葡萄樹進入休眠，而且需要足夠的低溫才能好好休息。","What does each individual vine flower become?":"葡萄樹的每一朵花會變成什麼？","One grape":"一顆葡萄","A new shoot":"一根新梢","A whole leaf":"一整片葉子","A whole bunch":"一整串葡萄","After flowering, each single flower turns into a small grape.":"開花之後，每一朵花都會變成一顆小葡萄。","Vine flowers come in clusters made up of many tiny flowers. After flowering, each one becomes a grape, so the cluster of flowers turns into a bunch of grapes. At first these grapes are small, hard and green; they only grow and ripen as the summer goes on.":"葡萄樹的花是由許多小花組成的花序。開花後，每朵小花各自變成一顆葡萄，於是花序就成了一串葡萄。這些葡萄起初又小又硬又綠，要隨著夏季推進才會長大、成熟。","What are grapes like just after flowering?":"剛開完花時，葡萄是什麼模樣？","Small, hard and green":"小、硬、綠","Small, soft and golden":"小、軟、金黃","Large, hard and purple":"大、硬、紫","Large, soft and sweet":"大、軟、甜","All young grapes are small, hard and green, white or black.":"不論白葡萄或黑葡萄，幼果都是又小又硬又綠。","Newly formed grapes are not ready yet: they are small, hard and green, and at this stage white and black grapes look the same. Only during summer ripening do they swell with water, become sweeter and change colour, towards golden for white grapes and purple for black ones.":"剛結成的葡萄還沒準備好：又小又硬又綠，這個階段白葡萄和黑葡萄看起來一模一樣。要到夏季成熟期，果實才會吸水膨大、變甜並轉色，白葡萄轉為金黃色，黑葡萄轉為紫色。","As grapes ripen, what happens to their sugar and acid levels?":"葡萄成熟時，糖分和酸度會如何變化？","Sugar rises and acid falls":"糖分上升，酸度下降","Sugar falls and acid rises":"糖分下降，酸度上升","Both rise at the same rate":"兩者以相同速度上升","Both stay the same":"兩者都維持不變","Ripening makes grapes sweeter and less acidic.":"成熟會讓葡萄更甜、酸度更低。","While grapes ripen over the summer, several things change: they swell with water, sugar goes up, acid goes down and the flavours become riper. This balance between sugar and acid will later influence the alcohol and freshness of the wine.":"葡萄在夏季成熟的過程中，會發生幾項變化：果實吸水膨大、糖分上升、酸度下降，風味也更加成熟。糖與酸之間的平衡，之後會影響葡萄酒的酒精濃度與清爽感。","What colour do white grapes turn as they ripen?":"白葡萄成熟時會轉為什麼顏色？","From green to golden":"從綠色轉為金黃色","From green to purple":"從綠色轉為紫色","From yellow to green":"從黃色轉為綠色","From golden to pink":"從金黃色轉為粉紅色","White grapes go from green to golden; black ones from green to purple.":"白葡萄從綠色轉為金黃色；黑葡萄從綠色轉為紫色。","At first all grapes are green. As they ripen, the skin changes colour: it becomes golden in white grapes and purple in black grapes. This colour change goes hand in hand with the other signs of ripening, namely more water, more sugar, less acid and riper flavours.":"一開始所有葡萄都是綠色的。隨著成熟，果皮會變色：白葡萄轉為金黃色，黑葡萄轉為紫色。轉色與其他成熟跡象同時發生，也就是水分增加、糖分增加、酸度降低、風味更成熟。","Which of these does NOT happen as grapes ripen?":"下列哪一項「不會」在葡萄成熟時發生？","Acidity increases":"酸度增加","Grapes swell with water":"葡萄吸水膨大","Sugar increases":"糖分增加","Flavours become riper":"風味變得更成熟","During ripening acidity falls, it does not rise.":"成熟過程中酸度是下降，而不是上升。","Ripening brings more water into the grapes, more sugar and riper flavours, but acid moves the other way and drops. That is why an unripe grape tastes sour, while a ripe one is sweet and less acidic. Remembering this trend also helps you understand the effect of climate.":"成熟會讓葡萄含有更多水分、更多糖分和更成熟的風味，但酸度卻往反方向走，逐漸下降。所以未熟的葡萄嚐起來很酸，成熟的葡萄則甜而酸度較低。記住這個趨勢，也有助於理解氣候的影響。","In the vine's yearly cycle, when are the grapes usually picked?":"在葡萄樹的年度週期中，葡萄通常在什麼時候採收？","In late summer":"夏末","In early spring":"早春","In midwinter":"隆冬","Just after flowering":"剛開完花時","Grapes ripen through summer and are picked in late summer.":"葡萄在夏季成熟，並於夏末採收。","The vine flowers in spring, the flowers become grapes and these ripen during the summer. Once they are ripe enough, towards the end of summer, they are picked. Just after flowering the grapes are still small, hard and green, far too unripe to make wine.":"葡萄樹在春季開花，花變成葡萄，並在夏季成熟。等到夏末成熟度足夠時就會採收。剛開完花的葡萄仍然又小又硬又綠，離可以釀酒的成熟度還差得遠。","Why do vines grow best where winters are cold?":"為什麼葡萄樹在冬季寒冷的地方長得最好？","The cold lets the vine rest":"寒冷讓葡萄樹得以休眠","The cold raises sugar levels":"寒冷會提高糖分","The cold makes the vine flower":"寒冷會讓葡萄樹開花","The cold colours the skins":"寒冷會讓果皮上色","A cold enough winter gives the vine a period of rest.":"夠冷的冬季能讓葡萄樹有一段休眠期。","Besides the right amount of sunlight and heat during the growing season, a vine needs a winter cold enough to let it rest. This is why most vineyards are found in particular bands of latitude, neither too cold nor too hot.":"除了生長季需要適量的日照與熱量，葡萄樹還需要夠冷的冬季才能休眠。這就是為什麼大多數葡萄園都位於特定的緯度帶，既不太冷也不太熱。","Which of these is an example of a cool climate wine region?":"下列哪一個是涼爽氣候產區的例子？","Parts of Australia":"澳洲部分地區","Parts of California":"加州部分地區","Areas on the Equator":"赤道地區","Germany, like northern France, lies nearer the poles and has a cool climate.":"德國和法國北部一樣較靠近兩極，屬於涼爽氣候。","Cool climate regions are those closer to the poles, such as Germany and northern France. Parts of Australia and California are examples of warm climates instead. Right at the Equator it is too hot for vines to grow well and rest in winter.":"涼爽氣候產區是較靠近兩極的地區，例如德國和法國北部。澳洲和加州的部分地區則是溫暖氣候的例子。赤道一帶太熱，葡萄樹無法好好生長，冬季也無法休眠。","Which type of grape is commonly grown in warm climate regions?":"溫暖氣候產區普遍種植哪一類葡萄？","Unripe grapes":"未成熟的葡萄","Skinless grapes":"沒有果皮的葡萄","Warm climates ripen grapes reliably, and black grapes are commonly grown.":"溫暖氣候能讓葡萄穩定成熟，普遍種植黑葡萄。","Warm regions, closer to the Equator, have high average temperatures and more intense sunshine, so grapes ripen reliably. Growing black grapes is common there. In cool regions, closer to the poles, where grapes sometimes struggle to ripen at all, white grapes are more commonly grown.":"溫暖產區較靠近赤道，平均氣溫高、日照更強，葡萄能穩定成熟，因此普遍種植黑葡萄。涼爽產區較靠近兩極，葡萄有時甚至難以成熟，所以較常種植白葡萄。","In a cool climate, grapes will usually have…":"在涼爽氣候下，葡萄通常會……","Less sugar and more acidity":"糖分較少、酸度較高","More sugar and less acidity":"糖分較多、酸度較低","More sugar and more acidity":"糖分較多、酸度較高","Less sugar and less acidity":"糖分較少、酸度較低","The cooler it is, the more acidic and less sugary the grapes stay.":"氣候越涼爽，葡萄的酸度越高、糖分越少。","With little heat and weaker sunshine, grapes ripen less: they build up less sugar and keep more acidity. In the glass this tends to give lighter, fresher wines. In a warm climate the opposite happens: more sugar, less acidity and riper flavours.":"熱量少、日照弱，葡萄的成熟度就較低：累積的糖分較少，保留的酸度較多。喝起來往往是較輕盈、清爽的葡萄酒。溫暖氣候則相反：糖分較多、酸度較低，風味也更成熟。","Why does a warm-climate wine tend to show riper fruit flavours?":"為什麼溫暖氣候的葡萄酒往往有更成熟的果香？","Heat ripens the grapes further":"熱量讓葡萄更成熟","Heat raises the grapes' acidity":"熱量會提高葡萄的酸度","Heat removes colour from the skins":"熱量會帶走果皮的顏色","Heat stops the vine flowering":"熱量會讓葡萄樹無法開花","More heat and sun ripen grapes further: more sugar, riper flavours.":"更多的熱量與陽光讓葡萄更成熟：糖分更多、風味更成熟。","In warm regions average temperatures are high and the sunshine is intense, so grapes ripen fully and reliably. This brings more sugar, less acidity and riper flavours. Chardonnay, for example, moves from apple and lemon aromas in a cool climate to peach and pineapple in a warm one.":"溫暖產區平均氣溫高、日照強，葡萄能穩定而充分地成熟，帶來更多糖分、更低的酸度和更成熟的風味。以夏多內為例，在涼爽氣候呈現蘋果和檸檬香氣，在溫暖氣候則轉為桃子和鳳梨。","A Chardonnay with apple and lemon aromas most likely comes from…":"一款帶有蘋果和檸檬香氣的夏多內最可能來自……","A tropical climate":"熱帶氣候","A very dry climate":"非常乾燥的氣候","Green fruit and citrus point to less ripe, cool-climate grapes.":"綠色水果和柑橘類香氣代表成熟度較低、來自涼爽氣候的葡萄。","Climate changes the type of fruit you find in a wine. In a cool climate Chardonnay gives green fruit such as apple and citrus such as lemon. In a warm climate, with riper grapes, it shows stone fruit such as peach and tropical fruit such as pineapple.":"氣候會改變葡萄酒中的水果類型。在涼爽氣候，夏多內呈現蘋果等綠色水果和檸檬等柑橘類水果。在溫暖氣候，葡萄更成熟，會出現桃子等核果和鳳梨等熱帶水果。","Why can grapes in cool regions struggle to ripen in some years?":"為什麼涼爽產區的葡萄在某些年份可能難以成熟？","Low temperatures and weaker sunlight":"氣溫低、日照較弱","High temperatures and stronger sunlight":"氣溫高、日照較強","Winters too mild for the vine to rest":"冬季太溫和，葡萄樹無法休眠","Vines too young to flower":"葡萄樹太年輕，無法開花","Little heat and weaker light slow down ripening.":"熱量少、日照弱，會讓成熟變慢。","Cool regions lie closer to the poles: average temperatures are low and the sunlight can be less intense than near the Equator. In especially cool years the grapes may not ripen fully. This is one reason white grapes are commonly grown there.":"涼爽產區較靠近兩極：平均氣溫低，日照也可能不如赤道附近強烈。在特別冷的年份，葡萄可能無法完全成熟。這也是當地普遍種植白葡萄的原因之一。","After planting, how long does a vine usually take before it gives a crop every year?":"葡萄樹種下之後，通常要多久才能每年結果？","A couple of years":"兩三年","A few months":"幾個月","About twenty years":"大約二十年","Half a century":"半個世紀","A vine matures a couple of years after planting, then crops every year.":"葡萄樹種下兩三年後成熟，之後每年都能結果。","The vine is a long-lived plant that can survive for several decades. After planting it needs a couple of years to become mature; from then on it gives a crop every year, always following the same cycle: flowering in spring, ripening in summer and harvest in late summer.":"葡萄樹壽命很長，可以存活數十年。種下後需要兩三年才會成熟；之後每年都有收成，並且始終依循相同的週期：春季開花、夏季成熟、夏末採收。","What is needed for alcoholic fermentation to take place?":"酒精發酵需要什麼才能進行？","Yeast are what turn the sugar in the juice into alcohol.":"把果汁中的糖轉化為酒精的正是酵母。","Without yeast, grape juice would stay juice. Yeast are microscopic organisms that feed on sugar and turn it into alcohol and carbon dioxide. Oak can be used to ferment or mature wine but is not essential, and carbon dioxide is a product of fermentation, not an ingredient.":"沒有酵母，葡萄汁就只會是葡萄汁。酵母是以糖為食的微生物，會把糖轉化為酒精和二氧化碳。橡木可用於發酵或熟成，但並非必要；二氧化碳則是發酵的產物，不是原料。","What are the two products of alcoholic fermentation?":"酒精發酵的兩種產物是什麼？","Alcohol and carbon dioxide":"酒精和二氧化碳","Alcohol and sugar":"酒精和糖","Sugar and acid":"糖和酸","Water and tannin":"水和單寧","Sugar + yeast → alcohol + carbon dioxide.":"糖 + 酵母 → 酒精 + 二氧化碳。","Yeast eat the sugar in the grape juice and turn it into alcohol and carbon dioxide. Sugar is therefore the starting point, not a product. The alcohol stays in the wine, while in most cases the carbon dioxide escapes into the atmosphere during fermentation.":"酵母吃掉葡萄汁中的糖，把它轉化為酒精和二氧化碳。所以糖是起點，不是產物。酒精會留在酒裡，而二氧化碳在大多數情況下會在發酵過程中散逸到空氣中。","During the fermentation of a still wine, what usually happens to the carbon dioxide?":"靜態酒發酵時，二氧化碳通常會怎麼樣？","It escapes into the air":"散逸到空氣中","It stays in the wine":"留在酒裡","It turns back into sugar":"變回糖","It is absorbed by the skins":"被果皮吸收","In most cases the gas escapes to the atmosphere; the alcohol stays.":"多數情況下氣體會散逸到空氣中，酒精則留下來。","During fermentation yeast produce alcohol and carbon dioxide. The alcohol remains in the new wine, while the gas normally escapes into the air, which gives a still wine with no bubbles. In sparkling wines, by contrast, some of this gas is trapped in the wine.":"發酵時酵母會產生酒精和二氧化碳。酒精留在新酒中，氣體通常散逸到空氣中，於是得到沒有氣泡的靜態酒。氣泡酒則相反，部分氣體被保留在酒中。","A label says 12% abv. What does this mean?":"酒標上寫著 12% abv，這是什麼意思？","12% of the liquid is alcohol":"液體的 12% 是酒精","12% of the liquid is sugar":"液體的 12% 是糖","12% of the grapes were black":"12% 的葡萄是黑葡萄","12% of the wine was oak-aged":"12% 的酒經過橡木桶熟成","Alcohol by volume tells you what share of the liquid is alcohol.":"酒精濃度（abv）告訴你液體中有多少比例是酒精。","Alcohol is expressed as a percentage of the volume. A wine at 10% abv is one tenth alcohol; one at 12% abv contains twelve parts alcohol in every hundred. The figure tells you nothing about sweetness, grape colour or the use of oak: it is only about alcohol.":"酒精是以體積百分比表示。10% abv 的葡萄酒有十分之一是酒精；12% abv 則是每一百份中有十二份酒精。這個數字與甜度、葡萄顏色或是否使用橡木桶都無關，它只說明酒精含量。","Why are most wines dry?":"為什麼大多數葡萄酒都是不甜的？","The yeast eat all the sugar":"酵母把糖全部吃掉了","The skins absorb the sugar":"果皮把糖吸收了","Oak removes the sugar":"橡木桶把糖去除了","Grapes contain no sugar":"葡萄不含糖","Fermentation usually continues until no sugar is left.":"發酵通常會持續到糖分耗盡為止。","Ripe grapes are full of sugar, but in most cases the yeast keep working until they have turned all of it into alcohol. The result is a dry wine, meaning one with no sugar or very little. To make sweet wines, some of the sugar has to remain in the wine.":"成熟的葡萄含有大量糖分，但多數情況下，酵母會持續作用，直到把糖全部轉化為酒精。結果就是不甜的葡萄酒，也就是不含糖或含糖極少。要釀造甜酒，就必須讓部分糖分留在酒中。","In white winemaking, what happens straight after crushing?":"釀造白酒時，破皮之後緊接著做什麼？","For white wine, crushed grapes are pressed before the juice ferments.":"釀白酒時，破皮後的葡萄先壓榨，果汁才發酵。","For white wine the order is: crushing, pressing, fermentation, maturation and bottling. Pressing collects the juice left in the crushed grapes, so that only the juice, without the skins, goes on to ferment. Draining, by contrast, is a typical step in making red and rosé wines.":"白酒的順序是：破皮、壓榨、發酵、熟成、裝瓶。壓榨能取得破皮後葡萄中剩餘的果汁，讓只有果汁、不含果皮進入發酵。排汁則是釀造紅酒和粉紅酒的典型步驟。","Where can a white wine be fermented?":"白酒可以在哪裡發酵？","Stainless steel tanks or oak barrels":"不鏽鋼槽或橡木桶","Only in oak barrels":"只能在橡木桶","Only in the bottle":"只能在瓶中","Only in stainless steel tanks":"只能在不鏽鋼槽","White wine can ferment in either stainless steel or oak.":"白酒可以在不鏽鋼槽或橡木桶中發酵。","After crushing and pressing, yeast are added to the juice. Fermentation can happen in stainless steel tanks or in oak barrels; it is the winemaker's choice. The maturation that follows can also take place in either of these two kinds of container.":"破皮、壓榨之後，會在果汁中加入酵母。發酵可以在不鏽鋼槽或橡木桶中進行，由釀酒師決定。之後的熟成同樣可以在這兩種容器中進行。","Why is it possible to make white wine from black grapes?":"為什麼可以用黑葡萄釀造白酒？","Their juice is colourless":"它們的果汁沒有顏色","Their skins are golden":"它們的果皮是金黃色","They contain no tannin":"它們不含單寧","They lose colour in oak":"它們在橡木桶中會褪色","Colour is only in the skin; black grape juice has no colour.":"顏色只在果皮裡；黑葡萄的果汁沒有顏色。","Black grapes have coloured skins but colourless juice, just like the pulp of white grapes. If they are pressed gently before fermentation and the juice is separated from the skins straight away, the colour does not pass into the juice and a white wine can be made.":"黑葡萄的果皮有顏色，但果汁無色，就和白葡萄的果肉一樣。只要在發酵前輕柔壓榨，並立刻把果汁與果皮分開，顏色就不會進入果汁，也就能釀出白酒。","In red winemaking, what goes into the fermentation vessel?":"釀造紅酒時，放進發酵容器的是什麼？","The juice together with the skins":"果汁連同果皮","The juice alone, without skins":"只有果汁，不含果皮","The skins alone, without juice":"只有果皮，不含果汁","Wine that is already pressed":"已經壓榨好的酒","Red wine ferments with the skins, which give colour and tannin.":"紅酒連同果皮一起發酵，果皮帶來顏色和單寧。","After black grapes are crushed, juice and skins go into the fermentation vessel together. This long contact is what draws colour and tannin out of the skins. For white wine, by contrast, the juice is separated from the skins by pressing before it ferments.":"黑葡萄破皮後，果汁和果皮一起放進發酵容器。正是這段長時間的接觸，把顏色和單寧從果皮中萃取出來。白酒則相反，果汁在發酵前就經由壓榨與果皮分開。","Why are juice and skins mixed thoroughly during red wine fermentation?":"紅酒發酵時，為什麼要把果汁和果皮充分混合？","To extract colour and tannin":"為了萃取顏色和單寧","To add oak flavours":"為了增添橡木風味","To remove sugar from the skins":"為了去除果皮中的糖","To release carbon dioxide":"為了釋放二氧化碳","Mixing helps colour and tannin pass from the skins into the wine.":"混合有助於顏色和單寧從果皮進入酒中。","The colour and tannin of red wine are found in the skins of black grapes. By mixing the skins well with the juice during fermentation, these substances pass into the wine. That is why a red wine has deep colour and a structure that dries the mouth, while a white does not.":"紅酒的顏色和單寧存在於黑葡萄的果皮中。發酵時把果皮和果汁充分混合，這些物質就會進入酒中。所以紅酒顏色深，並有讓口腔乾澀的結構，白酒則沒有。","In red winemaking, when is the wine drained off the skins?":"釀造紅酒時，什麼時候把酒液從果皮中排出？","Once fermentation has finished":"發酵結束之後","Straight after crushing":"破皮之後立刻","After bottling":"裝瓶之後","Red wine stays on the skins for the whole fermentation, then is drained.":"紅酒在整個發酵期間都與果皮接觸，之後才排出酒液。","For red wine the skins stay in contact with the juice for the whole fermentation, so they give plenty of colour and tannin. Only when fermentation is over is the new wine drained off the skins. Draining after just a few hours is, by contrast, the typical technique for rosé.":"釀紅酒時，果皮在整個發酵過程中都與果汁接觸，因此能釋出大量顏色和單寧。等發酵結束，才把新酒從果皮中排出。只接觸幾小時就排汁，則是粉紅酒的典型做法。","Why are the skins pressed after a red wine is drained?":"紅酒排出酒液後，為什麼還要壓榨果皮？","To release the remaining wine":"為了取出剩餘的酒液","To extract more sugar":"為了萃取更多糖分","To start fermentation":"為了啟動發酵","To turn the wine rosé":"為了把酒變成粉紅酒","The skins still hold wine, which pressing recovers.":"果皮中還含有酒液，壓榨可以把它取回。","After draining, the skins are still soaked with wine. Pressing them recovers this wine, which would otherwise be lost. So in red winemaking pressing comes after fermentation, the opposite of white winemaking, where the grapes are pressed before fermenting. Maturation and bottling then follow.":"排汁後，果皮仍然吸飽了酒液。壓榨可以把這些酒取回，否則就浪費了。所以釀紅酒時壓榨是在發酵之後，和白酒相反，白酒是先壓榨再發酵。接著是熟成和裝瓶。","Which is the correct order of steps for a red wine?":"下列哪一項是釀造紅酒的正確步驟順序？","Crushing, draining, fermentation, pressing":"破皮、排汁、發酵、壓榨","Red ferments on the skins, then is drained and the skins pressed.":"紅酒帶皮發酵，然後排出酒液，再壓榨果皮。","Red wine follows this sequence: crushing the black grapes, fermenting juice and skins together, draining the new wine, pressing the skins, maturation and bottling. Starting with crushing then pressing describes white winemaking instead, where pressing happens before fermentation and only the juice is fermented.":"紅酒依照這個順序：黑葡萄破皮、果汁與果皮一起發酵、排出新酒、壓榨果皮、熟成、裝瓶。先破皮再壓榨描述的是白酒的釀造，壓榨在發酵之前，而且只有果汁發酵。","Which type of grape is used to make rosé wine?":"釀造粉紅酒使用哪一類葡萄？","Dried grapes":"風乾的葡萄","Rosé comes from black grapes with brief skin contact.":"粉紅酒以黑葡萄釀造，只短暫與果皮接觸。","The pink colour comes from the skins of black grapes. The juice stays in contact with the skins for only a few hours, so it picks up just a little colour; it is then separated and finishes fermenting without the skins. White grapes do not have skins coloured enough to do this.":"粉紅色來自黑葡萄的果皮。果汁只與果皮接觸幾個小時，因此只染上一點顏色；之後與果皮分開，在不含果皮的情況下完成發酵。白葡萄的果皮顏色不夠深，做不到這一點。","For a rosé, when is the juice drained from the skins?":"釀造粉紅酒時，什麼時候把果汁從果皮中排出？","After only a few hours":"僅僅幾小時之後","After oak maturation":"橡木桶熟成之後","For rosé, skin contact lasts only a few hours.":"粉紅酒與果皮的接觸只有幾個小時。","Rosé starts out like a red: black grapes are crushed and fermentation begins with the skins. After only a few hours, though, the juice is drained off while it is still just pink. Fermentation then finishes without the skins. Draining at the end of fermentation would give a red wine instead.":"粉紅酒一開始和紅酒一樣：黑葡萄破皮，連同果皮開始發酵。但只過幾個小時，趁果汁還只是粉紅色時就把它排出，之後在不含果皮的情況下完成發酵。如果等發酵結束才排汁，得到的就會是紅酒。","What mainly explains the colour difference between a rosé and a red?":"粉紅酒和紅酒的顏色差異主要取決於什麼？","How long the juice stays on the skins":"果汁與果皮接觸的時間長短","The colour of the grape pulp":"葡萄果肉的顏色","The use of oak barrels":"是否使用橡木桶","The amount of yeast added":"加入的酵母量","A few hours on the skins gives pink; the whole fermentation gives red.":"與果皮接觸幾小時得到粉紅色；整個發酵期都接觸則得到紅色。","Rosé and red are both made from black grapes, whose pulp is the same colour as that of white grapes. The colour comes from the skins: for red they stay in the juice for the whole fermentation, for rosé only for a few hours. That is why rosé stays pink.":"粉紅酒和紅酒都以黑葡萄釀造，而黑葡萄的果肉顏色和白葡萄相同。顏色來自果皮：釀紅酒時果皮在整個發酵期間都留在果汁中，釀粉紅酒只留幾個小時。所以粉紅酒維持粉紅色。","Which statement about the maturation of rosé wines is correct?":"關於粉紅酒的熟成，下列哪一項敘述正確？","They are rarely matured in oak":"很少在橡木桶中熟成","They are always matured in oak":"一律在橡木桶中熟成","They are matured on their skins":"與果皮一起熟成","They are matured only in bottle":"只在瓶中熟成","Rosé can mature in steel or oak, but oak is rarely used.":"粉紅酒可在不鏽鋼槽或橡木桶熟成，但很少使用橡木桶。","After fermentation, both reds and rosés can be matured in stainless steel tanks or oak barrels. For rosé, however, oak is rarely used. The skins were already removed after a few hours, so maturation never takes place on the skins. The wine is then bottled.":"發酵後，紅酒和粉紅酒都可以在不鏽鋼槽或橡木桶中熟成，不過粉紅酒很少使用橡木桶。果皮在幾小時後就已移除，所以熟成絕不會與果皮一起進行。之後葡萄酒才裝瓶。","Which step is part of red winemaking but NOT rosé?":"哪一個步驟屬於紅酒釀造，而「不」屬於粉紅酒？","Pressing the skins after fermentation":"發酵後壓榨果皮","Crushing the black grapes":"黑葡萄破皮","Adding yeast":"加入酵母","Bottling":"裝瓶","Rosé skins are removed early, so there is nothing to press afterwards.":"粉紅酒的果皮很早就移除，之後沒有東西可以壓榨。","Both wines go through crushing, adding yeast, fermentation, draining, maturation and bottling. For red, however, the skins stay until fermentation ends and are then pressed to recover the wine. For rosé the juice leaves the skins after a few hours, so this final pressing does not happen.":"兩種酒都會經過破皮、加入酵母、發酵、排汁、熟成和裝瓶。但紅酒的果皮會留到發酵結束，再壓榨取回酒液。粉紅酒的果汁幾小時後就離開果皮，所以沒有最後這道壓榨。","In which wine is pressing done BEFORE fermentation?":"哪一種酒是在發酵「之前」壓榨？","White wine":"白酒","Rosé wine":"粉紅酒","None of them":"以上皆非","White grapes are pressed first so only the juice ferments.":"白葡萄先壓榨，讓只有果汁發酵。","For white wine the grapes are crushed and then pressed, so the juice is separated from the skins and ferments on its own. For red, fermentation happens with the skins, which are only pressed after draining. For rosé the juice is drained off the skins after a few hours, with no final pressing.":"釀白酒時，葡萄先破皮再壓榨，果汁與果皮分開後單獨發酵。釀紅酒時連同果皮發酵，排汁後才壓榨果皮。釀粉紅酒時，果汁幾小時後就從果皮中排出，沒有最後的壓榨。","Where can wines be matured after fermentation?":"發酵之後，葡萄酒可以在哪裡熟成？","In stainless steel tanks or oak barrels":"不鏽鋼槽或橡木桶中","Only among the pressed skins":"只能在壓榨過的果皮之間","Only on the vine":"只能在葡萄樹上","Only in an ice bucket":"只能在冰桶裡","Maturation uses stainless steel or oak, for whites, reds and rosés.":"白酒、紅酒和粉紅酒的熟成都使用不鏽鋼槽或橡木桶。","Once fermentation is over, the wine can rest in stainless steel tanks or oak barrels. This applies to whites, reds and rosés, although oak is rare for rosé. Oak, as you will see later, can give the wine aromas of its own. After maturation the wine is bottled.":"發酵結束後，葡萄酒可以在不鏽鋼槽或橡木桶中靜置。白酒、紅酒和粉紅酒都適用，只是粉紅酒很少用橡木桶。後面你會學到，橡木桶能為葡萄酒帶來它自己的香氣。熟成後葡萄酒就會裝瓶。","Which type of wine has had extra alcohol added?":"哪一類葡萄酒額外添加了酒精？","Still":"靜態酒","Fortified wines have alcohol added, which makes them stronger.":"加烈酒添加了酒精，因此酒精濃度更高。","There are three types of wine: still, sparkling and fortified. Only fortified wine has extra alcohol added, which lifts it to between 15% and 22% abv. Sparkling wine owes its bubbles to carbon dioxide from fermentation, and rosé is a colour, not a type of wine.":"葡萄酒有三種類型：靜態酒、氣泡酒和加烈酒。只有加烈酒額外添加酒精，使酒精濃度提高到 15% 至 22% abv。氣泡酒的氣泡來自發酵產生的二氧化碳；粉紅酒是一種顏色，不是一種類型。","What is the usual alcohol range of fortified wines?":"加烈酒的酒精濃度通常在什麼範圍？","15–22% abv":"15–22% abv","8–11% abv":"8–11% abv","11.5–14% abv":"11.5–14% abv","4–7% abv":"4–7% abv","The added alcohol puts fortified wines between 15% and 22% abv.":"添加的酒精讓加烈酒的酒精濃度落在 15% 至 22% abv。","Still and sparkling wines almost always sit between 11.5% and 14% abv, with extremes from 8% to 15%. Fortified wines such as Sherry and Port have extra alcohol added, so they move up into a higher band of 15% to 22% abv.":"靜態酒和氣泡酒幾乎都在 11.5% 至 14% abv 之間，極端值為 8% 到 15%。Sherry 和 Port 等加烈酒額外添加了酒精，因此落在更高的 15% 至 22% abv。","Where do the bubbles in sparkling wine come from?":"氣泡酒的氣泡從哪裡來？","Carbon dioxide from fermentation trapped in the wine":"發酵產生的二氧化碳被保留在酒中","Distilled alcohol added after fermentation":"發酵後加入的蒸餾酒精","Air entering through the oak barrel staves":"從橡木桶木板滲入的空氣","Fermentation makes carbon dioxide; when it is trapped, it becomes the bubbles.":"發酵會產生二氧化碳；把它保留在酒中，就成了氣泡。","Yeast turn sugar into alcohol and carbon dioxide. In still wines the gas escapes into the air, but in sparkling wines it is kept inside the wine. When the bottle is opened, the gas is released as bubbles, as in Champagne, Cava or Prosecco.":"酵母把糖轉化為酒精和二氧化碳。在靜態酒中氣體會散逸到空氣中，但在氣泡酒中則被保留在酒裡。開瓶時，氣體以氣泡的形式釋放，例如 Champagne、Cava 或 Prosecco。","Between which values do most still wines fall?":"大多數靜態酒的酒精濃度落在哪個範圍？","11.5% and 14% abv":"11.5% 至 14% abv","15% and 22% abv":"15% 至 22% abv","5% and 8% abv":"5% 至 8% abv","16% and 20% abv":"16% 至 20% abv","Still wines range from 8% to 15% abv, but most sit between 11.5% and 14%.":"靜態酒的範圍是 8% 至 15% abv，但大多數在 11.5% 至 14% 之間。","The full range for still wines runs from 8% to 15% abv, but the great majority sit between 11.5% and 14%. Figures of 15% to 22% are typical of fortified wines, which have alcohol added. White Zinfandel is an example of a still wine at the low end.":"靜態酒的完整範圍是 8% 至 15% abv，但絕大多數落在 11.5% 至 14% 之間。15% 至 22% 是添加了酒精的加烈酒的典型數字。White Zinfandel 就是酒精濃度偏低的靜態酒例子。","Which of these wines is named after its grape variety?":"下列哪一款葡萄酒是以葡萄品種命名？","Pinot Grigio is a grape; Rioja, Chianti and Sancerre are places.":"灰皮諾（Pinot Grigio）是葡萄品種；Rioja、Chianti 和 Sancerre 是地名。","Many European wines take the name of the area where they are made: Rioja in Spain, Chianti in Italy, Sancerre in France. Other wines show the grape variety on the label instead. Pinot Grigio is a typical example of a wine named after its grape.":"許多歐洲葡萄酒以產地命名：西班牙的 Rioja、義大利的 Chianti、法國的 Sancerre。另一些葡萄酒則在酒標上標示葡萄品種。灰皮諾（Pinot Grigio）就是以品種命名的典型例子。","Which of these is a Spanish sparkling wine?":"下列哪一款是西班牙的氣泡酒？","Cava is the sparkling wine from Spain.":"Cava 是來自西班牙的氣泡酒。","Three famous sparkling wines to remember: Champagne from France, Prosecco from Italy and Cava from Spain. Sherry is also Spanish, but it is a fortified wine, not a sparkling one: it has had alcohol added and has no bubbles. Sparkling wines are, in fact, now made in almost every wine-producing country.":"有三款著名的氣泡酒要記住：法國的 Champagne、義大利的 Prosecco 和西班牙的 Cava。Sherry 也來自西班牙，但它是加烈酒而不是氣泡酒：添加了酒精，沒有氣泡。事實上，現在幾乎每個葡萄酒生產國都釀造氣泡酒。","Why is a red wine red?":"紅酒為什麼是紅色的？","The skins stay in the juice during fermentation":"發酵時果皮留在果汁中","The pulp of black grapes is red in colour":"黑葡萄的果肉是紅色的","The oak barrels give their colour to the wine":"橡木桶把顏色傳給了酒","Unfermented black grape juice is added":"加入了未發酵的黑葡萄汁","The colour is in the skins, which release it during fermentation.":"顏色在果皮裡，發酵時由果皮釋出。","The pulp of white and black grapes is the same colour and the juice is colourless. To make a red wine, black grapes are used and the skins are kept in contact with the juice throughout fermentation, mixed in well, so colour and tannin pass into the wine.":"白葡萄和黑葡萄的果肉顏色相同，果汁都是無色的。釀造紅酒要使用黑葡萄，並在整個發酵期間讓果皮與果汁接觸、充分混合，顏色和單寧才會進入酒中。","Can a white wine be made from black grapes?":"可以用黑葡萄釀造白酒嗎？","Yes, by separating skins and juice before fermentation":"可以，只要在發酵前把果皮和果汁分開","Yes, but only if the wine is then aged in oak":"可以，但酒之後必須經橡木桶陳年","No, black grapes always give a red wine":"不行，黑葡萄一定釀出紅酒","No, black grapes can only make rosé wine":"不行，黑葡萄只能釀粉紅酒","Black grape juice is colourless, so without the skins the wine stays white.":"黑葡萄的果汁無色，所以沒有果皮，酒就維持白色。","All the colour of a black grape is in its skin. If the grapes are pressed gently and the skins are separated from the juice before fermentation, the juice stays pale and makes a white wine. This same idea is what allows Pinot Noir to be used in Champagne.":"黑葡萄所有的顏色都在果皮裡。只要輕柔壓榨，並在發酵前把果皮與果汁分開，果汁就維持淺色，釀出白酒。也正是這個原理，讓黑皮諾得以用於 Champagne。","How is a rosé wine made?":"粉紅酒是如何釀造的？","Black grapes with only a few hours of skin contact":"黑葡萄，只與果皮接觸幾小時","White grapes fermented together with their skins":"白葡萄連同果皮一起發酵","Black grapes kept on skins until fermentation ends":"黑葡萄帶皮直到發酵結束","White grapes aged for a long time in oak barrels":"白葡萄在橡木桶中長時間陳年","The juice sits with black grape skins for a few hours, then is drained off.":"果汁與黑葡萄果皮接觸幾小時後，就被排出。","Rosé comes from black grapes, like red wine, but the skin contact lasts only a few hours. The juice, now just pink, is drained off and finishes fermenting without the skins. If the skins stayed in until the end, the result would be a red wine instead.":"粉紅酒和紅酒一樣以黑葡萄釀造，但與果皮的接觸只有幾個小時。此時只呈粉紅色的果汁被排出，在不含果皮的情況下完成發酵。如果果皮留到最後，得到的就會是紅酒。","Which of these wines is a rosé?":"下列哪一款是粉紅酒？","Despite its name, White Zinfandel from California is a rosé.":"雖然名字裡有 White，加州的 White Zinfandel 其實是粉紅酒。","The name can mislead you: White Zinfandel is a Californian rosé, medium-sweet, low in alcohol, with strawberry and raspberry flavours. Chablis and Sauternes are French white wines, while Beaujolais is a light red with low tannin. So never judge a wine by its name alone.":"名稱可能會誤導你：White Zinfandel 是加州的粉紅酒，半甜、酒精濃度低，帶有草莓和覆盆子風味。Chablis 和 Sauternes 是法國白酒，Beaujolais 則是單寧低的輕盈紅酒。所以千萬別只憑名稱判斷一款酒。","What happens when a dry wine is made?":"釀造不甜的葡萄酒時會發生什麼事？","The yeast turn all of the sugar into alcohol":"酵母把所有的糖轉化為酒精","Distilled alcohol is added before fermentation ends":"發酵結束前加入蒸餾酒精","Unfermented grape juice is added to the wine":"在酒中加入未發酵的葡萄汁","The yeast are removed before they finish":"酵母在完成發酵前就被移除","A wine is dry when the yeast have eaten all the sugar.":"酵母把糖全部吃完，酒就是不甜的。","Most wines are dry: the yeast keep working until they have turned all the sugar into alcohol. The other answers describe ways of keeping sugar in the wine: removing yeast or adding juice for medium wines, and adding alcohol for sweet fortified wines.":"大多數葡萄酒都是不甜的：酵母持續作用，直到把所有的糖轉化為酒精。其他選項說的都是把糖留在酒中的方法：移除酵母或加入葡萄汁可釀出半甜酒，添加酒精則用於甜型加烈酒。","Which method is used to make a medium-sweet wine?":"釀造半甜葡萄酒會使用哪一種方法？","Adding unfermented grape juice to a dry wine":"在不甜的酒中加入未發酵的葡萄汁","Leaving the skins in the juice for longer":"讓果皮在果汁中停留更久","Maturing the wine in oak barrels":"讓酒在橡木桶中熟成","Picking the grapes before they ripen":"在葡萄成熟前採收","Unfermented juice brings sugar back into an already dry wine.":"未發酵的葡萄汁把糖分帶回已經不甜的酒中。","There are two routes to a medium-sweet wine: remove the yeast before they have eaten all the sugar, or add unfermented grape juice to a dry wine. Skins and oak affect colour, tannin and aromas, not the level of sweetness.":"釀造半甜酒有兩種途徑：在酵母吃完所有的糖之前把它移除，或是在不甜的酒中加入未發酵的葡萄汁。果皮和橡木桶影響的是顏色、單寧和香氣，而不是甜度。","In a sweet fortified wine, what stops the fermentation?":"在甜型加烈酒中，是什麼讓發酵停止？","Adding distilled alcohol, which kills the yeast":"加入蒸餾酒精，殺死酵母","Adding unfermented grape juice to the wine":"在酒中加入未發酵的葡萄汁","Moving the wine into oak barrels":"把酒移入橡木桶","Draining the wine off the skins":"把酒從果皮中排出","The strong added alcohol kills the yeast, leaving sugar in the wine.":"加入的高濃度酒精殺死酵母，讓糖分留在酒中。","In sweet fortified wines, high-strength distilled alcohol is added before the yeast have eaten all the sugar. The yeast die, the leftover sugar makes the wine sweet and the added alcohol makes it stronger. Port and some Sherries are made this way.":"釀造甜型加烈酒時，會在酵母吃完所有的糖之前加入高濃度的蒸餾酒精。酵母死亡，剩下的糖讓酒帶甜，添加的酒精則讓酒更烈。Port 和部分 Sherry 就是這樣釀成的。","Which sensation tells you a wine has high acidity?":"哪一種感覺能告訴你一款酒的酸度高？","It makes your mouth water":"讓你分泌唾液","It makes your mouth feel dry":"讓你口腔乾澀","It warms the back of your throat":"讓喉嚨深處發熱","It feels thick and syrupy":"感覺濃稠如糖漿","Acidity is easy to spot because it makes your mouth water.":"酸度很容易辨認，因為它會讓你分泌唾液。","Each part of a wine's structure has its own sensation. Acidity makes your mouth water and brings freshness. Tannin, by contrast, dries the mouth; alcohol is felt as warmth; and a very sweet wine can feel thick and syrupy. Too much acidity, however, makes a wine taste unpleasantly sharp.":"葡萄酒結構中的每個元素都有自己的感覺。酸度讓你分泌唾液，帶來清爽感。單寧則讓口腔乾澀；酒精帶來溫熱感；非常甜的酒可能感覺濃稠如糖漿。不過酸度太高，酒喝起來會尖銳得令人不舒服。","Why is acidity important in sweet wines?":"為什麼酸度對甜酒很重要？","It balances the sweetness so the wine is not cloying":"它能平衡甜味，讓酒不膩口","It raises the alcohol level of the wine":"它會提高酒的酒精濃度","It gives the wine a deeper colour":"它讓酒的顏色更深","It adds tannin and therefore more body":"它增添單寧，因此酒體更飽滿","Without acidity, a sweet wine would taste cloying.":"沒有酸度，甜酒喝起來會膩口。","Acidity comes from the grape juice and refreshes the wine. In sweet wines it acts as a counterweight to the sugar, which is why Sauternes and sweet Rieslings have high acidity. It does not change the colour, the tannin or the alcohol level. Without it, the wine would feel heavy.":"酸度來自葡萄汁，讓葡萄酒清爽。在甜酒中，酸度能與糖分抗衡，所以 Sauternes 和甜型麗絲玲都有高酸度。酸度不會改變顏色、單寧或酒精濃度。少了它，酒會顯得沉重。","Where does tannin in wine come from?":"葡萄酒中的單寧從哪裡來？","The skins of black grapes":"黑葡萄的果皮","The pulp of white grapes":"白葡萄的果肉","The sugar in the juice":"果汁中的糖","The yeast used in fermentation":"發酵使用的酵母","Tannin sits in black grape skins, which is why it is a red-wine feature.":"單寧存在於黑葡萄的果皮中，所以是紅酒的特徵。","Black grapes have coloured skins that contain tannins. When red wine ferments, the skins stay in the juice and release colour and tannin. How much tannin the wine ends up with depends on the grape and the winemaking: red Bordeaux has a lot, Beaujolais very little.":"黑葡萄的果皮有顏色，並含有單寧。紅酒發酵時，果皮留在果汁中，釋出顏色和單寧。酒中最後有多少單寧，取決於葡萄品種和釀造方式：波爾多紅酒單寧很多，Beaujolais 則非常少。","Which of these reds is low in tannin?":"下列哪一款紅酒單寧低？","Red Bordeaux":"波爾多紅酒","Beaujolais is a light, fresh red with low tannin.":"Beaujolais 是輕盈、清爽、單寧低的紅酒。","Beaujolais is a classic example of a low-tannin red, along with some Pinot Noir wines. Red Bordeaux and Chianti, by contrast, are standard examples of high-tannin reds, and Port, a sweet red fortified wine, also has high tannins. Remember that tannin leaves the mouth feeling dry.":"Beaujolais 和部分黑皮諾葡萄酒一樣，是低單寧紅酒的經典例子。波爾多紅酒和 Chianti 則是高單寧紅酒的標準例子，而甜型紅色加烈酒 Port 的單寧也高。記住，單寧會讓口腔感到乾澀。","Which of these is an example of a high-alcohol wine?":"下列哪一款是高酒精濃度葡萄酒的例子？","Châteauneuf-du-Pape is a full-bodied French red with high alcohol.":"Châteauneuf-du-Pape 是酒體飽滿、酒精濃度高的法國紅酒。","Châteauneuf-du-Pape, a red from the Rhône, is the classic example of a high-alcohol wine: dry and full-bodied, with strawberry and clove. At the other end, White Zinfandel is the standard low-alcohol example, while Beaujolais and Pinot Grigio are light-bodied wines.":"Châteauneuf-du-Pape 是隆河的紅酒，也是高酒精濃度葡萄酒的經典例子：不甜、酒體飽滿，帶有草莓和丁香風味。相反地，White Zinfandel 是低酒精濃度的標準例子，Beaujolais 和灰皮諾則是酒體輕盈的葡萄酒。","What does «12% abv» on a label mean?":"酒標上的「12% abv」是什麼意思？","The wine contains 12% sugar":"這款酒含有 12% 的糖","The wine spent 12 months in oak":"這款酒在橡木桶中待了 12 個月","Alcohol by volume shows what share of the wine is alcohol.":"酒精濃度（abv）顯示酒中有多少比例是酒精。","Alcohol is measured as a percentage of the total volume, called alcohol by volume or abv. A wine at 12% abv has twelve parts alcohol in every hundred. That is a typical figure for a still wine, as most sit between 11.5% and 14%.":"酒精以佔總體積的百分比來衡量，稱為酒精濃度（alcohol by volume，簡稱 abv）。12% abv 的葡萄酒每一百份中有十二份酒精。這是靜態酒的典型數字，因為大多數都在 11.5% 至 14% 之間。","What does the body of a wine describe?":"葡萄酒的酒體描述的是什麼？","How mouth-filling the wine feels":"酒在口中的飽滿程度","How much acidity the wine contains":"酒含有多少酸度","How deep the colour of the wine is":"酒的顏色有多深","How long the wine stayed in oak":"酒在橡木桶中待了多久","Body is the overall feel in the mouth: light, medium or full.":"酒體是酒在口中的整體感受：輕盈、中等或飽滿。","Many factors shape body, so the practical question is: how much does this wine fill my mouth? Full-bodied wines such as Sauternes or a Californian Cabernet Sauvignon feel dense and rich, while light ones such as Pinot Grigio and Beaujolais feel more delicate.":"影響酒體的因素很多，所以實際要問的是：這款酒在我口中有多飽滿？Sauternes 或加州卡本內蘇維濃這類酒體飽滿的酒感覺濃郁厚實，灰皮諾和 Beaujolais 這類酒體輕盈的酒則較為細緻。","Which of these wines is full-bodied?":"下列哪一款葡萄酒酒體飽滿？","Sauternes, the sweet white from Bordeaux, is full-bodied.":"Sauternes 是波爾多的甜白酒，酒體飽滿。","Sauternes is sweet and full-bodied, with apricot, honey and vanilla. Pinot Grigio and Beaujolais are examples of light-bodied wines, and Sancerre is a dry white with medium body. A Californian Cabernet Sauvignon would also be a good example of a full-bodied wine.":"Sauternes 甜而酒體飽滿，帶有杏桃、蜂蜜和香草風味。灰皮諾和 Beaujolais 是酒體輕盈的例子，Sancerre 則是酒體中等的不甜白酒。加州卡本內蘇維濃也是酒體飽滿葡萄酒的好例子。","Vanilla, cedar, smoke":"香草、雪松、煙燻","Apple, lemon, pear":"蘋果、檸檬、梨子","Grass, asparagus, bell pepper":"青草、蘆筍、甜椒","Oak gives vanilla, cedar, smoke, coconut and cloves.":"橡木桶帶來香草、雪松、煙燻、椰子和丁香。","When a wine is fermented or matured in oak barrels, the wood adds notes of vanilla, cedar, smoke, coconut and cloves. Apple, lemon and pear are fruit aromas, while grass, asparagus and bell pepper are herbaceous notes typical of Sauvignon Blanc, for example.":"葡萄酒在橡木桶中發酵或熟成時，木頭會增添香草、雪松、煙燻、椰子和丁香的氣息。蘋果、檸檬和梨子是水果香氣，青草、蘆筍和甜椒則是草本氣息，例如白蘇維濃的典型特徵。","Which aromas does a cool-climate Chardonnay usually show?":"涼爽氣候的夏多內通常呈現哪些香氣？","Peach and pineapple":"桃子和鳳梨","Blackcurrant and mint":"黑醋栗和薄荷","Strawberry and cherry":"草莓和櫻桃","In a cool climate grapes ripen less, giving green fruit and citrus.":"在涼爽氣候，葡萄成熟度較低，呈現綠色水果和柑橘類香氣。","How ripe the grapes are changes the fruit you notice. A cool-climate Chardonnay smells of green apple and lemon; a warm-climate one of peach and tropical fruit such as pineapple. Blackcurrant and mint are typical of Cabernet Sauvignon, and strawberry and cherry of Pinot Noir.":"葡萄的成熟度會改變你聞到的水果類型。涼爽氣候的夏多內有青蘋果和檸檬香氣；溫暖氣候的則有桃子和鳳梨等熱帶水果香氣。黑醋栗和薄荷是卡本內蘇維濃的典型香氣，草莓和櫻桃則屬於黑皮諾。","Which of these aromas belongs to the «other» family?":"下列哪一種香氣屬於「其他」類？","Pineapple":"鳳梨","Mushroom, earth, leather, grass and flowers are «other» aromas.":"蘑菇、泥土、皮革、青草和花香都屬於「其他」類香氣。","Aromas fall into three families: fruit, oak and other. Pineapple and blackcurrant are fruit, and vanilla comes from oak. The «other» family covers grass, flowers, herbs, vegetables, earth, mushroom and leather. These are the aromas that make wine so varied and interesting to explore.":"香氣分為三大類：水果、橡木和其他。鳳梨和黑醋栗屬於水果，香草來自橡木。「其他」類包含青草、花、香草植物、蔬菜、泥土、蘑菇和皮革。正是這些香氣讓葡萄酒如此多變，值得探索。","What is the style of a wine?":"葡萄酒的風格是什麼？","Its colour, structure and aromas combined":"顏色、結構和香氣的總和","Only the grape variety it is made from":"只是釀造它的葡萄品種","Only the region where it is produced":"只是生產它的產區","Only its level of alcohol":"只是它的酒精濃度","Style combines colour, structure, and aromas and flavours.":"風格結合了顏色、結構，以及香氣與風味。","Grape, region and alcohol all influence style, but none of them describes it alone. Style is the sum of colour, structure (sweetness, acidity, tannin, alcohol, body) and aromas and flavours. That is how two French whites such as Chablis and Sauternes can be complete opposites.":"品種、產區和酒精都會影響風格，但沒有任何一項能單獨說明它。風格是顏色、結構（甜度、酸度、單寧、酒精、酒體）以及香氣與風味的總和。所以同為法國白酒的 Chablis 和 Sauternes 可以截然相反。","What effect does a cool climate have on the grapes?":"涼爽氣候對葡萄有什麼影響？","Riper, more tropical flavours":"更成熟、更偏熱帶水果的風味","The cooler it is, the less sugar and the more acid the grapes have.":"氣候越涼爽，葡萄的糖分越少、酸度越高。","As a rule, the cooler the climate, the more acidic and the less sugary the grapes stay; the warmer it is, the more sugar and the less acidity, with riper flavours. That is why cool-climate wines tend to be fresher and lighter, with green fruit and citrus.":"一般而言，氣候越涼爽，葡萄的酸度越高、糖分越少；越溫暖，糖分越多、酸度越低，風味也越成熟。所以涼爽氣候的葡萄酒往往更清爽、更輕盈，帶有綠色水果和柑橘類風味。","What is a cool-climate Chardonnay usually like?":"涼爽氣候的夏多內通常是什麼樣子？","High acidity, light to medium body, apple and lemon":"高酸度，酒體輕盈至中等，蘋果和檸檬","Medium acidity, full body, pineapple and banana":"中等酸度，酒體飽滿，鳳梨和香蕉","Low acidity, full body, honey and apricot":"低酸度，酒體飽滿，蜂蜜和杏桃","Medium acidity, light body, pear and flowers":"中等酸度，酒體輕盈，梨子和花香","A cool climate keeps acidity high and gives green fruit and citrus.":"涼爽氣候讓酸度保持在高水準，並帶來綠色水果和柑橘類風味。","In cool climates the grapes ripen less, so they keep more acidity and less sugar. The resulting Chardonnay has high acidity, a light to medium body and aromas of apple and lemon. Chablis, from the coolest part of Burgundy, is the classic example of this style.":"在涼爽氣候，葡萄成熟度較低，因此保留較多酸度、糖分較少。釀出的夏多內酸度高、酒體輕盈至中等，帶有蘋果和檸檬香氣。來自布根地最涼爽地區的 Chablis 是這種風格的經典例子。","Which flavours does a warm-climate Chardonnay show?":"溫暖氣候的夏多內呈現哪些風味？","Grapefruit, asparagus and grass":"葡萄柚、蘆筍和青草","Warmth ripens the grapes further, giving stone and tropical fruit.":"溫暖讓葡萄更成熟，帶來核果和熱帶水果風味。","Warm-climate Chardonnay comes from riper grapes: medium acidity, medium to full body, and flavours of peach, pineapple and banana. Green apple and lemon point instead to a cool climate. Grapefruit and asparagus suggest Sauvignon Blanc, while blackcurrant and mint suggest Cabernet Sauvignon.":"溫暖氣候的夏多內來自更成熟的葡萄：中等酸度，酒體中等至飽滿，帶有桃子、鳳梨和香蕉風味。青蘋果和檸檬指向涼爽氣候。葡萄柚和蘆筍讓人想到白蘇維濃，黑醋栗和薄荷則讓人想到卡本內蘇維濃。","Which grape is used for white Burgundy?":"布根地白酒使用哪一個葡萄品種？","White Burgundy, including Chablis, is made from Chardonnay.":"布根地白酒（包括 Chablis）以夏多內釀造。","Burgundy (Bourgogne) is France's benchmark region for Chardonnay. Its whites are medium-bodied with high acidity, lemon and peach, and sometimes vanilla from oak. Chablis, from the coolest part of the region, is also Chardonnay. Sauvignon Blanc, by contrast, is the grape of Sancerre.":"布根地（Bourgogne）是法國夏多內的標竿產區。當地白酒酒體中等、酸度高，帶有檸檬和桃子風味，有時還有來自橡木桶的香草氣息。來自產區最涼爽地帶的 Chablis 也是夏多內。白蘇維濃則是 Sancerre 的品種。","Why does Chablis have high acidity?":"為什麼 Chablis 的酸度高？","It comes from the coolest part of Burgundy":"它來自布根地最涼爽的地區","It is aged for a long time in new oak":"它在新橡木桶中長時間陳年","It is made from pressed black grapes":"它以壓榨的黑葡萄釀造","The grapes are picked very ripe":"葡萄在非常成熟時才採收","A cool climate limits ripening, so the grapes stay more acidic.":"涼爽氣候限制了成熟度，所以葡萄的酸度較高。","Chablis comes from the coolest area of Burgundy. There the grapes ripen less, so they stay more acidic and give green apple and lemon flavours. The result is a dry white, light to medium in body, usually with no oak. Very ripe grapes would do the opposite and give lower acidity.":"Chablis 來自布根地最涼爽的地區。那裡的葡萄成熟度較低，因此酸度較高，並帶有青蘋果和檸檬風味。釀出的是不甜白酒，酒體輕盈至中等，通常不經橡木桶。非常成熟的葡萄則會相反，酸度較低。","Where do vanilla notes in some white Burgundies come from?":"部分布根地白酒中的香草氣息從哪裡來？","The region's cool climate":"產區的涼爽氣候","The grape skins":"葡萄果皮","Vanilla is a typical aroma from time in oak.":"香草是經過橡木桶的典型香氣。","White Burgundy can be matured in oak or not. When it spends time in barrel, the wood adds vanilla notes to the lemon and peach aromas. Stainless steel, by contrast, adds no aromas, and the cool climate affects acidity and the type of fruit rather than vanilla.":"布根地白酒可以經橡木桶熟成，也可以不經。在桶中待過的酒，木頭會在檸檬和桃子香氣之外增添香草氣息。不鏽鋼則不會增添任何香氣，而涼爽氣候影響的是酸度和水果類型，不是香草味。","In Champagne, Chardonnay is often blended with which grape?":"在 Champagne 中，夏多內經常與哪一個品種混釀？","Champagne is made from Chardonnay and Pinot Noir.":"Champagne 以夏多內和黑皮諾釀造。","Champagne, the famous French sparkling wine, is made from Chardonnay and Pinot Noir, often blended together. Pinot Noir is a black grape, but its juice is colourless, so removing the skins straight away gives a white wine. Merlot and Riesling are not Champagne grapes.":"Champagne 是法國著名的氣泡酒，以夏多內和黑皮諾釀造，兩者常常混釀。黑皮諾是黑葡萄，但果汁無色，只要立刻去除果皮就能釀出白酒。梅洛和麗絲玲不是 Champagne 的品種。","Besides Burgundy, which places are well known for Chardonnay?":"除了布根地，還有哪些地方以夏多內聞名？","Australia and California":"澳洲和加州","Germany and Alsace":"德國和阿爾薩斯","Spain and Portugal":"西班牙和葡萄牙","New Zealand and the Loire":"紐西蘭和羅亞爾河","Australia and California are well known for their Chardonnay.":"澳洲和加州以夏多內聞名。","Chardonnay is grown in many countries, but besides Burgundy, Australia and California are especially well known, often for warmer, fruitier styles. Germany and Alsace are famous for Riesling, while New Zealand and the Loire (Sancerre) are famous for Sauvignon Blanc.":"許多國家都種植夏多內，但除了布根地之外，澳洲和加州特別有名，風格往往較溫暖、果味更濃。德國和阿爾薩斯以麗絲玲聞名，紐西蘭和羅亞爾河（Sancerre）則以白蘇維濃聞名。","Which herbaceous notes are typical of Sauvignon Blanc?":"哪些草本氣息是白蘇維濃的典型特徵？","Asparagus, green bell pepper, grass":"蘆筍、青椒、青草","Vanilla, coconut, smoke":"香草、椰子、煙燻","Honey, apricot, peach":"蜂蜜、杏桃、桃子","Black pepper, liquorice, blackberry":"黑胡椒、甘草、黑莓","Sauvignon Blanc pairs fresh fruit with asparagus, green pepper and grass.":"白蘇維濃結合了新鮮果香與蘆筍、青椒和青草氣息。","Besides fruit (apple, grapefruit, passion fruit), Sauvignon Blanc often shows herbaceous notes: asparagus, green bell pepper and cut grass. Vanilla, coconut and smoke come from oak; black pepper and liquorice are typical of Syrah/Shiraz; and honey and apricot belong to Sauternes.":"除了果香（蘋果、葡萄柚、百香果），白蘇維濃常帶有草本氣息：蘆筍、青椒和剛割過的青草。香草、椰子和煙燻來自橡木桶；黑胡椒和甘草是希哈／希拉茲的典型香氣；蜂蜜和杏桃則屬於 Sauternes。","Why is Sauvignon Blanc usually not matured in oak?":"為什麼白蘇維濃通常不經橡木桶熟成？","To keep its characteristic aromas":"為了保留它的特色香氣","To increase the wine's tannin":"為了增加酒的單寧","To make the wine sweeter":"為了讓酒更甜","Without oak, the grape's intense aromas stay in the spotlight.":"不用橡木桶，品種本身濃郁的香氣才能成為主角。","Sauvignon Blanc is loved precisely for its intense fruity and herbaceous aromas. To protect them, it is often fermented in stainless steel and usually not matured in oak, which would add vanilla and toasty notes. Oak is not used to make it sweeter or darker.":"白蘇維濃受人喜愛，正是因為它濃郁的果香和草本香氣。為了保護這些香氣，它常在不鏽鋼槽中發酵，而且通常不經橡木桶熟成，否則會增添香草和烘烤氣息。使用橡木桶並不是為了讓酒更甜或顏色更深。","Which French wine is made from Sauvignon Blanc?":"哪一款法國葡萄酒以白蘇維濃釀造？","Sancerre, a white from the Loire, is made from Sauvignon Blanc.":"Sancerre 是羅亞爾河的白酒，以白蘇維濃釀造。","Sancerre is a dry, medium-bodied white from the Loire Valley with green apple, grass and high acidity. It is Sauvignon Blanc, even though the label usually does not say so. Chablis is made from Chardonnay, while Beaujolais and Côtes du Rhône are red wines.":"Sancerre 是來自羅亞爾河谷的不甜白酒，酒體中等，帶有青蘋果和青草香氣，酸度高。它是白蘇維濃，只是酒標上通常不會寫出來。Chablis 以夏多內釀造，Beaujolais 和 Côtes du Rhône 則是紅酒。","Which pair of wines are classic Sauvignon Blanc wines?":"哪一組是經典的白蘇維濃葡萄酒？","New Zealand Sauvignon Blanc and Sancerre":"紐西蘭白蘇維濃和 Sancerre","Chablis and white Burgundy":"Chablis 和布根地白酒","Alsace and Mosel Riesling":"阿爾薩斯和 Mosel 的麗絲玲","Prosecco and Cava":"Prosecco 和 Cava","They are the two most popular Sauvignon Blanc wines to know.":"這是最值得認識的兩款熱門白蘇維濃葡萄酒。","New Zealand Sauvignon Blanc, from Marlborough for example, and Sancerre from the Loire are the two most popular examples of the grape: dry, aromatic and high in acidity. Chablis and white Burgundy are Chardonnay, while Prosecco and Cava are sparkling wines made from other grapes.":"紐西蘭白蘇維濃（例如來自馬爾堡）和羅亞爾河的 Sancerre，是這個品種最受歡迎的兩個例子：不甜、芳香、酸度高。Chablis 和布根地白酒是夏多內，Prosecco 和 Cava 則是以其他品種釀造的氣泡酒。","What acidity and body are typical of Sauvignon Blanc?":"白蘇維濃典型的酸度和酒體是什麼？","High acidity, light to medium body":"高酸度，酒體輕盈至中等","Low acidity, full body":"低酸度，酒體飽滿","Medium acidity, full body":"中等酸度，酒體飽滿","Low acidity, light body":"低酸度，酒體輕盈","Sauvignon Blanc is crisp: high acidity with a light to medium body.":"白蘇維濃清脆爽口：高酸度，酒體輕盈至中等。","Sauvignon Blanc makes dry wines with refreshingly high acidity and a light to medium body. Together with its intense fruity and herbaceous aromas, that freshness defines its style. A full body with medium acidity would point more towards a warm-climate Chardonnay.":"白蘇維濃釀出不甜的葡萄酒，酸度高而清爽，酒體輕盈至中等。這份清爽感，加上濃郁的果香和草本香氣，構成了它的風格。酒體飽滿、酸度中等，則比較像溫暖氣候的夏多內。","Which range of fruit is found in Sauvignon Blanc?":"白蘇維濃有哪些水果香氣？","Apple, grapefruit, passion fruit":"蘋果、葡萄柚、百香果","Blackcurrant, black cherry, blackberry":"黑醋栗、黑櫻桃、黑莓","Apricot, honey, ripe peach":"杏桃、蜂蜜、熟桃子","Sauvignon Blanc ranges from green fruit to citrus to tropical fruit.":"白蘇維濃的果香從綠色水果、柑橘類到熱帶水果都有。","Sauvignon Blanc's fruit aromas run from green apple through grapefruit to passion fruit, often with herbaceous notes. Black fruit is typical of reds like Cabernet Sauvignon, red fruit of Pinot Noir, while apricot and honey bring Sauternes to mind. Recognising the family of fruit is the first step towards naming the grape.":"白蘇維濃的果香從青蘋果、葡萄柚一路到百香果，常伴隨草本氣息。黑色水果是卡本內蘇維濃等紅酒的典型香氣，紅色水果屬於黑皮諾，杏桃和蜂蜜則讓人想到 Sauternes。辨認水果的類別，是說出品種的第一步。","Which description matches a Pinot Grigio?":"哪一項描述符合灰皮諾？","Dry, light-bodied, pear and lemon":"不甜，酒體輕盈，梨子和檸檬","Sweet, full-bodied, apricot and honey":"甜，酒體飽滿，杏桃和蜂蜜","Dry, full-bodied, pineapple and vanilla":"不甜，酒體飽滿，鳳梨和香草","Medium, light, strawberry and raspberry":"半甜，酒體輕盈，草莓和覆盆子","Pinot Grigio is usually dry and light, with pear and lemon.":"灰皮諾通常不甜而輕盈，帶有梨子和檸檬風味。","Pinot Grigio usually makes dry, light-bodied wines with medium to high acidity and simple pear and lemon flavours. The other descriptions fit other wines: Sauternes (sweet, apricot and honey), an oaked warm-climate Chardonnay, and White Zinfandel. Think of it as a simple, fresh and easy white.":"灰皮諾通常釀成不甜、酒體輕盈的葡萄酒，酸度中等至高，帶有簡單的梨子和檸檬風味。其他描述對應的是別的酒：Sauternes（甜，杏桃和蜂蜜）、經橡木桶的溫暖氣候夏多內，以及 White Zinfandel。把它想成一款簡單、清爽、易飲的白酒就對了。","Which country is Pinot Grigio mainly associated with?":"灰皮諾主要與哪個國家有關？","Pinot Grigio is mainly linked with Italy, though grown elsewhere too.":"灰皮諾主要與義大利有關，不過其他地方也有種植。","Pinot Grigio is a hugely popular grape mainly associated with Italy, in areas such as Veneto or Trentino, although it is grown in several other countries too. Germany is the classic home of Riesling, and New Zealand is known for Sauvignon Blanc and Pinot Noir.":"灰皮諾是極受歡迎的品種，主要與義大利有關，例如唯內多（Veneto）或特倫提諾（Trentino），不過其他幾個國家也有種植。德國是麗絲玲的經典產地，紐西蘭則以白蘇維濃和黑皮諾聞名。","Why is Pinot Grigio usually made in stainless steel without oak?":"為什麼灰皮諾通常在不鏽鋼槽中釀造、不經橡木桶？","To keep its fruity flavours":"為了保留它的果味","To add notes of vanilla":"為了增添香草氣息","To increase its tannin":"為了增加單寧","To make it higher in alcohol":"為了提高酒精濃度","Steel adds no aromas, so the delicate fruit stays intact.":"不鏽鋼不會增添香氣，細緻的果香得以完整保留。","Pinot Grigio has delicate pear and lemon flavours. Fermenting it in stainless steel and skipping oak maturation protects that fruit and lightness. Oak would add exactly the vanilla notes the style avoids, while tannin and alcohol do not depend on the vessel used.":"灰皮諾有細緻的梨子和檸檬風味。在不鏽鋼槽中發酵、不經橡木桶熟成，可以保護這份果香與輕盈感。橡木桶會帶來這種風格正想避免的香草氣息，而單寧和酒精並不取決於使用的容器。","What range of sweetness can Riesling have?":"麗絲玲的甜度範圍有多廣？","Dry to sweet, always with high acidity":"從不甜到甜，酸度始終很高","Always sweet, with low acidity":"一定是甜的，酸度低","Always dry, with low acidity":"一定是不甜的，酸度低","Only medium, with medium acidity":"只有半甜，酸度中等","Riesling can be dry, medium or sweet, but always has high acidity.":"麗絲玲可以是不甜、半甜或甜，但酸度始終很高。","Riesling is versatile: it makes dry, medium and sweet wines. What does not change is its high acidity, which balances the sugar and keeps the wine fresh. So when you see «Riesling» on a label, check the origin or the description to work out how sweet it will be.":"麗絲玲用途多樣：可以釀成不甜、半甜和甜型葡萄酒。不變的是它的高酸度，能平衡糖分，讓酒保持清爽。所以在酒標上看到「Riesling」時，要查看產地或說明，才能判斷它有多甜。","Which country is the classic home of Riesling?":"哪個國家是麗絲玲的經典產地？","Germany is Riesling's classic home, making it from dry to sweet.":"德國是麗絲玲的經典產地，從不甜到甜都有釀造。","Riesling is the classic grape of Germany, where it is made across the full sweetness range, from dry to sweet. Fine dry Rieslings also come from Alsace in France and from Australia. Among the key white grapes, Italy is linked mainly with Pinot Grigio.":"麗絲玲是德國的經典品種，當地釀造的甜度範圍完整，從不甜到甜都有。法國的阿爾薩斯和澳洲也出產優質的不甜麗絲玲。在主要白葡萄品種中，義大利主要與灰皮諾有關。","In which style do Alsace and Australia make Riesling?":"阿爾薩斯和澳洲以哪一種風格釀造麗絲玲？","Alsace and Australia are known for dry Riesling.":"阿爾薩斯和澳洲以不甜的麗絲玲聞名。","While Germany makes Riesling from dry to sweet, Alsace in France and Australia make it in a dry style. These are very fresh wines with citrus such as lime and lemon, floral notes and sometimes peach. Knowing the origin therefore helps you predict the sweetness.":"德國釀造從不甜到甜的麗絲玲，法國的阿爾薩斯和澳洲則釀成不甜的風格。這些酒非常清爽，帶有萊姆和檸檬等柑橘類香氣、花香，有時還有桃子。所以知道產地有助於預測甜度。","Its high acidity balances the sweetness":"高酸度平衡了甜味","Oak flavours mask the sugar":"橡木風味掩蓋了糖分","Tannin dries out the mouth":"單寧讓口腔乾澀","High alcohol hides the sugar":"高酒精濃度掩蓋了糖分","All Rieslings are high in acid, which counterbalances the sugar.":"所有麗絲玲的酸度都高，能與糖分抗衡。","Riesling always has high acidity. In sweet or medium wines, that acidity balances the sugar and keeps each sip fresh. Riesling is usually not oaked, as a white wine it has almost no tannin, and sweet German Rieslings are often low in alcohol, so the other options do not apply.":"麗絲玲的酸度始終很高。在甜或半甜的酒中，酸度平衡了糖分，讓每一口都清爽。麗絲玲通常不經橡木桶；身為白酒，幾乎沒有單寧；而德國的甜型麗絲玲酒精濃度往往偏低，所以其他選項都不成立。","Which aromas can a Riesling show?":"麗絲玲可以呈現哪些香氣？","Floral, lime, peach":"花香、萊姆、桃子","Blackcurrant, mint, bell pepper":"黑醋栗、薄荷、甜椒","Riesling ranges from floral and citrus aromas to stone fruit.":"麗絲玲的香氣從花香、柑橘類到核果都有。","Riesling has pronounced aromas that can range from flowers and green apple to citrus such as lime and lemon, and on to peach and apricot. It is usually unoaked, so vanilla, cedar and smoke are not typical. Black pepper and blackcurrant belong to black grape varieties.":"麗絲玲香氣濃郁，從花香和青蘋果，到萊姆和檸檬等柑橘類，再到桃子和杏桃。它通常不經橡木桶，所以香草、雪松和煙燻並不典型。黑胡椒和黑醋栗則屬於黑葡萄品種。","Which of the four key white grapes is most often matured in oak?":"四大白葡萄品種中，哪一個最常經橡木桶熟成？","Chardonnay can be oaked; the other three usually are not.":"夏多內可以經橡木桶；其他三個通常不經。","Sauvignon Blanc, Pinot Grigio and Riesling are often fermented in stainless steel and usually not matured in oak, to protect their fruity aromas. Chardonnay, on the other hand, is often aged in oak, which adds vanilla: think of many white Burgundies or Californian Chardonnays.":"白蘇維濃、灰皮諾和麗絲玲常在不鏽鋼槽中發酵，而且通常不經橡木桶熟成，以保護果香。夏多內則常在橡木桶中陳年，增添香草氣息：想想許多布根地白酒或加州夏多內。","A wine list says «full-bodied, ripe tropical fruit and vanilla». Which wine is it?":"酒單上寫著「酒體飽滿，成熟的熱帶水果和香草」。這是哪一款酒？","A Californian Chardonnay":"加州夏多內","An Italian Pinot Grigio":"義大利灰皮諾","An Alsace Riesling":"阿爾薩斯麗絲玲","Warm climate plus oak gives body, tropical fruit and vanilla.":"溫暖氣候加上橡木桶，帶來酒體、熱帶水果和香草。","Ripe tropical fruit points to a warm climate, vanilla points to oak, and a full body completes the picture: this is the style of a Californian Chardonnay. Chablis is light and unoaked, Pinot Grigio is light with pear and lemon, and Alsace Riesling is dry, floral and unoaked.":"成熟的熱帶水果指向溫暖氣候，香草指向橡木桶，再加上飽滿的酒體：這就是加州夏多內的風格。Chablis 輕盈且不經橡木桶，灰皮諾輕盈並帶有梨子和檸檬，阿爾薩斯麗絲玲則不甜、帶花香、不經橡木桶。","Which white grape is used to make Champagne?":"釀造 Champagne 使用哪一個白葡萄品種？","Chardonnay is Champagne's white grape, often blended with Pinot Noir.":"夏多內是 Champagne 的白葡萄品種，常與黑皮諾混釀。","Of the four key white grapes, only Chardonnay goes into Champagne, where it is often blended with Pinot Noir, a black grape. The result is a sparkling wine that is usually dry, with high acidity, green apple, lemon and notes of toasted bread. The other three grapes are not used for Champagne.":"四大白葡萄品種中，只有夏多內用於 Champagne，並常與黑葡萄品種黑皮諾混釀。釀出的氣泡酒通常不甜、酸度高，帶有青蘋果、檸檬和烤麵包氣息。其他三個品種不用於 Champagne。","A list says «Australia, dry, aromas of lime and blossom». Which grape is it?":"酒單上寫著「澳洲，不甜，萊姆和花香」。這是哪一個品種？","Lime and blossom in a dry Australian white point to Riesling.":"不甜的澳洲白酒帶有萊姆和花香，指向麗絲玲。","Australia makes Riesling in a dry style, with citrus such as lime and floral notes, carried by high acidity. Australian Chardonnay leans towards riper fruit and often vanilla; Sauvignon Blanc pairs citrus with herbaceous notes; and Pinot Grigio shows pear and lemon without marked floral aromas.":"澳洲以不甜的風格釀造麗絲玲，帶有萊姆等柑橘類香氣和花香，並由高酸度支撐。澳洲夏多內偏向更成熟的果香，而且常有香草味；白蘇維濃結合柑橘與草本氣息；灰皮諾則呈現梨子和檸檬，沒有明顯的花香。","Which structure is typical of Cabernet Sauvignon?":"卡本內蘇維濃典型的結構是什麼？","High tannin and high acidity":"高單寧、高酸度","Low tannin and high acidity":"低單寧、高酸度","Medium tannin and medium acidity":"中等單寧、中等酸度","Low tannin and low acidity":"低單寧、低酸度","Cabernet Sauvignon is high in both tannin and acidity.":"卡本內蘇維濃的單寧和酸度都高。","Cabernet Sauvignon makes dry reds with high tannin and high acidity, and a medium to full body. Merlot has medium tannin and acidity, while Pinot Noir has high acidity but low to medium tannin. That high tannin is exactly why Cabernet is so often blended with Merlot.":"卡本內蘇維濃釀出不甜的紅酒，單寧高、酸度高，酒體中等至飽滿。梅洛的單寧和酸度中等，黑皮諾則酸度高但單寧低至中等。正因為單寧高，卡本內才這麼常與梅洛混釀。","Which fruit is the signature aroma of Cabernet Sauvignon?":"哪一種水果是卡本內蘇維濃的招牌香氣？","Pear":"梨子","Raspberry":"覆盆子","Blackcurrant is Cabernet Sauvignon's hallmark aroma.":"黑醋栗是卡本內蘇維濃的招牌香氣。","Cabernet Sauvignon smells of black fruit, above all blackcurrant and black cherry, often with notes of green bell pepper and mint. Strawberry and raspberry are red fruits typical of Pinot Noir or Beaujolais, while pear belongs to whites such as Pinot Grigio.":"卡本內蘇維濃有黑色水果香氣，尤其是黑醋栗和黑櫻桃，常帶有青椒和薄荷氣息。草莓和覆盆子是黑皮諾或 Beaujolais 典型的紅色水果，梨子則屬於灰皮諾等白酒。","Which herbaceous notes can Cabernet Sauvignon show?":"卡本內蘇維濃可以呈現哪些草本氣息？","Green bell pepper and mint":"青椒和薄荷","Dried herbs and cloves":"乾燥香草和丁香","Flowers and honey":"花香和蜂蜜","Green pepper and mint often sit alongside Cabernet's blackcurrant.":"青椒和薄荷常伴隨著卡本內的黑醋栗香氣。","Besides blackcurrant and black cherry, Cabernet Sauvignon often shows herbaceous notes of green bell pepper and mint. Black pepper and liquorice are spices typical of Syrah/Shiraz, dried herbs are found in Chianti, and cloves come from oak. Those «green» notes are therefore a useful clue for recognising it.":"除了黑醋栗和黑櫻桃，卡本內蘇維濃常帶有青椒和薄荷的草本氣息。黑胡椒和甘草是希哈／希拉茲典型的香料氣息，乾燥香草可在 Chianti 中找到，丁香則來自橡木桶。因此這些「青綠」氣息是辨認它的實用線索。","Which aromas does oak add to a Cabernet Sauvignon?":"橡木桶為卡本內蘇維濃增添哪些香氣？","Cedar and vanilla":"雪松和香草","Mint and green bell pepper":"薄荷和青椒","Blackcurrant and black cherry":"黑醋栗和黑櫻桃","Lemon and green apple":"檸檬和青蘋果","Oak brings cedar and vanilla; fruit and herbaceous notes come from the grape.":"橡木桶帶來雪松和香草；果香和草本氣息來自葡萄。","Cabernet Sauvignon is often matured in oak, which adds cedar and vanilla notes. Blackcurrant, black cherry, mint and green bell pepper, on the other hand, come from the grape itself. Separating grape aromas from oak aromas helps you understand how the wine was made.":"卡本內蘇維濃常在橡木桶中熟成，增添雪松和香草氣息。黑醋栗、黑櫻桃、薄荷和青椒則來自葡萄本身。把品種香氣和橡木香氣分開，有助於了解這款酒是怎麼釀成的。","Merlot softens the tannin and adds body":"梅洛讓單寧變柔和並增添酒體","Merlot raises acidity and tannin":"梅洛提高酸度和單寧","Merlot makes the wine sweet":"梅洛讓酒變甜","Merlot makes the colour lighter":"梅洛讓顏色變淺","Merlot softens Cabernet's high tannin and adds body.":"梅洛讓卡本內的高單寧變柔和，並增添酒體。","Cabernet Sauvignon has a lot of tannin. Blending it with Merlot, which has medium tannin and acidity, gives a softer wine with more body. It works the other way round too: Cabernet gives Merlot extra tannin and acidity. Bordeaux is the most famous region for this blend.":"卡本內蘇維濃的單寧很多。與單寧和酸度中等的梅洛混釀，能得到更柔和、酒體更飽滿的酒。反過來也成立：卡本內為梅洛補上單寧和酸度。波爾多是這種混釀最著名的產區。","In Australia, Cabernet Sauvignon is sometimes blended with which grape?":"在澳洲，卡本內蘇維濃有時會與哪一個品種混釀？","In Australia, Shiraz adds spicy aromas to Cabernet Sauvignon.":"在澳洲，希拉茲為卡本內蘇維濃增添香料氣息。","Cabernet Sauvignon is widely grown in Australia, where it is sometimes blended with Shiraz, which adds spicy aromas. Pinot Noir is not usually blended when making red wine, and Riesling and Chardonnay are white grapes that do not go into red blends.":"卡本內蘇維濃在澳洲廣泛種植，有時與希拉茲混釀，增添香料氣息。黑皮諾釀造紅酒時通常不混釀，麗絲玲和夏多內則是白葡萄品種，不會用於紅酒混釀。","What structure does Merlot usually have?":"梅洛通常有什麼樣的結構？","Medium acidity and tannin, medium to full body":"酸度和單寧中等，酒體中等至飽滿","High acidity and tannin, full body":"酸度和單寧高，酒體飽滿","High acidity, low tannin, light body":"高酸度，低單寧，酒體輕盈","Low acidity, high tannin, light body":"低酸度，高單寧，酒體輕盈","Merlot is soft: medium acidity and tannin, medium to full body.":"梅洛很柔和：酸度和單寧中等，酒體中等至飽滿。","Merlot makes wines that are generally dry, with a medium to full body and medium acidity and tannin. Cabernet Sauvignon has high tannin and acidity, while Pinot Noir has high acidity, low to medium tannin and a light to medium body. That is why Merlot feels softer.":"梅洛釀出的葡萄酒通常不甜，酒體中等至飽滿，酸度和單寧中等。卡本內蘇維濃的單寧和酸度高，黑皮諾則酸度高、單寧低至中等、酒體輕盈至中等。所以梅洛喝起來比較柔和。","Which fruits are typically found in Merlot?":"梅洛通常有哪些水果香氣？","Strawberry and red plum through to blackberry and black plum":"從草莓、紅李到黑莓、黑李","Green apple, lemon and grapefruit":"青蘋果、檸檬和葡萄柚","Apricot, peach and honey":"杏桃、桃子和蜂蜜","Pear, flowers and lime":"梨子、花香和萊姆","Merlot ranges from red fruit to black fruit.":"梅洛的果香從紅色水果到黑色水果都有。","Merlot can show red fruit such as strawberry and red plum, or black fruit such as blackberry and black plum. It is often matured in oak, which adds vanilla. The other options describe aromas of white wines such as Sauvignon Blanc, Sauternes or Riesling.":"梅洛可以呈現草莓、紅李等紅色水果，或黑莓、黑李等黑色水果。它常在橡木桶中熟成，增添香草氣息。其他選項描述的是白蘇維濃、Sauternes 或麗絲玲等白酒的香氣。","What does Cabernet Sauvignon add to a blend with Merlot?":"在與梅洛的混釀中，卡本內蘇維濃增添了什麼？","Tannin and acidity":"單寧和酸度","Sweetness and softness":"甜味和柔順感","Pale colour and lightness":"淺色和輕盈感","Cabernet brings tannin and acidity; Merlot brings softness and body.":"卡本內帶來單寧和酸度；梅洛帶來柔順感和酒體。","In the Bordeaux blend the two grapes complete each other. Merlot, with medium tannin and acidity, brings softness and body. Cabernet Sauvignon, with high tannin and acidity, gives the wine structure and freshness. The result is a dry, medium- to full-bodied red with black fruit, often with cedar from oak.":"在波爾多混釀中，兩個品種相輔相成。單寧和酸度中等的梅洛帶來柔順感和酒體。單寧和酸度高的卡本內蘇維濃則賦予酒結構和清爽感。成果是不甜、酒體中等至飽滿的紅酒，帶有黑色水果，並常有來自橡木桶的雪松氣息。","Which countries make soft, fruity Merlot?":"哪些地方出產柔順、果味豐富的梅洛？","Chile and California":"智利和加州","Portugal and Spain":"葡萄牙和西班牙","Chile and California are known for soft, fruity Merlot.":"智利和加州以柔順、果味豐富的梅洛聞名。","Merlot is grown in many places; Chile and California use it for soft, fruity, easy-drinking wines, often with black plum and blackberry. Germany and Alsace are linked with Riesling, New Zealand and the Loire with Sauvignon Blanc, and Portugal with Port.":"許多地方都種植梅洛；智利和加州用它釀造柔順、果味豐富、易飲的葡萄酒，常帶有黑李和黑莓風味。德國和阿爾薩斯與麗絲玲有關，紐西蘭和羅亞爾河與白蘇維濃有關，葡萄牙則與 Port 有關。","Which region is most famous for Merlot-Cabernet Sauvignon blends?":"哪個產區最以梅洛與卡本內蘇維濃的混釀聞名？","Bordeaux is the home of the Merlot-Cabernet Sauvignon blend.":"波爾多是梅洛與卡本內蘇維濃混釀的故鄉。","Bordeaux in France is the most famous region for blending Merlot and Cabernet Sauvignon, a blend now common in many other countries too. Burgundy uses Pinot Noir for its reds and Chardonnay for its whites, while Champagne is made from Chardonnay and Pinot Noir.":"法國的波爾多是梅洛與卡本內蘇維濃混釀最著名的產區，這種混釀如今在許多其他國家也很常見。布根地的紅酒使用黑皮諾、白酒使用夏多內，Champagne 則以夏多內和黑皮諾釀造。","Which description fits Pinot Noir?":"哪一項描述符合黑皮諾？","Light to medium body, high acidity, low to medium tannin":"酒體輕盈至中等，高酸度，單寧低至中等","Full body, medium acidity, high tannin":"酒體飽滿，中等酸度，高單寧","Full body, high acidity, high tannin":"酒體飽滿，高酸度，高單寧","Medium body, low acidity, medium tannin":"酒體中等，低酸度，中等單寧","Pinot Noir is a fresh, delicate red with modest tannin.":"黑皮諾是清爽、細緻、單寧不高的紅酒。","Pinot Noir makes reds that are usually dry, light to medium in body, with high acidity and low to medium tannin. It has red fruit aromas such as strawberry, red cherry and raspberry. A full body with high tannin describes Cabernet Sauvignon or Shiraz instead.":"黑皮諾釀出的紅酒通常不甜，酒體輕盈至中等，酸度高，單寧低至中等。它有草莓、紅櫻桃和覆盆子等紅色水果香氣。酒體飽滿、單寧高，描述的則是卡本內蘇維濃或希拉茲。","Strawberry, red cherry, raspberry":"草莓、紅櫻桃、覆盆子","Blackberry, black pepper, liquorice":"黑莓、黑胡椒、甘草","Pear, lemon, apple":"梨子、檸檬、蘋果","Pinot Noir smells of red fruit.":"黑皮諾有紅色水果香氣。","Pinot Noir is the red-fruit grape: strawberry, red cherry and raspberry, often with vanilla and smoke when oaked. Blackcurrant and mint point to Cabernet Sauvignon; blackberry, black pepper and liquorice point to Syrah/Shiraz; and pear and lemon are white-wine aromas.":"黑皮諾是紅色水果的品種：草莓、紅櫻桃和覆盆子，經橡木桶時常帶有香草和煙燻氣息。黑醋栗和薄荷指向卡本內蘇維濃；黑莓、黑胡椒和甘草指向希哈／希拉茲；梨子和檸檬則是白酒的香氣。","Which grape is used for red Burgundy?":"布根地紅酒使用哪一個葡萄品種？","Red Burgundy is made from Pinot Noir.":"布根地紅酒以黑皮諾釀造。","Burgundy (Bourgogne) uses Pinot Noir for its reds and Chardonnay for its whites. The reds are dry, light to medium-bodied, with high acidity, low to medium tannin and red fruit. Merlot and Cabernet Sauvignon are the grapes of Bordeaux, and Syrah is typical of the Northern Rhône.":"布根地（Bourgogne）的紅酒使用黑皮諾，白酒使用夏多內。紅酒不甜，酒體輕盈至中等，酸度高，單寧低至中等，帶有紅色水果。梅洛和卡本內蘇維濃是波爾多的品種，希哈則是北隆河的典型品種。","In which country is Pinot Noir the main black grape?":"在哪個國家，黑皮諾是最主要的黑葡萄品種？","In New Zealand, Pinot Noir is the leading black grape.":"在紐西蘭，黑皮諾是最主要的黑葡萄品種。","Besides Burgundy, Pinot Noir is the main black grape of New Zealand, in regions such as Central Otago. Australia, Chile and South Africa are mentioned mainly for Cabernet Sauvignon, and Australia also for Shiraz. New Zealand is also famous for its Sauvignon Blanc.":"除了布根地，黑皮諾也是紐西蘭最主要的黑葡萄品種，例如在中奧塔哥（Central Otago）等產區。澳洲、智利和南非主要因卡本內蘇維濃而被提及，澳洲還有希拉茲。紐西蘭也以白蘇維濃聞名。","When making red wine, Pinot Noir is usually...":"釀造紅酒時，黑皮諾通常……","made on its own, without other grapes":"單獨釀造，不與其他品種混釀","blended with Cabernet Sauvignon":"與卡本內蘇維濃混釀","blended with Shiraz":"與希拉茲混釀","blended with Merlot":"與梅洛混釀","For red wines, Pinot Noir is not usually blended.":"釀造紅酒時，黑皮諾通常不混釀。","Unlike Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot and Shiraz, which are often blended with each other, Pinot Noir is usually made on its own when producing red wine. The one important blend to remember is Champagne, where Pinot Noir is combined with Chardonnay to make a sparkling wine.":"卡本內蘇維濃、梅洛和希拉茲常常彼此混釀，黑皮諾則不同，釀造紅酒時通常單獨使用。唯一要記住的重要混釀是 Champagne，黑皮諾在那裡與夏多內結合，釀成氣泡酒。","What is Syrah called in Australia?":"希哈（Syrah）在澳洲叫什麼？","Syrah in France and Shiraz in Australia are the same grape.":"法國的希哈（Syrah）和澳洲的希拉茲（Shiraz）是同一個品種。","The same grape has two names: Syrah in France and Shiraz in Australia. The name on the label therefore hints at the origin and often the style, fresher and more peppery in France, fuller and riper in Australia's warm regions. Merlot and Pinot Noir are different grapes.":"同一個品種有兩個名字：在法國叫希哈（Syrah），在澳洲叫希拉茲（Shiraz）。所以酒標上的名字暗示了產地，往往也暗示風格：法國的較清爽、胡椒味較明顯，澳洲溫暖產區的則更飽滿、更成熟。梅洛和黑皮諾是不同的品種。","Which spices are typical of Syrah/Shiraz?":"哪些香料氣息是希哈／希拉茲的典型特徵？","White pepper and dried herbs":"白胡椒和乾燥香草","Syrah/Shiraz pairs black fruit with black pepper and liquorice.":"希哈／希拉茲結合了黑色水果與黑胡椒、甘草。","Syrah/Shiraz typically shows black fruit such as blackberry and black cherry, with spices such as black pepper and liquorice. Vanilla and coconut come from oak rather than the grape. Mint and green bell pepper are Cabernet Sauvignon notes, and white pepper is mentioned for Côtes du Rhône.":"希哈／希拉茲通常呈現黑莓和黑櫻桃等黑色水果，以及黑胡椒和甘草等香料氣息。香草和椰子來自橡木桶，而不是葡萄。薄荷和青椒是卡本內蘇維濃的氣息，白胡椒則在 Côtes du Rhône 中被提及。","What style does Northern Rhône Syrah often have?":"北隆河的希哈通常是什麼風格？","Medium body, fresh blackberry and black pepper":"酒體中等，新鮮黑莓和黑胡椒","Full body, jammy black cherry":"酒體飽滿，果醬般的黑櫻桃","Light body, strawberry and raspberry":"酒體輕盈，草莓和覆盆子","Sweet, black plum and honey":"甜，黑李和蜂蜜","Northern Rhône Syrah is fresher: medium body, blackberry and pepper.":"北隆河的希哈較清爽：酒體中等，黑莓和胡椒。","France's Northern Rhône can produce medium-bodied Syrah with fresh blackberry and black pepper. In warm parts of Australia the grapes ripen further and Shiraz becomes full-bodied, with jammy black cherry and liquorice. Same grape, different climates, different styles. Climate explains the difference.":"法國北隆河可以釀出酒體中等的希哈，帶有新鮮黑莓和黑胡椒風味。在澳洲的溫暖地區，葡萄更成熟，希拉茲變得酒體飽滿，帶有果醬般的黑櫻桃和甘草風味。同一個品種，不同的氣候，不同的風格。差異就來自氣候。","Why is Shiraz from warm parts of Australia often full-bodied?":"為什麼澳洲溫暖地區的希拉茲往往酒體飽滿？","The heat makes the grapes riper":"熱量讓葡萄更成熟","The grapes are picked unripe":"葡萄在未成熟時採收","The wine is made without skins":"酒在釀造時不帶果皮","Unfermented juice is added":"加入了未發酵的葡萄汁","More heat means riper, sweeter grapes and a fuller, riper wine.":"熱量越多，葡萄越成熟、越甜，酒也越飽滿、越成熟。","In warm climates grapes ripen reliably and build up more sugar. That gives riper, fuller wines: Shiraz from warm Australian regions such as the Barossa Valley is full-bodied, with jammy black cherry and liquorice. In the cooler Northern Rhône, the style is medium-bodied instead.":"在溫暖氣候，葡萄能穩定成熟並累積更多糖分，釀出更成熟、更飽滿的葡萄酒：來自巴羅莎谷（Barossa Valley）等澳洲溫暖產區的希拉茲酒體飽滿，帶有果醬般的黑櫻桃和甘草風味。在較涼爽的北隆河，風格則是酒體中等。","Which notes does oak add to many Syrah/Shiraz wines?":"橡木桶為許多希哈／希拉茲葡萄酒增添哪些氣息？","Vanilla or coconut":"香草或椰子","Black pepper or liquorice":"黑胡椒或甘草","Blackberry or black cherry":"黑莓或黑櫻桃","Grass or asparagus":"青草或蘆筍","Oak gives vanilla or coconut; black fruit and spice come from the grape.":"橡木桶帶來香草或椰子；黑色水果和香料氣息來自葡萄。","Many Syrahs and Shirazes are matured in oak, which adds vanilla or coconut notes. Black fruit (blackberry, black cherry) and spice (black pepper, liquorice), on the other hand, are the grape's own aromas. Grass and asparagus are herbaceous notes typical of Sauvignon Blanc.":"許多希哈和希拉茲都在橡木桶中熟成，增添香草或椰子氣息。黑色水果（黑莓、黑櫻桃）和香料（黑胡椒、甘草）則是品種本身的香氣。青草和蘆筍是白蘇維濃典型的草本氣息。","A list says «light-bodied, high acidity, strawberry and red cherry». Which grape?":"酒單上寫著「酒體輕盈，高酸度，草莓和紅櫻桃」。這是哪一個品種？","Light body, high acidity and red fruit point to Pinot Noir.":"酒體輕盈、酸度高、紅色水果，指向黑皮諾。","Of the four key black grapes, Pinot Noir is the lightest and freshest: light to medium body, high acidity, low to medium tannin and red fruit. Cabernet Sauvignon and Shiraz are fuller, with black fruit, while Merlot has medium acidity and a medium to full body.":"四大黑葡萄品種中，黑皮諾最輕盈、最清爽：酒體輕盈至中等，酸度高，單寧低至中等，帶有紅色水果。卡本內蘇維濃和希拉茲更飽滿，帶有黑色水果，梅洛則酸度中等、酒體中等至飽滿。","A list says «Australia, full-bodied, intense black cherry and liquorice». Which grape?":"酒單上寫著「澳洲，酒體飽滿，濃郁的黑櫻桃和甘草」。這是哪一個品種？","Black cherry and liquorice in a full Australian red point to Shiraz.":"酒體飽滿的澳洲紅酒帶有黑櫻桃和甘草，指向希拉茲。","Warm Australian regions such as the Barossa Valley make full-bodied Shiraz with ripe black cherry and liquorice. Pinot Noir is light with red fruit, Merlot is soft with plum and blackberry, and Riesling is a white grape, so none of them fits this description.":"巴羅莎谷等澳洲溫暖產區出產酒體飽滿的希拉茲，帶有成熟的黑櫻桃和甘草風味。黑皮諾輕盈、帶紅色水果，梅洛柔順、帶李子和黑莓，麗絲玲則是白葡萄品種，所以都不符合這項描述。","Which black grape is used to make Champagne?":"釀造 Champagne 使用哪一個黑葡萄品種？","Champagne often blends Pinot Noir with Chardonnay.":"Champagne 常以黑皮諾與夏多內混釀。","Of the four key black grapes, only Pinot Noir goes into Champagne, where it is often blended with Chardonnay. Although it is a black grape, its juice is colourless, so removing the skins straight away gives a pale base wine. Merlot, Cabernet Sauvignon and Syrah are not Champagne grapes.":"四大黑葡萄品種中，只有黑皮諾用於 Champagne，並常與夏多內混釀。雖然是黑葡萄，但果汁無色，只要立刻去除果皮，就能得到淺色的基酒。梅洛、卡本內蘇維濃和希哈都不是 Champagne 的品種。","In which regions is it common to grow black grapes like Cabernet Sauvignon?":"哪些產區普遍種植卡本內蘇維濃這類黑葡萄？","Warm regions, where grapes ripen reliably":"溫暖產區，葡萄能穩定成熟","Cool regions, where grapes struggle to ripen":"涼爽產區，葡萄難以成熟","Regions with no winter, where vines never rest":"沒有冬季的產區，葡萄樹從不休眠","Regions near the poles, with weak sunlight":"靠近兩極、日照微弱的產區","Warm climates ripen grapes well, so black grapes are commonly grown there.":"溫暖氣候讓葡萄充分成熟，所以當地普遍種植黑葡萄。","Warm regions closer to the Equator, such as parts of Australia and California, have high temperatures and intense sunshine, so grapes ripen reliably and black grapes are commonly grown. In cool regions such as Germany and northern France, white grapes are grown more often.":"較靠近赤道的溫暖產區，例如澳洲和加州的部分地區，氣溫高、日照強，葡萄能穩定成熟，因此普遍種植黑葡萄。在德國和法國北部等涼爽產區，則較常種植白葡萄。","Which grapes are used to make Champagne?":"釀造 Champagne 使用哪些葡萄品種？","Chardonnay and Sauvignon Blanc":"夏多內和白蘇維濃","Riesling and Pinot Grigio":"麗絲玲和灰皮諾","Champagne, the French sparkling wine, is made from Chardonnay and Pinot Noir, often blended. Pinot Noir is a black grape, but its juice is colourless, so it can give a pale wine. Cabernet Sauvignon and Merlot are the grapes of red Bordeaux, while Riesling and Pinot Grigio are not used in Champagne.":"Champagne 是法國的氣泡酒，以夏多內和黑皮諾釀造，常常混釀。黑皮諾是黑葡萄，但果汁無色，所以能釀出淺色的酒。卡本內蘇維濃和梅洛是波爾多紅酒的品種，麗絲玲和灰皮諾則不用於 Champagne。","What is the typical style of Champagne?":"Champagne 的典型風格是什麼？","Dry, high acidity, apple, lemon, toasted bread":"不甜，高酸度，蘋果、檸檬、烤麵包","Sweet, low acidity, apricot and honey":"甜，低酸度，杏桃和蜂蜜","Medium-sweet, light, strawberry and raspberry":"半甜，輕盈，草莓和覆盆子","Dry, tannic, blackcurrant and cedar":"不甜，單寧明顯，黑醋栗和雪松","Champagne is usually dry and fresh, with apple, lemon and toast.":"Champagne 通常不甜而清爽，帶有蘋果、檸檬和烤麵包氣息。","Champagne is typically dry, with high acidity, aromas of green apple and lemon, and notes of toasted bread. Apricot and honey describe Sauternes, medium-sweet strawberry and raspberry describe White Zinfandel, and tannin, blackcurrant and cedar are typical of red Bordeaux.":"Champagne 通常不甜、酸度高，帶有青蘋果和檸檬香氣，以及烤麵包氣息。杏桃和蜂蜜描述的是 Sauternes，半甜、草莓和覆盆子描述的是 White Zinfandel，單寧、黑醋栗和雪松則是波爾多紅酒的典型特徵。","Which of these wines typically shows notes of toasted bread?":"下列哪一款葡萄酒通常帶有烤麵包氣息？","Toasted bread is a typical note of Champagne.":"烤麵包是 Champagne 的典型氣息。","Alongside apple and lemon, Champagne often shows notes of toasted bread. Prosecco is a light sparkling wine with pear and floral aromas, Sancerre has apple and grass, and Chablis has apple and lemon: none of those three is described with toasted bread notes.":"除了蘋果和檸檬，Champagne 常帶有烤麵包氣息。Prosecco 是輕盈的氣泡酒，帶有梨子和花香；Sancerre 有蘋果和青草；Chablis 有蘋果和檸檬：這三款酒都不會用烤麵包來描述。","Which French region does Sancerre come from?":"Sancerre 來自法國的哪個產區？","The Rhône":"隆河","Sancerre is a white wine from the Loire Valley.":"Sancerre 是來自羅亞爾河谷的白酒。","Sancerre is a dry white from the Loire Valley made from Sauvignon Blanc: medium body, high acidity, green apple and grass. Burgundy is home to Chablis and Chardonnay whites, Bordeaux to reds from Cabernet Sauvignon and Merlot, and the Rhône to wines such as Côtes du Rhône.":"Sancerre 是羅亞爾河谷以白蘇維濃釀造的不甜白酒：酒體中等，酸度高，青蘋果和青草。布根地是 Chablis 和夏多內白酒的故鄉，波爾多出產卡本內蘇維濃和梅洛的紅酒，隆河則有 Côtes du Rhône 等葡萄酒。","Which description fits a Sancerre?":"哪一項描述符合 Sancerre？","Dry, medium body, green apple and grass":"不甜，酒體中等，青蘋果和青草","Sweet, full body, apricot and honey":"甜，酒體飽滿，杏桃和蜂蜜","Dry, full body, pineapple and vanilla":"不甜，酒體飽滿，鳳梨和香草","Medium-sweet, light body, pear and flowers":"半甜，酒體輕盈，梨子和花香","Sancerre is a dry, fresh, herbaceous Sauvignon Blanc.":"Sancerre 是不甜、清爽、帶草本氣息的白蘇維濃。","Sancerre is dry and medium-bodied, usually unoaked, with high acidity and pronounced aromas of green apple and grass. The other descriptions fit Sauternes, an oaked warm-climate Chardonnay and Prosecco, which can be dry or medium-sweet. Remember that the label names the place, not the grape.":"Sancerre 不甜、酒體中等，通常不經橡木桶，酸度高，有明顯的青蘋果和青草香氣。其他描述對應的是 Sauternes、經橡木桶的溫暖氣候夏多內，以及可以不甜或半甜的 Prosecco。記住，酒標上寫的是地名，不是品種。","Which grape is Chablis made from?":"Chablis 以哪一個葡萄品種釀造？","Chablis is Chardonnay from the coolest part of Burgundy.":"Chablis 是來自布根地最涼爽地區的夏多內。","Chablis is a white Burgundy made from Chardonnay. It comes from the region's coolest area, so it is dry, light to medium-bodied, with high acidity, green apple and lemon, and usually no oak. Sauvignon Blanc is the grape of Sancerre, and Pinot Noir is the grape of red Burgundy.":"Chablis 是以夏多內釀造的布根地白酒。它來自產區最涼爽的地帶，所以不甜、酒體輕盈至中等，酸度高，帶有青蘋果和檸檬，通常不經橡木桶。白蘇維濃是 Sancerre 的品種，黑皮諾則是布根地紅酒的品種。","Chablis is usually...":"Chablis 通常……","unoaked":"不經橡木桶","aged in new oak":"在新橡木桶中陳年","Chablis is usually unoaked: no vanilla, just fresh fruit.":"Chablis 通常不經橡木桶：沒有香草味，只有新鮮果香。","Chablis is typically unoaked. It therefore shows only fresh fruit, green apple and lemon, carried by high acidity, without the vanilla notes that oak would add. It is a still, dry wine, neither sparkling nor sweet. Other white Burgundies, on the other hand, may be oaked.":"Chablis 通常不經橡木桶，因此只呈現青蘋果和檸檬的新鮮果香，由高酸度支撐，沒有橡木桶會帶來的香草氣息。它是不甜的靜態酒，既不是氣泡酒也不是甜酒。其他布根地白酒則可能經過橡木桶。","Compared with Chablis, other white Burgundies often show...":"與 Chablis 相比，其他布根地白酒常呈現……","riper fruit, such as peach":"更成熟的水果，例如桃子","more herbaceous notes, like grass":"更多草本氣息，例如青草","red fruit such as raspberry":"覆盆子等紅色水果","more sweetness and a light body":"更甜，酒體輕盈","Outside the coolest area grapes ripen more: lemon and peach.":"在最涼爽的地帶之外，葡萄更成熟：檸檬和桃子。","Chablis comes from the coolest part of Burgundy and has green apple and lemon. The region's other whites, from riper grapes, often show citrus and stone fruit such as peach, and may have vanilla if oaked. They are still dry and medium-bodied.":"Chablis 來自布根地最涼爽的地區，帶有青蘋果和檸檬風味。產區其他白酒來自更成熟的葡萄，常呈現柑橘類和桃子等核果，如果經橡木桶還可能有香草味。它們同樣不甜、酒體中等。","What does «Bourgogne» on a label mean?":"酒標上的「Bourgogne」是什麼意思？","It is the French name for Burgundy":"它是布根地的法文名稱","It is the name of a white grape":"它是一個白葡萄品種的名稱","It means the wine is sweet":"它表示這款酒是甜的","It means the wine is sparkling":"它表示這款酒是氣泡酒","«Bourgogne» is French for Burgundy, used on whites and reds.":"「Bourgogne」是布根地的法文，白酒和紅酒都會使用。","«Bourgogne» is the French name for the Burgundy region, and it can appear on labels of both white and red wines. It does not refer to a grape or a style: to know what to expect, remember that the whites are Chardonnay and the reds are Pinot Noir.":"「Bourgogne」是布根地產區的法文名稱，白酒和紅酒的酒標上都可能出現。它指的不是品種或風格：想知道會喝到什麼，就記住白酒是夏多內，紅酒是黑皮諾。","White Burgundies can be...":"布根地白酒可以是……","oaked or unoaked":"經橡木桶或不經橡木桶","only sweet":"只有甜型","only sparkling":"只有氣泡酒","only fortified":"只有加烈酒","White Burgundy can be made with or without oak.":"布根地白酒可以使用橡木桶，也可以不使用。","White Burgundies are still, dry, medium-bodied wines made from Chardonnay. They can be matured in oak, which brings vanilla, or not: Chablis, for example, is usually unoaked. They are not sweet, sparkling or fortified wines. With oak, vanilla notes join the lemon and peach fruit.":"布根地白酒是以夏多內釀造、不甜、酒體中等的靜態酒。可以在橡木桶中熟成而帶有香草味，也可以不經橡木桶：例如 Chablis 通常就不經橡木桶。它們不是甜酒、氣泡酒或加烈酒。經橡木桶時，香草氣息會加入檸檬和桃子的果香之中。","What is the typical style of red Burgundy?":"布根地紅酒的典型風格是什麼？","Light to medium, high acidity, raspberry and cherry":"輕盈至中等，高酸度，覆盆子和櫻桃","Full, high tannin, blackcurrant and cedar":"飽滿，高單寧，黑醋栗和雪松","Full, high alcohol, strawberry and clove":"飽滿，高酒精濃度，草莓和丁香","Sweet, high tannin, blackberry":"甜，高單寧，黑莓","Red Burgundy is Pinot Noir: fresh, light to medium, red fruit.":"布根地紅酒就是黑皮諾：清爽，輕盈至中等，紅色水果。","Red Burgundies, made from Pinot Noir, are dry and light to medium-bodied, with high acidity, low to medium tannin and red fruit such as raspberry and red cherry. The other options describe red Bordeaux, Châteauneuf-du-Pape and Port respectively. They are fresh, elegant reds.":"布根地紅酒以黑皮諾釀造，不甜，酒體輕盈至中等，酸度高，單寧低至中等，帶有覆盆子和紅櫻桃等紅色水果。其他選項分別描述波爾多紅酒、Châteauneuf-du-Pape 和 Port。這是清爽而優雅的紅酒。","Which notes can oak give a red Burgundy?":"橡木桶可以為布根地紅酒帶來哪些氣息？","Vanilla and smoke":"香草和煙燻","Dried herbs and white pepper":"乾燥香草和白胡椒","Liquorice and black pepper":"甘草和黑胡椒","Honey and apricot":"蜂蜜和杏桃","In red Burgundy, oak can add vanilla and smoke.":"在布根地紅酒中，橡木桶可以增添香草和煙燻氣息。","The Pinot Noir in red Burgundy is often matured in oak, which can add vanilla and smoke to the red fruit. Dried herbs and white pepper suggest Chianti and Côtes du Rhône, liquorice and black pepper suggest Shiraz, and honey and apricot suggest Sauternes.":"布根地紅酒的黑皮諾常在橡木桶中熟成，為紅色水果增添香草和煙燻氣息。乾燥香草和白胡椒讓人想到 Chianti 和 Côtes du Rhône，甘草和黑胡椒讓人想到希拉茲，蜂蜜和杏桃則讓人想到 Sauternes。","What colour are Bordeaux wines most often?":"波爾多葡萄酒最常見的是什麼顏色？","Sparkling white":"白氣泡酒","Bordeaux is mostly known for red wine.":"波爾多最廣為人知的是紅酒。","The Bordeaux region makes mostly red wines, usually dry, tannic blends of Cabernet Sauvignon and Merlot. There are whites too, such as the famous sweet Sauternes, but when people simply say «Bordeaux», they generally mean a red wine. The sweet white is the exception worth remembering.":"波爾多產區以紅酒為主，通常是不甜、單寧明顯的卡本內蘇維濃與梅洛混釀。當地也有白酒，例如著名的甜酒 Sauternes，但一般只說「波爾多」時，指的通常是紅酒。這款甜白酒是值得記住的例外。","Red Bordeaux is typically a blend of which grapes?":"波爾多紅酒通常是哪些品種的混釀？","Pinot Noir and Chardonnay":"黑皮諾和夏多內","Syrah and Pinot Noir":"希哈和黑皮諾","Merlot and Pinot Noir":"梅洛和黑皮諾","Red Bordeaux blends Cabernet Sauvignon and Merlot.":"波爾多紅酒以卡本內蘇維濃和梅洛混釀。","Red Bordeaux is typically a blend of Cabernet Sauvignon, which brings tannin and acidity, and Merlot, which brings softness and body. Pinot Noir and Chardonnay are the grapes of Champagne, and Pinot Noir is not usually blended when making red wine.":"波爾多紅酒通常是卡本內蘇維濃與梅洛的混釀，前者帶來單寧和酸度，後者帶來柔順感和酒體。黑皮諾和夏多內是 Champagne 的品種，而黑皮諾在釀造紅酒時通常不混釀。","What structure does a red Bordeaux usually have?":"波爾多紅酒通常有什麼樣的結構？","High acidity and tannin, medium to full body":"酸度和單寧高，酒體中等至飽滿","Low tannin, light body":"低單寧，酒體輕盈","Low acidity, medium sweetness":"低酸度，半甜","Low tannin, low alcohol":"低單寧，低酒精濃度","Red Bordeaux is dry, tannic and fresh, with medium to full body.":"波爾多紅酒不甜、單寧高而清爽，酒體中等至飽滿。","Red Bordeaux is a classic example of a high-tannin wine. It is dry, with high acidity and a medium to full body. Low tannin and a light body describe Beaujolais instead, while medium sweetness and low alcohol describe White Zinfandel.":"波爾多紅酒是高單寧葡萄酒的經典例子。它不甜，酸度高，酒體中等至飽滿。低單寧、酒體輕盈描述的是 Beaujolais，半甜、低酒精濃度描述的則是 White Zinfandel。","Which aromas are typical of a red Bordeaux?":"哪些香氣是波爾多紅酒的典型特徵？","Blackberry, blackcurrant and cedar":"黑莓、黑醋栗和雪松","Strawberry, raspberry and cherry":"草莓、覆盆子和櫻桃","Apple, lemon and toasted bread":"蘋果、檸檬和烤麵包","Black fruit from Cabernet and Merlot, plus cedar from oak.":"黑色水果來自卡本內和梅洛，雪松來自橡木桶。","Red Bordeaux smells of black fruit such as blackberry and blackcurrant, from its Cabernet Sauvignon and Merlot, with cedar notes from oak. Red fruit is typical of wines like red Burgundy or Beaujolais, while apple, lemon and toasted bread describe Champagne.":"波爾多紅酒有黑莓和黑醋栗等黑色水果香氣，來自卡本內蘇維濃和梅洛，並有來自橡木桶的雪松氣息。紅色水果是布根地紅酒或 Beaujolais 等葡萄酒的典型香氣，蘋果、檸檬和烤麵包描述的則是 Champagne。","A Saint-Émilion is described as a «Merlot-dominant blend». Which region is it from?":"一款 Saint-Émilion 被形容為「以梅洛為主的混釀」。它來自哪個產區？","The Loire":"羅亞爾河","Saint-Émilion is an area of Bordeaux, home of Merlot blends.":"Saint-Émilion 是波爾多的一個產區，也是梅洛混釀的故鄉。","Many French wines show the name of a specific area on the label. Saint-Émilion is an area of Bordeaux, where Merlot is often the main grape in the blend with Cabernet Sauvignon. Burgundy uses Pinot Noir for its reds, and the Loire is known for white Sancerre.":"許多法國葡萄酒會在酒標上標示特定產區的名稱。Saint-Émilion 是波爾多的一個產區，當地與卡本內蘇維濃的混釀中，梅洛往往是主要品種。布根地的紅酒使用黑皮諾，羅亞爾河則以白酒 Sancerre 聞名。","Why do many European wines, such as Chablis, not name the grape?":"為什麼許多歐洲葡萄酒（例如 Chablis）不標示葡萄品種？","They are named after the region where they are made":"它們以產地命名","They are always blends of many grapes":"它們一定是多個品種的混釀","The grape is written only on the cork":"品種只寫在軟木塞上","They are made from unknown grapes":"它們以不知名的葡萄釀造","In Europe, many wines carry the name of the place, not the grape.":"在歐洲，許多葡萄酒標示的是地名，而不是品種。","In Europe many wines, such as Chablis, Sancerre, Burgundy or Bordeaux, take their name from the region where they are made. That is why you need to know which grapes lie behind those names: Chablis, for example, is Chardonnay, and Sancerre is Sauvignon Blanc.":"在歐洲，許多葡萄酒以產地命名，例如 Chablis、Sancerre、布根地或波爾多。所以你必須知道這些名稱背後是哪些品種：例如 Chablis 是夏多內，Sancerre 是白蘇維濃。","Which of these famous wines can be either white or red?":"下列哪一款著名葡萄酒可以是白酒，也可以是紅酒？","Burgundy makes Chardonnay whites and Pinot Noir reds.":"布根地出產夏多內白酒和黑皮諾紅酒。","Burgundy (Bourgogne) wines can be white, from Chardonnay, or red, from Pinot Noir. Chablis and Sancerre, as presented here, are dry white wines, while Champagne is a typically dry sparkling wine made from Chardonnay and Pinot Noir. So the rule is simple to remember.":"布根地（Bourgogne）葡萄酒可以是夏多內釀造的白酒，也可以是黑皮諾釀造的紅酒。這裡介紹的 Chablis 和 Sancerre 是不甜白酒，Champagne 則是以夏多內和黑皮諾釀造、通常不甜的氣泡酒。所以這條規則很好記。","A list says «Loire Valley, citrus and grass on nose and palate». Which wine is it?":"酒單上寫著「羅亞爾河谷，香氣與口感皆有柑橘和青草」。這是哪一款酒？","Red Burgundy":"布根地紅酒","Loire plus grass points to Sancerre, made from Sauvignon Blanc.":"羅亞爾河加上青草，指向以白蘇維濃釀造的 Sancerre。","A Loire Valley origin and grassy notes, typical of Sauvignon Blanc, point to Sancerre. Chablis is also a fresh white, but it comes from Burgundy and shows apple and lemon without marked herbaceous notes. Bordeaux and red Burgundy are red wines.":"產自羅亞爾河谷，加上白蘇維濃典型的青草氣息，指向 Sancerre。Chablis 也是清爽的白酒，但它來自布根地，呈現蘋果和檸檬，沒有明顯的草本氣息。波爾多和布根地紅酒都是紅酒。","What is Sauternes?":"Sauternes 是什麼？","A sweet white wine from Bordeaux":"波爾多的甜白酒","A dry white wine from the Loire":"羅亞爾河的不甜白酒","A sparkling wine from Burgundy":"布根地的氣泡酒","A fortified wine from Spain":"西班牙的加烈酒","Sauternes is the famous sweet white made in Bordeaux.":"Sauternes 是波爾多出產的著名甜白酒。","Sauternes is a sweet white wine from Bordeaux: full-bodied, with apricot, honey and vanilla from oak, and high acidity to balance the sugar. The dry white from the Loire is Sancerre, and the Spanish fortified wine is Sherry. So Bordeaux does not only make reds.":"Sauternes 是波爾多的甜白酒：酒體飽滿，帶有杏桃、蜂蜜和來自橡木桶的香草風味，並有高酸度來平衡糖分。羅亞爾河的不甜白酒是 Sancerre，西班牙的加烈酒是 Sherry。所以波爾多不只出產紅酒。","Which flavours are typical of Sauternes?":"哪些風味是 Sauternes 的典型特徵？","Apricot, honey and vanilla":"杏桃、蜂蜜和香草","Green apple, lemon and toast":"青蘋果、檸檬和烤麵包","Pear, flowers and apple":"梨子、花香和蘋果","Sauternes combines apricot and honey with vanilla from oak.":"Sauternes 結合了杏桃、蜂蜜與來自橡木桶的香草。","Sauternes has flavours of stone fruit (apricot), honey and vanilla from oak, all held up by high acidity. Apple, lemon and toasted bread describe Champagne; pear and flowers describe Prosecco; and medium-sweet strawberry and raspberry describe White Zinfandel. Remember its full body too.":"Sauternes 有核果（杏桃）、蜂蜜和來自橡木桶的香草風味，全由高酸度支撐。蘋果、檸檬和烤麵包描述的是 Champagne；梨子和花香描述的是 Prosecco；半甜、草莓和覆盆子描述的則是 White Zinfandel。也別忘了它飽滿的酒體。","Which statement about Sauternes is correct?":"關於 Sauternes，下列哪一項敘述正確？","It is full-bodied, with high acidity balancing the sugar":"酒體飽滿，高酸度平衡了糖分","It is light-bodied, with low acidity and little sugar":"酒體輕盈，酸度低、糖分少","It is dry and unoaked, with herbaceous notes":"不甜、不經橡木桶，帶草本氣息","It is sparkling, with notes of toasted bread":"是氣泡酒，帶烤麵包氣息","Sauternes is sweet and full, but high acidity keeps it fresh.":"Sauternes 甜而飽滿，但高酸度讓它保持清爽。","Sauternes is an example of both a sweet wine and a full-bodied wine. Its high acidity is essential because it balances the large amount of sugar. Herbaceous notes and no oak suggest Sancerre instead, while toasted bread is typical of Champagne.":"Sauternes 既是甜酒的例子，也是酒體飽滿葡萄酒的例子。它的高酸度不可或缺，因為能平衡大量的糖分。草本氣息、不經橡木桶讓人想到 Sancerre，烤麵包則是 Champagne 的典型特徵。","What kind of wine is White Zinfandel?":"White Zinfandel 是哪一種葡萄酒？","A Californian rosé, medium-sweet, low in alcohol":"加州粉紅酒，半甜，酒精濃度低","A Californian white, dry, high in alcohol":"加州白酒，不甜，酒精濃度高","A French red, dry and tannic":"法國紅酒，不甜、單寧明顯","An Italian sparkling wine, light and floral":"義大利氣泡酒，輕盈、帶花香","Despite its name, White Zinfandel is a rosé from California.":"雖然名字裡有 White，White Zinfandel 是加州的粉紅酒。","White Zinfandel is an unoaked Californian rosé, medium-sweet and low in alcohol, with strawberry and raspberry. It is the classic example of a low-alcohol wine. The light, floral Italian sparkling wine in the options is Prosecco, which is a different wine altogether. The name misleads: the wine is pink.":"White Zinfandel 是不經橡木桶的加州粉紅酒，半甜、酒精濃度低，帶有草莓和覆盆子風味。它是低酒精濃度葡萄酒的經典例子。選項中輕盈、帶花香的義大利氣泡酒是 Prosecco，完全是另一款酒。名稱會誤導人：這款酒是粉紅色的。","Which flavours does White Zinfandel usually have?":"White Zinfandel 通常有哪些風味？","Apricot and honey":"杏桃和蜂蜜","Blackberry and black pepper":"黑莓和黑胡椒","Apple and toasted bread":"蘋果和烤麵包","White Zinfandel shows fresh red fruit such as strawberry and raspberry.":"White Zinfandel 呈現草莓和覆盆子等新鮮紅色水果。","White Zinfandel, the Californian rosé, has red fruit flavours such as strawberry and raspberry, medium sweetness and low alcohol, and it is unoaked. Apricot and honey are typical of Sauternes, blackberry and black pepper of Syrah, and apple and toasted bread of Champagne.":"加州粉紅酒 White Zinfandel 有草莓和覆盆子等紅色水果風味，半甜、酒精濃度低，不經橡木桶。杏桃和蜂蜜是 Sauternes 的典型風味，黑莓和黑胡椒屬於希哈，蘋果和烤麵包則屬於 Champagne。","Which of these wines has the lowest alcohol?":"下列哪一款葡萄酒的酒精濃度最低？","White Zinfandel is the classic example of a low-alcohol wine.":"White Zinfandel 是低酒精濃度葡萄酒的經典例子。","White Zinfandel is the standard example of a low-alcohol wine, at around 10.5% abv. Châteauneuf-du-Pape, by contrast, is the example of a high-alcohol red, while Port and Sherry are fortified wines with added alcohol and a strength of 15% to 22% abv.":"White Zinfandel 是低酒精濃度葡萄酒的標準例子，大約 10.5% abv。Châteauneuf-du-Pape 則是高酒精濃度紅酒的例子，Port 和 Sherry 是添加了酒精的加烈酒，酒精濃度為 15% 至 22% abv。","What is the typical style of Beaujolais?":"Beaujolais 的典型風格是什麼？","Dry, light red with low tannin and no oak":"不甜、輕盈的紅酒，單寧低，不經橡木桶","Dry, full red with high tannin and oak":"不甜、飽滿的紅酒，單寧高，經橡木桶","Sweet rosé with low alcohol":"甜型粉紅酒，酒精濃度低","Sweet, full-bodied fortified red":"甜而酒體飽滿的紅色加烈酒","Beaujolais is a light, fresh French red with low tannin.":"Beaujolais 是輕盈、清爽、單寧低的法國紅酒。","Beaujolais is a dry, light-bodied, unoaked French red with fresh red fruit such as raspberry and red cherry and low tannin. The full, tannic red describes Bordeaux, the sweet rosé describes White Zinfandel, and the sweet fortified red describes Port.":"Beaujolais 是不甜、酒體輕盈、不經橡木桶的法國紅酒，帶有覆盆子和紅櫻桃等新鮮紅色水果，單寧低。飽滿、單寧高的紅酒描述的是波爾多，甜型粉紅酒描述的是 White Zinfandel，甜型紅色加烈酒描述的則是 Port。","A list says «light red, low tannin, strawberry and raspberry». Which wine is it?":"酒單上寫著「輕盈的紅酒，低單寧，草莓和覆盆子」。這是哪一款酒？","Light, low in tannin and red-fruited: that is Beaujolais.":"輕盈、單寧低、紅色水果：這就是 Beaujolais。","Beaujolais is the classic light, low-tannin red with fresh red fruit. Châteauneuf-du-Pape is full-bodied and high in alcohol, Chianti has high tannin and acidity, and Port is a sweet, tannic fortified wine. A red this light can even be served lightly chilled.":"Beaujolais 是經典的輕盈、低單寧紅酒，帶有新鮮紅色水果。Châteauneuf-du-Pape 酒體飽滿、酒精濃度高，Chianti 單寧和酸度高，Port 則是甜而單寧高的加烈酒。這麼輕盈的紅酒甚至可以稍微冰鎮後飲用。","Which spice is typical of Côtes du Rhône?":"哪一種香料是 Côtes du Rhône 的典型特徵？","White pepper":"白胡椒","Cinnamon":"肉桂","Ginger":"薑","Côtes du Rhône pairs red fruit with a white pepper note.":"Côtes du Rhône 結合了紅色水果與一絲白胡椒氣息。","Côtes du Rhône is a dry, medium-bodied French red with strawberry, red plum and white pepper, oaked or unoaked. Liquorice, by contrast, is typical of Shiraz from warm parts of Australia. Remember the difference: white pepper in Côtes du Rhône, black pepper in Syrah.":"Côtes du Rhône 是不甜、酒體中等的法國紅酒，帶有草莓、紅李和白胡椒風味，可經橡木桶，也可不經。甘草則是澳洲溫暖地區希拉茲的典型特徵。記住這個差別：Côtes du Rhône 是白胡椒，希哈是黑胡椒。","Which description fits Châteauneuf-du-Pape?":"哪一項描述符合 Châteauneuf-du-Pape？","Dry, full-bodied, high-alcohol red with strawberry and clove":"不甜、酒體飽滿、酒精濃度高的紅酒，草莓和丁香","Dry, light, unoaked red with raspberry":"不甜、輕盈、不經橡木桶的紅酒，覆盆子","Dry, medium red with white pepper and red plum":"不甜、酒體中等的紅酒，白胡椒和紅李","Sweet, fortified red with blackberry":"甜型紅色加烈酒，黑莓","Châteauneuf-du-Pape is full and high in alcohol, with strawberry and clove.":"Châteauneuf-du-Pape 飽滿、酒精濃度高，帶有草莓和丁香風味。","Châteauneuf-du-Pape is a dry, full-bodied, high-alcohol French red with strawberry and cloves from oak. The other options describe Beaujolais (light), Côtes du Rhône (medium, white pepper) and Port (sweet and fortified), so only the first one matches. It comes from the Rhône area.":"Châteauneuf-du-Pape 是不甜、酒體飽滿、酒精濃度高的法國紅酒，帶有草莓和來自橡木桶的丁香風味。其他選項描述的是 Beaujolais（輕盈）、Côtes du Rhône（中等、白胡椒）和 Port（甜型加烈酒），所以只有第一項符合。它來自隆河地區。","Which Italian red has high tannin and acidity with dried herb notes?":"哪一款義大利紅酒單寧和酸度高，並帶有乾燥香草氣息？","Chianti is the tannic, fresh Italian red with dried herbs.":"Chianti 是單寧高、清爽並帶有乾燥香草氣息的義大利紅酒。","Chianti is a dry, medium-bodied Italian red with high tannin and acidity, red cherry, red plum, dried herbs and sometimes cloves from oak. Rioja is Spanish, while Beaujolais and Côtes du Rhône are French reds, so only Chianti fits. It comes from Tuscany.":"Chianti 是不甜、酒體中等的義大利紅酒，單寧和酸度高，帶有紅櫻桃、紅李、乾燥香草，有時還有來自橡木桶的丁香氣息。Rioja 來自西班牙，Beaujolais 和 Côtes du Rhône 是法國紅酒，所以只有 Chianti 符合。它來自托斯卡尼。","Which aromas can oak give to Chianti?":"橡木桶可以為 Chianti 帶來哪些香氣？","Cloves":"丁香","Toasted bread":"烤麵包","In Chianti, oak can add notes of cloves.":"在 Chianti 中，橡木桶可以增添丁香氣息。","Chianti has red fruit and dried herbs and sometimes clove aromas from oak. In Châteauneuf-du-Pape, too, oak brings cloves. Toasted bread is typical of Champagne, green bell pepper of Cabernet Sauvignon, and honey of Sauternes. So oak can leave a spicy mark even on a fresh red like Chianti.":"Chianti 有紅色水果和乾燥香草，有時還有來自橡木桶的丁香香氣。在 Châteauneuf-du-Pape 中，橡木桶同樣帶來丁香。烤麵包是 Champagne 的典型氣息，青椒屬於卡本內蘇維濃，蜂蜜屬於 Sauternes。所以即使是 Chianti 這樣清爽的紅酒，橡木桶也能留下香料的印記。","Which country is Rioja from, and what does it usually taste of?":"Rioja 來自哪個國家，通常有什麼風味？","Spain; strawberry and vanilla":"西班牙；草莓和香草","Italy; cherry and dried herbs":"義大利；櫻桃和乾燥香草","Portugal; blackberry and high tannin":"葡萄牙；黑莓和高單寧","France; raspberry and cherry":"法國；覆盆子和櫻桃","Rioja is Spanish, with strawberry and vanilla from oak.":"Rioja 來自西班牙，帶有草莓和來自橡木桶的香草風味。","Rioja is a dry Spanish red with a medium to full body, red fruit such as strawberry, and vanilla from oak. Cherry and dried herbs describe Italian Chianti, blackberry and high tannin describe Portuguese Port, and raspberry and cherry describe French Beaujolais.":"Rioja 是不甜的西班牙紅酒，酒體中等至飽滿，帶有草莓等紅色水果和來自橡木桶的香草風味。櫻桃和乾燥香草描述的是義大利的 Chianti，黑莓和高單寧描述的是葡萄牙的 Port，覆盆子和櫻桃描述的則是法國的 Beaujolais。","Where does the vanilla in a Rioja come from?":"Rioja 中的香草氣息從哪裡來？","From oak":"來自橡木桶","From the warm climate":"來自溫暖的氣候","From added alcohol":"來自添加的酒精","Vanilla is a typical oak aroma.":"香草是典型的橡木桶香氣。","Rioja combines red fruit such as strawberry with vanilla notes, which come from maturation in oak. Skins provide colour and tannin, climate affects sugar, acidity and fruit ripeness, and Rioja is not a fortified wine, so the other options do not apply.":"Rioja 結合了草莓等紅色水果與香草氣息，後者來自橡木桶熟成。果皮提供顏色和單寧，氣候影響糖分、酸度和果實成熟度，而 Rioja 不是加烈酒，所以其他選項都不成立。","Which description fits Prosecco?":"哪一項描述符合 Prosecco？","Light Italian sparkling wine, pear and floral":"輕盈的義大利氣泡酒，梨子和花香","Dry Spanish sparkling wine, apple and lemon":"不甜的西班牙氣泡酒，蘋果和檸檬","French sparkling wine with toasted bread":"帶烤麵包氣息的法國氣泡酒","Sweet Italian fortified wine":"甜型義大利加烈酒","Prosecco is a light Italian sparkling wine with pear and flowers.":"Prosecco 是輕盈的義大利氣泡酒，帶有梨子和花香。","Prosecco is a light-bodied Italian sparkling wine with green fruit (pear) and floral aromas, either dry or medium-sweet. The dry Spanish sparkling wine with apple and lemon is Cava, and the French one with toasted bread notes is Champagne. None of the three is fortified.":"Prosecco 是酒體輕盈的義大利氣泡酒，帶有綠色水果（梨子）和花香，可以不甜或半甜。帶蘋果和檸檬的不甜西班牙氣泡酒是 Cava，帶烤麵包氣息的法國氣泡酒是 Champagne。三者都不是加烈酒。","Which of these sparkling wines can be medium-sweet?":"下列哪一款氣泡酒可以是半甜的？","Prosecco can be either dry or medium-sweet.":"Prosecco 可以不甜，也可以半甜。","Of the sparkling wines to know, Prosecco is the one that can be either dry or medium-sweet. Cava is described as dry and Champagne as typically dry. Sancerre is not a sparkling wine at all, but a still, dry white from the Loire.":"在必須認識的氣泡酒中，Prosecco 可以不甜，也可以半甜。Cava 被描述為不甜，Champagne 則通常不甜。Sancerre 根本不是氣泡酒，而是羅亞爾河不甜的靜態白酒。","Which description fits Cava?":"哪一項描述符合 Cava？","Sweet Italian sparkling wine, pear and flowers":"甜型義大利氣泡酒，梨子和花香","Spanish fortified wine, dry to sweet":"西班牙加烈酒，從不甜到甜","Spanish red, strawberry and vanilla":"西班牙紅酒，草莓和香草","Cava is Spain's dry sparkling wine, with apple and lemon.":"Cava 是西班牙的不甜氣泡酒，帶有蘋果和檸檬風味。","Cava is a dry Spanish sparkling wine with green fruit (apple) and citrus (lemon). Do not mix it up with the other Spanish wines: Sherry is a white fortified wine that can be dry, medium or sweet, and Rioja is a red with strawberry and vanilla.":"Cava 是不甜的西班牙氣泡酒，帶有綠色水果（蘋果）和柑橘類水果（檸檬）。別把它和其他西班牙葡萄酒搞混：Sherry 是白色加烈酒，可以不甜、半甜或甜；Rioja 則是帶草莓和香草的紅酒。","Which pair are both fortified wines?":"哪一組都是加烈酒？","Rioja and Chianti":"Rioja 和 Chianti","Sauternes and White Zinfandel":"Sauternes 和 White Zinfandel","Sherry and Port are wines with added alcohol.":"Sherry 和 Port 都是添加了酒精的葡萄酒。","Sherry from Spain and Port from Portugal are the two fortified wines to know: they have added alcohol and a strength of 15% to 22% abv. Prosecco and Cava are sparkling, Rioja and Chianti are still reds, and Sauternes and White Zinfandel are still wines that are sweet or medium-sweet.":"西班牙的 Sherry 和葡萄牙的 Port 是必須認識的兩款加烈酒：添加了酒精，酒精濃度為 15% 至 22% abv。Prosecco 和 Cava 是氣泡酒，Rioja 和 Chianti 是靜態紅酒，Sauternes 和 White Zinfandel 則是甜或半甜的靜態酒。","Which statement about Sherry is correct?":"關於 Sherry，下列哪一項敘述正確？","It is a white Spanish fortified wine, dry, medium or sweet":"它是西班牙的白色加烈酒，不甜、半甜或甜","It is a red Portuguese fortified wine, always sweet":"它是葡萄牙的紅色加烈酒，一定是甜的","It is a dry Spanish sparkling wine":"它是不甜的西班牙氣泡酒","It is a still Spanish red with vanilla":"它是帶香草味的西班牙靜態紅酒","Sherry is a white fortified wine from Spain, made dry to sweet.":"Sherry 是西班牙的白色加烈酒，從不甜到甜都有。","Sherry is a white fortified wine from Spain, made in a range of styles: it can be dry, medium or sweet. The sweet red fortified wine from Portugal is Port, the dry Spanish sparkling wine is Cava, and the Spanish red with vanilla is Rioja.":"Sherry 是西班牙的白色加烈酒，有多種風格：可以不甜、半甜或甜。葡萄牙的甜型紅色加烈酒是 Port，不甜的西班牙氣泡酒是 Cava，帶香草味的西班牙紅酒是 Rioja。","Which description fits Port?":"哪一項描述符合 Port？","Portuguese fortified wine: sweet, red, full, tannic":"葡萄牙加烈酒：甜、紅色、飽滿、單寧高","Spanish fortified wine: white, often dry":"西班牙加烈酒：白色，通常不甜","Still Portuguese red: light and dry":"葡萄牙靜態紅酒：輕盈而不甜","Sweet French white with honey":"帶蜂蜜味的法國甜白酒","Port is a sweet Portuguese fortified wine, usually red, full and tannic.":"Port 是葡萄牙的甜型加烈酒，通常是紅色、飽滿、單寧高。","Port is a fortified wine from Portugal, sweet and high in alcohol, made in a range of styles. It is usually red and full-bodied, with high tannin and black fruit such as blackberry. The white Spanish fortified wine is Sherry, and the sweet French white with honey is Sauternes.":"Port 是葡萄牙的加烈酒，甜而酒精濃度高，有多種風格。它通常是紅色、酒體飽滿，單寧高，帶有黑莓等黑色水果。西班牙的白色加烈酒是 Sherry，帶蜂蜜味的法國甜白酒是 Sauternes。","Why is Port both sweet and high in alcohol?":"為什麼 Port 既甜又酒精濃度高？","Added alcohol stops the yeast, leaving sugar behind":"添加的酒精讓酵母停止作用，留下糖分","Sugar is added after bottling":"裝瓶後才加糖","It ferments for a long time in oak":"在橡木桶中長時間發酵","In sweet fortified wines, added alcohol kills the yeast early.":"在甜型加烈酒中，添加的酒精提早殺死酵母。","With Port, high-strength distilled alcohol is added before the yeast have eaten all the sugar. The yeast die: the leftover sugar makes the wine sweet and the added alcohol raises its strength to around 20% abv. This is how sweet fortified wines work.":"釀造 Port 時，會在酵母吃完所有的糖之前加入高濃度的蒸餾酒精。酵母死亡：剩下的糖讓酒帶甜，添加的酒精則把酒精濃度提高到大約 20% abv。甜型加烈酒就是這樣釀成的。","How should wine be kept for long-term storage?":"葡萄酒長期保存時應該怎麼存放？","Cool, at a constant temperature":"涼爽、恆溫","Warm, at a constant temperature":"溫暖、恆溫","Cool at night, warm by day":"夜間涼爽、白天溫暖","Next to a bright window":"放在明亮的窗邊","Cool and steady: extremes and swings in temperature damage wine.":"涼爽而穩定：極端溫度和溫度劇烈變化都會損害葡萄酒。","For long-term storage, wine needs a cool place with a stable temperature. Extreme heat or cold, as well as big swings, can damage it, making it lose character and eventually causing faults. Bright light should also be avoided, because it makes the wine lose its fruitiness.":"長期保存葡萄酒需要涼爽、溫度穩定的地方。過熱、過冷以及劇烈的溫度變化都可能損害它，讓酒失去特色，最終產生缺陷。也要避免強光，因為強光會讓酒失去果味。","What can strong sunshine and bright artificial light do to wine?":"強烈的陽光和明亮的人工光線會對葡萄酒造成什麼影響？","Make it lose its fruity character":"讓它失去果味","Raise its alcohol level":"提高酒精濃度","Make it sweeter":"讓它變甜","Increase its tannins":"增加單寧","Light, and the heat it brings, strip wine of its fruitiness.":"光線和隨之而來的熱會奪走葡萄酒的果味。","Bottles should be kept away from strong sunshine and bright artificial light. Both the light and the heat it gives off can make a wine lose its fruity character. They do not change the alcohol, sugar or tannin: the damage is mainly to the fruit aromas and flavours.":"酒瓶應遠離強烈的陽光和明亮的人工光線。光線本身和它散發的熱，都可能讓葡萄酒失去果味。它們不會改變酒精、糖分或單寧：受損的主要是水果香氣和風味。","Why should a bottle sealed with a cork be stored on its side?":"為什麼用軟木塞封瓶的酒要橫放保存？","The cork stays moist and keeps air out":"軟木塞保持濕潤，阻隔空氣","The wine matures faster":"葡萄酒會熟成得更快","It saves space in the cellar":"可以節省酒窖空間","Lying down, the cork touches the wine and does not dry out.":"橫放時軟木塞接觸酒液，不會乾掉。","With the bottle on its side, the cork stays in contact with the wine and remains moist. A dried-out cork can let air into the bottle, and air makes the wine lose its fruity character. Screwcap bottles do not run this risk and can be stored upright.":"酒瓶橫放時，軟木塞與酒液接觸，保持濕潤。乾掉的軟木塞可能讓空氣進入瓶中，而空氣會讓酒失去果味。旋蓋酒瓶沒有這種風險，可以直立保存。","Standing up":"直立","Only on their side":"只能橫放","Only upside down":"只能倒放","Only near a heat source":"只能放在熱源旁","With no cork to keep moist, the bottle can stand up.":"沒有需要保持濕潤的軟木塞，酒瓶就可以直立。","Lying a bottle down only serves to keep a cork moist, so it does not dry out and let air in. A screwcap has no such problem, so the bottle can be stored standing up. The other rules, a cool and constant temperature and no bright light, still apply.":"酒瓶橫放只是為了讓軟木塞保持濕潤，以免乾掉而讓空氣進入。旋蓋沒有這個問題，所以酒瓶可以直立保存。其他規則仍然適用：涼爽恆溫、避免強光。","How does a vacuum system keep opened wine fresh?":"真空系統如何讓已開瓶的葡萄酒保鮮？","A pump removes air from the bottle":"用幫浦抽出瓶中的空氣","A gas pushes the air out":"用氣體把空氣排出","Ice chills the bottle neck":"用冰塊冷卻瓶頸","The cork is sealed with wax":"用蠟封住軟木塞","A vacuum pumps air out; a blanket system pushes it out with gas.":"真空系統把空氣抽出；氣體覆蓋系統則用氣體把空氣排出。","Opened wine goes stale because it reacts with air. Vacuum systems use a pump to draw the air out of the bottle, reducing this contact. They should not be confused with blanket systems, which instead pump in a harmless gas to push the air out.":"已開瓶的葡萄酒會走味，是因為與空氣發生反應。真空系統用幫浦把瓶中的空氣抽出，減少這種接觸。別把它和氣體覆蓋系統混淆，後者是灌入無害的氣體，把空氣排出。","How does a blanket system work?":"氣體覆蓋系統如何運作？","A harmless gas pushes the air out":"用無害的氣體把空氣排出","A pump draws out the wine":"用幫浦把酒抽出","A cloth covers the bottle":"用布蓋住酒瓶","Fresh wine is added daily":"每天添加新酒","The gas takes the air's place and does not harm the wine.":"氣體取代了空氣，而且不會傷害葡萄酒。","In blanket systems a gas is pumped into the bottle, pushing the air out. The gas does not harm the wine and shields it from contact with air, which would otherwise make it stale. It is an alternative to a vacuum system, which removes the air with a pump.":"氣體覆蓋系統把氣體灌入瓶中，將空氣排出。這種氣體不會傷害葡萄酒，並能隔絕空氣，否則酒會走味。它是真空系統之外的另一種選擇，真空系統是用幫浦把空氣抽走。","What is the simplest way to keep an opened wine fresher?":"讓已開瓶的葡萄酒保鮮更久，最簡單的方法是什麼？","Recork it and keep it in the fridge":"塞回軟木塞，放進冰箱","Leave it open on the table":"開著瓶放在桌上","Warm it near a radiator":"放在暖氣旁加溫","Put it in sunlight":"放在陽光下","Cork and fridge slow down the wine going stale.":"軟木塞和冰箱能減緩葡萄酒走味。","After opening, wine reacts with air and slowly loses its freshness. Putting the cork back and keeping it in the fridge helps it last longer. For even longer, vacuum or blanket systems can be used. Heat and light, on the other hand, only make things worse.":"開瓶後，葡萄酒會與空氣發生反應，慢慢失去新鮮感。把軟木塞塞回去並放進冰箱，有助於延長保存時間。想保存更久，可以使用真空系統或氣體覆蓋系統。熱和光則只會讓情況更糟。","Well chilled, 6–8°C (43–45°F)":"充分冰鎮，6–8°C（43–45°F）","Lightly chilled, 10–13°C (50–55°F)":"稍微冰鎮，10–13°C（50–55°F）","Lightly chilled, about 13°C (55°F)":"稍微冰鎮，約 13°C（55°F）","Room temperature, 15–18°C (59–64°F)":"室溫，15–18°C（59–64°F）","Sweet wines such as Sauternes are served well chilled, at 6–8°C.":"Sauternes 等甜酒要充分冰鎮，在 6–8°C 侍酒。","Sweet wines are among the coldest-served wines, together with sparkling wines. The recommended range for a sweet wine such as Sauternes is 6–8°C. By contrast, 10–13°C suits full-bodied whites, around 13°C suits light reds, and 15–18°C suits medium- and full-bodied reds.":"甜酒和氣泡酒一樣，屬於侍酒溫度最低的葡萄酒。Sauternes 等甜酒的建議範圍是 6–8°C。相較之下，10–13°C 適合酒體飽滿的白酒，約 13°C 適合輕盈的紅酒，15–18°C 則適合酒體中等和飽滿的紅酒。","How should a sparkling wine such as Champagne be served?":"Champagne 等氣泡酒應該如何侍酒？","Well chilled, 6–10°C (43–50°F)":"充分冰鎮，6–10°C（43–50°F）","Slightly warmed":"稍微加溫","Sparkling wines are served well chilled, between 6 and 10°C.":"氣泡酒要充分冰鎮，在 6 至 10°C 之間侍酒。","Champagne and other sparkling wines should be served well chilled, in the 6–10°C range. Cold also has a practical benefit: it reduces the pressure in the bottle and makes opening safer. To keep it cool, use an ice bucket with ice and cold water or an insulated container.":"Champagne 和其他氣泡酒應該充分冰鎮，在 6–10°C 的範圍內侍酒。低溫還有一個實際的好處：降低瓶內壓力，開瓶更安全。要保持低溫，可以使用裝有冰塊和冷水的冰桶，或是保冷容器。","At what temperature should a light white such as Pinot Grigio be served?":"灰皮諾這類輕盈的白酒應該在什麼溫度侍酒？","Chilled, 7–10°C (45–50°F)":"冰鎮，7–10°C（45–50°F）","Light and medium whites and rosés: chilled, at 7–10°C.":"酒體輕盈和中等的白酒與粉紅酒：冰鎮，7–10°C。","Light- and medium-bodied whites such as Pinot Grigio, and rosés, are served chilled at 7–10°C. Only fuller whites, such as an oaked Chardonnay, are served a little warmer, at 10–13°C. The remaining ranges, from lightly chilled to room temperature, apply to red wines.":"灰皮諾等酒體輕盈和中等的白酒，以及粉紅酒，要冰鎮至 7–10°C 侍酒。只有較飽滿的白酒，例如經橡木桶的夏多內，侍酒溫度稍高，為 10–13°C。其餘從稍微冰鎮到室溫的範圍，則適用於紅酒。","Which wine is served lightly chilled at 10–13°C (50–55°F)?":"哪一款酒要稍微冰鎮，在 10–13°C（50–55°F）侍酒？","An oaked Chardonnay":"經橡木桶的夏多內","A Champagne":"Champagne","A Shiraz":"希拉茲","Full-bodied whites, like oaked Chardonnay, are served lightly chilled.":"酒體飽滿的白酒，例如經橡木桶的夏多內，要稍微冰鎮後侍酒。","A full-bodied white, such as an oaked Chardonnay, is served a little less cold than other whites, at 10–13°C. Champagne and Sauternes are served well chilled, while a Shiraz, a medium- to full-bodied red, is served at room temperature, 15–18°C.":"酒體飽滿的白酒，例如經橡木桶的夏多內，侍酒溫度比其他白酒略高，為 10–13°C。Champagne 和 Sauternes 要充分冰鎮，而希拉茲這類酒體中等至飽滿的紅酒則在室溫 15–18°C 侍酒。","Warmed above 20°C (68°F)":"加溫到 20°C（68°F）以上","Light reds are served lightly chilled, at around 13°C.":"輕盈的紅酒要稍微冰鎮，在大約 13°C 侍酒。","Not all reds are served at room temperature. Light-bodied ones such as Beaujolais are more enjoyable lightly chilled, at around 13°C. Medium- and full-bodied reds such as Shiraz, on the other hand, are served at room temperature, between 15 and 18°C.":"不是所有紅酒都在室溫侍酒。Beaujolais 這類酒體輕盈的紅酒稍微冰鎮到大約 13°C 更好喝。希拉茲這類酒體中等和飽滿的紅酒，則在 15 至 18°C 的室溫侍酒。","Which range is recommended for a full-bodied red such as Shiraz?":"希拉茲這類酒體飽滿的紅酒，建議的侍酒溫度範圍是？","15–18°C (59–64°F)":"15–18°C（59–64°F）","6–8°C (43–45°F)":"6–8°C（43–45°F）","7–10°C (45–50°F)":"7–10°C（45–50°F）","10–13°C (50–55°F)":"10–13°C（50–55°F）","Medium and full reds are served at room temperature, 15–18°C.":"酒體中等和飽滿的紅酒在室溫 15–18°C 侍酒。","For medium- and full-bodied reds, 'room temperature' means 15–18°C. Because heating and air conditioning make room temperatures vary a lot, it is safer to rely on this range. The colder ranges are for whites, rosés, sparkling wines and sweet wines.":"對酒體中等和飽滿的紅酒來說，「室溫」指的是 15–18°C。由於暖氣和冷氣讓室內溫度差異很大，以這個範圍為準比較保險。更低的溫度範圍則適用於白酒、粉紅酒、氣泡酒和甜酒。","How should an ice bucket be filled to keep wine cool?":"冰桶裡應該裝什麼，才能讓葡萄酒保持低溫？","With ice and cold water":"冰塊和冷水","With ice only":"只裝冰塊","With room-temperature water only":"只裝室溫的水","With salt and dry ice":"鹽和乾冰","Ice alone cools much less efficiently.":"只用冰塊的冷卻效率差得多。","To keep a wine cool until the bottle is finished, you can use an insulated container or an ice bucket. If you choose a bucket, fill it with ice and cold water together: the water surrounds the bottle and chills it far more effectively than ice on its own.":"想讓葡萄酒在喝完之前都保持低溫，可以使用保冷容器或冰桶。如果選擇冰桶，要同時裝入冰塊和冷水：水會包圍整個酒瓶，冷卻效果遠比只有冰塊好。","A red wine is too cold. What should you do?":"紅酒太冰了，該怎麼辦？","Let it warm up naturally in the room":"讓它在室內自然回溫","Place it next to a radiator":"放在暖氣旁","Stand it in boiling water":"放進滾水裡","Heat it in a microwave":"用微波爐加熱","Heating damages the flavours; let the wine warm up by itself.":"加熱會破壞風味；讓酒自己慢慢回溫。","Putting wine near a heat source such as a radiator can damage its flavours. The right approach is to take the bottle into the room where it will be served and let its temperature rise naturally. With a little advance planning, the wine will reach the right temperature.":"把葡萄酒放在暖氣等熱源附近，可能會破壞它的風味。正確的做法是把酒瓶拿到要飲用的房間，讓溫度自然回升。只要提早一點準備，酒就能達到合適的溫度。","When opening sparkling wine, from when must your hand stay on the cork?":"開氣泡酒時，手從什麼時候開始必須一直按住軟木塞？","From loosening the wire cage":"從鬆開鐵絲罩開始","Only once the cork is out":"軟木塞拔出後才按","Only when pouring the wine":"倒酒時才按","From when it goes in the fridge":"從放進冰箱開始","Once the cage is loose, pressure can shoot the cork out.":"鐵絲罩一鬆開，壓力就可能把軟木塞彈出去。","A bottle of sparkling wine holds a lot of pressure, and even when chilled the cork can fly out and hurt someone. That is why, as soon as the wire cage is loosened, the cork must be covered by your hand and kept under control until it is fully out of the bottle.":"一瓶氣泡酒內的壓力很大，即使冰鎮過，軟木塞仍可能飛出去傷到人。所以鐵絲罩一鬆開，就必須用手蓋住軟木塞並加以控制，直到它完全離開瓶口。","What is the correct technique for opening sparkling wine?":"開氣泡酒的正確技巧是什麼？","Hold the bottle at an angle and turn the bottle":"把酒瓶傾斜拿著，轉動酒瓶","Hold the bottle upright and twist the cork":"把酒瓶直立拿著，轉動軟木塞","Shake the bottle and push the cork":"搖晃酒瓶，推出軟木塞","Use a screw corkscrew":"使用螺旋開瓶器","Hold the cork still and turn the tilted bottle.":"固定軟木塞，轉動傾斜的酒瓶。","After removing the foil and loosening the cage, tilt the bottle, hold the cork in one hand and the base in the other, and turn the bottle. Holding the cork firmly lets the pressure escape gently, with a quiet sigh and without losing any wine.":"除去錫箔、鬆開鐵絲罩後，把酒瓶傾斜，一手握住軟木塞，一手握住瓶底，然後轉動酒瓶。穩穩握住軟木塞，讓壓力輕輕釋放，只發出一聲輕嘆，一滴酒都不浪費。","What should you do right after pulling the cork from a still wine?":"拔出靜態酒的軟木塞後，緊接著該做什麼？","Wipe the neck inside and out with a cloth":"用布把瓶口內外擦乾淨","Put the capsule back on at once":"立刻把瓶口封套裝回去","Shake the bottle":"搖晃酒瓶","Warm the bottle neck":"把瓶頸加溫","Once the cork is out, wipe the neck inside and out.":"軟木塞拔出後，把瓶口內外擦乾淨。","To open a still wine with a cork, remove the top of the capsule and wipe the neck; then centre the corkscrew, screw it in and draw the cork out gently. Finally, run a cloth round the neck, both inside and outside, before serving.":"開軟木塞封瓶的靜態酒時，先除去瓶口封套的頂部並擦拭瓶口；接著把開瓶器對準中心旋入，輕輕拔出軟木塞。最後在侍酒前，用布把瓶口內外都擦一圈。","Why do the best wine glasses narrow at the rim?":"為什麼最好的葡萄酒杯杯口都向內收窄？","To concentrate the wine's aromas":"為了集中葡萄酒的香氣","To keep the wine warmer":"為了讓酒保持較高的溫度","To reduce the amount poured":"為了減少倒酒量","To make bubbles last longer":"為了讓氣泡更持久","The shape keeps aromas in the glass so they are easier to appreciate.":"這種形狀把香氣留在杯中，更容易欣賞。","There are many glass shapes, but the best have a bowl that narrows towards the top. This keeps the aromas concentrated inside so they can be appreciated better. It is the same reason a wide glass narrowing at the top is chosen for tasting.":"酒杯的形狀很多，但最好的都是杯身向上收窄。這樣能把香氣集中在杯內，更容易欣賞。品飲時選擇杯身寬、杯口收窄的酒杯，也是同樣的道理。","In which glass is sparkling wine usually served?":"氣泡酒通常用哪一種酒杯侍酒？","A flute":"笛型杯","A red wine glass":"紅酒杯","A white wine glass":"白酒杯","Sparkling wines go in flutes; reds in glasses slightly larger than whites.":"氣泡酒用笛型杯；紅酒杯比白酒杯稍大。","Sparkling wines are usually served in flutes, while red wine glasses are slightly larger than white wine glasses. Whatever the shape, the glass must be completely clean and polished before use, because dirt and traces of detergent can spoil the wine.":"氣泡酒通常用笛型杯侍酒，紅酒杯則比白酒杯稍大。不論形狀如何，酒杯在使用前都必須徹底洗淨並擦亮，因為髒汙和殘留的清潔劑會破壞葡萄酒。","Before serving, which smell suggests a wine may be faulty?":"侍酒前，哪一種氣味表示葡萄酒可能有缺陷？","A wet cardboard smell":"濕紙板味","A fresh fruit aroma":"新鮮水果香氣","Vanilla notes from oak":"來自橡木桶的香草氣息","Delicate floral aromas":"細緻的花香","Stale, wet cardboard or vinegar smells can signal a fault.":"不新鮮的氣味、濕紙板味或醋味都可能是缺陷的訊號。","Before serving, check the appearance for haziness or floating bits, then the nose. A sound wine should not smell stale or of wet cardboard or vinegar. Fruit, flowers and vanilla from oak, on the other hand, are normal and pleasant aromas.":"侍酒前，先檢查外觀是否混濁或有漂浮物，再聞香氣。健康的葡萄酒不應該有不新鮮的氣味，也不應該有濕紙板味或醋味。水果、花香和來自橡木桶的香草則是正常而宜人的香氣。","When checking a wine's appearance before serving, what may indicate a fault?":"侍酒前檢查葡萄酒的外觀時，哪一項可能表示有缺陷？","Haziness":"混濁","A pink colour":"粉紅色","A deep red colour":"深紅色","A hazy wine may be faulty; floating bits should also be avoided.":"混濁的葡萄酒可能有缺陷；也要避免酒中有漂浮物。","Pink, golden or deep red are simply the colours of different types of wine. A hazy wine, however, may point to a fault. Before serving you should also check that nothing is floating in the wine and that it does not smell stale or of vinegar.":"粉紅色、金黃色或深紅色只是不同類型葡萄酒的顏色。混濁的葡萄酒則可能表示有缺陷。侍酒前也要確認酒中沒有漂浮物，而且沒有不新鮮的氣味或醋味。","When recommending a wine with food, what matters most?":"為餐點推薦葡萄酒時，最重要的是什麼？","The person's own preferences":"對方的個人喜好","The price of the bottle":"這瓶酒的價格","The vintage of the wine":"葡萄酒的年份","The colour of the dish":"菜餚的顏色","If someone dislikes that style of wine, there is no point suggesting it.":"如果對方不喜歡那種風格的酒，推薦它就沒有意義。","A pairing may seem exceptional to the person suggesting it, but the first criterion is always what the person drinking the wine likes or dislikes. Only after that do the food and wine interactions come in, helping you avoid the combinations that most people find unpleasant.":"推薦的人可能覺得某個搭配非常出色，但第一條準則永遠是喝酒的人喜歡或不喜歡什麼。之後才輪到食物與葡萄酒的交互作用，幫你避開多數人覺得不舒服的組合。","Sweet food makes a wine seem…":"甜的食物會讓葡萄酒顯得……","More acidic and less fruity":"更酸、果味更少","Less acidic and more fruity":"酸度更低、果味更多","Less bitter and sweeter":"苦味更少、更甜","Sweetness in food makes wine more acidic, bitter and less fruity.":"食物中的甜味讓葡萄酒更酸、更苦、果味更少。","Sweetness is one of the hardest elements to pair. It makes a wine seem more drying and bitter, more acidic, and less sweet and fruity. That is why a dry wine served with a dessert can taste sour and dull. With sweet dishes, a wine with at least as much sweetness works better.":"甜味是最難搭配的元素之一。它會讓葡萄酒顯得更乾澀、更苦、更酸，甜味和果味都變少。所以不甜的酒搭配甜點時，喝起來可能又酸又平淡。搭配甜的菜餚，選擇甜度至少相當的葡萄酒效果更好。","Which food component has the same effect on wine as sweetness?":"食物中的哪一種成分對葡萄酒的影響和甜味相同？","Umami":"鮮味","Salt":"鹽","Fat":"脂肪","Umami and sweetness both make wine more bitter, acidic and less fruity.":"鮮味和甜味都會讓葡萄酒更苦、更酸、果味更少。","Umami and sweetness act on wine in the same way: they make it seem more drying and bitter, more acidic, and less sweet and fruity. Salt and acidity have the opposite effect, while fat only changes how acidic the wine seems, making it taste less acidic.":"鮮味和甜味對葡萄酒的作用相同：讓酒顯得更乾澀、更苦、更酸，甜味和果味都變少。鹽和酸的效果相反，脂肪則只改變酸度的感受，讓酒喝起來沒那麼酸。","With an umami-rich dish, which wine is most likely to taste harsh?":"搭配鮮味豐富的菜餚時，哪一款酒最可能顯得粗澀？","A very tannic red":"單寧非常高的紅酒","A fruity rosé":"果味豐富的粉紅酒","A sweet white":"甜白酒","A light, low-tannin red":"輕盈、低單寧的紅酒","Umami boosts bitterness and dryness, already strong in a tannic red.":"鮮味會加強苦味和乾澀感，而單寧高的紅酒本來就有這些特質。","Umami makes a wine seem more drying and bitter, more acidic and less fruity. In a very tannic red, which already dries the mouth and can taste bitter, this effect adds up and the wine can turn harsh. A light, low-tannin red suffers much less.":"鮮味讓葡萄酒顯得更乾澀、更苦、更酸、果味更少。單寧非常高的紅酒本來就讓口腔乾澀，還可能帶苦味，效果疊加之下，酒會變得粗澀。輕盈、低單寧的紅酒受到的影響就小得多。","What effect does salty food have on wine?":"鹹的食物對葡萄酒有什麼影響？","It seems fruitier and fuller-bodied":"顯得果味更多、酒體更飽滿","It seems more bitter and acidic":"顯得更苦、更酸","It seems less fruity":"顯得果味更少","It makes the alcohol stand out":"讓酒精感更突出","Salt makes wine less bitter and acidic, fruitier and fuller.":"鹽讓葡萄酒沒那麼苦、沒那麼酸，果味更多、更飽滿。","Salt is wine-friendly. Salty food makes a wine seem less drying and bitter, less acidic, fruitier and fuller-bodied. That is why salty dishes are generally easy to pair. Making the alcohol more noticeable, on the other hand, is the effect of chilli heat.":"鹽是葡萄酒的好朋友。鹹的食物讓葡萄酒顯得沒那麼乾澀、沒那麼苦、沒那麼酸，果味更多、酒體更飽滿。所以鹹的菜餚通常很好搭配。讓酒精感更明顯，則是辣味的作用。","Acidic food makes a wine seem…":"酸的食物會讓葡萄酒顯得……","More acidic and bitter":"更酸、更苦","Less sweet and fruity":"甜味和果味更少","Acid in food makes wine less acidic, sweeter and fruitier.":"食物中的酸讓葡萄酒沒那麼酸，更甜、果味更多。","It may sound surprising, but acidic food makes a wine taste less acidic. It also makes it seem less drying and bitter, sweeter and fruitier. That is why a dish with a sharp, acidic note can soften a very crisp wine that might seem sharp on its own.":"聽起來也許令人意外，但酸的食物會讓葡萄酒喝起來沒那麼酸，也顯得沒那麼乾澀、沒那麼苦，更甜、果味更多。所以帶有鮮明酸味的菜餚，可以讓一款單喝可能太尖銳的清脆葡萄酒變得柔和。","What happens to a delicate wine served with a very highly flavoured dish?":"細緻的葡萄酒搭配味道非常濃郁的菜餚時，會發生什麼事？","It is overwhelmed by the food":"被食物壓過","It seems fuller-bodied":"顯得酒體更飽滿","It seems sweeter":"顯得更甜","It seems more tannic":"顯得單寧更高","Very intense flavours cover the wine, which seems to vanish.":"非常濃郁的味道會蓋過葡萄酒，酒彷彿消失了。","When food is very highly flavoured, the wine can be overwhelmed: its aromas and flavours can hardly be noticed. This is mainly a risk for delicate or light wines. With strongly flavoured dishes, it is better to choose a wine with enough flavour intensity to hold its own.":"食物味道非常濃郁時，葡萄酒可能被壓過：香氣和風味幾乎感覺不到。細緻或輕盈的葡萄酒尤其有這種風險。搭配味道濃郁的菜餚，最好選擇風味強度足以抗衡的葡萄酒。","What effect does fatty or oily food have on wine?":"高脂肪或油膩的食物對葡萄酒有什麼影響？","It makes it seem less acidic":"讓它顯得沒那麼酸","It makes it seem more acidic":"讓它顯得更酸","It makes it seem more alcoholic":"讓它顯得酒精感更重","It makes it seem more bitter":"讓它顯得更苦","Fat softens how acidic the wine seems.":"脂肪會讓葡萄酒的酸度感覺變柔和。","Fatty or oily food makes a wine seem less acidic. This is a useful effect to remember: a wine with high acidity can be pleasant alongside a rich, fatty dish. A stronger feel of alcohol comes from chilli instead, while extra bitterness comes from sweetness and umami.":"高脂肪或油膩的食物讓葡萄酒顯得沒那麼酸。這個效果值得記住：高酸度的葡萄酒搭配豐腴油潤的菜餚會很討喜。酒精感變強來自辣椒，苦味增加則來自甜味和鮮味。","What happens when a high-alcohol wine is drunk with a chilli-hot dish?":"高酒精濃度的葡萄酒搭配辛辣的菜餚時，會發生什麼事？","The chilli burn increases":"辣椒的灼熱感增強","The chilli burn disappears":"辣椒的灼熱感消失","The wine seems sweeter":"酒顯得更甜","The wine seems less alcoholic":"酒顯得酒精感較低","Alcohol boosts chilli heat, and chilli makes alcohol more noticeable.":"酒精會加強辣味，辣味也會讓酒精感更明顯。","With chilli heat, the alcohol in the wine becomes more noticeable, and the alcohol in turn increases the burning sensation. The result is a pairing many people find uncomfortable. With chilli-hot dishes, it is therefore better to choose a wine that is not too high in alcohol.":"遇到辣味時，葡萄酒中的酒精感會更明顯，而酒精又反過來加強灼熱感。許多人覺得這樣的搭配不舒服。所以搭配辛辣的菜餚，最好選擇酒精濃度不太高的葡萄酒。","Where can bitterness in a wine come from?":"葡萄酒中的苦味可能來自哪裡？","Tannin or oak":"單寧或橡木桶","Leftover sugar":"殘留的糖","The grape pulp":"葡萄果肉","Bitterness comes from skin tannins or from oak.":"苦味來自果皮的單寧或橡木桶。","In food pairing you often hear that a wine becomes 'more bitter'. This bitterness can come from tannins, found mainly in reds because they come from black grape skins, or from oak used to ferment or mature the wine. Sweetness and umami in food make it stronger.":"談餐酒搭配時，常聽到葡萄酒變得「更苦」。這種苦味可能來自單寧（主要存在於紅酒，因為來自黑葡萄的果皮），也可能來自發酵或熟成時使用的橡木桶。食物中的甜味和鮮味會讓它更強烈。","Which pair of food components makes wine seem less bitter and less acidic?":"哪一組食物成分會讓葡萄酒顯得沒那麼苦、沒那麼酸？","Sweetness and chilli":"甜味和辣味","Umami and chilli":"鮮味和辣味","Salt and acidity are the wine-friendly components that soften it.":"鹽和酸是對葡萄酒友善、能讓酒變柔和的成分。","Salt and acidity make a wine seem less drying and bitter and less acidic; salt also makes it fruitier and fuller, acidity sweeter and fruitier. Sweetness and umami do the opposite, while chilli heat makes alcohol more noticeable and is boosted by it in turn.":"鹽和酸讓葡萄酒顯得沒那麼乾澀、沒那麼苦、沒那麼酸；鹽還讓酒果味更多、更飽滿，酸則讓酒更甜、果味更多。甜味和鮮味的作用相反，而辣味會讓酒精感更明顯，並反過來被酒精加強。","With a very sweet dessert, which wine is the safest choice?":"搭配非常甜的甜點，哪一款酒是最保險的選擇？","A wine at least as sweet":"甜度至少相當的葡萄酒","A dry, tannic red":"不甜、單寧高的紅酒","A dry, high-acid white":"不甜、高酸度的白酒","A dry, light rosé":"不甜、輕盈的粉紅酒","Sweet food strips sweetness and fruit from wine, so pick a sweet wine.":"甜的食物會奪走葡萄酒的甜味和果味，所以要選甜酒。","Sweet food makes a wine seem less sweet and fruity, more acidic and more bitter. A dry wine, especially a tannic or very acidic one, is likely to taste sour and harsh. A wine with at least as much sweetness as the dish keeps its balance instead.":"甜的食物讓葡萄酒顯得甜味和果味更少、更酸、更苦。不甜的酒，尤其是單寧高或酸度很高的，很可能喝起來又酸又澀。甜度至少與菜餚相當的葡萄酒則能保持平衡。","With a chilli-hot dish, which wine is generally best avoided?":"搭配辛辣的菜餚，一般最好避開哪一款酒？","A fruity wine":"果味豐富的葡萄酒","Chilli brings out alcohol, which in turn increases the burn.":"辣味會凸顯酒精感，酒精又反過來加強灼熱感。","The interaction between chilli and alcohol works both ways: chilli heat makes the wine's alcohol more noticeable, and the alcohol makes the dish burn more. A high-alcohol wine is therefore likely to create an unpleasant pairing, while a wine with less alcohol accompanies the dish in better balance.":"辣味和酒精的交互作用是雙向的：辣味讓葡萄酒的酒精感更明顯，酒精則讓菜餚更辣。所以高酒精濃度的葡萄酒很可能造成不愉快的搭配，酒精濃度較低的葡萄酒搭配起來則更平衡。","Which statement about food and wine pairing is correct?":"關於餐酒搭配，下列哪一項敘述正確？","Most wines suit most foods for most people":"對多數人來說，多數葡萄酒都適合多數食物","Every dish has only one right wine":"每道菜只有一款正確的酒","Red wine only suits meat":"紅酒只適合搭配肉類","White wine only suits fish":"白酒只適合搭配魚類","For most people, most wines are an acceptable match for most foods.":"對多數人來說，多數葡萄酒搭配多數食物都可以接受。","Pairing is not a matter of rigid rules. For most people, most wines are an acceptable partner for most foods. You only need to know the few interactions that usually cause trouble, such as sweetness, umami and chilli, and your choices then become almost limitless.":"餐酒搭配不是死板的規則。對多數人來說，多數葡萄酒搭配多數食物都可以接受。你只需要知道少數幾種常常出問題的交互作用，例如甜味、鮮味和辣味，選擇就幾乎沒有限制了。","A very high-acid white tastes too sharp. Which dish will make it seem softer?":"一款酸度非常高的白酒喝起來太尖銳。哪一道菜會讓它顯得更柔和？","A dish with an acidic touch":"帶點酸味的菜餚","A very sweet dessert":"非常甜的甜點","An umami-rich dish":"鮮味豐富的菜餚","A very hot chilli dish":"非常辣的菜餚","Acidic food makes a wine seem less acidic, sweeter and fruitier.":"酸的食物讓葡萄酒顯得沒那麼酸，更甜、果味更多。","Acidic food 'absorbs' some of the perceived acidity: the wine seems less acidic, sweeter and fruitier. Sweetness and umami would do the opposite, making it even more acidic. Chilli does not reduce acidity but brings out alcohol. Salt or fat can also help.":"酸的食物會「吸收」一部分感受到的酸度：葡萄酒顯得沒那麼酸，更甜、果味更多。甜味和鮮味則相反，會讓酒更酸。辣味不會降低酸度，而是凸顯酒精感。鹽或脂肪也有幫助。","Which type of food makes a wine seem fuller-bodied?":"哪一類食物會讓葡萄酒顯得酒體更飽滿？","Salty food":"鹹的食物","Sweet food":"甜的食物","Umami-rich food":"鮮味豐富的食物","Chilli-hot food":"辛辣的食物","Salt makes wine seem fruitier and fuller-bodied.":"鹽讓葡萄酒顯得果味更多、酒體更飽滿。","Among the food components, salt is the one that adds perceived body to a wine, as well as making it fruitier, less bitter and less acidic. Sweetness and umami make it seem harsher and less fruity, while chilli heat mainly makes its alcohol stand out.":"在食物的各種成分中，鹽能增加葡萄酒的酒體感，同時讓酒果味更多、沒那麼苦、沒那麼酸。甜味和鮮味讓酒顯得更粗澀、果味更少，辣味則主要凸顯酒精感。","Which wine is most at risk with a sweet dish?":"搭配甜的菜餚時，哪一款酒風險最高？","A dry red with high tannin":"不甜、高單寧的紅酒","A sweet white with good acidity":"酸度良好的甜白酒","A medium-sweet, fruity white":"半甜、果味豐富的白酒","A sweet, fruity rosé":"甜而果味豐富的粉紅酒","Sweet food boosts bitterness and dryness and removes fruit: a tannic red suffers.":"甜的食物會加強苦味和乾澀感，並帶走果味：單寧高的紅酒最吃虧。","Sweet food makes a wine more drying and bitter, more acidic and less fruity. A dry, tannic red already has a strong drying feel and no sweetness to push back, so it becomes harsh. Sweet wines, by contrast, keep their balance better next to a sweet dish.":"甜的食物讓葡萄酒更乾澀、更苦、更酸、果味更少。不甜、單寧高的紅酒本來就有強烈的乾澀感，又沒有甜味可以抗衡，於是變得粗澀。甜酒搭配甜的菜餚時，則更能保持平衡。","A red wine tastes fruitier and less bitter with a dish. Which food component is most likely responsible?":"一款紅酒搭配某道菜時，果味更多、苦味更少。最可能是哪一種食物成分造成的？","Chilli heat":"辣味","Salt makes wine fruitier and less bitter.":"鹽讓葡萄酒果味更多、沒那麼苦。","Of the options given, only salt makes a wine fruitier and less bitter, as well as less acidic and fuller-bodied. Sweetness and umami have the opposite effect: more bitterness, less fruit. Chilli heat does not act on fruit and bitterness, but it makes the wine's alcohol stand out.":"在這些選項中，只有鹽能讓葡萄酒果味更多、沒那麼苦，同時沒那麼酸、酒體更飽滿。甜味和鮮味的效果相反：更苦、果味更少。辣味不影響果味和苦味，但會凸顯葡萄酒的酒精感。","Why is it useful to know the common food and wine interactions?":"為什麼了解常見的食物與葡萄酒交互作用很有用？","To avoid what most people find unpleasant":"為了避開多數人覺得不舒服的情況","To impose your taste on others":"為了把自己的口味強加給別人","To always choose the same wine":"為了永遠選同一款酒","To pair only expensive wines":"為了只搭配昂貴的葡萄酒","Knowing what to avoid makes your pairing options almost limitless.":"知道該避開什麼，搭配的選擇就幾乎沒有限制。","Knowing the typical reactions, from sweetness, umami, salt and acid to intense flavour, fat and chilli, is not about finding the one right wine. It is about knowing what most people would want to avoid. That way you are never tied to one pairing and can always start from the person's own taste.":"了解甜味、鮮味、鹽、酸、濃郁風味、脂肪和辣味的典型反應，不是為了找出唯一正確的那款酒，而是為了知道多數人想避開什麼。這樣你就不會被綁在某一種搭配上，永遠可以從對方的口味出發。","Which food component makes a medium-sweet wine seem LESS sweet?":"哪一種食物成分會讓半甜的葡萄酒顯得「沒那麼」甜？","Umami takes away sweetness and fruit, just as sweet food does.":"鮮味和甜的食物一樣，會帶走甜味和果味。","Umami works like sweetness in food: the wine seems less sweet and less fruity, more bitter and more acidic. Acidity in food does the opposite and makes the wine seem sweeter and fruitier; salt makes it fruitier and fuller, while fat only reduces the perceived acidity.":"鮮味的作用和食物中的甜味一樣：葡萄酒顯得甜味和果味更少、更苦、更酸。食物中的酸則相反，讓酒顯得更甜、果味更多；鹽讓酒果味更多、更飽滿，脂肪只會降低感受到的酸度。","In what order does the systematic approach to tasting run?":"系統化品飲法的順序是什麼？","Appearance, nose, palate":"外觀、香氣、口感","Nose, appearance, palate":"香氣、外觀、口感","Palate, nose, appearance":"口感、香氣、外觀","Appearance, palate, nose":"外觀、口感、香氣","First look, then smell, then taste.":"先看，再聞，然後嚐。","The systematic approach always follows the same order: appearance (colour), nose (fruit, oak and other aromas) and palate (structure and flavours). Repeating the same route for every wine lets you write consistent, accurate notes that you can compare over time.":"系統化品飲法永遠依照相同的順序：外觀（顏色）、香氣（水果、橡木和其他香氣）、口感（結構和風味）。每一款酒都走同一條路線，就能寫出一致、準確、日後可以比較的品飲筆記。","Why is it useful to take the same approach with every wine you taste?":"為什麼品飲每一款酒都用同樣的方法很有用？","To write accurate notes you can compare":"為了寫出準確、可以比較的筆記","To drink more wine in less time":"為了在更短的時間內喝更多酒","To warm the wine in the glass":"為了讓杯中的酒回溫","To avoid looking at the colour":"為了不必看顏色","A consistent method gives accurate notes to refer back to.":"方法一致，才能得到準確、可回頭參考的筆記。","Approaching every sample the same way helps you not to miss anything and to describe wines with the same words. Your tasting notes are then accurate and can be read again and compared later, for example to remember the differences between two grape varieties.":"用同樣的方式面對每一個酒樣，有助於不遺漏任何細節，並用相同的詞彙描述葡萄酒。這樣你的品飲筆記才準確，日後可以重讀和比較，例如回想兩個葡萄品種之間的差異。","Why do you need a white surface when tasting?":"為什麼品飲時需要白色的表面？","To judge the colour better":"為了更準確地判斷顏色","To smell the aromas better":"為了更清楚地聞到香氣","To keep the wine cool":"為了讓酒保持低溫","To measure the alcohol":"為了測量酒精","A white background helps you assess the wine's appearance.":"白色背景有助於評估葡萄酒的外觀。","Colour is what you look at during the appearance stage, and a white background lets you see it without interference. The other preparations are for the nose and palate: no distracting smells, a glass that concentrates the aromas, and a palate free of flavours such as coffee or toothpaste.":"顏色是外觀階段要觀察的項目，白色背景能讓你不受干擾地看清楚。其他準備則是為了香氣和口感：沒有干擾的氣味、能集中香氣的酒杯，以及沒有咖啡或牙膏等味道殘留的口腔。","Which of these could spoil a tasting?":"下列哪一項可能破壞品飲？","Having just brushed your teeth":"剛刷完牙","Using a white surface":"使用白色的表面","Using a glass that narrows at the top":"使用杯口收窄的酒杯","Tasting in a room with no smells":"在沒有異味的房間品飲","Lingering flavours like toothpaste or coffee distort the wine.":"牙膏或咖啡等殘留的味道會扭曲葡萄酒的味道。","Tasting needs a clean palate, without flavours lingering in the mouth such as toothpaste or coffee, which would change how the wine tastes. A white surface, a glass that concentrates the aromas and a room free of smells are, on the other hand, ideal conditions for a good tasting.":"品飲需要乾淨的口腔，不能有牙膏或咖啡等味道殘留，否則會改變葡萄酒的味道。白色的表面、能集中香氣的酒杯和沒有異味的房間，則是良好品飲的理想條件。","At this level, what do you assess at the appearance stage?":"在這個級別，外觀階段要評估什麼？","Colour: white, rosé or red":"顏色：白、粉紅或紅","The wine's body":"葡萄酒的酒體","The fruit aromas":"水果香氣","The tannin level":"單寧的多寡","At appearance you look only at the wine's colour.":"外觀階段只看葡萄酒的顏色。","In the basic systematic approach, appearance is only about colour: white, rosé or red. Aromas are assessed on the nose, while body, tannin and the other structural characteristics are judged on the palate, meaning when you actually taste the wine.":"在基礎的系統化品飲法中，外觀只看顏色：白、粉紅或紅。香氣在聞香時評估，酒體、單寧和其他結構特徵則在口感階段判斷，也就是實際品嚐葡萄酒的時候。","Which three aroma families are used on the nose?":"聞香時使用哪三大類香氣？","Fruit, oak, other":"水果、橡木、其他","Sweet, sour, bitter":"甜、酸、苦","White, rosé, red":"白、粉紅、紅","Light, medium, full":"輕盈、中等、飽滿","Aromas are grouped into fruit, oak and other.":"香氣分為水果、橡木和其他三類。","On the nose, aromas are described by grouping them into three families: fruit, which depends on grape variety and ripeness; oak, which gives notes such as vanilla or cedar; and other, which covers grass, flowers, earth, mushroom, leather and so on. The same families are then used for flavours on the palate.":"聞香時，會把香氣歸入三大類來描述：水果，取決於葡萄品種和成熟度；橡木，帶來香草或雪松等氣息；其他，包含青草、花、泥土、蘑菇、皮革等。口感階段描述風味時，也使用相同的分類。","Which of these aromas usually comes from oak?":"下列哪一種香氣通常來自橡木桶？","Grass":"青草","Oak gives notes such as vanilla, coconut, cloves, cedar and smoke.":"橡木桶帶來香草、椰子、丁香、雪松和煙燻等氣息。","When a wine is fermented or matured in oak barrels, it can pick up aromas such as vanilla, coconut, cloves, cedar and smoke. Lemon and strawberry belong to the fruit family instead, while grass falls into the 'other' family, along with flowers, earth and leather.":"葡萄酒在橡木桶中發酵或熟成時，可能帶上香草、椰子、丁香、雪松和煙燻等香氣。檸檬和草莓屬於水果類，青草則歸入「其他」類，和花、泥土、皮革一起。","Which aroma family do mushroom and leather belong to?":"蘑菇和皮革屬於哪一類香氣？","Other":"其他","Structure":"結構","Mushroom and leather are neither fruit nor oak, so they are 'other'.":"蘑菇和皮革既不是水果也不是橡木，所以屬於「其他」。","The 'other' family gathers all aromas that are neither fruit nor oak: grass, flowers, herbs, vegetables, earth, mushroom and leather. This wide variety is what makes wine so interesting. Structure, by contrast, is not an aroma family at all; it covers sensations such as acidity and tannin.":"「其他」類包含所有既不是水果也不是橡木的香氣：青草、花、香草植物、蔬菜、泥土、蘑菇和皮革。正是這份多樣性讓葡萄酒如此有趣。結構則根本不是香氣類別，它涵蓋的是酸度和單寧等感受。","Which structural characteristic makes your mouth water?":"哪一項結構特徵會讓你分泌唾液？","Acidity makes your mouth water and gives freshness.":"酸度讓你分泌唾液，並帶來清爽感。","Acidity comes straight from the grape juice and is easy to spot because it makes your mouth water. It gives wine a refreshing character: too much makes it unpleasantly sharp, too little makes it lose freshness. Tannin, by contrast, dries the mouth, while body describes how much the wine fills it.":"酸度直接來自葡萄汁，很容易辨認，因為它會讓你分泌唾液。它賦予葡萄酒清爽的特質：太多會尖銳得令人不舒服，太少則失去清爽感。單寧則讓口腔乾澀，酒體描述的是酒在口中的飽滿程度。","What does the 'body' of a wine describe?":"葡萄酒的「酒體」描述的是什麼？","How deep the colour is":"顏色有多深","How much sugar it contains":"含有多少糖","How fruity it smells":"聞起來果味有多濃","Body is the overall sense of fullness in the mouth.":"酒體是口中整體的飽滿感。","Many factors contribute to body, so the easiest way to judge it is to ask how mouth-filling the wine is. Full-bodied wines feel dense and mouth-filling, light-bodied wines more delicate. Body is assessed on the palate, not by looking at the colour or smelling the wine.":"影響酒體的因素很多，所以最簡單的判斷方法，就是問這款酒在口中有多飽滿。酒體飽滿的葡萄酒感覺濃厚、充滿口腔，酒體輕盈的則較為細緻。酒體是在口感階段評估，不是靠看顏色或聞香。","Which list shows the structural characteristics assessed on the palate?":"哪一組列出了口感階段評估的結構特徵？","Sweetness, acidity, tannin, alcohol, body":"甜度、酸度、單寧、酒精、酒體","Colour, fruit, oak, alcohol, body":"顏色、水果、橡木、酒精、酒體","Fruit, oak, other, acidity, tannin":"水果、橡木、其他、酸度、單寧","Sweetness, colour, fruit, alcohol, body":"甜度、顏色、水果、酒精、酒體","The five structural characteristics are sweetness, acidity, tannin, alcohol and body.":"五項結構特徵是甜度、酸度、單寧、酒精和酒體。","On the palate you assess two things: structure and flavours. Structure covers sweetness, acidity, tannin, alcohol and body. Fruit, oak and other, on the other hand, are families of aromas and flavours, while colour belongs to the appearance stage. Keeping these categories apart makes your notes clearer.":"口感階段要評估兩件事：結構和風味。結構包含甜度、酸度、單寧、酒精和酒體。水果、橡木和其他則是香氣與風味的類別，顏色屬於外觀階段。把這些類別分清楚，筆記會更清晰。","Tasting a red wine, your mouth feels dry. Which characteristic are you noticing?":"品嚐一款紅酒時，你的口腔感到乾澀。你注意到的是哪一項特徵？","Fruitiness":"果味","Tannin, from the grape skins, dries the mouth.":"來自葡萄果皮的單寧會讓口腔乾澀。","Tannin is typical of red wines because it comes from the skins of black grapes, which stay in contact with the juice during fermentation. It is felt more than tasted: the mouth dries out. Acidity, by contrast, makes your mouth water.":"單寧是紅酒的典型特徵，因為它來自黑葡萄的果皮，而果皮在發酵期間一直與果汁接觸。與其說是嚐到，不如說是感覺到：口腔會變得乾澀。酸度則相反，會讓你分泌唾液。","Inside a grape":"葡萄的內部","Wine starts from a simple idea: crush grapes to free their sweet juice, then let that juice ferment. That is why wine can be described as fermented grape juice. To understand what ends up in the glass, it helps to start with the grape itself, which has two main parts: the skin on the outside and the pulp on the inside. Each one gives something different to the wine.":"葡萄酒源自一個簡單的概念：把葡萄破皮，釋出甜美的果汁，再讓果汁發酵。所以葡萄酒可以說是發酵的葡萄汁。想了解杯中的酒是怎麼來的，不妨從葡萄本身開始。葡萄有兩個主要部分：外面的果皮和裡面的果肉，各自為葡萄酒帶來不同的東西。","There are two broad families of grapes: white and black. Cut in half, they look very much alike, because the real difference lies mainly in the skin. Black grapes have deeply coloured skins that also hold tannins, substances that leave your mouth feeling dry. White grapes, once ripe, have skins with a golden colour.":"葡萄分為兩大類：白葡萄和黑葡萄。切成兩半時，它們看起來非常相似，因為真正的差別主要在果皮。黑葡萄的果皮顏色很深，還含有單寧，這種物質會讓口腔感到乾澀。白葡萄成熟後，果皮呈金黃色。","The pulp is the soft, fleshy part of the grape and it holds the juice. That juice is made up mostly of water, sugar and acid. One important detail: the pulp has the same colour whether the grape is white or black. So the colour of a red wine does not come from the juice but from the skins, a key idea for understanding later how the different wines are made.":"果肉是葡萄柔軟多肉的部分，裡面含有果汁。果汁主要由水、糖和酸組成。有個重要的細節：不論白葡萄或黑葡萄，果肉的顏色都一樣。所以紅酒的顏色不是來自果汁，而是來自果皮。這是之後理解各種葡萄酒如何釀造的關鍵概念。","Wine is fermented grape juice.":"葡萄酒是發酵的葡萄汁。","Black grape skins: deep colour and tannins.":"黑葡萄果皮：深色與單寧。","Tannins make the mouth feel dry.":"單寧讓口腔感到乾澀。","Pulp: juice made of water, sugar and acid.":"果肉：由水、糖和酸組成的果汁。","Pulp is the same colour in white and black grapes.":"白葡萄和黑葡萄的果肉顏色相同。","The vine's year":"葡萄樹的一年","Grapes are the fruit of the grape vine, a plant that can live for several decades. After planting, a vine needs a couple of years to become mature; from then on it gives a crop every year. Its cycle follows the seasons: it flowers in spring, the fruit ripens through the summer and the grapes are picked towards the end of summer.":"葡萄是葡萄樹的果實，這種植物可以存活數十年。種下後，葡萄樹需要兩三年才會成熟；之後每年都有收成。它的週期跟著四季走：春季開花，果實在夏季成熟，葡萄在夏末採收。","In spring the vine produces clusters of tiny flowers. Each single flower is set to become one grape. Right after flowering, the young grapes are small, hard and green, whether they will end up white or black: at this stage you cannot yet tell them apart, and they are far from ready to make wine.":"春季，葡萄樹長出由許多小花組成的花序。每一朵花都會變成一顆葡萄。剛開完花時，幼果又小又硬又綠，不論之後會成為白葡萄還是黑葡萄：這個階段還分辨不出來，離可以釀酒也還很遠。","To grow well and give good quality fruit, a vine needs the right amount of sunlight and heat: if it is too cold or too hot, it cannot manage. Vines also do best where the winter is cold enough to let them rest. That is why most vineyards lie in two bands around the globe, roughly between 30° and 50° of latitude, north and south of the Equator.":"葡萄樹要長得好、結出優質的果實，需要適量的日照和熱量：太冷或太熱都不行。葡萄樹也最適合生長在冬季夠冷、能讓它休眠的地方。所以大多數葡萄園分布在環繞地球的兩條帶狀區域，大約在赤道以北和以南的緯度 30° 到 50° 之間。","A mature vine gives a crop every year and can live for decades.":"成熟的葡萄樹每年都有收成，可以存活數十年。","Spring: flowering; each flower becomes a grape.":"春季：開花；每朵花變成一顆葡萄。","Summer: ripening; late summer: harvest.":"夏季：成熟；夏末：採收。","Vines need the right sun and heat, plus a cold winter to rest.":"葡萄樹需要適量的日照和熱量，以及寒冷的冬季來休眠。","What happens as grapes ripen":"葡萄成熟時發生了什麼","Over the summer the small, hard grapes change a great deal. They swell as they fill with water, while their sugar content goes up and their acid content goes down. Their flavours also develop and become riper. An unripe grape is therefore sour and not very tasty, whereas a ripe grape is bigger, sweeter and less acidic.":"經過一個夏天，又小又硬的葡萄變化很大。果實吸水膨大，糖分上升，酸度下降，風味也逐漸發展、變得更成熟。所以未熟的葡萄很酸、沒什麼味道，成熟的葡萄則更大、更甜、酸度更低。","Ripening also changes the colour of the skin. White grapes turn from green to golden, while black grapes turn from green to purple. Colour is therefore a first clue to how close the grapes are to harvest, alongside the other changes: more water, more sugar, less acid and riper flavours.":"成熟也會改變果皮的顏色。白葡萄從綠色轉為金黃色，黑葡萄從綠色轉為紫色。因此顏色是判斷葡萄離採收還有多遠的第一個線索，其他變化還有：水分增加、糖分增加、酸度降低、風味更成熟。","These changes matter because they pass straight into the wine. The sugar in the grape is what yeast will turn into alcohol, so more sugar generally means a stronger wine. The acid stays in the wine and gives it freshness. The grape's flavours become the fruit aromas in the glass. The moment of picking therefore already shapes the style of the wine.":"這些變化很重要，因為它們會直接反映在葡萄酒中。葡萄中的糖會被酵母轉化為酒精，所以糖分越多，通常酒精濃度越高。酸會留在酒中，帶來清爽感。葡萄的風味則成為杯中的水果香氣。所以採收的時機已經決定了葡萄酒的風格。","Ripening grapes swell with water.":"成熟中的葡萄吸水膨大。","Sugar rises, acid falls.":"糖分上升，酸度下降。","Flavours become riper.":"風味變得更成熟。","White grapes: green to golden; black grapes: green to purple.":"白葡萄：綠色轉金黃色；黑葡萄：綠色轉紫色。","Cool climate and warm climate":"涼爽氣候與溫暖氣候","Wine regions closer to the poles have a cool climate. Germany and northern France are typical examples. Average temperatures are low and the sunshine can be weaker than nearer the Equator; in some years the grapes even struggle to ripen. In cool climates, growing white grapes is common.":"較靠近兩極的葡萄酒產區屬於涼爽氣候，德國和法國北部是典型的例子。當地平均氣溫低，日照可能比靠近赤道的地方弱；在某些年份，葡萄甚至難以成熟。涼爽氣候普遍種植白葡萄。","Regions closer to the Equator have a warm climate instead, such as parts of Australia and parts of California. Average temperatures are high, the sunshine is more intense and the grapes ripen reliably year after year. In warm climates it is common to grow black grapes, which make the most of all that heat.":"較靠近赤道的產區則屬於溫暖氣候，例如澳洲和加州的部分地區。當地平均氣溫高，日照更強，葡萄年年都能穩定成熟。溫暖氣候普遍種植黑葡萄，能充分利用這些熱量。","Climate leaves a clear mark on the grapes. As a rule, the cooler it is, the less sugar and the more acidity the grapes have; the warmer it is, the more sugar and the less acidity, together with riper flavours. This leads to different styles: a cool-climate wine tends to be lighter and fresher, a warm-climate wine richer and riper.":"氣候在葡萄上留下清楚的印記。一般而言，越涼爽，葡萄的糖分越少、酸度越高；越溫暖，糖分越多、酸度越低，風味也越成熟。這就形成了不同的風格：涼爽氣候的葡萄酒往往較輕盈、清爽，溫暖氣候的葡萄酒則較濃郁、成熟。","Chardonnay is a good example. Grown in a cool climate, it gives wines with aromas of green fruit such as apple and citrus such as lemon. Grown in a warm climate, the same grape shows stone fruit such as peach and tropical fruit such as pineapple instead. Same grape, very different style: the climate makes the difference.":"夏多內（Chardonnay）就是很好的例子。種在涼爽氣候時，釀出的酒帶有蘋果等綠色水果和檸檬等柑橘類水果的香氣。種在溫暖氣候時，同一個品種則呈現桃子等核果和鳳梨等熱帶水果。同一個品種，風格大不相同：差別就在氣候。","Cool climate: nearer the poles (e.g. Germany, northern France).":"涼爽氣候：較靠近兩極（例如德國、法國北部）。","Warm climate: nearer the Equator (e.g. parts of Australia and California).":"溫暖氣候：較靠近赤道（例如澳洲和加州的部分地區）。","Cooler → less sugar, more acidity → lighter, fresher wine.":"越涼爽 → 糖分越少、酸度越高 → 葡萄酒越輕盈、清爽。","Warmer → more sugar, less acidity, riper flavours.":"越溫暖 → 糖分越多、酸度越低、風味越成熟。","Cool: often white grapes; warm: often black grapes.":"涼爽：多為白葡萄；溫暖：多為黑葡萄。","The step that turns grape juice into wine is called alcoholic fermentation. The workers behind it are yeast, organisms so tiny you cannot see them with the naked eye. Yeast feed on the sugar in the juice and turn it into two products: alcohol and carbon dioxide, which is a gas. In short: sugar + yeast → alcohol + carbon dioxide.":"把葡萄汁變成葡萄酒的步驟叫做酒精發酵。幕後的功臣是酵母，一種小到肉眼看不見的生物。酵母以果汁中的糖為食，並把它轉化為兩種產物：酒精和二氧化碳（一種氣體）。簡單來說：糖 + 酵母 → 酒精 + 二氧化碳。","In most cases fermentation carries on until the yeast have used up all the sugar, which gives a dry wine. The alcohol stays in the newly made wine, while the carbon dioxide usually escapes into the air. There are exceptions, such as sweet wines and sparkling wines, which you will meet when looking at the types and styles of wine.":"多數情況下，發酵會持續到酵母把糖全部用完，得到不甜的葡萄酒。酒精留在剛釀成的酒中，二氧化碳通常散逸到空氣中。也有例外，例如甜酒和氣泡酒，你會在葡萄酒的類型與風格中認識它們。","The amount of alcohol in a wine is usually given as alcohol by volume, shortened to abv. A wine at 10% abv means that one tenth of the liquid is alcohol. Remember the link with the vineyard: it is the sugar the grapes built up while ripening that the yeast turn into alcohol.":"葡萄酒中的酒精含量通常以酒精濃度（alcohol by volume，簡稱 abv）表示。10% abv 的葡萄酒，表示液體的十分之一是酒精。別忘了它與葡萄園的關聯：酵母轉化為酒精的，正是葡萄在成熟過程中累積的糖分。","Yeast are microscopic organisms that eat sugar.":"酵母是以糖為食的微生物。","Usually the yeast eat all the sugar: a dry wine.":"酵母通常會把糖全部吃掉：得到不甜的葡萄酒。","Alcohol stays in the wine; carbon dioxide usually escapes.":"酒精留在酒中；二氧化碳通常會散逸。","10% abv = one tenth of the liquid is alcohol.":"10% abv = 液體的十分之一是酒精。","How white wine is made":"白酒如何釀造","White wine is usually made from white grapes. After picking, the grapes are crushed, which releases some of the juice. Straight afterwards the crushed grapes are pressed, squeezing the skins to collect the rest of the juice. The key idea is that, for white wine, the juice is separated from the skins before fermentation begins.":"白酒通常以白葡萄釀造。採收後，葡萄先破皮，釋出一部分果汁。緊接著壓榨破皮後的葡萄，擠壓果皮以取得剩餘的果汁。關鍵在於：釀造白酒時，果汁在發酵開始前就與果皮分開。","Yeast are then added to the juice and fermentation starts. It can take place in stainless steel tanks or in oak barrels. Once fermentation is over comes maturation, when the wine rests, again either in stainless steel or in oak. The final step is bottling, after which the wine is ready to reach the table.":"接著在果汁中加入酵母，發酵隨即開始，可以在不鏽鋼槽或橡木桶中進行。發酵結束後是熟成，讓酒靜置，同樣可以在不鏽鋼槽或橡木桶中進行。最後一步是裝瓶，之後葡萄酒就可以上桌了。","A useful point for the exam: white wine can also be made from black grapes. The colour of black grapes is all in the skin, and their juice is colourless. If black grapes are pressed gently before fermentation and the skins are removed straight away, the juice obtained is suitable for making a white wine.":"一個對考試很有用的重點：白酒也可以用黑葡萄釀造。黑葡萄的顏色全在果皮，果汁是無色的。只要在發酵前輕柔壓榨黑葡萄，並立刻去除果皮，得到的果汁就適合釀造白酒。","White: crushing → pressing → fermentation → maturation → bottling.":"白酒：破皮 → 壓榨 → 發酵 → 熟成 → 裝瓶。","For white wine, pressing comes before fermentation.":"釀造白酒時，壓榨在發酵之前。","Fermentation and maturation: stainless steel or oak.":"發酵與熟成：不鏽鋼槽或橡木桶。","Black grape juice is colourless, so it can make white wine.":"黑葡萄的果汁無色，所以可以釀白酒。","How red wine is made":"紅酒如何釀造","Red wine is always made from black grapes. After picking, the grapes are crushed and, unlike white wine, the juice is not separated: juice and skins go into the fermentation vessel together. This is the big difference from white winemaking, because it is the skins that will provide the colour and the tannins.":"紅酒一定是以黑葡萄釀造。採收後葡萄先破皮，但和白酒不同，果汁不會被分離出來：果汁和果皮一起放進發酵容器。這是與白酒釀造最大的差別，因為提供顏色和單寧的正是果皮。","Yeast are added and fermentation begins. During this stage the juice and skins are mixed thoroughly so that colour and tannin are drawn out of the skins. The more thorough the contact, the more colour and structure the wine gains. When fermentation has finished, the new red wine is drained off the skins.":"加入酵母後，發酵開始。在這個階段，果汁和果皮會充分混合，把顏色和單寧從果皮中萃取出來。接觸越充分，酒獲得的顏色和結構就越多。發酵結束後，新釀成的紅酒會從果皮中排出。","The leftover skins still hold some wine, so they are pressed to release it: for red wine pressing comes after fermentation, whereas for white it comes before. Next is maturation, in stainless steel tanks or oak barrels, and finally bottling. The sequence to remember: crushing, fermentation, draining, pressing, maturation, bottling.":"剩下的果皮中還含有一些酒，所以要壓榨把它取出：紅酒的壓榨在發酵之後，白酒則在發酵之前。接著是在不鏽鋼槽或橡木桶中熟成，最後裝瓶。要記住的順序：破皮、發酵、排汁、壓榨、熟成、裝瓶。","Red wine: black grapes fermented with their skins.":"紅酒：黑葡萄連同果皮一起發酵。","Mixing juice and skins extracts colour and tannin.":"混合果汁和果皮，萃取顏色和單寧。","After fermentation: draining, then pressing the skins.":"發酵後：排汁，然後壓榨果皮。","Red: crushing → fermentation → draining → pressing → maturation → bottling.":"紅酒：破皮 → 發酵 → 排汁 → 壓榨 → 熟成 → 裝瓶。","How rosé wine is made":"粉紅酒如何釀造","Rosé is also made from black grapes, and at first the method is the same as for red: the grapes are crushed, juice and skins go into the vessel together, yeast are added and fermentation starts. Colour begins to move from the skins into the juice, but rosé stands out for one clear choice: the contact is kept very short.":"粉紅酒也是以黑葡萄釀造，一開始的方法和紅酒相同：葡萄破皮，果汁和果皮一起放進容器，加入酵母，發酵開始。顏色開始從果皮進入果汁，但粉紅酒有一個明確的做法：接觸時間非常短。","After only a few hours the juice is drained off the skins. At that point it has picked up just a pink colour, and without the skins it cannot get any darker. Fermentation then finishes without the skins. It is the time spent in contact with the skins, a few hours rather than the whole fermentation, that explains why rosé is pink rather than red.":"只過幾個小時，果汁就從果皮中排出。這時它只染上粉紅色，沒有了果皮，顏色也不會再變深。之後在不含果皮的情況下完成發酵。與果皮接觸的時間只有幾個小時，而不是整個發酵期，這就是粉紅酒是粉紅色而不是紅色的原因。","After fermentation the rosé moves on to maturation, which can take place in stainless steel or oak, although oak is rarely used for rosé wines. Then it is bottled. Compared with red wine there is no pressing of the skins after fermentation, because the skins were removed early on. Sequence: crushing, fermentation, draining, maturation, bottling.":"發酵後，粉紅酒進入熟成，可以在不鏽鋼槽或橡木桶中進行，不過粉紅酒很少使用橡木桶。接著裝瓶。和紅酒相比，發酵後沒有壓榨果皮的步驟，因為果皮很早就移除了。順序：破皮、發酵、排汁、熟成、裝瓶。","Rosé is made from black grapes.":"粉紅酒以黑葡萄釀造。","Only a few hours on the skins: the juice turns just pink.":"只與果皮接觸幾小時：果汁只染上粉紅色。","Fermentation finishes without the skins.":"在不含果皮的情況下完成發酵。","Rosé is rarely matured in oak.":"粉紅酒很少在橡木桶中熟成。","Rosé: crushing → fermentation → draining → maturation → bottling.":"粉紅酒：破皮 → 發酵 → 排汁 → 熟成 → 裝瓶。","Three types of wine: still, sparkling, fortified":"三種類型的葡萄酒：靜態酒、氣泡酒、加烈酒","When people simply say «wine», they usually mean a still wine: one without bubbles. This is by far the biggest category. Still wines range from 8% to 15% abv, though most sit between 11.5% and 14%. The abv figure (alcohol by volume) tells you how much of the liquid is alcohol, so a wine at 10% abv is one tenth alcohol.":"一般只說「葡萄酒」時，通常指的是靜態酒：沒有氣泡的酒。這是目前為止最大的類別。靜態酒的範圍是 8% 至 15% abv，不過大多數在 11.5% 至 14% 之間。abv（酒精濃度）這個數字告訴你液體中有多少是酒精，所以 10% abv 的葡萄酒有十分之一是酒精。","Many still wines take their name from the place where they are made: Sancerre and Burgundy in France, Rioja in Spain, Chianti in Italy. Others carry the name of the grape variety instead, such as a Pinot Grigio. Spotting which of the two naming logics a label uses is a quick first step towards knowing what will be in the glass.":"許多靜態酒以產地命名：法國的 Sancerre 和布根地、西班牙的 Rioja、義大利的 Chianti。另一些則以葡萄品種命名，例如灰皮諾（Pinot Grigio）。看出酒標使用的是哪一種命名方式，是快速了解杯中會是什麼酒的第一步。","Sparkling wines are fizzy. Fermentation creates carbon dioxide gas, and if that gas is kept trapped inside the wine, it is released as bubbles once the bottle is opened. Champagne from France is the most famous example; Cava from Spain and Prosecco from Italy are also very well known. Sparkling wine is now made all around the world.":"氣泡酒帶有氣泡。發酵會產生二氧化碳氣體，如果把這些氣體保留在酒中，開瓶時就會以氣泡的形式釋放。法國的 Champagne 是最著名的例子；西班牙的 Cava 和義大利的 Prosecco 也非常有名。現在世界各地都釀造氣泡酒。","Fortified wines have had extra alcohol added to them. That is why they are stronger than still wines, usually somewhere between 15% and 22% abv. Two classic examples to remember are Sherry, from Spain, and Port, from Portugal. You will meet both again in the chapter on other wines to know.":"加烈酒額外添加了酒精，所以比靜態酒更烈，通常在 15% 至 22% abv 之間。要記住兩個經典例子：西班牙的 Sherry 和葡萄牙的 Port。在「其他必須認識的葡萄酒」那一章，你還會再遇到它們。","Still: no bubbles, 8–15% abv (mostly 11.5–14%)":"靜態酒：沒有氣泡，8–15% abv（多數為 11.5–14%）","Sparkling: carbon dioxide from fermentation trapped in the wine":"氣泡酒：發酵產生的二氧化碳被保留在酒中","Fortified: extra alcohol added, 15–22% abv (Sherry, Port)":"加烈酒：額外添加酒精，15–22% abv（Sherry、Port）","A wine may be named after its region or its grape":"葡萄酒可能以產區或品種命名","Colour: white, red, rosé":"顏色：白、紅、粉紅","A wine's colour depends on two things: the grape variety and the way the wine is made. There are white grapes and black grapes, but inside they look very alike: the pulp is the same colour in both and the juice has no colour. All the colour of a black grape sits in its skin, which also holds the tannins.":"葡萄酒的顏色取決於兩件事：葡萄品種和釀造方式。葡萄有白葡萄和黑葡萄，但內部看起來非常相似：兩者的果肉顏色相同，果汁都沒有顏色。黑葡萄所有的顏色都在果皮，果皮同時也含有單寧。","White wines are usually made from white grapes, as in Chablis or a Riesling. Yet black grapes can also give a white wine. The trick is to separate the skins from the juice before fermentation, for example by pressing gently: since the colour lives in the skins, the juice stays pale and the finished wine is white.":"白酒通常以白葡萄釀造，例如 Chablis 或麗絲玲。不過黑葡萄也能釀出白酒。訣竅是在發酵前把果皮和果汁分開，例如輕柔壓榨：既然顏色在果皮裡，果汁就維持淺色，釀成的酒就是白酒。","A red wine, on the other hand, must come from black grapes. During fermentation the skins stay in the juice and are mixed in thoroughly, so they pass colour and tannin into the wine. Once fermentation is over, the new wine is drained off the skins. Rioja from Spain and Cabernet Sauvignon wines are red examples.":"紅酒則必須以黑葡萄釀造。發酵期間果皮留在果汁中並充分混合，把顏色和單寧帶入酒中。發酵結束後，新酒從果皮中排出。西班牙的 Rioja 和卡本內蘇維濃葡萄酒都是紅酒的例子。","Rosé is also made from black grapes, but the skin contact is short: just a few hours. The juice, by then only pink, is drained off and finishes fermenting without the skins, giving a lightly coloured wine. White Zinfandel from California is a rosé example. Rosé wines are also only rarely aged in oak.":"粉紅酒也是以黑葡萄釀造，但與果皮的接觸時間很短：只有幾個小時。此時只呈粉紅色的果汁被排出，在不含果皮的情況下完成發酵，釀成顏色淺淡的葡萄酒。加州的 White Zinfandel 就是粉紅酒的例子。粉紅酒也很少在橡木桶中陳年。","Black grape colour is in the skin; the juice is colourless":"黑葡萄的顏色在果皮；果汁無色","White: usually white grapes, possible from black grapes without skins":"白酒：通常用白葡萄，也可用去除果皮的黑葡萄","Red: black grapes only, skins kept through fermentation":"紅酒：只用黑葡萄，發酵全程保留果皮","Rosé: black grapes, a few hours of skin contact":"粉紅酒：黑葡萄，與果皮接觸幾小時","Structure (1): sweetness and acidity":"結構（1）：甜度與酸度","Sweetness comes from sugar left in the wine. Most wines are dry: to make one, the yeast must turn all the sugar in the juice into alcohol, leaving little or none behind. Dry examples include Chablis and Sauvignon Blanc wines among whites, and Côtes du Rhône, Chianti and Cabernet Sauvignon wines among reds.":"甜度來自留在酒中的糖。大多數葡萄酒都是不甜的：要釀出不甜的酒，酵母必須把果汁中的糖全部轉化為酒精，只留下極少或完全不留。不甜的例子，白酒有 Chablis 和白蘇維濃葡萄酒，紅酒有 Côtes du Rhône、Chianti 和卡本內蘇維濃葡萄酒。","Medium-sweet wines are mostly white or rosé. There are two main ways to make them: remove the yeast before it has turned all the sugar into alcohol, or blend some unfermented grape juice into a dry wine. Some German Rieslings and White Zinfandel, the Californian rosé, are good examples.":"半甜葡萄酒多半是白酒或粉紅酒。主要有兩種釀造方法：在酵母把糖全部轉化為酒精之前把它移除，或是在不甜的酒中調入一些未發酵的葡萄汁。部分德國麗絲玲和加州粉紅酒 White Zinfandel 都是很好的例子。","Sweet wines hold so much sugar that they can feel thick, almost syrupy. They can come from grapes so rich in sugar that the yeast stop before eating it all, as in Sauternes or some German Rieslings. In fortified wines, strong distilled alcohol is added, killing the yeast early; the sugar left behind makes Port and some Sherries sweet.":"甜酒含有大量的糖，喝起來可能濃稠，幾乎像糖漿。它們可以來自糖分極高的葡萄，酵母還沒把糖吃完就停止了，例如 Sauternes 或部分德國麗絲玲。在加烈酒中，則是加入高濃度的蒸餾酒精，提早殺死酵母；留下的糖讓 Port 和部分 Sherry 帶有甜味。","Acidity comes straight from the grape juice, and it is what makes a wine refreshing. It is easy to spot because it makes your mouth water. Too much tastes unpleasantly sharp; too little and the wine loses its freshness. Chablis, Chianti and wines from Sauvignon Blanc, Riesling, Cabernet Sauvignon and Pinot Noir all have high acidity.":"酸度直接來自葡萄汁，正是它讓葡萄酒清爽。酸度很容易辨認，因為它會讓你分泌唾液。太多會尖銳得令人不舒服；太少則讓酒失去清爽感。Chablis、Chianti，以及白蘇維濃、麗絲玲、卡本內蘇維濃和黑皮諾釀造的葡萄酒，酸度都很高。","In sweet wines, acidity is vital. It acts as a counterweight to the sugar and stops the wine from tasting cloying. That is why a good Sauternes or a sweet Riesling always has high acidity: sweetness and freshness balance each other, and every sip stays enjoyable to the end.":"在甜酒中，酸度至關重要。它與糖分抗衡，讓酒不會膩口。所以好的 Sauternes 或甜型麗絲玲一定有高酸度：甜味和清爽感彼此平衡，每一口都讓人愉快，直到最後。","Dry: yeast turn all the sugar into alcohol":"不甜：酵母把所有的糖轉化為酒精","Medium: yeast removed early, or unfermented juice added":"半甜：提早移除酵母，或加入未發酵的葡萄汁","Sweet: very sugary grapes, or added alcohol killing the yeast":"甜：糖分極高的葡萄，或添加酒精殺死酵母","Acidity: from the juice, makes the mouth water, balances sweetness":"酸度：來自果汁，讓人分泌唾液，平衡甜味","Structure (2): tannin, alcohol and body":"結構（2）：單寧、酒精與酒體","Tannin belongs to red wines and comes from the skins of black grapes. How much a wine has depends on the grape variety and on the winemaking. It can taste a little bitter, but mostly it is something you feel: it leaves your mouth dry. Red Bordeaux and Chianti are high in tannin; Beaujolais and some Pinot Noir wines are low.":"單寧屬於紅酒，來自黑葡萄的果皮。酒中單寧的多寡取決於葡萄品種和釀造方式。它可能帶一點苦味，但主要是一種觸感：讓口腔乾澀。波爾多紅酒和 Chianti 單寧高；Beaujolais 和部分黑皮諾葡萄酒單寧低。","Nearly all still and sparkling wines sit between 11.5% and 14% abv. A few reach 15%, while others go as low as 8%. Châteauneuf-du-Pape, a French red, is an example of a high-alcohol wine; White Zinfandel from California is an example of a low-alcohol one. Remember that alcohol is produced when yeast ferment sugar.":"幾乎所有靜態酒和氣泡酒都在 11.5% 至 14% abv 之間。少數達到 15%，也有低至 8% 的。法國紅酒 Châteauneuf-du-Pape 是高酒精濃度葡萄酒的例子；加州的 White Zinfandel 則是低酒精濃度的例子。記住，酒精是酵母發酵糖時產生的。","Body describes the overall feel of a wine in your mouth. Many things contribute to it, so the easiest question to ask is: how mouth-filling is it? Full-bodied wines feel dense and rich, while light-bodied ones feel more delicate. Light: Pinot Grigio, Beaujolais. Medium: Sancerre, Côtes du Rhône. Full: Californian Cabernet Sauvignon, Sauternes.":"酒體描述的是葡萄酒在口中的整體感受。影響它的因素很多，所以最簡單的問法是：它在口中有多飽滿？酒體飽滿的葡萄酒感覺濃郁厚實，酒體輕盈的則較為細緻。輕盈：灰皮諾、Beaujolais。中等：Sancerre、Côtes du Rhône。飽滿：加州卡本內蘇維濃、Sauternes。","Tannin: from skins, dries the mouth, a red-wine feature":"單寧：來自果皮，讓口腔乾澀，是紅酒的特徵","Alcohol: usually 11.5–14% abv, 8–15% for still and sparkling":"酒精：通常 11.5–14% abv，靜態酒和氣泡酒為 8–15%","Body: how mouth-filling the wine is (light, medium, full)":"酒體：酒在口中的飽滿程度（輕盈、中等、飽滿）","Aromas and flavours: fruit, oak, other":"香氣與風味：水果、橡木、其他","A wine's aromas and flavours come from different places. Some come straight from the grapes, while others develop during winemaking and maturation. Putting them into words feels hard at first, but it is a skill that grows with practice. A simple method is to ask three questions: do I notice fruit? Oak? Something else?":"葡萄酒的香氣和風味有不同的來源。有些直接來自葡萄，有些則在釀造和熟成過程中形成。一開始要用文字描述它們並不容易，但這是一種會隨練習進步的能力。有個簡單的方法，就是問三個問題：我有沒有聞到水果？橡木？還有其他的嗎？","Almost every wine smells of fruit. The kind of fruit depends first on the grape variety: Cabernet Sauvignon, for instance, smells of blackcurrant. Ripeness matters too. A Chardonnay from a cool climate shows green apple and lemon, whereas one from a warm climate leans towards peach and tropical fruit such as pineapple.":"幾乎每一款葡萄酒都有水果香氣。是哪一種水果，首先取決於葡萄品種：例如卡本內蘇維濃有黑醋栗香氣。成熟度也很重要。涼爽氣候的夏多內呈現青蘋果和檸檬，溫暖氣候的則偏向桃子和鳳梨等熱帶水果。","Wine can be fermented and/or matured in oak barrels. When it is, the wood adds notes such as vanilla, coconut, cloves, cedar and smoke. The use of oak is sometimes mentioned on the label. If you pick up these aromas alongside the fruit, it is a good clue that the wine has spent time in barrel.":"葡萄酒可以在橡木桶中發酵和（或）熟成。這時木頭會增添香草、椰子、丁香、雪松和煙燻等氣息。酒標上有時會註明使用橡木桶。如果你在果香之外聞到這些香氣，就是這款酒曾在桶中待過的好線索。","Finally, there are the «other» aromas that make wine so varied and interesting: grass, flowers, herbs, vegetables, earth, mushroom and leather. A Sauvignon Blanc, for example, can bring cut grass to mind, while Chianti can show dried herbs. Keeping them in a family of their own stops you confusing them with fruit.":"最後是讓葡萄酒如此多變有趣的「其他」香氣：青草、花、香草植物、蔬菜、泥土、蘑菇和皮革。例如白蘇維濃會讓人想到剛割過的青草，Chianti 則可能帶有乾燥香草。把它們獨立成一類，就不會和水果混淆。","Fruit: depends on the grape variety and its ripeness":"水果：取決於葡萄品種和成熟度","Cool climate = apple, lemon; warm climate = peach, pineapple":"涼爽氣候 = 蘋果、檸檬；溫暖氣候 = 桃子、鳳梨","Oak: vanilla, coconut, cloves, cedar, smoke":"橡木：香草、椰子、丁香、雪松、煙燻","Other: grass, flowers, herbs, vegetables, earth, mushroom, leather":"其他：青草、花、香草植物、蔬菜、泥土、蘑菇、皮革","Style: the sum of the characteristics":"風格：所有特徵的總和","Each of the three types of wine, still, sparkling or fortified, can come in many different styles. A style brings together three elements: colour, structure (sweetness, acidity, tannin, alcohol, body) and aromas and flavours. Describing a style means putting these pieces together into one complete portrait of the wine.":"靜態酒、氣泡酒、加烈酒這三種類型，每一種都可以有許多不同的風格。風格結合了三個元素：顏色、結構（甜度、酸度、單寧、酒精、酒體）以及香氣與風味。描述風格，就是把這些拼圖組合成一幅完整的葡萄酒肖像。","A comparison makes this clear. Chablis and Sauternes are both French white wines, yet their styles are opposites. Chablis is dry, high in acidity, light to medium in body, with green apple and lemon and no oak. Sauternes is sweet and full-bodied, with apricot, honey and vanilla from oak, held up by high acidity.":"比較一下就清楚了。Chablis 和 Sauternes 都是法國白酒，風格卻截然相反。Chablis 不甜、酸度高，酒體輕盈至中等，帶有青蘋果和檸檬，不經橡木桶。Sauternes 甜而酒體飽滿，帶有杏桃、蜂蜜和來自橡木桶的香草，並由高酸度支撐。","Style depends a lot on the climate where the grapes grow. The cooler it is, the less sugar and the more acidity the grapes have, giving fresher, lighter wines with green fruit and citrus. The warmer it is, the more sugar and the less acidity: flavours taste riper and, since sugar becomes alcohol, wines tend to be stronger and fuller.":"風格很大程度取決於葡萄生長地的氣候。越涼爽，葡萄的糖分越少、酸度越高，釀出更清爽、更輕盈、帶有綠色水果和柑橘類風味的葡萄酒。越溫暖，糖分越多、酸度越低：風味更成熟，而且因為糖會變成酒精，葡萄酒的酒精濃度往往更高、酒體更飽滿。","To describe a style, you follow a systematic approach to tasting. First the appearance: the colour (white, red, rosé). Then the nose: aromas of fruit, oak or other. Finally the palate: sweetness, acidity, tannin, alcohol and body, plus the flavours. Always using the same order makes it easier to compare wines and remember them.":"描述風格時，要依照系統化品飲法。先看外觀：顏色（白、紅、粉紅）。再聞香氣：水果、橡木或其他香氣。最後是口感：甜度、酸度、單寧、酒精和酒體，加上風味。永遠使用相同的順序，比較和記憶葡萄酒就更容易。","Style = colour + structure + aromas and flavours":"風格 = 顏色 + 結構 + 香氣與風味","Cool climate: more acid, less sugar, lighter and fresher wines":"涼爽氣候：酸度較高、糖分較少，葡萄酒較輕盈清爽","Warm climate: more sugar, less acid, riper flavours":"溫暖氣候：糖分較多、酸度較低，風味較成熟","Tasting: appearance, nose, palate, always in the same order":"品飲：外觀、香氣、口感，永遠依照相同的順序","Chardonnay is one of the most popular and widely planted grape varieties in the world. It makes dry wines, but in very different styles. The main reason is that it does well in both cool and warm climates and changes character with the ripeness of the grapes. Choices in the winery, above all the use of oak, also shape its style.":"夏多內（Chardonnay）是全世界最受歡迎、種植最廣的葡萄品種之一。它釀出不甜的葡萄酒，但風格差異極大。主要原因是它在涼爽和溫暖氣候都能生長良好，並隨葡萄的成熟度而改變特性。酒廠裡的選擇，尤其是橡木桶的使用，也會塑造它的風格。","In a cool climate the grapes ripen less, so they stay more acidic and less sugary. The result is a Chardonnay with high acidity, a light to medium body and aromas of green fruit (apple) and citrus (lemon). In a warm climate the grapes ripen further: the wine has medium acidity, a medium to full body and flavours of stone fruit (peach) and tropical fruit (pineapple, banana).":"在涼爽氣候，葡萄成熟度較低，因此酸度較高、糖分較少。釀出的夏多內酸度高、酒體輕盈至中等，帶有綠色水果（蘋果）和柑橘類水果（檸檬）的香氣。在溫暖氣候，葡萄更成熟：酒的酸度中等、酒體中等至飽滿，帶有核果（桃子）和熱帶水果（鳳梨、香蕉）的風味。","Chardonnay can be fermented and matured in stainless steel tanks or in oak barrels. Without oak it keeps pure, fresh fruit. With oak it picks up vanilla notes and often a richer character. A typical example of the warm, oaked style is a full-bodied Californian Chardonnay with ripe tropical fruit and vanilla.":"夏多內可以在不鏽鋼槽或橡木桶中發酵和熟成。不用橡木桶時，它保有純淨新鮮的果香。使用橡木桶時，會帶上香草氣息，往往也更濃郁。溫暖氣候、經橡木桶風格的典型例子，是酒體飽滿、帶有成熟熱帶水果和香草風味的加州夏多內。","Chardonnay is the grape behind white Burgundy (Bourgogne) in France: medium-bodied, high-acid wines with lemon and peach, sometimes with vanilla from oak. Chablis comes from the coolest part of Burgundy: high acidity, light to medium body, apple and lemon, and usually no oak. Outside France, Australia and California are well known for Chardonnay.":"夏多內是法國布根地（Bourgogne）白酒背後的品種：酒體中等、酸度高，帶有檸檬和桃子，有時有來自橡木桶的香草氣息。Chablis 來自布根地最涼爽的地區：酸度高，酒體輕盈至中等，蘋果和檸檬，通常不經橡木桶。在法國之外，澳洲和加州以夏多內聞名。","Chardonnay is also used to make Champagne, where it is often blended with Pinot Noir. In short, when you meet a Chardonnay, ask two questions: was the climate cool or warm (apple and lemon, or peach and pineapple)? And did the wine see oak (vanilla or not)? The answers tell you almost everything about its style.":"夏多內也用於釀造 Champagne，常與黑皮諾混釀。總之，遇到一款夏多內時，問兩個問題：氣候是涼爽還是溫暖（蘋果和檸檬，還是桃子和鳳梨）？這款酒有沒有經過橡木桶（有沒有香草味）？答案幾乎就能說明它的整體風格。","Dry wines in many styles; one of the most planted grapes":"不甜，風格多樣；種植最廣的品種之一","Cool: high acidity, apple and lemon; warm: peach, pineapple, banana":"涼爽：高酸度，蘋果和檸檬；溫暖：桃子、鳳梨、香蕉","Oak adds vanilla":"橡木桶增添香草氣息","White Burgundy and Chablis (unoaked); also Australia and California":"布根地白酒和 Chablis（不經橡木桶）；還有澳洲和加州","In Champagne with Pinot Noir":"在 Champagne 中與黑皮諾搭配","Sauvignon Blanc makes dry wines with intense aromas and refreshingly high acidity. The body ranges from light to medium. It is an easy grape to spot by its nose: as soon as you lift the glass, you notice sharp, lively aromas that set it apart from more delicate whites such as Pinot Grigio.":"白蘇維濃（Sauvignon Blanc）釀出不甜的葡萄酒，香氣濃郁，酸度高而清爽，酒體輕盈至中等。這個品種很容易靠香氣辨認：一舉起酒杯，就能聞到鮮明活潑的香氣，和灰皮諾等較細緻的白酒截然不同。","The fruit ranges from green apple to citrus such as grapefruit, and on to tropical fruit such as passion fruit. Alongside the fruit there are often herbaceous notes: asparagus, green bell pepper and freshly cut grass. This mix of fresh fruit and «green» notes is Sauvignon Blanc's signature.":"果香從青蘋果、葡萄柚等柑橘類，到百香果等熱帶水果都有。除了果香，常常還有草本氣息：蘆筍、青椒和剛割過的青草。這種新鮮果香與「青綠」氣息的組合，就是白蘇維濃的招牌。","In the winery the aim is to protect those aromas. So Sauvignon Blanc is often fermented in stainless steel tanks and usually not matured in oak: wood would add vanilla and toasty notes that would hide the grape's typical aromas. The result is a fresh, direct and very aromatic wine.":"在酒廠裡，目標是保護這些香氣。所以白蘇維濃常在不鏽鋼槽中發酵，而且通常不經橡木桶熟成：木頭會增添香草和烘烤氣息，蓋過品種的典型香氣。成果是一款清爽、直接、香氣奔放的葡萄酒。","Two very popular wines to remember: New Zealand Sauvignon Blanc (from Marlborough, for example), often showing grapefruit, lemon and grass, and Sancerre, a dry, medium-bodied white from France's Loire Valley with green apple and herbaceous notes. Sancerre labels usually do not name the grape, so you need to know it is Sauvignon Blanc.":"要記住兩款非常受歡迎的葡萄酒：紐西蘭白蘇維濃（例如來自馬爾堡 Marlborough），常帶有葡萄柚、檸檬和青草氣息；以及 Sancerre，來自法國羅亞爾河谷的不甜白酒，酒體中等，帶有青蘋果和草本氣息。Sancerre 的酒標通常不標示品種，所以你必須知道它是白蘇維濃。","Dry, pronounced aromas, high acidity, light to medium body":"不甜，香氣濃郁，高酸度，酒體輕盈至中等","Apple, grapefruit, passion fruit + asparagus, green pepper, grass":"蘋果、葡萄柚、百香果 + 蘆筍、青椒、青草","Stainless steel, usually no oak, to keep its aromas":"不鏽鋼槽，通常不經橡木桶，以保留香氣","Key wines: New Zealand and Sancerre (Loire)":"重點酒款：紐西蘭和 Sancerre（羅亞爾河）","Pinot Grigio is a hugely popular grape variety. Its wines are usually dry and light-bodied, with medium to high acidity. The flavours are simple and delicate: mostly pear and lemon. It is not about power or complexity; it is an easy, fresh and straightforward white made to be enjoyed without fuss.":"灰皮諾（Pinot Grigio）是極受歡迎的葡萄品種。它的葡萄酒通常不甜、酒體輕盈，酸度中等至高。風味簡單而細緻：主要是梨子和檸檬。它追求的不是力道或複雜度，而是一款易飲、清爽、直接的白酒，讓人輕鬆享用。","Here too, winemaking choices are about protecting the fruit. Pinot Grigio is usually fermented in stainless steel tanks and not matured in oak. That way it keeps its fruity flavours and its lightness: oak, with its vanilla and toasty notes, would easily cover such delicate fruit.":"這裡的釀造選擇同樣是為了保護果香。灰皮諾通常在不鏽鋼槽中發酵，不經橡木桶熟成。這樣才能保留它的果味和輕盈感：橡木桶的香草和烘烤氣息很容易蓋過如此細緻的果香。","Pinot Grigio is linked above all with Italy, for example areas such as Veneto or Trentino, but it is grown in other countries too. The name on the label is the grape's name, making it the classic example of a wine named after its variety. Being light, it is served chilled, like other light and medium-bodied whites.":"灰皮諾主要與義大利有關，例如唯內多（Veneto）或特倫提諾（Trentino）等地區，不過其他國家也有種植。酒標上的名字就是品種名，所以它是以品種命名的經典例子。因為輕盈，它和其他酒體輕盈及中等的白酒一樣，要冰鎮後侍酒。","Usually dry, light body, medium to high acidity":"通常不甜，酒體輕盈，酸度中等至高","Simple pear and lemon flavours":"簡單的梨子和檸檬風味","Stainless steel, no oak, to keep the fruit":"不鏽鋼槽，不經橡木桶，以保留果香","Mainly associated with Italy":"主要與義大利有關","Riesling is a versatile grape: it makes wines from dry through medium to sweet. One thing never changes, though: every Riesling has high acidity. That acidity balances any sugar, so even a sweet Riesling stays fresh rather than cloying. The body ranges from light to medium.":"麗絲玲（Riesling）是用途多樣的品種：能釀出從不甜、半甜到甜的葡萄酒。但有一點永遠不變：每一款麗絲玲的酸度都高。酸度能平衡糖分，所以即使是甜型麗絲玲也清爽而不膩口。酒體輕盈至中等。","The aromas are pronounced and can range from flowers and green apple to citrus (lime, lemon) and on to stone fruit (peach, apricot). Like Sauvignon Blanc and Pinot Grigio, Riesling is often fermented in stainless steel and not matured in oak, so that the grape's pure aromas take centre stage.":"它的香氣濃郁，從花香和青蘋果，到柑橘類（萊姆、檸檬），再到核果（桃子、杏桃）。和白蘇維濃、灰皮諾一樣，麗絲玲常在不鏽鋼槽中發酵，不經橡木桶熟成，讓品種純淨的香氣成為主角。","Riesling is the classic grape of Germany, where it is made across the whole range from dry to sweet; some German Rieslings, from the Mosel for example, are medium-sweet, balanced by acidity and low in alcohol. Alsace in France and Australia, on the other hand, make Riesling in a dry style, often with lime, lemon and floral notes.":"麗絲玲是德國的經典品種，當地從不甜到甜的完整範圍都有釀造；部分德國麗絲玲，例如來自 Mosel 的，是半甜型，由酸度平衡，酒精濃度低。法國的阿爾薩斯和澳洲則以不甜的風格釀造麗絲玲，常帶有萊姆、檸檬和花香。","Watch the label: because the same grape can make dry, medium or sweet wines, the word «Riesling» alone does not tell you how sweet the wine will be. The origin helps: Alsace and Australia point to a dry style, while Germany covers the whole range. It is also worth reading the wine's description.":"留意酒標：同一個品種可以釀出不甜、半甜或甜的葡萄酒，所以光看「Riesling」一字無法知道酒有多甜。產地能幫上忙：阿爾薩斯和澳洲指向不甜的風格，德國則涵蓋完整範圍。也值得讀一讀酒款的說明。","Dry to sweet, but always high in acidity":"從不甜到甜，但酸度始終很高","Floral, apple, lime, lemon, peach, apricot":"花香、蘋果、萊姆、檸檬、桃子、杏桃","Stainless steel, no oak":"不鏽鋼槽，不經橡木桶","Germany: full range; Alsace and Australia: dry style":"德國：完整範圍；阿爾薩斯和澳洲：不甜的風格","Cabernet Sauvignon is a black grape planted all over the world. It makes dry red wines with high tannin and high acidity: you notice both the drying grip and the mouth-watering freshness straight away. The body ranges from medium to full. Like other black grapes, it does well in warm regions, where the grapes ripen reliably.":"卡本內蘇維濃（Cabernet Sauvignon）是全世界都有種植的黑葡萄品種。它釀出不甜的紅酒，單寧高、酸度高：乾澀的收斂感和令人分泌唾液的清爽感，一入口就能感受到。酒體中等至飽滿。和其他黑葡萄一樣，它在葡萄能穩定成熟的溫暖產區生長良好。","Its signature aroma is blackcurrant, often with black cherry. Alongside the fruit there are herbaceous notes such as green bell pepper and mint. Many Cabernet Sauvignons are matured in oak, which adds cedar and vanilla. A Californian Cabernet, for example, can be full-bodied, with intense blackcurrant and cedar notes.":"它的招牌香氣是黑醋栗，常伴隨黑櫻桃。除了果香，還有青椒和薄荷等草本氣息。許多卡本內蘇維濃都在橡木桶中熟成，增添雪松和香草氣息。例如加州的卡本內可以酒體飽滿，帶有濃郁的黑醋栗和雪松氣息。","Because its tannin is so high, Cabernet Sauvignon is often blended with other grapes. In Bordeaux it is paired with Merlot, which softens the wine and adds body. In Australia it is sometimes blended with Shiraz, which brings spicy aromas. Blending is therefore a way to round out or enrich the style.":"因為單寧很高，卡本內蘇維濃常與其他品種混釀。在波爾多，它與梅洛搭配，梅洛讓酒更柔和並增添酒體。在澳洲，它有時與希拉茲混釀，帶來香料氣息。所以混釀是讓風格更圓潤或更豐富的方法。","Beyond Bordeaux, Cabernet Sauvignon is widely grown in California, Australia, Chile and South Africa. In these countries it often appears on its own on the label, under the grape's name. In Bordeaux, by contrast, the label shows the region and the wine is usually a blend, so you need to know it contains Cabernet Sauvignon and Merlot.":"除了波爾多，卡本內蘇維濃在加州、澳洲、智利和南非也廣泛種植。在這些國家，它常以品種名單獨出現在酒標上。在波爾多則相反，酒標標示的是產區，而且通常是混釀，所以你必須知道裡面有卡本內蘇維濃和梅洛。","Dry, high tannin, high acidity, medium to full body":"不甜，高單寧，高酸度，酒體中等至飽滿","Blackcurrant, black cherry, green pepper, mint; oak: cedar, vanilla":"黑醋栗、黑櫻桃、青椒、薄荷；橡木：雪松、香草","Bordeaux: blended with Merlot (softness and body)":"波爾多：與梅洛混釀（柔順感和酒體）","Also California, Australia (sometimes with Shiraz), Chile, South Africa":"還有加州、澳洲（有時與希拉茲混釀）、智利、南非","Merlot makes wines that are generally dry and medium- to full-bodied, with medium acidity and medium tannin. That makes it softer and rounder than Cabernet Sauvignon. Its fruit ranges from red fruit such as strawberry and red plum to black fruit such as blackberry and black plum.":"梅洛（Merlot）釀出的葡萄酒通常不甜，酒體中等至飽滿，酸度中等、單寧中等，因此比卡本內蘇維濃更柔和圓潤。它的果香從草莓、紅李等紅色水果，到黑莓、黑李等黑色水果都有。","Merlot is often matured in oak, which adds vanilla notes to the fruit. Chile and California use it to make soft, fruity, easy-drinking wines: on a wine list, a Chilean Merlot might be described as «smooth, with black plum and blackberry». It is one of the most approachable reds for beginners.":"梅洛常在橡木桶中熟成，為果香增添香草氣息。智利和加州用它釀造柔順、果味豐富、易飲的葡萄酒：在酒單上，一款智利梅洛可能被形容為「柔順，帶有黑李和黑莓」。它是最適合初學者入門的紅酒之一。","Merlot is Cabernet Sauvignon's classic partner. In a blend the two complete each other: Merlot brings softness and body, while Cabernet Sauvignon adds tannin and acidity. Bordeaux is the most famous region for this blend; in some parts of Bordeaux, such as Saint-Émilion, Merlot is often the main grape. The blend is now common in many other countries.":"梅洛是卡本內蘇維濃的經典搭檔。在混釀中兩者相輔相成：梅洛帶來柔順感和酒體，卡本內蘇維濃則增添單寧和酸度。波爾多是這種混釀最著名的產區；在波爾多的某些地區，例如 Saint-Émilion，梅洛往往是主要品種。這種混釀如今在許多其他國家也很常見。","Dry, medium to full body, medium acidity and tannin":"不甜，酒體中等至飽滿，酸度和單寧中等","From strawberry and red plum to blackberry and black plum; oak: vanilla":"從草莓、紅李到黑莓、黑李；橡木：香草","Chile and California: soft, fruity wines":"智利和加州：柔順、果味豐富的葡萄酒","Bordeaux: blend with Cabernet Sauvignon (which adds tannin and acidity)":"波爾多：與卡本內蘇維濃混釀（後者增添單寧和酸度）","Pinot Noir makes reds that are usually dry and light- to medium-bodied, with high acidity and low to medium tannin. It is an elegant, delicate red, very different from Cabernet Sauvignon. Its aromas are of red fruit: strawberry, red cherry and raspberry. It is often matured in oak, which adds notes of vanilla and smoke.":"黑皮諾（Pinot Noir）釀出的紅酒通常不甜，酒體輕盈至中等，酸度高，單寧低至中等。它是優雅細緻的紅酒，和卡本內蘇維濃大不相同。它的香氣是紅色水果：草莓、紅櫻桃和覆盆子。它常在橡木桶中熟成，增添香草和煙燻氣息。","Pinot Noir is the grape of red Burgundy (Bourgogne) in France: dry, light to medium-bodied, very fresh wines with raspberry and red cherry, and sometimes vanilla and smoke from oak. It is also the main black grape of New Zealand, for example in the Central Otago region.":"黑皮諾是法國布根地（Bourgogne）紅酒的品種：不甜、酒體輕盈至中等、非常清爽的葡萄酒，帶有覆盆子和紅櫻桃，有時還有來自橡木桶的香草和煙燻氣息。它也是紐西蘭最主要的黑葡萄品種，例如在中奧塔哥（Central Otago）產區。","Unlike Cabernet Sauvignon and Merlot, Pinot Noir is not usually blended with other grapes when making red wine; producers prefer to show its pure character. There is one important exception: in Champagne, Pinot Noir is often blended with Chardonnay. There the skins are removed straight away, so the juice stays pale.":"和卡本內蘇維濃、梅洛不同，黑皮諾釀造紅酒時通常不與其他品種混釀；生產者偏好展現它純粹的特質。有一個重要的例外：在 Champagne 中，黑皮諾常與夏多內混釀。那裡會立刻去除果皮，所以果汁維持淺色。","Dry, light to medium body, high acidity, low to medium tannin":"不甜，酒體輕盈至中等，高酸度，單寧低至中等","Strawberry, red cherry, raspberry; oak: vanilla, smoke":"草莓、紅櫻桃、覆盆子；橡木：香草、煙燻","Red Burgundy; New Zealand's main black grape":"布根地紅酒；紐西蘭最主要的黑葡萄品種","Not usually blended for reds; in Champagne with Chardonnay":"釀紅酒時通常不混釀；在 Champagne 中與夏多內搭配","This is one grape with two names: it is called Syrah in France and Shiraz in Australia, so the name on the label also hints at the origin and often the style. It makes dry wines with medium to full body, medium to high tannin and medium acidity. Typical flavours are black fruit (blackberry, black cherry) and spice (black pepper, liquorice).":"這是一個有兩個名字的品種：在法國叫希哈（Syrah），在澳洲叫希拉茲（Shiraz），所以酒標上的名字也暗示了產地，往往還有風格。它釀出不甜的葡萄酒，酒體中等至飽滿，單寧中等至高，酸度中等。典型風味是黑色水果（黑莓、黑櫻桃）和香料（黑胡椒、甘草）。","Many Syrahs and Shirazes are matured in oak, which adds vanilla or coconut notes. Alongside the black fruit and spice, these oak aromas make the wine richer. For anyone studying, the pairing «black fruit + black pepper» is an excellent clue for recognising this grape.":"許多希哈和希拉茲都在橡木桶中熟成，增添香草或椰子氣息。加上黑色水果和香料，這些橡木香氣讓酒更豐富。對備考的人來說，「黑色水果 + 黑胡椒」這個組合是辨認這個品種的絕佳線索。","Climate changes the style a great deal. In France's Northern Rhône, Syrah can make medium-bodied wines with fresh blackberry and black pepper. In warm parts of Australia, such as the Barossa Valley, the grapes ripen further, and Shiraz becomes full-bodied, with jammy black cherry and liquorice.":"氣候對風格的影響很大。在法國北隆河，希哈可以釀出酒體中等的葡萄酒，帶有新鮮黑莓和黑胡椒風味。在澳洲的溫暖地區，例如巴羅莎谷（Barossa Valley），葡萄更成熟，希拉茲變得酒體飽滿，帶有果醬般的黑櫻桃和甘草風味。","Australian Shiraz is also blended with Cabernet Sauvignon, and in that blend it contributes spicy aromas. To sum up: France and the Northern Rhône = fresher, peppery Syrah; warm Australia = full, ripe Shiraz. Same grape, two climates, two different styles.":"澳洲希拉茲也會與卡本內蘇維濃混釀，在混釀中貢獻香料氣息。總結一下：法國與北隆河 = 較清爽、帶胡椒味的希哈；溫暖的澳洲 = 飽滿、成熟的希拉茲。同一個品種，兩種氣候，兩種不同的風格。","Syrah in France, Shiraz in Australia: the same grape":"法國叫希哈（Syrah），澳洲叫希拉茲（Shiraz）：同一個品種","Dry, medium to full body, medium to high tannin, medium acidity":"不甜，酒體中等至飽滿，單寧中等至高，酸度中等","Blackberry, black cherry, black pepper, liquorice; oak: vanilla, coconut":"黑莓、黑櫻桃、黑胡椒、甘草；橡木：香草、椰子","Northern Rhône: medium, peppery; warm Australia: full, jammy, liquorice":"北隆河：酒體中等、帶胡椒味；溫暖的澳洲：飽滿、果醬感、甘草","Sancerre and Chablis: two dry French whites":"Sancerre 與 Chablis：兩款不甜的法國白酒","In Europe many wines are named after the place they come from, not the grape. That is why a Sancerre or Chablis label usually does not mention the grape variety: it is up to the drinker to know what is inside. Learning these few famous wines lets you read a great many wine lists with confidence.":"在歐洲，許多葡萄酒以產地命名，而不是品種。所以 Sancerre 或 Chablis 的酒標通常不會提到葡萄品種：瓶中是什麼，得靠喝的人自己知道。學會這幾款名酒，就能自信地讀懂許多酒單。","Sancerre is a white wine from France's Loire Valley, made from Sauvignon Blanc. It is dry and medium-bodied, with high acidity and pronounced aromas of green fruit (apple) and herbaceous notes (grass). It is usually unoaked, so the grape's aromas stay crisp and clear. A wine list might describe it with «citrus and grass on the nose».":"Sancerre 是法國羅亞爾河谷的白酒，以白蘇維濃釀造。它不甜、酒體中等，酸度高，有明顯的綠色水果（蘋果）香氣和草本氣息（青草）。它通常不經橡木桶，所以品種香氣清脆鮮明。酒單上可能會用「香氣帶有柑橘和青草」來形容它。","Chablis is a white Burgundy made from Chardonnay. It comes from the coolest part of the region, where grapes ripen less and keep their acidity. The result is a dry, light to medium-bodied wine with high acidity and aromas of green apple and lemon. It is unoaked, so there is no vanilla: just fresh fruit and plenty of freshness.":"Chablis 是以夏多內釀造的布根地白酒。它來自產區最涼爽的地帶，葡萄成熟度較低，保留了酸度。成果是不甜、酒體輕盈至中等的葡萄酒，酸度高，帶有青蘋果和檸檬香氣。它不經橡木桶，所以沒有香草味：只有新鮮果香和滿滿的清爽感。","Sancerre and Chablis have a lot in common: both dry, fresh and unoaked, with green apple. To tell them apart, look for the «extra» notes: Sancerre has more pronounced aromas and herbaceous notes like cut grass, typical of Sauvignon Blanc, while Chablis is more restrained, with apple and lemon and a body that can be lighter.":"Sancerre 和 Chablis 有許多共同點：都不甜、清爽、不經橡木桶，帶有青蘋果。要分辨兩者，就找「額外」的氣息：Sancerre 香氣更濃郁，並有白蘇維濃典型的草本氣息，例如剛割過的青草；Chablis 則較內斂，帶有蘋果和檸檬，酒體可能更輕盈。","Many European wines are named after the place, not the grape":"許多歐洲葡萄酒以產地命名，而不是品種","Sancerre: Loire, Sauvignon Blanc, dry, medium body, apple and grass, unoaked":"Sancerre：羅亞爾河，白蘇維濃，不甜，酒體中等，蘋果和青草，不經橡木桶","Chablis: coolest Burgundy, Chardonnay, light-medium, apple and lemon, unoaked":"Chablis：布根地最涼爽的地區，夏多內，輕盈至中等，蘋果和檸檬，不經橡木桶","Both: high acidity":"兩者：酸度都高","Burgundy (Bourgogne): white and red":"布根地（Bourgogne）：白酒與紅酒","Burgundy is a French region that makes both white and red wines. The French name, «Bourgogne», often appears on labels of both colours. Some labels show the name of a village in the region instead, such as Meursault, Puligny-Montrachet or Volnay. The rule is simple: the whites are Chardonnay and the reds are Pinot Noir.":"布根地是同時出產白酒和紅酒的法國產區。它的法文名稱「Bourgogne」常出現在兩種顏色的酒標上。有些酒標則標示產區內的村莊名稱，例如 Meursault、Puligny-Montrachet 或 Volnay。規則很簡單：白酒是夏多內，紅酒是黑皮諾。","White Burgundies are dry and medium-bodied, with high acidity. They can be oaked or unoaked. Compared with Chablis, which comes from the coolest area, they often show riper fruit: citrus such as lemon, but also stone fruit such as peach. When they have been aged in oak, they add vanilla notes.":"布根地白酒不甜、酒體中等，酸度高，可以經橡木桶，也可以不經。與來自最涼爽地區的 Chablis 相比，它們常呈現更成熟的果香：有檸檬等柑橘類水果，也有桃子等核果。經橡木桶陳年的，還會多一份香草氣息。","Red Burgundies are dry, light to medium-bodied, with high acidity and low to medium tannin. They smell of red fruit such as raspberry and red cherry and sometimes of vanilla and smoke from oak. They are elegant, fresh reds: the opposite of powerful, tannic reds such as Bordeaux.":"布根地紅酒不甜，酒體輕盈至中等，酸度高，單寧低至中等。它們有覆盆子和紅櫻桃等紅色水果香氣，有時還有來自橡木桶的香草和煙燻氣息。這是優雅清爽的紅酒：和波爾多那種強勁、單寧高的紅酒正好相反。","«Bourgogne» = Burgundy in French, on whites and reds":"「Bourgogne」= 布根地的法文，白酒和紅酒都使用","White: Chardonnay, dry, medium body, lemon and peach, oaked or unoaked":"白酒：夏多內，不甜，酒體中等，檸檬和桃子，可經或不經橡木桶","Red: Pinot Noir, light-medium, high acidity, raspberry and red cherry":"紅酒：黑皮諾，輕盈至中等，高酸度，覆盆子和紅櫻桃","Riper fruit than Chablis":"果香比 Chablis 更成熟","Bordeaux is a French region famous above all for its red wines. Red Bordeaux is usually a blend of Cabernet Sauvignon and Merlot. The two grapes complete each other: Cabernet Sauvignon brings tannin and acidity, Merlot brings softness and body. The label shows the region or one of its areas, not the grapes.":"波爾多是法國產區，最著名的是紅酒。波爾多紅酒通常是卡本內蘇維濃與梅洛的混釀。兩個品種相輔相成：卡本內蘇維濃帶來單寧和酸度，梅洛帶來柔順感和酒體。酒標標示的是產區或其中的某個地區，而不是品種。","The style of red Bordeaux is dry, medium to full-bodied, with high acidity and high tannin. The aromas are of black fruit such as blackberry and blackcurrant, with cedar notes from oak. It is one of the classic examples of a high-tannin red: you clearly feel the drying sensation in your mouth.":"波爾多紅酒的風格是不甜、酒體中等至飽滿，酸度高、單寧高。香氣是黑莓和黑醋栗等黑色水果，並有來自橡木桶的雪松氣息。它是高單寧紅酒的經典例子之一：口腔的乾澀感非常明顯。","On a wine list, a Bordeaux may appear under the name of an area within the region. A Saint-Émilion, for example, might be described as «a Merlot-dominant blend with blackberry and cedar», and a Margaux as «high tannin, concentrated blackcurrant and cedar». Remember too that Bordeaux makes a famous sweet white, Sauternes.":"在酒單上，波爾多可能以產區內某個地區的名稱出現。例如 Saint-Émilion 可能被形容為「以梅洛為主的混釀，帶有黑莓和雪松」，Margaux 則是「高單寧，濃縮的黑醋栗和雪松」。也別忘了波爾多出產著名的甜白酒 Sauternes。","Mostly red: a blend of Cabernet Sauvignon and Merlot":"以紅酒為主：卡本內蘇維濃與梅洛的混釀","Dry, medium to full body, high acidity and tannin":"不甜，酒體中等至飽滿，酸度和單寧高","Blackberry, blackcurrant, cedar from oak":"黑莓、黑醋栗、來自橡木桶的雪松","Areas on labels: e.g. Saint-Émilion, Margaux":"酒標上的地區名：例如 Saint-Émilion、Margaux","Champagne is the world's most famous sparkling wine, and it comes from France. It is made from Chardonnay and Pinot Noir, often blended together. Pinot Noir is a black grape, but because its juice is colourless, removing the skins straight away gives a pale wine. The bubbles come from fermentation carbon dioxide that is kept in the wine.":"Champagne 是全世界最著名的氣泡酒，來自法國。它以夏多內和黑皮諾釀造，兩者常常混釀。黑皮諾是黑葡萄，但果汁無色，只要立刻去除果皮就能得到淺色的酒。氣泡來自發酵產生、被保留在酒中的二氧化碳。","Champagne's typical style is dry, with high acidity and aromas of green fruit (apple) and citrus (lemon). On top of that come notes of toasted bread, which set it apart from simpler, fruitier sparkling wines. A wine list might read: «dry sparkling, apple and lemon, high acidity», at around 12.5% abv.":"Champagne 的典型風格是不甜、酸度高，帶有綠色水果（蘋果）和柑橘類水果（檸檬）的香氣。此外還有烤麵包氣息，讓它有別於較簡單、果味較重的氣泡酒。酒單上可能寫著：「不甜氣泡酒，蘋果和檸檬，高酸度」，酒精濃度約 12.5% abv。","Champagne is also the reference point for serving sparkling wine: it should be served well chilled, around 6–10 °C, and the bottle opened with care, always keeping a hand on the cork because of the pressure inside. Champagne therefore links two topics: the key grapes and wine service.":"Champagne 也是氣泡酒侍酒的參考標準：應該充分冰鎮，大約 6–10 °C，開瓶時要小心，因為瓶內有壓力，手要一直按住軟木塞。所以 Champagne 連結了兩個主題：主要品種和侍酒。","French sparkling wine, the best known":"法國氣泡酒，最廣為人知","Serve well chilled (6–10 °C)":"充分冰鎮後侍酒（6–10 °C）","A sweet white and a rosé: Sauternes and White Zinfandel":"一款甜白酒和一款粉紅酒：Sauternes 與 White Zinfandel","The wines in this chapter are not made from the four key white and four key black grapes, but they are so well known that they are worth learning. For each one, just remember the essentials: where it comes from, what type of wine it is (still, sparkling or fortified), its colour and its key style traits. Let us start with two very different wines.":"這一章的葡萄酒不是以四大白葡萄和四大黑葡萄品種釀造，但因為太有名，很值得認識。每一款只要記住重點：來自哪裡、屬於哪一種類型（靜態酒、氣泡酒或加烈酒）、顏色，以及主要的風格特徵。先從兩款截然不同的酒開始。","Sauternes is a sweet white wine made in Bordeaux. It is full-bodied, with flavours of stone fruit (apricot), honey and vanilla from oak. Its high acidity is vital: it balances the sugar and stops the wine from tasting cloying. One way to make sweet wines like this is to use grapes so rich in sugar that the yeast stop before they have eaten it all.":"Sauternes 是波爾多出產的甜白酒。它酒體飽滿，帶有核果（杏桃）、蜂蜜和來自橡木桶的香草風味。高酸度至關重要：它平衡了糖分，讓酒不會膩口。釀造這類甜酒的方法之一，是使用糖分極高的葡萄，讓酵母還沒把糖吃完就停止。","White Zinfandel, despite its name, is a rosé from California. It is unoaked, low in alcohol and medium-sweet, with fresh red fruit flavours such as strawberry and raspberry. It is the classic example both of a low-alcohol wine and of a rosé with some sweetness: on a list you might see it at around 10.5% abv.":"White Zinfandel 雖然名字裡有 White，卻是加州的粉紅酒。它不經橡木桶，酒精濃度低，半甜，帶有草莓和覆盆子等新鮮紅色水果風味。它既是低酒精濃度葡萄酒的經典例子，也是帶有甜味的粉紅酒的經典例子：在酒單上你可能看到它標示約 10.5% abv。","Sauternes: sweet white from Bordeaux, full-bodied":"Sauternes：波爾多甜白酒，酒體飽滿","Sauternes: apricot, honey, vanilla, balancing high acidity":"Sauternes：杏桃、蜂蜜、香草，高酸度帶來平衡","White Zinfandel: Californian rosé, medium-sweet, low alcohol":"White Zinfandel：加州粉紅酒，半甜，酒精濃度低","White Zinfandel: strawberry and raspberry, unoaked":"White Zinfandel：草莓和覆盆子，不經橡木桶","Three French reds: Beaujolais, Côtes du Rhône, Châteauneuf-du-Pape":"三款法國紅酒：Beaujolais、Côtes du Rhône、Châteauneuf-du-Pape","The easiest way to remember these three reds is to line them up by body, from lightest to fullest. Beaujolais is light, Côtes du Rhône is medium and Châteauneuf-du-Pape is full. All three are French and dry, but each has a very different character.":"要記住這三款紅酒，最簡單的方法是依酒體排列，從最輕盈到最飽滿。Beaujolais 輕盈，Côtes du Rhône 中等，Châteauneuf-du-Pape 飽滿。三款都是不甜的法國紅酒，但個性大不相同。","Beaujolais is a dry, light-bodied, unoaked red with fresh red fruit flavours such as raspberry and red cherry and low tannin. It is the standard example of a light, low-tannin red. Precisely because it is light, it can be served lightly chilled, at around 13 °C.":"Beaujolais 是不甜、酒體輕盈、不經橡木桶的紅酒，帶有覆盆子和紅櫻桃等新鮮紅色水果風味，單寧低。它是輕盈、低單寧紅酒的標準例子。正因為輕盈，可以稍微冰鎮到大約 13 °C 侍酒。","Côtes du Rhône is a dry, medium-bodied red with red fruit such as strawberry and red plum and a spicy note of white pepper. It can be oaked or unoaked. Châteauneuf-du-Pape, also from the Rhône area, is dry, full-bodied and high in alcohol, with strawberry and cloves from oak.":"Côtes du Rhône 是不甜、酒體中等的紅酒，帶有草莓和紅李等紅色水果，以及白胡椒的香料氣息。它可以經橡木桶，也可以不經。同樣來自隆河地區的 Châteauneuf-du-Pape 則不甜、酒體飽滿、酒精濃度高，帶有草莓和來自橡木桶的丁香風味。","Beaujolais: light, unoaked, raspberry and red cherry, low tannin":"Beaujolais：輕盈，不經橡木桶，覆盆子和紅櫻桃，低單寧","Côtes du Rhône: medium, strawberry, red plum, white pepper; oaked or not":"Côtes du Rhône：中等，草莓、紅李、白胡椒；可經或不經橡木桶","Châteauneuf-du-Pape: full, high alcohol, strawberry and clove":"Châteauneuf-du-Pape：飽滿，酒精濃度高，草莓和丁香","Chianti and Rioja":"Chianti 與 Rioja","Chianti is a dry, medium-bodied Italian red. It has high tannin and high acidity, so it feels both drying and very fresh. The flavours are of red fruit such as red cherry and red plum, with dried herb notes and sometimes cloves from oak. It comes from Tuscany; on a list you might find a Chianti Classico, for example.":"Chianti 是不甜、酒體中等的義大利紅酒。它單寧高、酸度高，所以既讓口腔乾澀，又非常清爽。風味是紅櫻桃和紅李等紅色水果，帶有乾燥香草氣息，有時還有來自橡木桶的丁香。它來自托斯卡尼；在酒單上你可能看到 Chianti Classico。","Rioja is a dry Spanish red with a medium to full body. It typically shows red fruit, especially strawberry, and vanilla from oak. That «strawberry + vanilla» combination is its signature. On a wine list you may see Rioja Crianza, described for example as «strawberry fruit with notes of vanilla».":"Rioja 是不甜的西班牙紅酒，酒體中等至飽滿。它通常呈現紅色水果，尤其是草莓，以及來自橡木桶的香草。「草莓 + 香草」這個組合就是它的招牌。在酒單上你可能看到 Rioja Crianza，例如被形容為「草莓果香，帶有香草氣息」。","To tell them apart: both show red fruit, but Chianti is built on high tannin and acidity with dried herbs, while Rioja is rounder and marked by vanilla from oak. Remember the countries too: Chianti = Italy, Rioja = Spain. Both are classic examples of wines named after the region where they are made.":"分辨兩者的方法：都有紅色水果，但 Chianti 以高單寧、高酸度和乾燥香草為骨幹，Rioja 則較圓潤，並帶有橡木桶的香草印記。也要記住國家：Chianti = 義大利，Rioja = 西班牙。兩者都是以產區命名的經典例子。","Chianti: Italy, dry, medium body, high tannin and acidity":"Chianti：義大利，不甜，酒體中等，單寧和酸度高","Chianti: red cherry and plum, dried herbs, sometimes cloves":"Chianti：紅櫻桃和紅李，乾燥香草，有時有丁香","Rioja: Spain, dry, medium to full body":"Rioja：西班牙，不甜，酒體中等至飽滿","Rioja: strawberry and vanilla from oak":"Rioja：草莓和來自橡木桶的香草","Two sparkling wines: Prosecco and Cava":"兩款氣泡酒：Prosecco 與 Cava","Alongside Champagne, two very well-known sparkling wines are Prosecco and Cava. Like all sparkling wines, they owe their bubbles to carbon dioxide produced by fermentation and kept trapped in the wine. To tell them apart, remember the country, sweetness and typical fruit of each.":"除了 Champagne，Prosecco 和 Cava 也是兩款非常有名的氣泡酒。和所有氣泡酒一樣，它們的氣泡來自發酵產生、被保留在酒中的二氧化碳。要分辨它們，就記住各自的國家、甜度和典型的水果。","Prosecco is a light-bodied Italian sparkling wine with green fruit (pear) and floral aromas. It can be dry or medium-sweet: a list might describe it as «light-bodied, medium sweetness, pear aromas», at around 12% abv. It is a fresh, fruity sparkling wine without Champagne's toasted bread notes.":"Prosecco 是酒體輕盈的義大利氣泡酒，帶有綠色水果（梨子）和花香。它可以不甜或半甜：酒單上可能形容為「酒體輕盈，半甜，梨子香氣」，酒精濃度約 12% abv。這是一款清爽、果味豐富的氣泡酒，沒有 Champagne 的烤麵包氣息。","Cava is a dry sparkling wine from Spain with green fruit (apple) and citrus (lemon) flavours. To sum up: Prosecco = Italy, pear and flowers, dry or medium; Cava = Spain, apple and lemon, dry; Champagne = France, apple, lemon and toasted bread, dry.":"Cava 是西班牙的不甜氣泡酒，帶有綠色水果（蘋果）和柑橘類水果（檸檬）風味。總結一下：Prosecco = 義大利，梨子和花香，不甜或半甜；Cava = 西班牙，蘋果和檸檬，不甜；Champagne = 法國，蘋果、檸檬和烤麵包，不甜。","Prosecco: Italy, light-bodied, pear and floral":"Prosecco：義大利，酒體輕盈，梨子和花香","Prosecco: dry or medium-sweet":"Prosecco：不甜或半甜","Cava: Spain, dry, apple and lemon":"Cava：西班牙，不甜，蘋果和檸檬","Two fortified wines: Sherry and Port":"兩款加烈酒：Sherry 與 Port","Sherry and Port are the two fortified wines to know. Fortified means that alcohol has been added to the wine, which is why they are stronger than still wines, at 15% to 22% abv. If the alcohol is added before the yeast have eaten all the sugar, the yeast die and the wine stays sweet.":"Sherry 和 Port 是必須認識的兩款加烈酒。加烈的意思是在酒中添加了酒精，所以它們比靜態酒更烈，酒精濃度為 15% 至 22% abv。如果在酵母吃完所有的糖之前加入酒精，酵母會死亡，酒就保有甜味。","Sherry is a white fortified wine from Spain. It is made in a range of styles and can be dry, medium or sweet. So, as with Riesling, the name alone does not tell you how sweet it will be: you need to check the style. Above all, remember: Sherry = Spain, fortified, white, dry to sweet.":"Sherry 是西班牙的白色加烈酒。它有多種風格，可以不甜、半甜或甜。所以和麗絲玲一樣，光看名稱無法知道它有多甜：必須查看風格。最重要的是記住：Sherry = 西班牙、加烈酒、白色、從不甜到甜。","Port is a fortified wine from Portugal. It is sweet and high in alcohol, and it too comes in a range of styles. It is usually red and full-bodied, with high tannin and black fruit flavours such as blackberry. A wine list might describe it as «sweet, full-bodied, intense blackberry and high tannins», at around 20% abv.":"Port 是葡萄牙的加烈酒。它甜而酒精濃度高，同樣有多種風格。它通常是紅色、酒體飽滿，單寧高，帶有黑莓等黑色水果風味。酒單上可能形容為「甜，酒體飽滿，濃郁的黑莓和高單寧」，酒精濃度約 20% abv。","Fortified = alcohol added, 15–22% abv":"加烈 = 添加酒精，15–22% abv","Sherry: Spain, white, dry, medium or sweet":"Sherry：西班牙，白色，不甜、半甜或甜","Port: Portugal, sweet, high alcohol, usually red":"Port：葡萄牙，甜，酒精濃度高，通常是紅色","Port: full body, high tannin, blackberry":"Port：酒體飽滿，高單寧，黑莓","A wine that is stored badly loses quality. At first it may simply lose some of its character; over time it can end up developing real faults. Three simple rules are enough to prevent this, covering temperature, light and the position of the bottle. They apply at home just as much as in a restaurant or a wine shop.":"保存不當的葡萄酒，品質會下降。一開始可能只是失去一些特色；時間久了，可能產生真正的缺陷。三條簡單的規則就足以避免，分別關於溫度、光線和酒瓶的擺放方式。在家裡、餐廳或酒專都同樣適用。","Rule one: for long-term storage, keep wine somewhere cool at a steady temperature. Extreme cold or heat, as well as big swings in temperature, can damage it. Rule two: keep bottles away from strong sunshine and bright artificial light. Light, and the heat that comes with it, can make a wine lose its fruity character.":"規則一：長期保存時，把葡萄酒放在涼爽、恆溫的地方。過冷、過熱以及劇烈的溫度變化都可能損害它。規則二：讓酒瓶遠離強烈的陽光和明亮的人工光線。光線和隨之而來的熱，可能讓葡萄酒失去果味。","Rule three: bottles closed with a cork should be stored on their side. This keeps the cork in contact with the wine so that it stays moist. If the cork dries out, it can let air into the bottle and the wine loses its fruitiness. Bottles with a screwcap do not have this problem and can be stored standing up.":"規則三：用軟木塞封瓶的酒應該橫放保存。這樣軟木塞能與酒液接觸，保持濕潤。如果軟木塞乾掉，可能讓空氣進入瓶中，酒就會失去果味。旋蓋酒瓶沒有這個問題，可以直立保存。","Poor storage makes wine lose character and can cause faults.":"保存不當會讓葡萄酒失去特色，並可能產生缺陷。","Cool, constant temperature; no extremes or big swings.":"涼爽、恆溫；避免極端溫度和劇烈變化。","Away from sunshine and bright artificial light.":"遠離陽光和明亮的人工光線。","Cork: store on its side. Screwcap: can stand up.":"軟木塞：橫放保存。旋蓋：可以直立。","Keeping opened wine fresh":"讓已開瓶的葡萄酒保鮮","Once a bottle is opened, the wine comes into contact with air and slowly starts to lose its freshness, eventually tasting stale. The first fix is simple: put the cork back in and keep the bottle in the fridge. The cold slows things down and helps the wine stay fresh for longer.":"酒瓶一打開，葡萄酒就接觸到空氣，慢慢開始失去新鮮感，最後會走味。第一個對策很簡單：把軟木塞塞回去，並把酒瓶放進冰箱。低溫會減緩變化，幫助葡萄酒保鮮更久。","To keep a wine going for even longer, there are systems designed to keep it away from air. Vacuum systems use a small pump to draw the air out of the bottle. Blanket systems pump a gas into the bottle that pushes the air out and sits over the wine without harming it. Both share the same goal: limiting contact with air.":"想讓葡萄酒保存得更久，有專門隔絕空氣的系統。真空系統用小幫浦把瓶中的空氣抽出。氣體覆蓋系統則把氣體灌入瓶中，將空氣排出，並覆蓋在酒液上方而不傷害酒。兩者的目標相同：減少與空氣的接觸。","The reasoning to remember is always the same: air is the enemy of opened wine, and it is also air that spoils wine when a cork dries out in storage. The fridge, a vacuum pump and an inert gas are three different ways to slow this down so that the wine is still enjoyable the next day.":"要記住的道理始終如一：空氣是已開瓶葡萄酒的敵人；保存時軟木塞乾掉，讓酒變質的也是空氣。冰箱、真空幫浦和惰性氣體是三種減緩這個過程的方法，讓酒到了隔天依然好喝。","Opened wine goes stale as it reacts with air.":"已開瓶的葡萄酒會與空氣發生反應而走味。","Cork back in and fridge keep it fresher for longer.":"塞回軟木塞並放進冰箱，能保鮮更久。","Vacuum system: a pump removes the air.":"真空系統：用幫浦抽出空氣。","Blanket system: a harmless gas pushes the air out.":"氣體覆蓋系統：用無害的氣體把空氣排出。","Temperature makes a big difference to how we experience a wine. In general, whites, rosés and sparkling wines are served chilled, while reds are served at room temperature or lightly chilled. These are guidelines, not laws: if a guest prefers a wine at a different temperature, the host should respect that preference.":"溫度對我們品嚐葡萄酒的感受影響很大。一般而言，白酒、粉紅酒和氣泡酒要冰鎮後侍酒，紅酒則在室溫或稍微冰鎮後侍酒。這些是指引，不是定律：如果客人偏好不同的溫度，主人應該尊重這份喜好。","The coldest wines are sweet wines such as Sauternes, served well chilled at 6–8°C (43–45°F), and sparkling wines such as Champagne, well chilled at 6–10°C (43–50°F). Light- and medium-bodied whites and rosés, such as Pinot Grigio, are served chilled at 7–10°C (45–50°F). Full-bodied whites, such as an oaked Chardonnay, are served lightly chilled at 10–13°C (50–55°F).":"侍酒溫度最低的是甜酒和氣泡酒：Sauternes 等甜酒要充分冰鎮至 6–8°C（43–45°F），Champagne 等氣泡酒要充分冰鎮至 6–10°C（43–50°F）。灰皮諾等酒體輕盈和中等的白酒與粉紅酒，要冰鎮至 7–10°C（45–50°F）。經橡木桶的夏多內等酒體飽滿的白酒，則稍微冰鎮至 10–13°C（50–55°F）。","Among reds, light ones such as Beaujolais are served lightly chilled, at around 13°C (55°F). Medium- and full-bodied reds, such as Shiraz, are served at room temperature, 15–18°C (59–64°F). Because central heating and air conditioning make 'room temperature' very variable, the range of degrees is a better guide than the room itself.":"紅酒當中，Beaujolais 等輕盈的紅酒要稍微冰鎮，大約 13°C（55°F）。希拉茲等酒體中等和飽滿的紅酒則在室溫 15–18°C（59–64°F）侍酒。由於暖氣和冷氣讓「室溫」變化很大，以溫度範圍為準比依賴房間本身更可靠。","To keep wine cool until the bottle is finished, you can use an insulated container or an ice bucket. If you use a bucket, fill it with ice and cold water: ice alone cools far less efficiently. On the other hand, a red that is too cold should never be warmed next to a radiator, because heat damages its flavours; instead, leave it in the room where it will be served and let it warm up naturally.":"想讓葡萄酒在喝完之前都保持低溫，可以使用保冷容器或冰桶。如果用冰桶，要裝入冰塊和冷水：只用冰塊的冷卻效率差得多。另一方面，太冰的紅酒絕不能放在暖氣旁加溫，因為熱會破壞風味；應該把它放在要飲用的房間，讓它自然回溫。","Sweet and sparkling: well chilled (6–8°C / 6–10°C).":"甜酒和氣泡酒：充分冰鎮（6–8°C / 6–10°C）。","Light/medium whites and rosés: chilled, 7–10°C.":"酒體輕盈／中等的白酒與粉紅酒：冰鎮，7–10°C。","Full whites: lightly chilled, 10–13°C; light reds: lightly chilled, 13°C.":"酒體飽滿的白酒：稍微冰鎮，10–13°C；輕盈的紅酒：稍微冰鎮，13°C。","Medium/full reds: room temperature, 15–18°C.":"酒體中等／飽滿的紅酒：室溫，15–18°C。","Ice bucket with ice and water; never heat wine by a radiator.":"冰桶裝冰塊和水；絕不要在暖氣旁加熱葡萄酒。","Opening a bottle":"開瓶","For a still wine sealed with a cork, the method is as follows. First remove the top of the capsule, using a foil cutter or the blade of a waiter's friend corkscrew, and wipe the neck of the bottle with a cloth. Then centre the corkscrew in the middle of the cork, screw it in and draw the cork out gently. Finally, wipe the neck again, both inside and outside.":"軟木塞封瓶的靜態酒，開瓶方法如下。先用割箔刀或侍者開瓶器上的小刀除去瓶口封套的頂部，並用布擦拭瓶口。接著把開瓶器對準軟木塞中心旋入，輕輕拔出軟木塞。最後再擦一次瓶口，內外都要擦。","Sparkling wine needs more care, because there is a lot of pressure inside the bottle. Chilling reduces it, but even when the wine is cold the cork can shoot out and injure someone. The golden rule: from the moment the wire cage is loosened, the cork must stay under your hand until it is completely out of the bottle.":"氣泡酒需要更小心，因為瓶內壓力很大。冰鎮可以降低壓力，但即使酒是冰的，軟木塞仍可能彈出傷人。黃金法則：從鬆開鐵絲罩的那一刻起，手必須一直按住軟木塞，直到它完全離開酒瓶。","The steps are: remove the foil and loosen the cage while keeping the cork covered with your hand. Tilt the bottle at an angle, hold the cork in one hand and the base in the other, and turn the bottle, not the cork. Holding the cork firmly lets the pressure escape slowly, with a quiet sigh and no wine lost.":"步驟如下：除去錫箔，一邊用手蓋住軟木塞，一邊鬆開鐵絲罩。把酒瓶傾斜，一手握住軟木塞，一手握住瓶底，轉動酒瓶，而不是軟木塞。穩穩握住軟木塞，讓壓力慢慢釋放，只發出一聲輕嘆，一滴酒都不浪費。","Still wine: remove capsule top, wipe, ease the cork out, wipe the neck.":"靜態酒：除去封套頂部、擦拭、輕輕拔出軟木塞、擦拭瓶口。","Sparkling: high pressure; the cork can injure.":"氣泡酒：壓力大；軟木塞可能傷人。","Once the cage is loosened, keep a hand on the cork.":"鐵絲罩一鬆開，手就要按住軟木塞。","Bottle at an angle; turn the bottle, not the cork.":"酒瓶傾斜；轉動酒瓶，不是軟木塞。","Glasses and checks before serving":"酒杯與侍酒前的檢查","There are hundreds of glass shapes, but the best ones share one feature: the bowl narrows towards the rim. This shape holds and concentrates the aromas inside the glass, so they can be appreciated better. Red wine glasses are usually slightly larger than white wine glasses, and sparkling wines are served in flutes.":"酒杯的形狀有數百種，但最好的都有一個共同點：杯身向杯口收窄。這種形狀能把香氣留住並集中在杯內，更容易欣賞。紅酒杯通常比白酒杯稍大，氣泡酒則用笛型杯。","The glass must be perfectly clean. Dirt or traces of detergent can spoil a wine by changing its aromas and flavours. That is why glasses should always be polished before use, to remove any lingering dirt or finger marks. It is a simple habit that makes a real difference to what ends up in the glass.":"酒杯必須徹底乾淨。髒汙或殘留的清潔劑會改變香氣和風味，破壞葡萄酒。所以使用前一定要把酒杯擦亮，去除殘留的髒汙或指紋。這個簡單的習慣，對杯中的酒影響很大。","Before serving, it is good practice to check the wine. Look at its appearance: haziness can point to a fault, and there should be no bits floating in it. Then smell it: the wine should not smell stale or have aromas of wet cardboard or vinegar. If something seems wrong, it is better not to serve it.":"侍酒前最好先檢查葡萄酒。看外觀：混濁可能表示有缺陷，酒中也不應該有漂浮物。再聞一聞：酒不應該有不新鮮的氣味，也不應該有濕紙板味或醋味。如果覺得不對勁，最好不要端上桌。","The best glasses narrow at the rim to concentrate aromas.":"最好的酒杯杯口收窄，能集中香氣。","Red: slightly larger glass; sparkling: flute.":"紅酒：稍大的酒杯；氣泡酒：笛型杯。","Clean, polished glasses: dirt and detergent spoil wine.":"酒杯要乾淨、擦亮：髒汙和清潔劑會破壞葡萄酒。","Check: no haze or bits; no stale, wet cardboard or vinegar smells.":"檢查：不混濁、無漂浮物；沒有不新鮮的氣味、濕紙板味或醋味。","Food and wine: the basics":"餐酒搭配：基本概念","Food and wine pairing can look complicated, but at this level it comes down to two simple ideas: personal preference and a few predictable reactions between food and wine. The first idea matters most. When recommending a wine to a customer or a friend, what counts above all is what that person likes or dislikes.":"餐酒搭配看起來很複雜，但在這個級別，可以歸結為兩個簡單的概念：個人喜好，以及食物與葡萄酒之間幾種可預測的反應。第一個概念最重要。向客人或朋友推薦葡萄酒時，最要緊的是對方喜歡或不喜歡什麼。","A pairing may seem perfect to the person suggesting it, but if the other person does not enjoy that style of wine, there is no point recommending it. It also helps to remember that, for most people, most wines go acceptably with most foods. So there is not just one right wine for each dish.":"推薦的人可能覺得某個搭配很完美，但如果對方不喜歡那種風格的酒，推薦它就沒有意義。也要記得，對多數人來說，多數葡萄酒搭配多數食物都可以接受。所以每道菜並不是只有一款正確的酒。","Some features of food do, however, usually change how we perceive a wine: sweetness, umami, salt, acidity, flavour intensity, fat and chilli heat. Each one can make a wine seem better or worse. Knowing them lets you avoid the pairings most people dislike, and after that your options become almost limitless.":"不過，食物的某些特性通常會改變我們對葡萄酒的感受：甜味、鮮味、鹽、酸、風味強度、脂肪和辣味。每一項都可能讓酒顯得更好或更差。了解它們，就能避開多數人不喜歡的搭配，之後你的選擇幾乎沒有限制。","On the wine side, the elements that change are the ones you learn to spot when tasting: sweetness, acidity, bitterness, fruitiness, alcohol and body. Bitterness in wine, and the drying feel in the mouth, can come from the tannins in red wines or from oak. Keeping these words in mind makes the pairing table much easier to remember.":"在葡萄酒這一邊，會改變的是你在品飲時學會辨認的元素：甜度、酸度、苦味、果味、酒精和酒體。葡萄酒中的苦味和口腔的乾澀感，可能來自紅酒的單寧，也可能來自橡木桶。記住這些詞，搭配表就好記多了。","The person's own taste comes first.":"對方的個人口味優先。","For most people, most wines suit most foods.":"對多數人來說，多數葡萄酒適合多數食物。","Food: sweet, umami, salt, acid, intense flavour, fat, chilli.":"食物：甜、鮮味、鹽、酸、濃郁風味、脂肪、辣味。","Wine: sweetness, acidity, bitterness, fruit, alcohol, body.":"葡萄酒：甜度、酸度、苦味、果味、酒精、酒體。","Bitterness in wine comes from tannin or oak.":"葡萄酒中的苦味來自單寧或橡木桶。","What food does to wine":"食物對葡萄酒的影響","Sweetness and umami are the two 'difficult' elements. Sweet or umami-rich food makes a wine seem more drying and bitter, more acidic, and less sweet and fruity. A tannic red or a heavily oaked wine can therefore turn harsh. With a dessert, for example, a dry wine is likely to taste sour and lacking in fruit.":"甜味和鮮味是兩個「難搞」的元素。甜的或鮮味豐富的食物會讓葡萄酒顯得更乾澀、更苦、更酸，甜味和果味都變少。因此單寧高的紅酒或橡木味重的葡萄酒可能變得粗澀。例如搭配甜點時，不甜的酒很可能喝起來又酸又缺乏果味。","Salt and acidity, on the other hand, are wine-friendly. Salty food makes a wine seem less drying and bitter, less acidic, fruitier and fuller in body. Acidic food makes it seem less drying and bitter and less acidic, but also sweeter and fruitier. A dish with a sharp, acidic touch can therefore soften a very crisp wine.":"鹽和酸則是葡萄酒的好朋友。鹹的食物讓葡萄酒顯得沒那麼乾澀、沒那麼苦、沒那麼酸，果味更多、酒體更飽滿。酸的食物讓酒顯得沒那麼乾澀、沒那麼苦、沒那麼酸，同時更甜、果味更多。所以帶有鮮明酸味的菜餚，可以讓非常清脆的葡萄酒變得柔和。","Three cases remain. A dish with very intense flavours can overwhelm a wine, which will seem to disappear, so a wine with enough flavour of its own works better. Fatty or oily food makes a wine seem less acidic. Finally, chilli heat makes the alcohol in a wine more noticeable, and the alcohol in turn increases the burning sensation of the chilli.":"還有三種情況。風味非常濃郁的菜餚可能壓過葡萄酒，酒彷彿消失了，所以選擇本身風味夠強的酒比較好。高脂肪或油膩的食物讓葡萄酒顯得沒那麼酸。最後，辣味會讓酒中的酒精感更明顯，而酒精又反過來加強辣椒的灼熱感。","A way to remember it all: sweetness and umami 'take away' a wine's sweetness and fruit and boost its acidity and bitterness, while salt and acid do the opposite. Useful reasoning follows: with a sweet dish, choose a wine at least as sweet; with a spicy dish, a wine that is not too high in alcohol; with an umami-rich dish, a wine that is not too tannic.":"一個全部記住的方法：甜味和鮮味會「帶走」葡萄酒的甜味和果味，並加強酸度和苦味；鹽和酸則相反。由此可以推出實用的原則：搭配甜的菜餚，選甜度至少相當的葡萄酒；搭配辛辣的菜餚，選酒精濃度不太高的葡萄酒；搭配鮮味豐富的菜餚，選單寧不太高的葡萄酒。","Sweet or umami → wine more drying, bitter, acidic; less sweet, fruity.":"甜味或鮮味 → 葡萄酒更乾澀、更苦、更酸；甜味和果味更少。","Salty → wine less bitter and acidic; fruitier, fuller.":"鹹 → 葡萄酒沒那麼苦、沒那麼酸；果味更多、更飽滿。","Acidic → wine less bitter and acidic; sweeter, fruitier.":"酸 → 葡萄酒沒那麼苦、沒那麼酸；更甜、果味更多。","Intense flavours overwhelm wine; fat makes it seem less acidic.":"濃郁的風味會壓過葡萄酒；脂肪讓酒顯得沒那麼酸。","Chilli + alcohol: more burn, alcohol more noticeable.":"辣味 + 酒精：灼熱感更強，酒精感更明顯。","Getting ready and looking at colour":"準備工作與觀察顏色","Tasting well needs a method: approach every wine in the same order each time. This systematic approach to tasting lets you write accurate notes that you can look back on and compare in the future. At this level there are three stages: appearance, nose and palate. At each stage you look at only a few things, but always the same ones.":"要品飲得好，需要一套方法：每次都用相同的順序面對每一款酒。這套系統化品飲法能讓你寫出準確、日後可以回顧和比較的筆記。在這個級別有三個階段：外觀、香氣和口感。每個階段只看少數幾項，但永遠是同樣那幾項。","Before starting, it is worth preparing your surroundings. There should be no distracting smells, such as strong perfume or cooking. You need a white surface to judge the colour properly. The ideal glass has a wide bowl that narrows at the top, to concentrate the aromas. Your palate should be clean too, with no lingering flavours such as toothpaste or coffee.":"開始之前，值得先把環境準備好。不應該有干擾的氣味，例如濃烈的香水或烹飪的味道。你需要白色的表面，才能準確判斷顏色。理想的酒杯杯身寬、杯口收窄，能集中香氣。口腔也要乾淨，不能有牙膏或咖啡等殘留的味道。","The first stage is appearance. At this level you look at just one thing: the colour, which can be white, rosé or red. Colour is already a clue to how the wine was made: a red fermented with its skins for a long time, a rosé for only a few hours.":"第一個階段是外觀。在這個級別只看一件事：顏色，可以是白、粉紅或紅。顏色本身就是釀造方式的線索：紅酒長時間連同果皮發酵，粉紅酒只接觸幾個小時。","Systematic approach: appearance, nose, palate, always in that order.":"系統化品飲法：外觀、香氣、口感，永遠依照這個順序。","No distracting smells; a white surface.":"沒有干擾的氣味；白色的表面。","Wide glass narrowing at the top; a clean palate.":"杯身寬、杯口收窄的酒杯；乾淨的口腔。","Appearance: colour white, rosé or red.":"外觀：顏色為白、粉紅或紅。","The nose: fruit, oak and other":"香氣：水果、橡木與其他","The second stage is the nose, meaning the wine's aromas. Bring the glass to your nose and try to recognise what the smells remind you of. Finding the words is hard at first, but it is a skill that improves with practice. To find your way, three broad families are used: fruit, oak and 'other'.":"第二個階段是香氣，也就是葡萄酒的氣味。把酒杯湊近鼻子，試著辨認這些氣味讓你想到什麼。一開始很難找到合適的詞，但這是一種會隨練習進步的能力。為了有所依循，會使用三大類：水果、橡木和「其他」。","Fruit is the most common family: nearly all wines smell of fruit. The type of fruit depends on the grape variety, for example Cabernet Sauvignon reminds you of blackcurrant, and on how ripe the grapes were. Cool-climate Chardonnay gives apple and lemon; warm-climate Chardonnay gives peach and pineapple. This is how climate shows up directly in the glass.":"水果是最常見的一類：幾乎所有葡萄酒都有水果香氣。水果的類型取決於葡萄品種（例如卡本內蘇維濃讓人想到黑醋栗），也取決於葡萄的成熟度。涼爽氣候的夏多內呈現蘋果和檸檬；溫暖氣候的夏多內呈現桃子和鳳梨。氣候就是這樣直接反映在杯中。","Oak shows up when the wine has been fermented or matured in barrels. It brings aromas such as vanilla, coconut, cloves, cedar and smoke. The 'other' family covers everything else: grass, flowers, herbs, vegetables, earth, mushroom and leather. This variety is exactly what makes wine so interesting to smell.":"橡木香氣出現在曾於桶中發酵或熟成的葡萄酒，帶來香草、椰子、丁香、雪松和煙燻等香氣。「其他」類涵蓋其餘的一切：青草、花、香草植物、蔬菜、泥土、蘑菇和皮革。正是這份多樣性，讓葡萄酒聞起來如此有趣。","Nose: fruit, oak and 'other' aromas.":"香氣：水果、橡木和「其他」香氣。","Fruit depends on grape variety and ripeness.":"水果取決於葡萄品種和成熟度。","Oak: vanilla, coconut, cloves, cedar, smoke.":"橡木：香草、椰子、丁香、雪松、煙燻。","Other: grass, flowers, herbs, vegetables, earth, mushroom, leather.":"其他：青草、花、香草植物、蔬菜、泥土、蘑菇、皮革。","The palate: structure and flavours":"口感：結構與風味","The third stage is the palate: take a small sip and move it around your mouth. Here you assess five structural characteristics. Sweetness depends on how much sugar is left in the wine, and most wines are dry. Acidity makes your mouth water and gives freshness. Tannin, typical of red wines, dries the mouth.":"第三個階段是口感：啜一小口，讓酒在口中流動。這時要評估五項結構特徵。甜度取決於酒中殘留多少糖，而大多數葡萄酒都是不甜的。酸度讓你分泌唾液，帶來清爽感。單寧是紅酒的典型特徵，會讓口腔乾澀。","The other two characteristics are alcohol and body. Many still and sparkling wines have between 11.5% and 14% abv, though some are as low as 8% and others reach 15%. Body is the overall feel of the wine in your mouth: simply ask yourself how mouth-filling it is. A light-bodied wine feels delicate, a full-bodied one feels dense and mouth-filling.":"另外兩項特徵是酒精和酒體。許多靜態酒和氣泡酒的酒精濃度在 11.5% 至 14% abv 之間，不過有些低至 8%，有些則達到 15%。酒體是葡萄酒在口中的整體感受：只要問自己它有多飽滿。酒體輕盈的酒感覺細緻，酒體飽滿的酒感覺濃厚、充滿口腔。","Finally, on the palate you look for flavours, using the same families as on the nose: fruit, oak and other. You will often find the aromas you already smelled, and sometimes discover new ones. One last important note: in moderation alcohol is not regarded as harmful, but in excess it damages health and behaviour. Many countries publish official guidelines on low-risk drinking.":"最後，在口感階段要尋找風味，使用和聞香時相同的分類：水果、橡木和其他。你常會找到先前聞到的香氣，有時還會發現新的。最後一個重要提醒：適量飲酒不被視為有害，但過量會損害健康並影響行為。許多國家都公布了低風險飲酒的官方指引。","Structure: sweetness, acidity, tannin, alcohol, body.":"結構：甜度、酸度、單寧、酒精、酒體。","Acidity = mouth waters; tannin = mouth dries.":"酸度 = 分泌唾液；單寧 = 口腔乾澀。","Body = how mouth-filling the wine feels.":"酒體 = 酒在口中的飽滿程度。","Flavours: fruit, oak, other.":"風味：水果、橡木、其他。","Black grape skin":"黑葡萄果皮","Deep colour and tannins, which make the mouth feel dry.":"深色與單寧，單寧會讓口腔感到乾澀。","Grape pulp":"葡萄果肉","Soft part holding the juice: water, sugar and acid. Same colour in all grapes.":"含有果汁的柔軟部分：水、糖和酸。所有葡萄的果肉顏色都相同。","Substances in black grape skins that dry out the mouth.":"黑葡萄果皮中讓口腔乾澀的物質。","The vine's yearly cycle":"葡萄樹的年度週期","Flowering in spring, ripening in summer, picking in late summer.":"春季開花，夏季成熟，夏末採收。","What changes as grapes ripen?":"葡萄成熟時有哪些變化？","More water and sugar, less acid, riper flavours, colour change.":"水分和糖分增加，酸度降低，風味更成熟，顏色改變。","Cool climate":"涼爽氣候","Nearer the poles (Germany, northern France): less sugar, more acidity; often white grapes.":"較靠近兩極（德國、法國北部）：糖分較少、酸度較高；多為白葡萄。","Warm climate":"溫暖氣候","Nearer the Equator (parts of Australia and California): more sugar, less acidity, riper flavours; often black grapes.":"較靠近赤道（澳洲和加州的部分地區）：糖分較多、酸度較低、風味較成熟；多為黑葡萄。","Chardonnay: cool or warm climate?":"夏多內：涼爽還是溫暖氣候？","Cool: apple and lemon. Warm: peach and pineapple.":"涼爽：蘋果和檸檬。溫暖：桃子和鳳梨。","Microscopic organisms that eat sugar and make alcohol and carbon dioxide.":"以糖為食並產生酒精和二氧化碳的微生物。","Alcohol by volume: 10% abv = one tenth of the liquid is alcohol.":"酒精濃度（alcohol by volume）：10% abv = 液體的十分之一是酒精。","White wine steps":"白酒的釀造步驟","Crushing, pressing, fermentation, maturation, bottling.":"破皮、壓榨、發酵、熟成、裝瓶。","Red wine steps":"紅酒的釀造步驟","Crushing, fermentation on skins, draining, pressing, maturation, bottling.":"破皮、帶皮發酵、排汁、壓榨、熟成、裝瓶。","Rosé wine steps":"粉紅酒的釀造步驟","Crushing, fermentation, draining after a few hours, maturation, bottling.":"破皮、發酵、幾小時後排汁、熟成、裝瓶。","White wine from black grapes?":"用黑葡萄釀白酒？","Yes: the juice is colourless; press gently before fermentation.":"可以：果汁無色；在發酵前輕柔壓榨。","Stainless steel or oak":"不鏽鋼槽或橡木桶","Vessels for fermenting and maturing wine; oak is rare for rosé.":"葡萄酒發酵和熟成的容器；粉紅酒很少使用橡木桶。","Still wine":"靜態酒","Wine without bubbles; 8–15% abv, mostly 11.5–14%.":"沒有氣泡的葡萄酒；8–15% abv，多數為 11.5–14%。","Sparkling wine":"氣泡酒","Bubbles of carbon dioxide from fermentation. E.g. Champagne, Cava, Prosecco.":"來自發酵的二氧化碳氣泡。例如 Champagne、Cava、Prosecco。","Wine with added alcohol, 15–22% abv. E.g. Sherry, Port.":"添加了酒精的葡萄酒，15–22% abv。例如 Sherry、Port。","Alcohol by volume: 10% means one tenth of the liquid is alcohol.":"酒精濃度（alcohol by volume）：10% 表示液體的十分之一是酒精。","Dry wine":"不甜的葡萄酒","No or very little sugar: the yeast turned it all into alcohol.":"不含糖或含糖極少：酵母把糖全部轉化為酒精。","Comes from the juice, makes the mouth water, refreshes and balances sweetness.":"來自果汁，讓人分泌唾液，帶來清爽感並平衡甜味。","From black grape skins; dries the mouth. High: red Bordeaux, Chianti.":"來自黑葡萄果皮；讓口腔乾澀。高單寧：波爾多紅酒、Chianti。","How mouth-filling a wine is: light (Pinot Grigio), medium (Sancerre), full (Sauternes).":"酒在口中的飽滿程度：輕盈（灰皮諾）、中等（Sancerre）、飽滿（Sauternes）。","Oak aromas":"橡木香氣","Vanilla, coconut, cloves, cedar, smoke.":"香草、椰子、丁香、雪松、煙燻。","Black grapes, a few hours on the skins, then fermented without them.":"黑葡萄，與果皮接觸幾小時，之後不帶果皮發酵。","High acidity, light to medium body, green apple and lemon (e.g. Chablis).":"高酸度，酒體輕盈至中等，青蘋果和檸檬（例如 Chablis）。","Medium acidity, medium to full body, peach, pineapple, banana; often vanilla from oak.":"中等酸度，酒體中等至飽滿，桃子、鳳梨、香蕉；常有來自橡木桶的香草。","White Burgundy: which grape?":"布根地白酒：哪一個品種？","Chardonnay; medium body, high acidity, lemon and peach, sometimes vanilla.":"夏多內；酒體中等，高酸度，檸檬和桃子，有時有香草。","Dry, pronounced aromas, high acidity; fruit from apple to grapefruit to passion fruit.":"不甜，香氣濃郁，高酸度；果香從蘋果、葡萄柚到百香果。","Sauvignon Blanc herbaceous notes":"白蘇維濃的草本氣息","Asparagus, green bell pepper, cut grass.":"蘆筍、青椒、剛割過的青草。","Key Sauvignon Blanc wines":"白蘇維濃的重點酒款","New Zealand Sauvignon Blanc and Sancerre (Loire, France).":"紐西蘭白蘇維濃和 Sancerre（法國羅亞爾河）。","Usually dry, light, medium to high acidity, pear and lemon; mainly Italy.":"通常不甜、輕盈，酸度中等至高，梨子和檸檬；主要在義大利。","Dry to sweet, always high acidity; floral, lime, lemon, peach, apricot.":"從不甜到甜，酸度始終很高；花香、萊姆、檸檬、桃子、杏桃。","Riesling: where and in what style?":"麗絲玲：哪裡出產？什麼風格？","Germany: dry to sweet. Alsace and Australia: dry.":"德國：從不甜到甜。阿爾薩斯和澳洲：不甜。","Aromatic whites without oak":"不經橡木桶的芳香型白酒","Sauvignon Blanc, Pinot Grigio and Riesling: usually stainless steel, to keep the fruit.":"白蘇維濃、灰皮諾和麗絲玲：通常用不鏽鋼槽，以保留果香。","Dry, high tannin and acidity, medium to full body; blackcurrant, green pepper, mint.":"不甜，單寧和酸度高，酒體中等至飽滿；黑醋栗、青椒、薄荷。","Cabernet Sauvignon + oak":"卡本內蘇維濃 + 橡木桶","Cedar and vanilla notes.":"雪松和香草氣息。","Dry, medium to full body, medium acidity and tannin; red and black fruit, vanilla from oak.":"不甜，酒體中等至飽滿，酸度和單寧中等；紅色和黑色水果，來自橡木桶的香草。","Bordeaux blend":"波爾多混釀","Cabernet Sauvignon (tannin, acidity) + Merlot (softness, body).":"卡本內蘇維濃（單寧、酸度）+ 梅洛（柔順感、酒體）。","Dry, light to medium, high acidity, low to medium tannin; strawberry, red cherry, raspberry.":"不甜，輕盈至中等，高酸度，單寧低至中等；草莓、紅櫻桃、覆盆子。","Where is Pinot Noir key?":"黑皮諾在哪些地方是重點品種？","Red Burgundy, New Zealand (main black grape) and Champagne with Chardonnay.":"布根地紅酒、紐西蘭（最主要的黑葡萄品種），以及與夏多內搭配的 Champagne。","Syrah or Shiraz?":"希哈還是希拉茲？","Same grape: Syrah in France, Shiraz in Australia.":"同一個品種：法國叫希哈（Syrah），澳洲叫希拉茲（Shiraz）。","Syrah/Shiraz: aromas":"希哈／希拉茲：香氣","Blackberry, black cherry, black pepper, liquorice; oak: vanilla, coconut.":"黑莓、黑櫻桃、黑胡椒、甘草；橡木：香草、椰子。","Northern Rhône vs warm Australia":"北隆河與溫暖的澳洲","Rhône: medium body, fresh blackberry, black pepper. Australia: full, jammy black cherry, liquorice.":"隆河：酒體中等，新鮮黑莓、黑胡椒。澳洲：飽滿，果醬般的黑櫻桃、甘草。","Where is Cabernet Sauvignon widely grown?":"卡本內蘇維濃在哪些地方廣泛種植？","Bordeaux, California, Australia, Chile, South Africa.":"波爾多、加州、澳洲、智利、南非。","French sparkling from Chardonnay and Pinot Noir; dry, high acidity, apple, lemon, toasted bread.":"以夏多內和黑皮諾釀造的法國氣泡酒；不甜，高酸度，蘋果、檸檬、烤麵包。","Loire white from Sauvignon Blanc; dry, medium body, high acidity, apple and grass, unoaked.":"以白蘇維濃釀造的羅亞爾河白酒；不甜，酒體中等，高酸度，蘋果和青草，不經橡木桶。","Chardonnay from Burgundy's coolest part; dry, light-medium, apple and lemon, unoaked.":"來自布根地最涼爽地區的夏多內；不甜，輕盈至中等，蘋果和檸檬，不經橡木桶。","French name for Burgundy, used on labels of whites and reds.":"布根地的法文名稱，白酒和紅酒的酒標都使用。","White Burgundy":"布根地白酒","Chardonnay; dry, medium body, high acidity, lemon and peach; oaked or unoaked.":"夏多內；不甜，酒體中等，高酸度，檸檬和桃子；可經或不經橡木桶。","Pinot Noir; dry, light-medium, high acidity, raspberry and red cherry, sometimes vanilla and smoke.":"黑皮諾；不甜，輕盈至中等，高酸度，覆盆子和紅櫻桃，有時有香草和煙燻。","Cabernet Sauvignon + Merlot blend; dry, medium-full, high acidity and tannin, blackberry, blackcurrant, cedar.":"卡本內蘇維濃 + 梅洛混釀；不甜，中等至飽滿，酸度和單寧高，黑莓、黑醋栗、雪松。","Sancerre or Chablis?":"Sancerre 還是 Chablis？","Grassy = Sancerre (Sauvignon Blanc, Loire). Restrained apple and lemon = Chablis (Chardonnay, Burgundy).":"帶青草味 = Sancerre（白蘇維濃，羅亞爾河）。內斂的蘋果和檸檬 = Chablis（夏多內，布根地）。","Sweet white from Bordeaux; full, apricot, honey, vanilla, high acidity.":"波爾多的甜白酒；飽滿，杏桃、蜂蜜、香草，高酸度。","Californian rosé; medium-sweet, low alcohol, strawberry and raspberry, unoaked.":"加州粉紅酒；半甜，酒精濃度低，草莓和覆盆子，不經橡木桶。","Dry, light French red, unoaked, raspberry and red cherry, low tannin.":"不甜、輕盈的法國紅酒，不經橡木桶，覆盆子和紅櫻桃，低單寧。","Dry, medium-bodied French red; strawberry, red plum, white pepper; oaked or not.":"不甜、酒體中等的法國紅酒；草莓、紅李、白胡椒；可經或不經橡木桶。","Dry, full-bodied, high-alcohol French red; strawberry and clove from oak.":"不甜、酒體飽滿、酒精濃度高的法國紅酒；草莓和來自橡木桶的丁香。","Dry, medium-bodied Italian red, high tannin and acidity; cherry, red plum, dried herbs.":"不甜、酒體中等的義大利紅酒，單寧和酸度高；櫻桃、紅李、乾燥香草。","Dry Spanish red, medium to full body; strawberry and vanilla from oak.":"不甜的西班牙紅酒，酒體中等至飽滿；草莓和來自橡木桶的香草。","Light Italian sparkling wine; pear and floral; dry or medium-sweet.":"輕盈的義大利氣泡酒；梨子和花香；不甜或半甜。","Dry sparkling wine from Spain; apple and lemon.":"西班牙的不甜氣泡酒；蘋果和檸檬。","White fortified wine from Spain; dry, medium or sweet.":"西班牙的白色加烈酒；不甜、半甜或甜。","Fortified wine from Portugal; sweet, high alcohol, usually red, full, tannic, blackberry.":"葡萄牙的加烈酒；甜，酒精濃度高，通常是紅色，飽滿、單寧高，黑莓。","3 storage rules":"3 條保存規則","Cool and constant; away from light; cork = bottle on its side.":"涼爽恆溫；遠離光線；軟木塞 = 酒瓶橫放。","Why lay corked bottles down?":"為什麼軟木塞封瓶的酒要橫放？","The cork stays moist; a dry cork lets air in and the wine loses fruit.":"軟木塞保持濕潤；乾掉的軟木塞會讓空氣進入，酒就失去果味。","A pump removes air from the opened bottle.":"用幫浦抽出已開瓶酒瓶中的空氣。","Blanket system":"氣體覆蓋系統","A harmless gas is pumped in to push the air out.":"灌入無害的氣體，把空氣排出。","Sauternes and Champagne":"Sauternes 與 Champagne","Well chilled: 6–8°C (sweet) and 6–10°C (sparkling).":"充分冰鎮：6–8°C（甜酒）和 6–10°C（氣泡酒）。","Pinot Grigio and oaked Chardonnay":"灰皮諾與經橡木桶的夏多內","Chilled 7–10°C (light white); lightly chilled 10–13°C (full white).":"冰鎮 7–10°C（輕盈的白酒）；稍微冰鎮 10–13°C（飽滿的白酒）。","Beaujolais and Shiraz":"Beaujolais 與希拉茲","Lightly chilled 13°C (light red); room temperature 15–18°C (full red).":"稍微冰鎮 13°C（輕盈的紅酒）；室溫 15–18°C（飽滿的紅酒）。","Hand on the cork once the cage is loose; bottle tilted; turn the bottle.":"鐵絲罩一鬆開，手就按住軟木塞；酒瓶傾斜；轉動酒瓶。","Pairing rule no. 1":"搭配的第一條規則","Start with the person's taste: never push a style they dislike.":"從對方的口味出發：絕不硬推對方不喜歡的風格。","Wine more drying, bitter and acidic; less sweet and fruity.":"葡萄酒更乾澀、更苦、更酸；甜味和果味更少。","Same as sweetness: wine more bitter and acidic, less fruity.":"和甜味相同：葡萄酒更苦、更酸，果味更少。","Wine less bitter and acidic; fruitier and fuller.":"葡萄酒沒那麼苦、沒那麼酸；果味更多、更飽滿。","Acidic food":"酸的食物","Wine less bitter and acidic; sweeter and fruitier.":"葡萄酒沒那麼苦、沒那麼酸；更甜、果味更多。","Highly flavoured food":"味道濃郁的食物","Can overwhelm the wine.":"可能壓過葡萄酒。","Makes the wine seem less acidic.":"讓葡萄酒顯得沒那麼酸。","Alcohol increases the burn; the wine's alcohol stands out more.":"酒精加強灼熱感；葡萄酒的酒精感更突出。","Systematic approach to tasting":"系統化品飲法","Appearance (colour) → nose (aromas) → palate (structure and flavours).":"外觀（顏色）→ 香氣 → 口感（結構和風味）。","Preparing to taste":"品飲前的準備","No smells, white surface, wide glass narrowing at the top, clean palate.":"沒有異味、白色的表面、杯身寬而杯口收窄的酒杯、乾淨的口腔。","'Other' aromas":"「其他」香氣","Grass, flowers, herbs, vegetables, earth, mushroom, leather.":"青草、花、香草植物、蔬菜、泥土、蘑菇、皮革。","Structure on the palate":"口感中的結構","Sweetness, acidity, tannin, alcohol, body.":"甜度、酸度、單寧、酒精、酒體。","How mouth-filling the wine is: light = delicate, full = dense.":"酒在口中的飽滿程度：輕盈 = 細緻，飽滿 = 濃厚。","Welcome to the very first lesson. Before we talk about famous wines, grape varieties or how to serve a bottle, we need to start where every wine starts: in the vineyard. In this lesson we look inside a grape and see what its skin and its pulp each bring to the wine. Then we follow the vine through its year, from the first flowers to the harvest. We see what changes as the grapes ripen. And finally we discover why the climate of a region shapes the grapes, and so the wine, so strongly.":"歡迎來到第一堂課。在談論名酒、葡萄品種或如何侍酒之前，我們得從每一款葡萄酒的起點開始：葡萄園。這堂課會先看看葡萄的內部，了解果皮和果肉各自為葡萄酒帶來什麼。接著跟著葡萄樹走過一年，從第一朵花到採收，看看葡萄成熟時有哪些變化。最後我們會發現，為什麼產區的氣候對葡萄、進而對葡萄酒的影響如此之大。","Let's begin with a simple definition. Wine is fermented grape juice. The grapes are crushed to release their sweet juice, and that juice is then transformed by fermentation, which we will explore in the next lesson. So to understand wine, we first need to understand the grape. There are two main kinds: white grapes and black grapes. And here is the first surprise: if you cut one of each in half, the inside looks almost exactly the same. The real difference is on the outside.":"先從一個簡單的定義開始。葡萄酒是發酵的葡萄汁。葡萄經過破皮，釋出甜美的果汁，再由發酵轉化，這部分下一堂課會談到。所以要了解葡萄酒，得先了解葡萄。葡萄主要有兩種：白葡萄和黑葡萄。第一個驚喜來了：如果各拿一顆切成兩半，裡面看起來幾乎一模一樣。真正的差別在外面。","That outside is the skin. Black grapes have deeply coloured skins, and those skins hold something else too: tannins. Tannins are the substances that make your mouth feel dry, a little like a strong cup of black tea left to brew too long. White grapes, once they are ripe, have skins with a golden colour, and no deep colour to give. So whenever you think of colour and tannin in a wine, think of the skin of a black grape.":"外面指的就是果皮。黑葡萄的果皮顏色很深，而且還含有另一樣東西：單寧。單寧是讓口腔感到乾澀的物質，有點像一杯泡太久的濃紅茶。白葡萄成熟後果皮呈金黃色，沒有深色可以釋出。所以每當想到葡萄酒的顏色和單寧，就想到黑葡萄的果皮。","Now the inside, the pulp. It is soft and fleshy, and it holds the juice. That juice is mostly water, sugar and acid. The sugar will later become alcohol, and the acid will give the wine its freshness. And remember this detail, because it comes back again and again: the pulp has the same colour whatever the colour of the skin. Black grape or white grape, the juice is pale. Hold on to that idea; it explains how rosé is made, and even how a white wine can come from black grapes.":"接著看裡面，也就是果肉。它柔軟多肉，含有果汁。果汁主要是水、糖和酸。糖之後會變成酒精，酸則為葡萄酒帶來清爽感。請記住這個細節，因為它會一再出現：不論果皮是什麼顏色，果肉的顏色都一樣。黑葡萄也好，白葡萄也好，果汁都是淺色的。記牢這個概念；它能解釋粉紅酒是怎麼釀的，甚至解釋白酒為什麼可以來自黑葡萄。","Next, the life of the vine. Grapes are the fruit of the grape vine, a plant that can live for several decades. A young vine is not productive straight away: it needs a couple of years after planting to reach maturity. From then on, it gives a crop of grapes every single year. And that year follows the seasons in a very regular rhythm, which is easy to learn.":"接下來是葡萄樹的一生。葡萄是葡萄樹的果實，這種植物可以存活數十年。年輕的葡萄樹不會馬上有產量：種下後需要兩三年才會成熟。從那之後，它每一年都會結出葡萄。而這一年跟著四季走，節奏非常規律，很容易記住。","In spring, the vine flowers. The flowers are tiny and grow in clusters, and here is the lovely part: each individual flower becomes one grape. Just after flowering, the young grapes are small, hard and green, all of them, whether they will one day be white or black. Through the summer they ripen, and in late summer the grapes are picked. That moment is the harvest. So: flowering in spring, ripening in summer, picking at the end of summer.":"春季，葡萄樹開花。花很小，成簇生長，最美妙的是：每一朵小花都會變成一顆葡萄。剛開完花時，幼果又小又硬又綠，全都一樣，不論將來是白葡萄還是黑葡萄。它們在夏季成熟，到了夏末就採收葡萄，這個時刻就是採收季。所以：春季開花，夏季成熟，夏末採收。","What actually happens as grapes ripen? There are five changes, worth learning in a row. The grapes swell with water. Their sugar levels rise. Their acid levels fall. Their flavours become riper. And their colour changes: white grapes go from green to golden, and black grapes go from green to purple. Think of an apple picked too early, hard and sour, and then the same apple fully ripe, juicy and sweet. Grapes follow exactly the same path.":"葡萄成熟時究竟發生了什麼？共有五項變化，值得依序記住。葡萄吸水膨大。糖分上升。酸度下降。風味變得更成熟。顏色也會改變：白葡萄從綠色轉為金黃色，黑葡萄從綠色轉為紫色。想像一顆太早摘下的蘋果，又硬又酸；再想像同一顆蘋果完全成熟時，多汁又香甜。葡萄走的是一模一樣的路。","Now, where do vines grow? A vine needs the right amount of sunlight and heat to produce good quality fruit. If it is too cold or too hot, it simply cannot do the job. It also likes a winter cold enough to let it rest. That is why most of the world's vineyards sit in two bands around the globe, roughly between thirty and fifty degrees of latitude, one band north of the Equator and one band south of it, where the grapes find the right amount of sunlight, heat and water.":"那麼，葡萄樹生長在哪裡？葡萄樹需要適量的日照和熱量，才能結出優質的果實。太冷或太熱，它都辦不到。它也喜歡夠冷的冬季，好讓自己休眠。所以全世界大多數葡萄園都位於環繞地球的兩條帶狀區域，大約在緯度三十度到五十度之間，一條在赤道以北，一條在赤道以南，葡萄在那裡能得到適量的日照、熱量和水分。","Within those bands, we can separate cool and warm climates. Cool climate regions are closer to the poles; Germany and northern France are good examples. Average temperatures are low, the sunlight can be weaker, and in some years the grapes struggle to ripen at all. In cool regions it is common to grow white grapes. Warm climate regions are closer to the Equator, such as parts of Australia and parts of California. Temperatures are high, the sunlight is more intense, and the grapes ripen reliably every year. There, black grapes are commonly grown.":"在這兩條帶狀區域內，可以再分出涼爽氣候和溫暖氣候。涼爽氣候產區較靠近兩極；德國和法國北部就是好例子。平均氣溫低，日照可能較弱，在某些年份葡萄甚至難以成熟。涼爽產區普遍種植白葡萄。溫暖氣候產區較靠近赤道，例如澳洲和加州的部分地區。氣溫高，日照更強，葡萄每年都能穩定成熟。那裡普遍種植黑葡萄。","Why does this matter so much? Because climate shapes the grape. The cooler it is, the lower the sugar and the higher the acidity. The warmer it is, the higher the sugar and the lower the acidity, and the flavours taste riper. Take Chardonnay as an example. From a cool region it smells of green apple and lemon; from a warm region the same grape gives peach and pineapple. And since sugar becomes alcohol, warm-climate wines also tend to be stronger and fuller.":"這為什麼這麼重要？因為氣候塑造了葡萄。越涼爽，糖分越低、酸度越高。越溫暖，糖分越高、酸度越低，風味也越成熟。以夏多內為例：來自涼爽產區時，它有青蘋果和檸檬的香氣；來自溫暖產區時，同一個品種呈現桃子和鳳梨。而且因為糖會變成酒精，溫暖氣候的葡萄酒往往酒精濃度更高、酒體更飽滿。","Here is a tip to remember it all: picture a thermometer standing next to the grape. As the thermometer goes up, sugar goes up with it, acidity slides down, and the fruit moves from apple and lemon towards peach and pineapple. As the thermometer goes down, everything moves the other way: more freshness, less sugar, crisper fruit. Same grape, different thermometer, different wine.":"這裡有個幫你全部記住的訣竅：想像葡萄旁邊立著一支溫度計。溫度計上升，糖分跟著上升，酸度下滑，果香從蘋果和檸檬移向桃子和鳳梨。溫度計下降，一切就往反方向走：更清爽、糖分更少、果香更清脆。同一個品種，不同的溫度，不同的葡萄酒。","Before the quiz, remember three things. First, the skin of a black grape brings colour and tannin, while the pulp holds a juice of water, sugar and acid that is pale in every grape. Second, the vine flowers in spring, and over the summer the grapes swell, gain sugar, lose acid, ripen in flavour and change colour, before being picked in late summer. Third, cool climates give grapes with less sugar and more acidity, while warm climates give more sugar, less acidity and riper flavours.":"測驗之前，記住三件事。第一，黑葡萄的果皮帶來顏色和單寧，果肉則含有由水、糖和酸組成的果汁，所有葡萄的果汁都是淺色的。第二，葡萄樹在春季開花，葡萄在夏季吸水膨大、糖分增加、酸度降低、風味成熟並轉色，然後在夏末採收。第三，涼爽氣候的葡萄糖分較少、酸度較高，溫暖氣候的葡萄糖分較多、酸度較低、風味更成熟。","In the last lesson we followed the grapes all the way to the harvest. Now we carry them into the winery. In this lesson we look first at the one step that turns juice into wine: alcoholic fermentation. Then we follow three simple recipes, one for white wine, one for red and one for rosé. All three give still wines, meaning wines without bubbles. Sparkling and fortified wines are made in other ways, and those methods belong to a later level; here we keep to the essentials.":"上一堂課我們跟著葡萄一路走到採收。現在把它們帶進酒廠。這堂課先看把果汁變成葡萄酒的那個步驟：酒精發酵。接著依序認識三套簡單的做法，分別是白酒、紅酒和粉紅酒。三者釀出的都是靜態酒，也就是沒有氣泡的葡萄酒。氣泡酒和加烈酒用的是其他方法，那些屬於更高級別的內容；這裡只談基本重點。","Let's start with fermentation. The workers behind it are yeast: microscopic living organisms, far too small to see. Yeast eat sugar, and as they eat it they convert it into two things: alcohol and carbon dioxide, which is a gas. So the whole story fits in one line: sugar plus yeast gives alcohol plus carbon dioxide. Learn that line by heart, because it is the heart of every wine, and the exam likes to check that you know both of the things fermentation produces.":"先從發酵開始。幕後的功臣是酵母：一種微小的生物，小到完全看不見。酵母吃糖，一邊吃一邊把糖轉化為兩樣東西：酒精和二氧化碳（一種氣體）。所以整個故事一句話就能說完：糖加酵母，得到酒精加二氧化碳。把這句話背起來，因為它是每一款葡萄酒的核心，考試也喜歡確認你知道發酵的這兩種產物。","In most cases fermentation carries on until the yeast have eaten all of the sugar. The result is a dry wine, which is what most wines are. The alcohol stays in the newly made wine, while the carbon dioxide usually escapes into the air, a bit like the bubbles rising from a pan of water close to boiling. There are exceptions. Sometimes the fermentation stops before all the sugar is gone, which leaves a sweet wine; sometimes the gas is trapped, which gives a sparkling wine. We meet both in the chapter on types and styles.":"多數情況下，發酵會持續到酵母把糖全部吃完，得到不甜的葡萄酒，大多數葡萄酒都是如此。酒精留在剛釀成的酒中，二氧化碳通常散逸到空氣中，有點像鍋裡快要煮沸的水冒出的氣泡。也有例外。有時發酵在糖用完之前就停止，留下甜酒；有時氣體被保留下來，得到氣泡酒。這兩種都會在類型與風格那一章談到。","How do we measure the alcohol? With a figure called alcohol by volume. A wine at ten percent alcohol by volume is a wine in which ten percent of the liquid is alcohol. And here is the link with the vineyard: the sugar that the grapes built up as they ripened is exactly what the yeast turn into alcohol. Riper, sweeter grapes give the yeast more to eat, so they usually give a stronger wine.":"酒精怎麼衡量？用一個叫做酒精濃度（alcohol by volume）的數字。酒精濃度百分之十的葡萄酒，就是液體中有百分之十是酒精。這裡又連回葡萄園：葡萄成熟時累積的糖分，正是酵母轉化為酒精的原料。越成熟、越甜的葡萄，讓酵母有更多糖可吃，所以通常釀出酒精濃度更高的酒。","Now, our first recipe: white wine. It is usually made from white grapes. After picking, the grapes are crushed, which breaks them open and releases some of the juice. Next, the crushed grapes are pressed, squeezing out the rest of the juice and leaving the skins behind. This is the key idea for white wine: the juice is separated from the skins before fermentation begins. The skins never get the chance to give colour or tannin.":"現在是第一套做法：白酒。白酒通常以白葡萄釀造。採收後，葡萄先破皮，把果實弄破，釋出一部分果汁。接著壓榨破皮後的葡萄，擠出剩餘的果汁，把果皮留下。這是白酒的關鍵：果汁在發酵開始前就與果皮分開。果皮完全沒有機會釋出顏色或單寧。","Then yeast are added to the juice and fermentation starts. It can take place in stainless steel tanks or in oak barrels. Once fermentation has finished, the wine is matured, again either in stainless steel or in oak. Steel keeps things neutral, so the fruit stays fresh and pure; oak can add flavours such as vanilla or smoke. Finally comes bottling. So the white wine sequence is: crushing, pressing, fermentation, maturation, bottling.":"接著在果汁中加入酵母，發酵開始，可以在不鏽鋼槽或橡木桶中進行。發酵結束後，葡萄酒進行熟成，同樣可以用不鏽鋼槽或橡木桶。不鏽鋼保持中性，讓果香清新純淨；橡木桶則可以增添香草或煙燻等風味。最後是裝瓶。所以白酒的順序是：破皮、壓榨、發酵、熟成、裝瓶。","A small detail that often appears in quizzes: a white wine can also be made from black grapes. Remember the last lesson. The colour of a black grape is all in its skin, and its juice is colourless. So if black grapes are pressed gently before fermentation, the pale juice can be separated quickly from the skins and used to make a white wine. Champagne, for example, is often made partly from a black grape, yet the wine is pale.":"一個常在測驗中出現的小細節：白酒也可以用黑葡萄釀造。回想上一堂課：黑葡萄的顏色全在果皮，果汁是無色的。所以只要在發酵前輕柔壓榨黑葡萄，就能迅速把淺色的果汁與果皮分開，用來釀造白酒。例如 Champagne 常有一部分是以黑葡萄釀造，酒色卻是淺的。","Our second recipe: red wine. It must be made from black grapes. After picking, the grapes are crushed, and this time the juice is not separated. Juice and skins go into the fermentation vessel together. Yeast are added and fermentation starts. During fermentation the juice and skins are mixed thoroughly, so that colour and tannin are drawn out of the skins and into the wine. This contact with the skins is the whole secret of red wine.":"第二套做法：紅酒。紅酒必須以黑葡萄釀造。採收後葡萄先破皮，但這一次果汁不會被分離出來。果汁和果皮一起放進發酵容器，加入酵母，發酵開始。發酵期間，果汁和果皮充分混合，把顏色和單寧從果皮中萃取到酒裡。與果皮的接觸，就是紅酒全部的祕密。","Once the fermentation has finished, the new red wine is drained off the skins. But those skins are still soaked with wine, so they are pressed to release what remains. Notice the difference: for white wine, pressing comes before fermentation; for red wine, it comes after. Then the red wine is matured in stainless steel tanks or oak barrels, and bottled. The red sequence is: crushing, fermentation, draining, pressing, maturation, bottling.":"發酵結束後，新釀成的紅酒從果皮中排出。但果皮仍然吸飽了酒液，所以要壓榨，把剩下的酒取出。注意這個差別：白酒的壓榨在發酵之前；紅酒則在發酵之後。接著紅酒在不鏽鋼槽或橡木桶中熟成，然後裝瓶。紅酒的順序是：破皮、發酵、排汁、壓榨、熟成、裝瓶。","Our third recipe: rosé. It is made from black grapes and begins just like red: the grapes are crushed, juice and skins go into the vessel together, and fermentation starts. But after only a few hours, the juice is drained off the skins. At that point it is just pink. Without the skins it cannot get any darker, and it finishes fermenting on its own. Rosé is then matured, very rarely in oak, and bottled. The sequence: crushing, fermentation, draining, maturation, bottling. There is no pressing of the skins at the end, because they were removed so early.":"第三套做法：粉紅酒。粉紅酒以黑葡萄釀造，開頭和紅酒一模一樣：葡萄破皮，果汁和果皮一起放進容器，發酵開始。但只過幾個小時，果汁就從果皮中排出。這時它只呈粉紅色。沒有了果皮，顏色不會再變深，果汁就單獨完成發酵。之後粉紅酒進行熟成（極少使用橡木桶），然後裝瓶。順序：破皮、發酵、排汁、熟成、裝瓶。最後沒有壓榨果皮的步驟，因為果皮很早就移除了。","Here is a memory tip. Picture the skins of black grapes as a tea bag and the juice as a cup of hot water. For a white wine, the tea bag never goes into the cup. For a rosé, you dip it in for a short moment and take it out: the water turns just pink. For a red, you leave it in for the whole time, and you get deep colour and that drying grip of tannin.":"這裡有個記憶訣竅。把黑葡萄的果皮想成茶包，把果汁想成一杯熱水。釀白酒時，茶包從頭到尾沒有放進杯子。釀粉紅酒時，把茶包浸一下就拿出來：水只變成淡淡的粉紅色。釀紅酒時，茶包從頭泡到尾，於是得到深濃的顏色，以及單寧那種乾澀的收斂感。","Before the quiz, remember three things. First, fermentation is yeast eating sugar and turning it into alcohol and carbon dioxide; when all the sugar is eaten the wine is dry. Second, white wine is pressed before fermentation, so the juice ferments without the skins, and red wine is fermented with the skins, then drained and pressed afterwards. Third, rosé starts like a red but the juice is drained off the skins after only a few hours, and it is rarely matured in oak.":"測驗之前，記住三件事。第一，發酵就是酵母吃糖，把糖轉化為酒精和二氧化碳；糖全部吃完，酒就是不甜的。第二，白酒在發酵前壓榨，所以果汁不帶果皮發酵；紅酒連同果皮發酵，之後才排汁、壓榨。第三，粉紅酒的開頭和紅酒一樣，但果汁只過幾個小時就從果皮中排出，而且很少在橡木桶中熟成。","So far we have seen how still, dry wines are made: white, red and rosé. But the world of wine is wider than that. In this lesson we sort wines into their three types: still, sparkling and fortified. Then we learn the words used to describe any wine's style: its colour, its structure, meaning sweetness, acidity, tannin, alcohol and body, and finally its aromas and flavours. This chapter carries a lot of weight in the exam, so take it slowly.":"到目前為止，我們看過不甜的靜態酒是怎麼釀成的：白酒、紅酒和粉紅酒。但葡萄酒的世界遠不止於此。這堂課會把葡萄酒分成三種類型：靜態酒、氣泡酒和加烈酒。接著學習描述任何一款酒的風格所用的詞彙：顏色、結構（也就是甜度、酸度、單寧、酒精和酒體），最後是香氣與風味。這一章在考試中佔的比重很大，所以慢慢來。","The first type is still wine, and it is by far the biggest family. It is what most people picture when someone says wine: no bubbles. Still wines range from eight to fifteen percent alcohol by volume, and most sit between eleven and a half and fourteen. Many are named after the region where they are made, such as Sancerre and Burgundy in France, Rioja in Spain and Chianti in Italy. Others carry the name of their grape variety instead, such as Pinot Grigio. Knowing which logic a label follows is already a big step.":"第一種類型是靜態酒，這是目前為止最大的家族。多數人聽到葡萄酒時想到的就是它：沒有氣泡。靜態酒的酒精濃度從百分之八到百分之十五，大多數在百分之十一點五到百分之十四之間。許多靜態酒以產區命名，例如法國的 Sancerre 和布根地、西班牙的 Rioja、義大利的 Chianti。另一些則以葡萄品種命名，例如灰皮諾（Pinot Grigio）。知道酒標遵循哪一種命名方式，就已經邁出一大步。","The second type is sparkling wine: wine that is bubbly or fizzy. Remember that fermentation makes carbon dioxide. Here that gas is trapped in the wine, and when the bottle is opened it escapes as bubbles. The best-known example is Champagne from France; Cava from Spain and Prosecco from Italy are also famous, and sparkling wine is now made all over the world. The third type is fortified wine. These wines have had extra alcohol added, so they are stronger, from fifteen to twenty-two percent alcohol by volume. The two to know are Sherry from Spain and Port from Portugal.":"第二種類型是氣泡酒：帶有氣泡的葡萄酒。還記得發酵會產生二氧化碳吧。在這裡，氣體被保留在酒中，開瓶時就以氣泡的形式散逸。最著名的例子是法國的 Champagne；西班牙的 Cava 和義大利的 Prosecco 也很有名，現在世界各地都釀造氣泡酒。第三種類型是加烈酒。這類酒額外添加了酒精，所以更烈，酒精濃度從百分之十五到百分之二十二。必須認識的兩款是西班牙的 Sherry 和葡萄牙的 Port。","Any of these three types can come in many styles, and a style starts with colour. Colour depends on the grape and on how the wine is made. White wines are usually made from white grapes, such as Chablis or a Riesling, although, as we saw, a white can also come from black grapes if the skins are removed before fermentation. Red wines must be made from black grapes, whose skins stay with the juice during fermentation; Rioja and Cabernet Sauvignon are examples. Rosé comes from black grapes with only a short contact with the skins; White Zinfandel is the classic example.":"這三種類型都可以有許多風格，而風格從顏色開始。顏色取決於葡萄和釀造方式。白酒通常以白葡萄釀造，例如 Chablis 或麗絲玲，不過如前面所見，只要在發酵前去除果皮，白酒也可以來自黑葡萄。紅酒必須以黑葡萄釀造，發酵期間果皮與果汁在一起；Rioja 和卡本內蘇維濃就是例子。粉紅酒來自黑葡萄，只短暫與果皮接觸；White Zinfandel 是經典例子。","Next comes structure, five characteristics you will learn to feel in your mouth. The first is sweetness, which is simply the sugar left in the wine. Most wines are dry, with no sugar or very little: the yeast have turned all the sugar into alcohol. Chablis, Sauvignon Blanc, Côtes du Rhône, Chianti and Cabernet Sauvignon are all dry. Most wines with a medium level of sweetness are white or rosé. They are made in two ways: either the yeast are removed before all the sugar has become alcohol, or some unfermented grape juice is added to a dry wine. Some German Rieslings and White Zinfandel are good examples.":"接著是結構，也就是你會學著在口中感受的五項特徵。第一項是甜度，簡單說就是留在酒中的糖。大多數葡萄酒都是不甜的，不含糖或含糖極少：酵母已把所有的糖轉化為酒精。Chablis、白蘇維濃、Côtes du Rhône、Chianti 和卡本內蘇維濃都是不甜的。半甜的葡萄酒多半是白酒或粉紅酒，有兩種釀法：在糖全部變成酒精之前移除酵母，或是在不甜的酒中加入一些未發酵的葡萄汁。部分德國麗絲玲和 White Zinfandel 都是好例子。","Sweet wines have so much sugar that they can feel thick, almost syrupy. There are two key ways to make them. In the first, the grapes are so rich in sugar that the yeast stop working before they have eaten it all; Sauternes and some German Rieslings are made this way. In the second, used for fortified wines, high-strength distilled alcohol is added during fermentation; it kills the yeast before they finish, and the sugar left behind makes the wine sweet. Port and some Sherries are sweet for this reason.":"甜酒含有大量的糖，喝起來可能濃稠，幾乎像糖漿。主要有兩種釀造方法。第一種，葡萄的糖分極高，酵母還沒把糖吃完就停止作用；Sauternes 和部分德國麗絲玲就是這樣釀成的。第二種用於加烈酒，在發酵期間加入高濃度的蒸餾酒精；酒精在酵母完成發酵前就把它殺死，留下的糖讓酒帶甜。Port 和部分 Sherry 就是因此而甜。","The second structural characteristic is acidity. It comes straight from the grape juice, and it is what makes a wine refreshing. It is easy to recognise because it makes your mouth water, just like biting into a lemon. Too much acidity tastes unpleasantly sharp; too little and the wine loses its refreshing character. Chablis, Chianti and wines made from Sauvignon Blanc, Riesling, Cabernet Sauvignon or Pinot Noir all have high acidity. And acidity is vital in sweet wines: it balances the sugar and stops the wine from being unpleasantly sweet.":"第二項結構特徵是酸度。它直接來自葡萄汁，正是它讓葡萄酒清爽。酸度很容易辨認，因為它會讓你分泌唾液，就像咬一口檸檬。酸度太高會尖銳得令人不舒服；太低則讓酒失去清爽的特質。Chablis、Chianti，以及白蘇維濃、麗絲玲、卡本內蘇維濃或黑皮諾釀造的葡萄酒，酸度都很高。酸度在甜酒中更是至關重要：它平衡了糖分，讓酒不會甜得膩口。","The third is tannin, a characteristic of red wines that comes from the grape skins. How much a wine has depends on the grape variety and on how the wine is made. Tannin can taste a little bitter, but mostly it is something you feel rather than taste: it makes your mouth feel dry. Red Bordeaux and Chianti are high in tannin. Beaujolais and some Pinot Noir wines are low in tannin. So remember the pair: acidity makes your mouth water, tannin makes it dry.":"第三項是單寧，這是紅酒的特徵，來自葡萄果皮。酒中單寧的多寡取決於葡萄品種和釀造方式。單寧可能帶一點苦味，但主要是感覺到，而不是嚐到：它讓口腔感到乾澀。波爾多紅酒和 Chianti 單寧高。Beaujolais 和部分黑皮諾葡萄酒單寧低。所以記住這一組：酸度讓你分泌唾液，單寧讓口腔乾澀。","The fourth is alcohol. Most still and sparkling wines sit between eleven and a half and fourteen percent alcohol by volume, but some reach fifteen and others go as low as eight. Châteauneuf-du-Pape from France is an example of a high-alcohol wine; White Zinfandel from California is an example of a low-alcohol one. The fifth is body, the overall feel of the wine in your mouth. Just ask yourself: how mouth-filling is it? Think of the difference between skimmed milk and whole milk. Pinot Grigio and Beaujolais are light-bodied, Sancerre and Côtes du Rhône medium-bodied, Californian Cabernet Sauvignon and Sauternes full-bodied.":"第四項是酒精。大多數靜態酒和氣泡酒的酒精濃度在百分之十一點五到百分之十四之間，但有些達到百分之十五，有些低至百分之八。法國的 Châteauneuf-du-Pape 是高酒精濃度葡萄酒的例子；加州的 White Zinfandel 是低酒精濃度的例子。第五項是酒體，也就是葡萄酒在口中的整體感受。只要問自己：它在口中有多飽滿？想想脫脂牛奶和全脂牛奶的差別。灰皮諾和 Beaujolais 酒體輕盈，Sancerre 和 Côtes du Rhône 酒體中等，加州卡本內蘇維濃和 Sauternes 酒體飽滿。","Finally, aromas and flavours. Some come from the grapes themselves, others develop during winemaking and maturation. Putting them into words is hard at first, but it comes with practice, and three families make it easier: fruit, oak and other. Almost every wine smells of fruit. The kind of fruit depends on the grape variety, so Cabernet Sauvignon smells of blackcurrant, and on ripeness: cool-climate Chardonnay shows green apple and lemon, warm-climate Chardonnay shows peach and pineapple.":"最後是香氣與風味。有些來自葡萄本身，有些在釀造和熟成過程中形成。一開始很難用文字描述，但多練習就會進步，而分成三大類會容易得多：水果、橡木和其他。幾乎每一款葡萄酒都有水果香氣。水果的類型取決於葡萄品種，例如卡本內蘇維濃有黑醋栗香氣；也取決於成熟度：涼爽氣候的夏多內呈現青蘋果和檸檬，溫暖氣候的夏多內呈現桃子和鳳梨。","Oak appears when a wine has been fermented or matured, or both, in oak barrels; sometimes the label even says so. It brings flavours such as cedar, cloves, coconut, smoke and vanilla. Then there is the family called other, which is part of what makes wine so fascinating: grass, flowers, herbs, vegetables, earth, mushroom and leather. Keeping these three drawers separate in your mind stops you from mixing up, for example, a vanilla note from the barrel with the fruit of the grape.":"橡木風味出現在曾於橡木桶中發酵或熟成（或兩者皆有）的葡萄酒；有時酒標上甚至會註明。它帶來雪松、丁香、椰子、煙燻和香草等風味。再來是稱為「其他」的一類，葡萄酒之所以迷人，這也是原因之一：青草、花、香草植物、蔬菜、泥土、蘑菇和皮革。在腦中把這三個抽屜分開，就不會把來自橡木桶的香草氣息和葡萄的果香搞混。","So what is a style? It is the sum of all these characteristics: colour, structure, aromas and flavours. Compare two French whites, Chablis and Sauternes. Chablis is dry, high in acidity, light to medium-bodied, with green apple and lemon and no oak. Sauternes is sweet and full-bodied, with apricot, honey and vanilla from oak, held up by high acidity. Here is a tip: think of a style as an identity card for the wine, with a line for colour, five lines for structure and a line for aromas. Fill in every line, and you have described the wine.":"那麼風格是什麼？就是所有這些特徵的總和：顏色、結構、香氣與風味。比較兩款法國白酒，Chablis 和 Sauternes。Chablis 不甜、酸度高，酒體輕盈至中等，帶有青蘋果和檸檬，不經橡木桶。Sauternes 甜而酒體飽滿，帶有杏桃、蜂蜜和來自橡木桶的香草，並由高酸度支撐。這裡有個訣竅：把風格想成葡萄酒的身分證，一行寫顏色，五行寫結構，一行寫香氣。每一行都填好，你就完成了這款酒的描述。","Before the quiz, remember three things. First, there are three types of wine: still, from eight to fifteen percent alcohol; sparkling, with trapped carbon dioxide; and fortified, with added alcohol, from fifteen to twenty-two percent. Second, structure has five parts: sweetness from sugar, acidity that makes the mouth water, tannin from red grape skins that dries the mouth, alcohol, and body, meaning how mouth-filling the wine is. Third, aromas and flavours fall into three families, fruit, oak and other, and a wine's style is the sum of colour, structure and aromas.":"測驗之前，記住三件事。第一，葡萄酒有三種類型：靜態酒，酒精濃度百分之八到十五；氣泡酒，保留了二氧化碳；加烈酒，添加了酒精，酒精濃度百分之十五到二十二。第二，結構有五個部分：來自糖的甜度、讓人分泌唾液的酸度、來自黑葡萄果皮並讓口腔乾澀的單寧、酒精，以及酒體，也就是酒在口中的飽滿程度。第三，香氣與風味分為水果、橡木和其他三大類，而葡萄酒的風格就是顏色、結構和香氣的總和。","There are hundreds of grape varieties that can make wine, yet only a handful have built a reputation all over the world. The grape, or the blend of grapes, is one of the main things that decides a wine's style and quality. In this lesson we meet the four key white grapes: Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Pinot Grigio and Riesling. For each one we look at its structure, its typical aromas, whether it usually sees oak, and the places and wines it is famous for.":"能釀酒的葡萄品種有數百個，但只有少數幾個在全世界建立了名聲。品種或品種的混釀，是決定葡萄酒風格和品質的主要因素之一。這堂課要認識四大白葡萄品種：夏多內（Chardonnay）、白蘇維濃（Sauvignon Blanc）、灰皮諾（Pinot Grigio）和麗絲玲（Riesling）。每一個品種，我們都會看它的結構、典型香氣、通常是否經橡木桶，以及它聞名的產地和酒款。","First, Chardonnay, one of the most popular and widely planted grapes on earth. It makes dry wines, but in a whole range of styles, because it changes with the climate. In a cool climate, Chardonnay gives wines with high acidity, a light to medium body and aromas of green fruit and citrus: think apple and lemon. In a warm climate, the same grape gives medium acidity, a medium to full body and flavours of stone fruit and tropical fruit: peach, pineapple, even banana.":"首先是夏多內，全世界最受歡迎、種植最廣的品種之一。它釀出不甜的葡萄酒，但風格多樣，因為它會隨氣候而變。在涼爽氣候，夏多內釀出酸度高、酒體輕盈至中等的葡萄酒，帶有綠色水果和柑橘類香氣：想想蘋果和檸檬。在溫暖氣候，同一個品種則是酸度中等、酒體中等至飽滿，帶有核果和熱帶水果風味：桃子、鳳梨，甚至香蕉。","Chardonnay also takes well to oak, which adds notes of vanilla. It is the grape of the white wines of Burgundy, in France. These are medium-bodied, with high acidity, lemon and peach, and sometimes vanilla from oak. On a label you may see the region's French name, Bourgogne, or the name of a village, such as Mâcon, Meursault or Puligny-Montrachet. Chablis comes from the coolest part of Burgundy: high acidity, light to medium body, apple and lemon, and typically no oak at all.":"夏多內也很適合使用橡木桶，增添香草氣息。它是法國布根地白酒的品種。這些酒酒體中等、酸度高，帶有檸檬和桃子，有時還有來自橡木桶的香草。在酒標上，你可能看到產區的法文名稱 Bourgogne，或是村莊的名稱，例如 Mâcon、Meursault 或 Puligny-Montrachet。Chablis 來自布根地最涼爽的地區：酸度高，酒體輕盈至中等，蘋果和檸檬，通常完全不經橡木桶。","Outside France, Australia and California are well known for Chardonnay. A warm Californian example might be full-bodied, with ripe tropical fruit and vanilla from oak. Chardonnay is also one of the grapes of Champagne, where it is often blended with Pinot Noir. And a practical note: a full-bodied, oaked Chardonnay is served only lightly chilled, at around ten to thirteen degrees, so its richer flavours can show.":"在法國之外，澳洲和加州以夏多內聞名。溫暖的加州酒款可能酒體飽滿，帶有成熟的熱帶水果和來自橡木桶的香草。夏多內也是 Champagne 的品種之一，常與黑皮諾混釀。還有一個實用的提醒：酒體飽滿、經橡木桶的夏多內只要稍微冰鎮，大約十到十三度侍酒，才能展現它較濃郁的風味。","Second, Sauvignon Blanc. It makes dry wines with a pronounced intensity of aromas and refreshingly high acidity, and a light to medium body. Lift a glass and it practically jumps out at you. The fruit ranges from green apple to citrus such as grapefruit, and on to tropical fruit such as passion fruit. Alongside the fruit come herbaceous notes: asparagus, green bell pepper and freshly cut grass. That mix of zesty fruit and green notes is its signature.":"第二個是白蘇維濃。它釀出不甜的葡萄酒，香氣濃郁，酸度高而清爽，酒體輕盈至中等。一舉起酒杯，香氣簡直撲鼻而來。果香從青蘋果、葡萄柚等柑橘類，到百香果等熱帶水果都有。除了果香，還有草本氣息：蘆筍、青椒和剛割過的青草。這種鮮活果香與青綠氣息的組合，就是它的招牌。","In the winery, the aim is to protect those aromas. Sauvignon Blanc is often fermented in stainless steel tanks and is usually not matured in oak, because the wood would cover the grape's character. Two popular wines to know are New Zealand Sauvignon Blanc, from regions such as Marlborough, with grapefruit, lemon and grass, and Sancerre, from France's Loire Valley. Sancerre labels usually name the place, not the grape, so it is up to you to know that Sancerre means Sauvignon Blanc.":"在酒廠裡，目標是保護這些香氣。白蘇維濃常在不鏽鋼槽中發酵，而且通常不經橡木桶熟成，因為木頭會蓋過品種的特色。有兩款受歡迎的葡萄酒要認識：紐西蘭白蘇維濃，來自馬爾堡（Marlborough）等產區，帶有葡萄柚、檸檬和青草氣息；以及來自法國羅亞爾河谷的 Sancerre。Sancerre 的酒標通常寫的是地名，不是品種，所以你得自己知道 Sancerre 就是白蘇維濃。","Third, Pinot Grigio, a hugely popular grape. Its wines are typically dry, light-bodied, with medium to high acidity and simple flavours of pear and lemon. It is not about power or complexity; it is the fresh, easy white you might pour on a summer terrace. To keep that fruity freshness, Pinot Grigio is usually fermented in stainless steel and not matured in oak. It is mainly associated with Italy, in areas such as Veneto and Trentino, but it is grown in other countries too, and it is a classic example of a wine named after its grape.":"第三個是灰皮諾，極受歡迎的品種。它的葡萄酒通常不甜、酒體輕盈，酸度中等至高，帶有簡單的梨子和檸檬風味。它追求的不是力道或複雜度；它是那種夏日在露台上隨手倒一杯的清爽易飲白酒。為了保留果香與清爽感，灰皮諾通常在不鏽鋼槽中發酵，不經橡木桶熟成。它主要與義大利有關，例如唯內多（Veneto）和特倫提諾（Trentino）等地區，不過其他國家也有種植。它也是以品種命名的經典例子。","Fourth, Riesling, the acrobat of the group. It makes wines that range from dry, through medium, to sweet, but one thing never changes: every Riesling has high acidity. That acidity balances any sweetness, so even a sweet Riesling tastes fresh rather than sticky. The aromas are pronounced and can run from floral and green apple to citrus such as lime and lemon, and on to stone fruit such as peach and apricot. The body is light to medium. Like Sauvignon Blanc and Pinot Grigio, it is often fermented in stainless steel and not matured in oak.":"第四個是麗絲玲，這一組裡的特技演員。它釀出的葡萄酒從不甜、半甜到甜都有，但有一點永遠不變：每一款麗絲玲的酸度都高。酸度能平衡甜味，所以即使是甜型麗絲玲，喝起來也清爽而不黏膩。它的香氣濃郁，從花香和青蘋果，到萊姆和檸檬等柑橘類，再到桃子和杏桃等核果。酒體輕盈至中等。和白蘇維濃、灰皮諾一樣，它常在不鏽鋼槽中發酵，不經橡木桶熟成。","Riesling is the classic grape of Germany, where it is made in every style from dry to sweet. Some German Rieslings, from the Mosel for example, are medium-sweet, balanced by high acidity, and low in alcohol, sometimes around nine percent. Alsace in France and Australia, by contrast, make Riesling in a dry style, often with lime, lemon and blossom. So be careful: the word Riesling alone does not tell you how sweet the wine is. The place, or the wine's description, gives you the clue.":"麗絲玲是德國的經典品種，當地從不甜到甜的各種風格都有釀造。部分德國麗絲玲，例如來自 Mosel 的，是半甜型，由高酸度平衡，酒精濃度低，有時只有百分之九左右。法國的阿爾薩斯和澳洲則以不甜的風格釀造麗絲玲，常帶有萊姆、檸檬和花香。所以要小心：光看 Riesling 這個字，無法知道酒有多甜。產地或酒款的說明才是線索。","Now let's look at the four side by side. Three of them, Sauvignon Blanc, Pinot Grigio and Riesling, are usually fermented in stainless steel and kept away from oak, to protect their fruit. Chardonnay is the one that often meets oak. So if a white wine shows vanilla, Chardonnay is a very good first guess. On acidity, Sauvignon Blanc and Riesling are always high; Pinot Grigio is medium to high; Chardonnay depends on the climate.":"現在把四個品種放在一起看。其中三個，白蘇維濃、灰皮諾和麗絲玲，通常在不鏽鋼槽中發酵，不接觸橡木桶，以保護果香。夏多內則是常與橡木桶相遇的那一個。所以如果一款白酒有香草味，先猜夏多內準沒錯。酸度方面，白蘇維濃和麗絲玲始終很高；灰皮諾中等至高；夏多內則要看氣候。","Here is a memory tip: give each grape a personality. Chardonnay is the chameleon, changing with climate and oak, from apple and lemon to peach, pineapple and vanilla. Sauvignon Blanc is the green one, with grapefruit, passion fruit, grass and asparagus. Pinot Grigio is the quiet one, light and simple, with pear and lemon. And Riesling is the acrobat, from dry to sweet but always on the tightrope of high acidity, with flowers, lime and peach.":"這裡有個記憶訣竅：給每個品種一種個性。夏多內是變色龍，隨氣候和橡木桶而變，從蘋果和檸檬到桃子、鳳梨和香草。白蘇維濃是青綠派，帶有葡萄柚、百香果、青草和蘆筍。灰皮諾是安靜派，輕盈而簡單，帶有梨子和檸檬。麗絲玲則是特技演員，從不甜到甜都行，但永遠走在高酸度的鋼索上，帶有花香、萊姆和桃子。","Before the quiz, remember three things. First, Chardonnay changes with climate, apple and lemon when cool, peach and pineapple when warm, often takes oak and vanilla, and is the grape of white Burgundy and Chablis. Second, Sauvignon Blanc is aromatic, high in acidity, herbaceous and usually unoaked, famous in New Zealand and in Sancerre, while Pinot Grigio is light, simple and Italian in spirit, with pear and lemon. Third, Riesling can be dry, medium or sweet but always has high acidity, with Germany making every style and Alsace and Australia making it dry.":"測驗之前，記住三件事。第一，夏多內隨氣候而變，涼爽時是蘋果和檸檬，溫暖時是桃子和鳳梨，常經橡木桶而帶香草味，是布根地白酒和 Chablis 的品種。第二，白蘇維濃芳香、酸度高、帶草本氣息，通常不經橡木桶，以紐西蘭和 Sancerre 聞名；灰皮諾則輕盈、簡單，帶有義大利風情，有梨子和檸檬風味。第三，麗絲玲可以不甜、半甜或甜，但酸度始終很高；德國各種風格都有，阿爾薩斯和澳洲則釀成不甜的。","After the whites, it is time for the reds. In this lesson we meet the four key black grapes: Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot, Pinot Noir, and one grape with two names, Syrah or Shiraz. Remember that red wine takes its colour and tannin from the skins of black grapes, so with these varieties tannin becomes a big part of the story. For each grape we look at structure, typical aromas, oak, blending partners, and the places where it shines.":"白酒之後，輪到紅酒了。這堂課要認識四大黑葡萄品種：卡本內蘇維濃（Cabernet Sauvignon）、梅洛（Merlot）、黑皮諾（Pinot Noir），以及一個有兩個名字的品種，希哈（Syrah）或希拉茲（Shiraz）。還記得紅酒的顏色和單寧來自黑葡萄的果皮，所以談到這些品種，單寧就成了重頭戲。每一個品種，我們都會看結構、典型香氣、橡木桶、混釀搭檔，以及它大放異彩的產地。","First, Cabernet Sauvignon, planted widely around the world. It makes dry wines with high tannin and high acidity: you feel both the drying grip and the mouth-watering freshness at once. The body ranges from medium to full. Its signature aroma is blackcurrant, often with black cherry, plus herbaceous notes such as green bell pepper and mint. Many Cabernets are matured in oak, which adds cedar and vanilla. A full-bodied Cabernet from Napa Valley in California, for instance, might show intense blackcurrant and cedar.":"首先是卡本內蘇維濃，在世界各地廣泛種植。它釀出不甜的葡萄酒，單寧高、酸度高：乾澀的收斂感和令人分泌唾液的清爽感會同時出現。酒體中等至飽滿。它的招牌香氣是黑醋栗，常伴隨黑櫻桃，還有青椒和薄荷等草本氣息。許多卡本內都在橡木桶中熟成，增添雪松和香草氣息。例如加州納帕谷（Napa Valley）酒體飽滿的卡本內，可能帶有濃郁的黑醋栗和雪松氣息。","Because its tannin is so high, Cabernet Sauvignon is often blended with other grapes. In Bordeaux it is blended with Merlot, which adds softness and body. In Australia it is sometimes blended with Shiraz, which adds spicy aromas. Cabernet is also grown widely in California, Australia, Chile and South Africa, where it often appears on the label under its own name. In Bordeaux, the label shows the place instead, so you need to know the grapes behind it.":"因為單寧很高，卡本內蘇維濃常與其他品種混釀。在波爾多，它與梅洛混釀，梅洛增添柔順感和酒體。在澳洲，它有時與希拉茲混釀，增添香料氣息。卡本內在加州、澳洲、智利和南非也廣泛種植，在這些地方它常以自己的名字出現在酒標上。在波爾多，酒標標示的則是地名，所以你必須知道背後是哪些品種。","Second, Merlot. Its wines are generally dry and medium to full-bodied, with medium acidity and medium tannin. That makes it softer and rounder than Cabernet Sauvignon. The fruit can range from red fruit, strawberry and red plum, to black fruit, blackberry and black plum. Merlot is often matured in oak, which brings vanilla. In places such as Chile and California it is used to make soft, fruity, easy-drinking wines: smooth, with plum and blackberry.":"第二個是梅洛。它的葡萄酒通常不甜，酒體中等至飽滿，酸度中等、單寧中等，因此比卡本內蘇維濃更柔和圓潤。果香從草莓、紅李等紅色水果，到黑莓、黑李等黑色水果都有。梅洛常在橡木桶中熟成，帶來香草氣息。在智利和加州等地，它被用來釀造柔順、果味豐富、易飲的葡萄酒：順口，帶有李子和黑莓風味。","Merlot is Cabernet Sauvignon's classic partner, and the two complete each other. Merlot brings softness and body; Cabernet brings tannin and acidity. Bordeaux is the most famous region for this blend, and in some parts of Bordeaux, such as Saint-Émilion, Merlot is often the main grape. The Merlot and Cabernet blend is now made in many other places too. Think of them as a duo: one gives the backbone, the other gives the cushion.":"梅洛是卡本內蘇維濃的經典搭檔，兩者相輔相成。梅洛帶來柔順感和酒體；卡本內帶來單寧和酸度。波爾多是這種混釀最著名的產區，而在波爾多的某些地區，例如 Saint-Émilion，梅洛往往是主要品種。梅洛與卡本內的混釀如今在許多其他地方也有釀造。把它們想成二重唱：一個提供骨架，另一個提供軟墊。","Third, Pinot Noir, the most delicate of the four. Its wines tend to be dry and light to medium-bodied, with low to medium tannin and high acidity. The fruit is red: strawberry, red cherry and raspberry. Pinot Noir is often matured in oak, which can bring vanilla and smoke. If Cabernet is a deep, dark bass note, Pinot Noir is a lighter, brighter melody, fresh and elegant rather than powerful.":"第三個是黑皮諾，四者中最細緻的一個。它的葡萄酒多半不甜，酒體輕盈至中等，單寧低至中等，酸度高。果香是紅色水果：草莓、紅櫻桃和覆盆子。黑皮諾常在橡木桶中熟成，可以帶來香草和煙燻氣息。如果卡本內是低沉渾厚的貝斯音，黑皮諾就是更輕快明亮的旋律，清爽優雅，而不是強勁有力。","Pinot Noir is the grape of red Burgundy, in France; on labels you may see Bourgogne or the name of a village, such as Volnay. It is also the principal black grape of New Zealand, in regions such as Central Otago. When making red wine, Pinot Noir is not usually blended with other grapes. The big exception is Champagne, where Pinot Noir is often blended with Chardonnay, and the juice is kept away from the skins so the sparkling wine stays pale.":"黑皮諾是法國布根地紅酒的品種；在酒標上你可能看到 Bourgogne 或村莊的名稱，例如 Volnay。它也是紐西蘭最主要的黑葡萄品種，例如在中奧塔哥（Central Otago）等產區。釀造紅酒時，黑皮諾通常不與其他品種混釀。最大的例外是 Champagne，黑皮諾在那裡常與夏多內混釀，而且果汁不與果皮接觸，所以氣泡酒維持淺色。","Fourth, Syrah, or Shiraz. It is the same grape: it is called Syrah in France and Shiraz in Australia. It makes dry wines that are medium to full-bodied, with medium to high tannin and medium acidity. The typical flavours are black fruit, blackberry and black cherry, together with spice: black pepper and liquorice. Many are matured in oak, which adds vanilla or coconut. Black fruit plus black pepper is the clue to spot it.":"第四個是希哈，或稱希拉茲。它們是同一個品種：在法國叫 Syrah，在澳洲叫 Shiraz。它釀出不甜的葡萄酒，酒體中等至飽滿，單寧中等至高，酸度中等。典型風味是黑莓、黑櫻桃等黑色水果，加上香料：黑胡椒和甘草。許多都在橡木桶中熟成，增添香草或椰子氣息。黑色水果加黑胡椒，就是辨認它的線索。","Climate shapes its style strongly. In the Northern Rhône, in France, Syrah can make medium-bodied wines with fresh blackberry and black pepper. In warm regions of Australia, such as the Barossa Valley, Shiraz becomes full-bodied, with jammy black cherry and liquorice, and it can reach high levels of alcohol, sometimes around fifteen percent. Same grape, two climates, two styles: fresher and peppery in France, riper and richer in warm Australia.":"氣候對它的風格影響很大。在法國北隆河，希哈可以釀出酒體中等的葡萄酒，帶有新鮮黑莓和黑胡椒風味。在澳洲的溫暖產區，例如巴羅莎谷（Barossa Valley），希拉茲變得酒體飽滿，帶有果醬般的黑櫻桃和甘草風味，酒精濃度也可能很高，有時達到百分之十五左右。同一個品種，兩種氣候，兩種風格：法國的較清爽、帶胡椒味，溫暖的澳洲則更成熟、更濃郁。","Now let's line the four up. On tannin, Pinot Noir is low to medium, Merlot medium, Syrah medium to high, Cabernet Sauvignon high. On acidity, Cabernet and Pinot Noir are high, Merlot and Syrah medium. On fruit, Pinot Noir is red, Merlot moves from red to black, Cabernet and Syrah are black. And on service: medium and full-bodied reds are served at room temperature, around fifteen to eighteen degrees, but never warmed by a radiator.":"現在把四個品種排在一起。單寧方面，黑皮諾低至中等，梅洛中等，希哈中等至高，卡本內蘇維濃高。酸度方面，卡本內和黑皮諾高，梅洛和希哈中等。果香方面，黑皮諾是紅色水果，梅洛從紅色到黑色水果，卡本內和希哈是黑色水果。侍酒方面：酒體中等和飽滿的紅酒在室溫侍酒，大約十五到十八度，但絕不要放在暖氣旁加溫。","Here is a memory tip, a small fruit bowl. Blackcurrant with a sprig of mint: that is Cabernet Sauvignon. A soft, ripe plum: that is Merlot. A punnet of strawberries and raspberries: that is Pinot Noir. A blackberry dusted with black pepper: that is Syrah. When you taste a red, ask which corner of the fruit bowl it comes from, then check the tannin to confirm.":"這裡有個記憶訣竅：一個小小的水果盤。黑醋栗配上一枝薄荷：那是卡本內蘇維濃。一顆柔軟成熟的李子：那是梅洛。一盒草莓和覆盆子：那是黑皮諾。一顆撒了黑胡椒的黑莓：那是希哈。品嚐紅酒時，先問它來自水果盤的哪個角落，再用單寧確認。","Before the quiz, remember three things. First, Cabernet Sauvignon is high in tannin and acidity, with blackcurrant, green bell pepper, mint and cedar from oak, and is blended with Merlot in Bordeaux, which adds softness and body. Second, Merlot is softer, with medium acidity and tannin and red to black plum fruit, while Pinot Noir is light, high in acidity and low in tannin, with strawberry and raspberry, the grape of red Burgundy and New Zealand. Third, Syrah in France and Shiraz in Australia are one grape, with blackberry and black pepper, medium in the Northern Rhône and full and jammy in warm Australia.":"測驗之前，記住三件事。第一，卡本內蘇維濃單寧和酸度高，帶有黑醋栗、青椒、薄荷和來自橡木桶的雪松氣息；在波爾多與梅洛混釀，梅洛增添柔順感和酒體。第二，梅洛較柔和，酸度和單寧中等，帶有紅李到黑李的果香；黑皮諾則輕盈、酸度高、單寧低，帶有草莓和覆盆子，是布根地紅酒和紐西蘭的品種。第三，法國的希哈和澳洲的希拉茲是同一個品種，帶有黑莓和黑胡椒，在北隆河酒體中等，在溫暖的澳洲則飽滿而有果醬感。","You now know the eight key grapes. But walk into a wine shop in Europe and you will often not see their names at all. In Europe, many wines are named after the region where they are made, and the label expects you to know which grape is inside. In this lesson we connect the grapes to six famous French wines: three whites, Sancerre, Chablis and white Burgundy; two reds, red Burgundy and Bordeaux; and one sparkling wine, Champagne. Learn these, and a wine list suddenly becomes much easier to read.":"現在你認識了八個主要品種。但走進歐洲的酒專，往往完全看不到這些名字。在歐洲，許多葡萄酒以產區命名，酒標預設你知道裡面是哪個品種。這堂課要把這些品種和六款著名的法國葡萄酒連結起來：三款白酒，Sancerre、Chablis 和布根地白酒；兩款紅酒，布根地紅酒和波爾多；以及一款氣泡酒，Champagne。學會這些，酒單一下子就好讀多了。","Let's start with Sancerre, from the Loire Valley in France. It is made from Sauvignon Blanc. Sancerre is a dry, medium-bodied white wine, typically unoaked, with high acidity. Its aromas are pronounced: green fruit such as apple, and herbaceous notes such as grass. So everything you learned about Sauvignon Blanc applies: a lively, aromatic, refreshing wine, kept away from oak to protect its fresh fruit and its green character.":"先從法國羅亞爾河谷的 Sancerre 開始。它以白蘇維濃釀造。Sancerre 是不甜、酒體中等的白酒，通常不經橡木桶，酸度高。香氣濃郁：蘋果等綠色水果，以及青草等草本氣息。所以你學過關於白蘇維濃的一切都適用：一款活潑、芳香、清爽的葡萄酒，不接觸橡木桶，以保護新鮮果香和青綠特色。","Next, Chablis. It is made from Chardonnay, and it comes from the coolest part of Burgundy. Remember the thermometer from the first lesson: cool climate means less sugar and more acidity. So Chablis is a dry, light to medium-bodied white with high acidity and aromas of green apple and lemon. It is unoaked, so there is no vanilla, just crisp fruit and freshness. Chablis is the perfect example of cool-climate Chardonnay.":"接著是 Chablis。它以夏多內釀造，來自布根地最涼爽的地區。還記得第一堂課的溫度計嗎：涼爽氣候代表糖分較少、酸度較高。所以 Chablis 是不甜、酒體輕盈至中等的白酒，酸度高，帶有青蘋果和檸檬香氣。它不經橡木桶，所以沒有香草味，只有清脆的果香和清爽感。Chablis 是涼爽氣候夏多內的完美例子。","Sancerre and Chablis are easy to mix up: both are dry, French, high in acidity, unoaked and full of green apple. How do you tell them apart? Look at the extra notes. Sancerre, being Sauvignon Blanc, has more pronounced aromas and that herbaceous, grassy edge, and a medium body. Chablis, being cool Chardonnay, is more restrained, with apple and lemon, and its body can be lighter.":"Sancerre 和 Chablis 很容易搞混：都不甜、來自法國、酸度高、不經橡木桶，而且滿是青蘋果香。怎麼分辨？看額外的氣息。Sancerre 是白蘇維濃，香氣更濃郁，帶有草本、青草的特色，酒體中等。Chablis 是涼爽氣候的夏多內，較為內斂，帶有蘋果和檸檬，酒體可能更輕盈。","Now Burgundy, or Bourgogne in French, a region that makes both white and red wines. The French name often appears on labels of both colours, and some labels show the name of a village within the region instead, such as Mâcon, Meursault or Puligny-Montrachet for whites, or Volnay for reds. The rule to remember is wonderfully simple: in Burgundy, the whites are Chardonnay and the reds are Pinot Noir.":"接著是布根地，法文是 Bourgogne，一個同時出產白酒和紅酒的產區。這個法文名稱常出現在兩種顏色的酒標上，有些酒標則標示產區內的村莊名稱，白酒例如 Mâcon、Meursault 或 Puligny-Montrachet，紅酒例如 Volnay。要記住的規則簡單得很：在布根地，白酒是夏多內，紅酒是黑皮諾。","White Burgundy is dry and medium-bodied, with high acidity. It can be oaked or unoaked. Compared with Chablis, which comes from the coolest corner of the region, white Burgundy often shows riper fruit: still citrus such as lemon, but also stone fruit such as peach. When oak has been used, you may also find notes of vanilla. So think of white Burgundy as a step up in ripeness from Chablis, sometimes with a touch of oak.":"布根地白酒不甜、酒體中等，酸度高，可以經橡木桶，也可以不經。與來自產區最涼爽角落的 Chablis 相比，布根地白酒常呈現更成熟的果香：仍有檸檬等柑橘類水果，但也有桃子等核果。使用橡木桶時，還可能出現香草氣息。所以可以把布根地白酒想成成熟度比 Chablis 高一階，有時帶一點橡木味。","Red Burgundy is made from Pinot Noir and is dry. It tends to have low to medium tannin, a light to medium body and high acidity. Its flavours are of red fruit, raspberry and red cherry, sometimes with vanilla and smoke from oak. It is an elegant, fresh red, the opposite of a powerful, tannic one. And that powerful, tannic red is exactly where we go next.":"布根地紅酒以黑皮諾釀造，是不甜的。它通常單寧低至中等，酒體輕盈至中等，酸度高。風味是覆盆子和紅櫻桃等紅色水果，有時有來自橡木桶的香草和煙燻氣息。它是優雅清爽的紅酒，和強勁、單寧高的紅酒正好相反。而那種強勁、單寧高的紅酒，正是我們的下一站。","Bordeaux is a region in the south-west of France, and its wines are most often red. Red Bordeaux is typically a blend of Cabernet Sauvignon and Merlot. Remember the duo: Cabernet brings tannin and acidity, Merlot brings softness and body. As in Burgundy, the label shows the region, or an area within it, not the grapes. Bordeaux also makes a famous sweet white, Sauternes, which we meet in the next lesson.":"波爾多是法國西南部的產區，葡萄酒以紅酒居多。波爾多紅酒通常是卡本內蘇維濃與梅洛的混釀。還記得那組二重唱：卡本內帶來單寧和酸度，梅洛帶來柔順感和酒體。和布根地一樣，酒標標示的是產區或其中的某個地區，而不是品種。波爾多還出產著名的甜白酒 Sauternes，下一堂課會談到。","Red Bordeaux is dry and medium to full-bodied, with high acidity and high tannin. Its aromas are of black fruit, blackberry and blackcurrant, with cedar notes from oak. It is one of the classic examples of a high-tannin red: you clearly feel that drying sensation in your mouth. On a wine list, you might see names of areas within Bordeaux, such as Saint-Émilion, where the blend is often led by Merlot, or Margaux, where you would expect concentrated blackcurrant, cedar and firm tannin.":"波爾多紅酒不甜，酒體中等至飽滿，酸度高、單寧高。香氣是黑莓和黑醋栗等黑色水果，並有來自橡木桶的雪松氣息。它是高單寧紅酒的經典例子之一：口腔的乾澀感非常明顯。在酒單上，你可能看到波爾多產區內的地區名稱，例如混釀常以梅洛為主的 Saint-Émilion，或是可以期待濃縮黑醋栗、雪松和紮實單寧的 Margaux。","Finally, Champagne, the most famous sparkling wine in the world, from the Champagne region in France. It is made from Chardonnay and Pinot Noir, often blended together. Yes, Pinot Noir is a black grape, but its juice is colourless, so if the skins are kept away from the juice, the wine stays pale. And the bubbles, as you know, come from carbon dioxide made by fermentation and kept trapped in the wine.":"最後是 Champagne，全世界最著名的氣泡酒，來自法國的 Champagne 產區。它以夏多內和黑皮諾釀造，兩者常常混釀。沒錯，黑皮諾是黑葡萄，但果汁無色，只要不讓果皮接觸果汁，酒就維持淺色。至於氣泡，你已經知道，來自發酵產生、被保留在酒中的二氧化碳。","Champagne is typically dry, with high acidity, aromas of green fruit and citrus, apple and lemon, and notes of toasted bread. That toasty note is what sets it apart from simpler, fruitier sparkling wines. Champagne is served well chilled, at six to ten degrees, and the bottle is opened carefully, with a hand always on the cork, as we will see in the lesson on service.":"Champagne 通常不甜、酸度高，帶有綠色水果和柑橘類香氣，也就是蘋果和檸檬，以及烤麵包氣息。正是這股烘烤氣息，讓它有別於較簡單、果味較重的氣泡酒。Champagne 要充分冰鎮，在六到十度侍酒，開瓶時要小心，手要一直按住軟木塞，侍酒那堂課會再說明。","Here is a memory tip that works wonders. Sancerre and Sauvignon both start with S. Chablis and Chardonnay both start with Ch. Burgundy is one region with two colours: white Chardonnay, red Pinot Noir. Bordeaux is the duo: Cabernet Sauvignon and Merlot. And Champagne borrows one grape from each Burgundy colour: Chardonnay and Pinot Noir.":"這裡有個非常好用的記憶訣竅。Sancerre 和 Sauvignon 都以 S 開頭。Chablis 和 Chardonnay 都以 Ch 開頭。布根地是一個產區、兩種顏色：白的是夏多內，紅的是黑皮諾。波爾多是二重唱：卡本內蘇維濃和梅洛。Champagne 則向布根地的兩種顏色各借一個品種：夏多內和黑皮諾。","Before the quiz, remember three things. First, Sancerre is dry, unoaked Sauvignon Blanc from the Loire with apple and grass, and Chablis is dry, unoaked Chardonnay from the coolest part of Burgundy with apple and lemon, both high in acidity. Second, in Burgundy, or Bourgogne, whites are Chardonnay with lemon, peach and sometimes oak, and reds are Pinot Noir, light, fresh and fruity with raspberry and red cherry, while red Bordeaux is a high-tannin blend of Cabernet Sauvignon and Merlot with blackcurrant and cedar. Third, Champagne is a dry sparkling wine from Chardonnay and Pinot Noir, with apple, lemon and toasted bread.":"測驗之前，記住三件事。第一，Sancerre 是羅亞爾河不甜、不經橡木桶的白蘇維濃，帶有蘋果和青草；Chablis 是布根地最涼爽地區不甜、不經橡木桶的夏多內，帶有蘋果和檸檬；兩者酸度都高。第二，在布根地（Bourgogne），白酒是夏多內，帶有檸檬、桃子，有時有橡木味；紅酒是黑皮諾，輕盈、清爽、果味豐富，帶有覆盆子和紅櫻桃；波爾多紅酒則是卡本內蘇維濃與梅洛的高單寧混釀，帶有黑醋栗和雪松。第三，Champagne 是以夏多內和黑皮諾釀造的不甜氣泡酒，帶有蘋果、檸檬和烤麵包氣息。","In this lesson we meet twelve more famous wines. They are not made from the eight key grapes, but you will find them on wine lists everywhere, so they are well worth knowing. For each one, keep four things in mind: the country, the type, meaning still, sparkling or fortified, the colour, and a few key style traits. We will travel in small groups: a sweet white and a rosé, three French reds, an Italian and a Spanish red, two sparkling wines, and finally two fortified wines.":"這堂課要再認識十二款著名的葡萄酒。它們不是以八個主要品種釀造，但到處的酒單上都看得到，所以很值得認識。每一款都記住四件事：國家、類型（靜態酒、氣泡酒或加烈酒）、顏色，以及幾項主要的風格特徵。我們分成幾小組來看：一款甜白酒和一款粉紅酒、三款法國紅酒、一款義大利紅酒和一款西班牙紅酒、兩款氣泡酒，最後是兩款加烈酒。","We start in Bordeaux with Sauternes, a sweet white wine. It is full-bodied, with flavours of stone fruit such as apricot, honey, and vanilla from oak. Above all, it has high acidity, which balances all that sugar and stops it from tasting cloying. Sauternes is made from grapes so rich in sugar that the yeast stop before they have eaten it all. It is served well chilled, at six to eight degrees, among the coldest of all wines.":"我們從波爾多的 Sauternes 開始，這是一款甜白酒。它酒體飽滿，帶有杏桃等核果、蜂蜜和來自橡木桶的香草風味。最重要的是，它有高酸度，能平衡大量的糖分，讓酒不會膩口。Sauternes 以糖分極高的葡萄釀造，酵母還沒把糖吃完就停止了。它要充分冰鎮，在六到八度侍酒，是侍酒溫度最低的葡萄酒之一。","Next, White Zinfandel. Despite its name, it is not a white wine: it is a rosé, from California. It is unoaked, with a medium level of sweetness and fresh red fruit flavours of strawberry and raspberry. It is also the classic example of a low-alcohol wine, often around ten and a half percent. So whenever the exam asks for a low-alcohol wine, or a rosé with some sweetness, White Zinfandel should come to mind.":"接著是 White Zinfandel。雖然名字裡有 White，它卻不是白酒：它是加州的粉紅酒。它不經橡木桶，半甜，帶有草莓和覆盆子等新鮮紅色水果風味。它也是低酒精濃度葡萄酒的經典例子，通常在百分之十點五左右。所以每當考試問到低酒精濃度的葡萄酒，或是帶有甜味的粉紅酒，就該想到 White Zinfandel。","Now three French reds, and the easiest way to remember them is to line them up by body, from lightest to fullest: Beaujolais, then Côtes du Rhône, then Châteauneuf-du-Pape. Beaujolais is a dry, light-bodied red, unoaked, with fresh red fruit, raspberry and red cherry, and low tannin. It is the standard example of a light, low-tannin red, and because it is so light it is served lightly chilled, at around thirteen degrees.":"現在是三款法國紅酒，最簡單的記法是依酒體排列，從最輕盈到最飽滿：Beaujolais，然後 Côtes du Rhône，再來是 Châteauneuf-du-Pape。Beaujolais 是不甜、酒體輕盈的紅酒，不經橡木桶，帶有覆盆子和紅櫻桃等新鮮紅色水果，單寧低。它是輕盈、低單寧紅酒的標準例子，而且因為非常輕盈，要稍微冰鎮，在大約十三度侍酒。","Côtes du Rhône is a dry, medium-bodied red with red fruit, strawberry and red plum, and a spicy touch of white pepper. It can be oaked or unoaked. Châteauneuf-du-Pape, also from the Rhône, is the big one: dry, full-bodied and high in alcohol, often around fourteen and a half percent, with strawberry and cloves from oak. It is the go-to example of a high-alcohol wine.":"Côtes du Rhône 是不甜、酒體中等的紅酒，帶有草莓和紅李等紅色水果，以及一絲白胡椒的香料氣息。它可以經橡木桶，也可以不經。同樣來自隆河的 Châteauneuf-du-Pape 則是大塊頭：不甜、酒體飽滿、酒精濃度高，通常在百分之十四點五左右，帶有草莓和來自橡木桶的丁香風味。它是高酒精濃度葡萄酒的首選例子。","Crossing into Italy, we find Chianti, from Tuscany; on a list you may see Chianti Classico. It is a dry, medium-bodied red with high tannin and high acidity, so it feels both drying and very fresh. Its flavours are of red fruit, red cherry and red plum, with dried herb notes and sometimes cloves from oak. Remember those dried herbs: they are part of what makes Chianti recognisable.":"跨進義大利，我們遇到來自托斯卡尼的 Chianti；在酒單上你可能看到 Chianti Classico。它是不甜、酒體中等的紅酒，單寧高、酸度高，所以既讓口腔乾澀，又非常清爽。風味是紅櫻桃和紅李等紅色水果，帶有乾燥香草氣息，有時還有來自橡木桶的丁香。記住這些乾燥香草：Chianti 之所以容易辨認，它們功不可沒。","Then Spain, and Rioja. It is a dry red, medium to full-bodied, typically with red fruit, especially strawberry, and vanilla from oak. Strawberry and vanilla together are its signature; on a list you may see Rioja Crianza, described with exactly those notes. To tell Chianti and Rioja apart: both show red fruit, but Chianti is built on high tannin, high acidity and dried herbs, while Rioja is rounder and marked by vanilla. And of course, Chianti is Italian, Rioja Spanish.":"接著是西班牙和 Rioja。它是不甜的紅酒，酒體中等至飽滿，通常帶有紅色水果，尤其是草莓，以及來自橡木桶的香草。草莓加香草就是它的招牌；在酒單上你可能看到 Rioja Crianza，描述的正是這些氣息。分辨 Chianti 和 Rioja 的方法：兩者都有紅色水果，但 Chianti 以高單寧、高酸度和乾燥香草為骨幹，Rioja 則較圓潤，並帶有香草的印記。當然，Chianti 來自義大利，Rioja 來自西班牙。","Now the bubbles. Alongside Champagne, two sparkling wines are very well known. Prosecco, from Italy, is light-bodied, with green fruit such as pear and floral aromas; it can be dry or medium in sweetness. Cava, from Spain, is dry, with flavours of green fruit and citrus, apple and lemon. So Prosecco means pear and flowers, dry or medium; Cava means apple and lemon, dry; and Champagne adds that note of toasted bread.":"現在輪到氣泡了。除了 Champagne，還有兩款非常有名的氣泡酒。義大利的 Prosecco 酒體輕盈，帶有梨子等綠色水果和花香；可以不甜或半甜。西班牙的 Cava 不甜，帶有綠色水果和柑橘類風味，也就是蘋果和檸檬。所以 Prosecco 代表梨子和花香，不甜或半甜；Cava 代表蘋果和檸檬，不甜；Champagne 則多了烤麵包氣息。","Finally, the fortified wines. Remember that fortified wines have had alcohol added, so they range from fifteen to twenty-two percent. Sherry is a fortified white wine from Spain. It is made in a range of styles and can be dry, medium or sweet. So, as with Riesling, the name alone does not tell you how sweet the wine is: you need to know the style. If the alcohol is added before the yeast finish, the yeast die and the wine stays sweet.":"最後是加烈酒。還記得加烈酒添加了酒精，所以酒精濃度從百分之十五到百分之二十二。Sherry 是西班牙的白色加烈酒。它有多種風格，可以不甜、半甜或甜。所以和麗絲玲一樣，光看名稱無法知道酒有多甜：必須知道風格。如果在酵母完成發酵前加入酒精，酵母會死亡，酒就保有甜味。","Port is a fortified wine from Portugal. It is sweet and high in alcohol, often around twenty percent, and it too comes in a range of styles. Typically it is red and full-bodied, with high tannin and black fruit flavours such as blackberry. Port and Sherry are easy to keep apart: Port is Portuguese, usually red and always sweet; Sherry is Spanish, white and anywhere from dry to sweet.":"Port 是葡萄牙的加烈酒。它甜而酒精濃度高，通常在百分之二十左右，同樣有多種風格。它通常是紅色、酒體飽滿，單寧高，帶有黑莓等黑色水果風味。Port 和 Sherry 很好區分：Port 來自葡萄牙，通常是紅色，而且一定是甜的；Sherry 來自西班牙，是白色，從不甜到甜都有。","Here is a memory tip: a quick tour around the table by country. France gives us Sauternes and the three reds, Beaujolais, Côtes du Rhône and Châteauneuf-du-Pape. Italy gives a pair, Chianti and Prosecco. Spain gives a trio, Rioja, Cava and Sherry. Portugal gives Port, and California gives White Zinfandel. And watch the three classic traps: White Zinfandel is pink, not white; Sauternes is sweet, even though it comes from a region famous for dry reds; and Sherry can be bone dry.":"這裡有個記憶訣竅：按國家繞桌子走一圈。法國給我們 Sauternes 和三款紅酒：Beaujolais、Côtes du Rhône 和 Châteauneuf-du-Pape。義大利給一對：Chianti 和 Prosecco。西班牙給三款：Rioja、Cava 和 Sherry。葡萄牙給 Port，加州給 White Zinfandel。還要留意三個經典陷阱：White Zinfandel 是粉紅色的，不是白色；Sauternes 是甜的，儘管它來自以不甜紅酒聞名的產區；而 Sherry 可以完全不甜。","Before the quiz, remember three things. First, Sauternes is a sweet, full-bodied white from Bordeaux with apricot, honey and high acidity, and White Zinfandel is a medium-sweet, low-alcohol rosé from California with strawberry. Second, the reds line up by body: Beaujolais light and low in tannin, Côtes du Rhône medium with white pepper, Châteauneuf-du-Pape full and high in alcohol; Chianti from Italy has high tannin, high acidity and dried herbs, and Rioja from Spain has strawberry and vanilla. Third, Prosecco is Italian, pear and flowers, dry or medium; Cava is Spanish and dry; Sherry is Spanish, white, dry to sweet; Port is Portuguese, sweet, red and tannic.":"測驗之前，記住三件事。第一，Sauternes 是波爾多甜而酒體飽滿的白酒，帶有杏桃、蜂蜜和高酸度；White Zinfandel 是加州半甜、低酒精濃度的粉紅酒，帶有草莓風味。第二，紅酒依酒體排列：Beaujolais 輕盈、單寧低，Côtes du Rhône 中等、帶白胡椒，Châteauneuf-du-Pape 飽滿、酒精濃度高；義大利的 Chianti 單寧高、酸度高、帶乾燥香草，西班牙的 Rioja 帶有草莓和香草。第三，Prosecco 來自義大利，梨子和花香，不甜或半甜；Cava 來自西班牙，不甜；Sherry 來自西班牙，白色，從不甜到甜；Port 來自葡萄牙，甜、紅色、單寧高。","Wine is surrounded by traditions about how to keep it and how to serve it. Whatever their history, they should all have one goal: to put the wine in the glass in the best possible condition. In this lesson we see how to store wine, how to keep an opened bottle fresh, which temperature suits each style, how to open still and sparkling wines safely, which glasses to use, and what to check before you pour.":"關於葡萄酒該怎麼保存、怎麼侍酒，有許多傳統。不論這些傳統的由來如何，都應該只有一個目標：讓葡萄酒以最佳狀態進到杯中。這堂課要看如何保存葡萄酒、如何讓已開瓶的酒保鮮、每種風格適合什麼溫度、如何安全地開靜態酒和氣泡酒、該用哪種酒杯，以及倒酒前要檢查什麼。","Let's start with storage. A wine stored badly first loses some of its character, and in the end it can develop real faults. Three rules prevent this. Rule one: for long-term storage, keep wine at a cool, constant temperature. Extremes of cold and heat, and big swings in temperature, can damage it. Rule two: keep wine away from strong sunshine and bright artificial light. Both the light and the heat it brings can make a wine lose its fruity character.":"先從保存開始。保存不當的葡萄酒會先失去一些特色，最後可能產生真正的缺陷。三條規則可以避免。規則一：長期保存時，讓葡萄酒處於涼爽、恆定的溫度。過冷、過熱以及劇烈的溫度變化都可能損害它。規則二：讓葡萄酒遠離強烈的陽光和明亮的人工光線。光線和隨之而來的熱，都可能讓葡萄酒失去果味。","Rule three is about the closure. If a bottle is sealed with a cork, store it on its side. That way the cork stays in contact with the wine and stays moist. If the cork dries out, it can let air into the bottle, and air makes the wine lose its fruit. Bottles with a screwcap have no such problem, and can be stored standing up. So, in short: cool and steady, out of the light, and corks lying down.":"規則三和封瓶方式有關。如果酒瓶用軟木塞封瓶，就要橫放保存。這樣軟木塞能與酒液接觸，保持濕潤。如果軟木塞乾掉，可能讓空氣進入瓶中，而空氣會讓酒失去果味。旋蓋酒瓶沒有這個問題，可以直立保存。簡單來說：涼爽穩定、避開光線、軟木塞的酒橫放。","What about a bottle you have already opened? As soon as wine meets the air, it slowly begins to go stale. The simplest help is to put the cork back in and keep the bottle in the fridge: it will stay fresher for longer. To go further, there are simple systems that keep the wine away from air. Vacuum systems use a small pump to remove the air from inside the bottle. Blanket systems pump a gas into the bottle that pushes the air out; the gas does no harm to the wine.":"已經開瓶的酒呢？葡萄酒一接觸空氣，就會慢慢開始走味。最簡單的辦法是把軟木塞塞回去，並把酒瓶放進冰箱：這樣能保鮮更久。想更進一步，有一些簡單的系統可以隔絕空氣。真空系統用小幫浦抽出瓶內的空氣。氣體覆蓋系統則把氣體灌入瓶中，將空氣排出；這種氣體不會傷害葡萄酒。","Now service temperatures. As a rule, white, rosé and sparkling wines are served chilled, while reds are served at room temperature or lightly chilled. These are recommendations, not laws: if someone prefers their wine at a different temperature, a good host respects that. Let's go from coldest to warmest. Sweet wines such as Sauternes are served well chilled, at six to eight degrees Celsius. Sparkling wines such as Champagne are also well chilled, at six to ten degrees.":"接著是侍酒溫度。一般而言，白酒、粉紅酒和氣泡酒要冰鎮後侍酒，紅酒則在室溫或稍微冰鎮後侍酒。這些是建議，不是定律：如果有人偏好不同的溫度，好的主人會尊重對方。我們從最冰到最溫來看。Sauternes 等甜酒要充分冰鎮，在攝氏六到八度侍酒。Champagne 等氣泡酒同樣要充分冰鎮，在六到十度侍酒。","Light and medium-bodied whites and rosés, such as Pinot Grigio, are served chilled, at seven to ten degrees. Full-bodied whites, such as an oaked Chardonnay, are served lightly chilled, at ten to thirteen degrees, so their richer flavours can show. Light-bodied reds, such as Beaujolais, are also served lightly chilled, at around thirteen degrees. And medium to full-bodied reds, such as Shiraz, are served at room temperature, fifteen to eighteen degrees.":"灰皮諾等酒體輕盈和中等的白酒與粉紅酒，要冰鎮至七到十度侍酒。經橡木桶的夏多內等酒體飽滿的白酒，則稍微冰鎮至十到十三度，才能展現較濃郁的風味。Beaujolais 等酒體輕盈的紅酒也要稍微冰鎮，大約十三度。希拉茲等酒體中等至飽滿的紅酒，則在室溫十五到十八度侍酒。","Be careful with that phrase, room temperature. With air conditioning and central heating, rooms vary a lot, so the range of degrees is the better guide. If a red is too cold, never warm it next to a radiator: sudden heat can damage its flavours. Simply place it in the room where it will be served and let it warm up naturally. And to keep a white, rosé or sparkling wine cold until the bottle is finished, use an insulated container or an ice bucket. With a bucket, fill it with cold water as well as ice: ice alone works far less efficiently.":"要小心「室溫」這個說法。有了冷氣和暖氣，室內溫度差異很大，所以溫度範圍才是更好的依據。如果紅酒太冰，絕不要放在暖氣旁加溫：突然的高溫會破壞風味。只要把它放在要飲用的房間，讓它自然回溫就好。而要讓白酒、粉紅酒或氣泡酒在喝完之前都保持低溫，可以使用保冷容器或冰桶。用冰桶時，除了冰塊還要加冷水：只用冰塊的效率差得多。","Next, opening the bottle. For a still wine with a cork, first remove the top of the capsule, using a capsule cutter or the small knife on a waiter's friend corkscrew, and clean the neck of the bottle with a cloth. Then centre the corkscrew in the middle of the cork, screw it in and draw the cork out gently. Once the cork is out, wipe round the inside and outside of the neck with the cloth.":"接下來是開瓶。軟木塞封瓶的靜態酒，先用割箔刀或侍者開瓶器上的小刀除去瓶口封套的頂部，並用布把瓶口擦乾淨。接著把開瓶器對準軟木塞中心旋入，輕輕拔出軟木塞。軟木塞拔出後，用布把瓶口內外擦一圈。","Sparkling wine needs much more care, because the bottle is under a lot of pressure. Chilling reduces that pressure, but even when the wine is cold, the cork can fly out and injure someone. So here is the golden rule: from the moment you loosen the wire cage, the cork stays under your hand until it is safely out. Remove the foil and loosen the cage, keeping the cork covered. Hold the bottle at an angle, with the cork in one hand and the base in the other. Then turn the bottle, not the cork.":"氣泡酒需要小心得多，因為瓶內壓力很大。冰鎮可以降低壓力，但即使酒是冰的，軟木塞仍可能飛出去傷到人。所以黃金法則是：從鬆開鐵絲罩的那一刻起，手要一直按住軟木塞，直到它安全取出。除去錫箔、鬆開鐵絲罩，同時蓋住軟木塞。把酒瓶傾斜拿著，一手握住軟木塞，一手握住瓶底。然後轉動酒瓶，而不是軟木塞。","Hold the cork firmly so the pressure does not push it out too fast. Controlled like this, the gas escapes with a quiet little sigh, rather than a loud pop, and not a drop of wine is lost. That quiet sigh is the sign of a professional. A loud pop and a fountain of foam might look festive, but it wastes wine and can be dangerous.":"穩穩握住軟木塞，別讓壓力太快把它推出來。這樣控制之下，氣體會以輕輕的一聲嘆息釋放，而不是響亮的「砰」一聲，一滴酒都不會浪費。這聲輕嘆正是專業的象徵。響亮的「砰」聲和噴湧的泡沫看起來也許很有節慶氣氛，但既浪費酒，又可能造成危險。","Now the glasses. There are hundreds of designs, but the best ones share one feature: the bowl narrows towards the rim. This concentrates the aromas inside the glass, so you can appreciate them better. Typically, red wine glasses are slightly larger than white wine glasses, and sparkling wines are served in flutes. Glasses must be completely clean, because dirt or a trace of detergent can spoil a wine, and they should always be polished before use to remove any lingering dirt or finger marks.":"現在來看酒杯。酒杯的款式有數百種，但最好的都有一個共同點：杯身向杯口收窄。這能把香氣集中在杯內，讓你更容易欣賞。一般而言，紅酒杯比白酒杯稍大，氣泡酒則用笛型杯。酒杯必須徹底乾淨，因為髒汙或殘留的清潔劑會破壞葡萄酒；使用前也一定要擦亮，去除殘留的髒汙或指紋。","Last, a quick check before you serve. Look at the wine: any haziness could mean it is faulty, and there should be no bits floating in it. Then smell it: it should not smell stale, nor of wet cardboard or vinegar. Here is a tip to remember the whole lesson: think of three enemies of wine, heat, light and air. Storage keeps out heat and light, the cork lying down and the vacuum pump keep out air, and the right temperature lets the wine show its best.":"最後，侍酒前快速檢查一下。看看酒：只要混濁，就可能有缺陷，酒中也不應該有漂浮物。再聞一聞：不應該有不新鮮的氣味，也不應該有濕紙板味或醋味。這裡有個記住整堂課的訣竅：想想葡萄酒的三個敵人，熱、光和空氣。妥善保存能擋住熱和光，橫放的軟木塞和真空幫浦能擋住空氣，合適的溫度則讓葡萄酒展現最好的一面。","Before the quiz, remember three things. First, store wine cool and steady, away from strong light, with corked bottles on their side, and keep opened wine in the fridge with the cork in, or protect it with a vacuum or blanket system. Second, sweet and sparkling wines are served well chilled, light and medium whites and rosés chilled, full whites and light reds lightly chilled, and medium to full reds at room temperature, fifteen to eighteen degrees. Third, when opening sparkling wine, keep a hand on the cork from the moment the cage is loosened and turn the bottle; then pour into clean, polished glasses that narrow at the rim.":"測驗之前，記住三件事。第一，葡萄酒要保存在涼爽穩定、遠離強光的地方，軟木塞封瓶的酒要橫放；已開瓶的酒塞回軟木塞放進冰箱，或用真空系統、氣體覆蓋系統保護。第二，甜酒和氣泡酒要充分冰鎮，酒體輕盈和中等的白酒與粉紅酒要冰鎮，酒體飽滿的白酒和輕盈的紅酒稍微冰鎮，酒體中等至飽滿的紅酒則在室溫十五到十八度侍酒。第三，開氣泡酒時，從鬆開鐵絲罩的那一刻起手就按住軟木塞，並轉動酒瓶；然後倒進乾淨、擦亮、杯口收窄的酒杯。","Wine can be a marvellous partner at the table. Pairing food and wine is often presented as a complicated art, but at this level it comes down to two simple ideas: personal preference, and a handful of predictable reactions between food and wine. In this lesson we look at both. We meet the main features of food, sweetness, umami, salt, acidity, flavour intensity, fat and chilli heat, and we see what each one does to a wine.":"葡萄酒可以是餐桌上的絕佳夥伴。餐酒搭配常被說成一門複雜的藝術，但在這個級別，可以歸結為兩個簡單的概念：個人喜好，以及食物與葡萄酒之間少數幾種可預測的反應。這堂課兩者都會談到。我們會認識食物的主要特性：甜味、鮮味、鹽、酸、風味強度、脂肪和辣味，並看看每一項對葡萄酒有什麼影響。","Let's start with the most important idea: the person in front of you. When you recommend a wine to a customer or a friend, the first thing to consider is what that person likes and dislikes. You might find a particular pairing exceptional, but if the person asking for advice does not enjoy that style of wine, there is no point recommending it. Taste is personal, and good advice starts by listening.":"先從最重要的概念開始：你面前的那個人。向客人或朋友推薦葡萄酒時，首先要考慮的是對方喜歡和不喜歡什麼。你也許覺得某個搭配非常出色，但如果來請教的人不喜歡那種風格的酒，推薦它就沒有意義。口味是個人的，好的建議從傾聽開始。","The second idea is reassuring: for most people, most wines are an acceptable partner for most foods. There is no single correct wine for each dish. However, some features of food usually have a positive or a negative effect on wine. If you understand these interactions, you are never stuck recommending one particular wine with one particular dish; once you know what most people want to avoid, your options become almost limitless.":"第二個概念讓人安心：對多數人來說，多數葡萄酒搭配多數食物都可以接受。每道菜並沒有唯一正確的酒。不過，食物的某些特性通常會對葡萄酒產生正面或負面的影響。了解這些交互作用，你就不會被困在只能為某道菜推薦某一款酒；一旦知道多數人想避開什麼，你的選擇就幾乎沒有限制。","Before we look at the food, let's name what changes in the wine. The wine can seem more or less sweet, more or less acidic, more or less fruity, more or less bitter and drying, and the alcohol can seem more or less noticeable. Where does bitterness in wine come from? From two sources: the tannins of red wines, and oak. Keep that in mind, because tannic and oaky wines are the ones most affected by the troublemakers we meet next.":"在看食物之前，先說清楚葡萄酒會有哪些變化。酒可能顯得更甜或沒那麼甜、更酸或沒那麼酸、果味更多或更少、更苦澀或沒那麼苦澀，酒精感也可能更明顯或更不明顯。葡萄酒的苦味從哪裡來？有兩個來源：紅酒的單寧，以及橡木桶。記住這一點，因為單寧高和橡木味重的葡萄酒，最容易受到接下來那些麻煩製造者的影響。","The first troublemaker is sweetness in food. A sweet dish makes a wine seem more drying and bitter, more acidic, and less sweet and fruity. Picture a dry, crisp white served with a sweet dessert: the wine suddenly tastes sour and thin, as if its fruit had vanished. The usual answer is to choose a wine at least as sweet as the dish, for example a sweet wine such as Sauternes with a fruit tart.":"第一個麻煩製造者是食物中的甜味。甜的菜餚讓葡萄酒顯得更乾澀、更苦、更酸，甜味和果味都變少。想像一款不甜、清脆的白酒搭配甜點：酒突然變得又酸又單薄，彷彿果味消失了。常見的解決方法是選擇甜度至少與菜餚相當的葡萄酒，例如用 Sauternes 這樣的甜酒搭配水果塔。","The second troublemaker is umami, the savoury taste found in foods such as mushrooms or ripe cheeses. Umami has exactly the same effects as sweetness: the wine seems more drying and bitter, more acidic, and less sweet and fruity. That is why a very tannic red, or a heavily oaked wine, can turn harsh and bitter beside an umami-rich dish. With such dishes, a fruitier wine with less tannin is usually a safer choice.":"第二個麻煩製造者是鮮味，也就是蘑菇或熟成乳酪等食物中的鮮美滋味。鮮味的作用和甜味完全相同：葡萄酒顯得更乾澀、更苦、更酸，甜味和果味都變少。所以單寧非常高的紅酒，或橡木味很重的葡萄酒，搭配鮮味豐富的菜餚時可能變得粗澀而苦。搭配這類菜餚，果味較多、單寧較低的葡萄酒通常是更保險的選擇。","Now the friends. Salt in food is very wine-friendly. A salty dish makes a wine seem less drying and bitter, less acidic, and more fruity, with more body. So a salty snack can soften a firm red, and a wine that seemed a little lean on its own can feel rounder and more generous. Acidity in food is another friend. An acidic dish makes a wine seem less drying and bitter and less acidic, and sweeter and fruitier.":"現在輪到好朋友了。食物中的鹽對葡萄酒非常友善。鹹的菜餚讓葡萄酒顯得沒那麼乾澀、沒那麼苦、沒那麼酸，果味更多、酒體更飽滿。所以鹹的小點可以讓結構紮實的紅酒變柔和，而單喝時顯得有點清瘦的酒，也會變得更圓潤、更豐滿。食物中的酸是另一個好朋友。酸的菜餚讓葡萄酒顯得沒那麼乾澀、沒那麼苦、沒那麼酸，而且更甜、果味更多。","Think of a squeeze of lemon over grilled fish. That acidity in the food tames the acidity of the wine, so a very crisp white suddenly tastes softer and fruitier. But be careful the other way round: if the food is more acidic than the wine, a wine with low acidity can seem flat. A high-acid wine is usually the safest partner for an acidic dish.":"想想在烤魚上擠一點檸檬汁。食物中的酸馴服了葡萄酒的酸度，於是非常清脆的白酒突然變得更柔和、果味更多。但反過來要小心：如果食物比酒還酸，酸度低的葡萄酒可能顯得平淡無力。搭配酸的菜餚，高酸度的葡萄酒通常是最保險的夥伴。","Three special cases remain. The first is flavour intensity. A highly flavoured dish can overwhelm a wine, which then seems to disappear. A delicate, light white, such as a Pinot Grigio, would be lost beside a rich, spicy stew, so with intense dishes, choose a wine with enough flavour of its own. The second is fat and oil. Fatty or oily food makes a wine seem less acidic, which is why a fresh, high-acid wine can feel nicely balanced alongside a rich, oily dish.":"還有三種特殊情況。第一種是風味強度。味道濃郁的菜餚可能壓過葡萄酒，酒彷彿消失了。灰皮諾這類細緻輕盈的白酒，搭配濃郁辛香的燉菜就會被淹沒，所以搭配味道濃郁的菜餚，要選擇本身風味夠強的葡萄酒。第二種是脂肪和油。高脂肪或油膩的食物讓葡萄酒顯得沒那麼酸，所以清爽、高酸度的葡萄酒搭配豐腴油潤的菜餚會顯得很平衡。","The third special case is chilli heat. Chilli increases the burning sensation of the alcohol, so the alcohol in the wine seems more noticeable; and in turn, the alcohol makes the chilli feel hotter. A powerful, high-alcohol red with a fiery curry can feel like pouring fuel on a fire. With spicy food, a wine with lower alcohol is usually more comfortable, for instance a light, medium-sweet Riesling.":"第三種特殊情況是辣味。辣椒會加強酒精的灼熱感，所以酒中的酒精感更明顯；酒精又反過來讓辣椒顯得更辣。強勁、高酒精濃度的紅酒搭配火辣的咖哩，就像火上加油。搭配辛辣的食物，酒精濃度較低的葡萄酒通常更舒服，例如輕盈、半甜的麗絲玲。","Here is a memory tip: picture a dinner party with two troublemakers, two friends and three special guests. The troublemakers are sweetness and umami: they make wine harder, more bitter and more acidic, and steal its sweetness and fruit. The friends are salt and acid: they make wine softer, smoother and fruitier. The special guests each have one trick: intense flavour drowns the wine, fat softens its acidity, and chilli turns up the alcohol.":"這裡有個記憶訣竅：想像一場晚宴，來了兩個麻煩製造者、兩個好朋友和三位特別來賓。麻煩製造者是甜味和鮮味：它們讓葡萄酒更生硬、更苦、更酸，還偷走甜味和果味。好朋友是鹽和酸：它們讓葡萄酒更柔和、更順口、果味更多。三位特別來賓各有一招：濃郁的風味會淹沒葡萄酒，脂肪讓酸度變柔和，辣味則把酒精感調高。","Before the quiz, remember three things. First, personal preference comes first, and for most people most wines go acceptably with most foods. Second, sweet and umami foods make wine seem more drying, bitter and acidic, and less sweet and fruity, while salty and acidic foods make it seem less drying, bitter and acidic, and fruitier; bitterness in wine comes from tannin or oak. Third, highly flavoured food can overwhelm a wine, fatty food makes it seem less acidic, and chilli heat makes the alcohol more noticeable, while alcohol makes the chilli hotter.":"測驗之前，記住三件事。第一，個人喜好優先，而且對多數人來說，多數葡萄酒搭配多數食物都可以接受。第二，甜的和鮮味豐富的食物讓葡萄酒顯得更乾澀、更苦、更酸，甜味和果味更少；鹹的和酸的食物則讓酒顯得沒那麼乾澀、沒那麼苦、沒那麼酸，果味更多；葡萄酒的苦味來自單寧或橡木桶。第三，味道濃郁的食物可能壓過葡萄酒，高脂肪的食物讓酒顯得沒那麼酸，辣味讓酒精感更明顯，酒精則讓辣味更辣。","Drinking a glass of wine and tasting it are two different things. To get the most out of tasting, you need to take the same approach with every single wine. Do that, and you can write tasting notes that describe a wine accurately, notes you can come back to and compare later. In this final lesson we prepare for a tasting, and then walk through the three stages of the approach: appearance, nose and palate.":"喝一杯葡萄酒和品飲葡萄酒是兩回事。要從品飲中得到最多收穫，就得用同樣的方法面對每一款酒。這麼做，你就能寫出準確描述葡萄酒的品飲筆記，日後可以回頭查看和比較。在這最後一堂課，我們先為品飲做準備，再走過這套方法的三個階段：外觀、香氣和口感。","First, get ready. Make sure there are no distracting smells around you: no strong perfume, no cooking, no scented candles. Have a white surface, such as a sheet of paper or a white tablecloth, to help you judge the colour. Use a glass with a wide bowl that narrows towards the top; that shape concentrates the aromas and makes the nose easier to assess. And start with a clean palate, with no lingering flavours such as toothpaste or coffee. Ever tasted orange juice just after brushing your teeth? Then you know why.":"首先，做好準備。確認周圍沒有干擾的氣味：沒有濃烈的香水、沒有烹飪的味道、沒有香氛蠟燭。準備一個白色的表面，例如一張白紙或白色桌巾，幫助你判斷顏色。使用杯身寬、向上收窄的酒杯；這種形狀能集中香氣，讓聞香更容易。還要從乾淨的口腔開始，不能有牙膏或咖啡等殘留的味道。有沒有在剛刷完牙後喝過柳橙汁？那你就知道為什麼了。","Stage one is appearance, and at this level you look at just one thing: the colour. Tilt the glass over your white surface and decide: is the wine white, rosé or red? It sounds simple, and it is, but it already tells a story. A red wine has spent its whole fermentation with the skins of black grapes; a rosé only a few hours; a white has usually been pressed away from the skins before fermentation even started.":"第一階段是外觀，在這個級別只看一件事：顏色。把酒杯在白色表面上方傾斜，然後判斷：這款酒是白、粉紅還是紅？聽起來很簡單，也確實簡單，但它已經說出一段故事。紅酒整個發酵期間都與黑葡萄的果皮在一起；粉紅酒只有幾個小時；白酒通常在發酵開始前就經壓榨與果皮分開了。","Stage two is the nose. Give the glass a gentle swirl to release the aromas, then bring it to your nose and breathe in. Ask yourself what the smells remind you of, and sort them into three families: fruit, oak and other. Fruit is almost always there. Its type depends on the grape variety and on ripeness: blackcurrant suggests Cabernet Sauvignon, while apple and lemon point to a cool climate, and peach and pineapple to a warm one.":"第二階段是香氣。輕輕搖晃酒杯讓香氣釋放，再把酒杯湊近鼻子吸氣。問問自己這些氣味讓你想到什麼，並把它們分成三大類：水果、橡木和其他。水果幾乎一定會有。它的類型取決於葡萄品種和成熟度：黑醋栗讓人想到卡本內蘇維濃，蘋果和檸檬指向涼爽氣候，桃子和鳳梨則指向溫暖氣候。","Next, look for oak. If the wine was fermented or matured in oak barrels, you may find cedar, cloves, coconut, smoke or vanilla. Then the family called other: grass, flowers, herbs, vegetables, earth, mushroom or leather. Do not worry if words fail you at first; describing aromas is a skill that comes with practice. Every glass you smell adds a little more to your memory.":"接著找橡木香氣。如果葡萄酒曾在橡木桶中發酵或熟成，你可能會聞到雪松、丁香、椰子、煙燻或香草。然後是稱為「其他」的一類：青草、花、香草植物、蔬菜、泥土、蘑菇或皮革。一開始想不出詞彙也別擔心；描述香氣是一種會隨練習進步的能力。你聞過的每一杯酒，都會為你的記憶多添一筆。","Stage three is the palate. Take a small sip and move the wine all around your mouth, so it touches everywhere. Here you assess the structure, the five characteristics we met earlier: sweetness, acidity, tannin, alcohol and body. Then you note the flavours. Let's take the five one at a time, with a simple question for each.":"第三階段是口感。啜一小口，讓酒在口中四處流動，接觸到每個角落。這時要評估結構，也就是前面學過的五項特徵：甜度、酸度、單寧、酒精和酒體。然後記下風味。我們一項一項來看，每一項配一個簡單的問題。","Sweetness: is there any sugar? Most wines are dry; some have a medium level of sweetness, such as many White Zinfandels; and a few are truly sweet, like Sauternes, which can feel thick, almost syrupy. Acidity: does your mouth water? Pay attention to how much: the more your mouth waters, the higher the acidity. A Chablis or a Sauvignon Blanc will make it water a lot.":"甜度：有沒有糖？大多數葡萄酒都是不甜的；有些是半甜，例如許多 White Zinfandel；少數是真正的甜酒，像 Sauternes，喝起來可能濃稠，幾乎像糖漿。酸度：你有沒有分泌唾液？注意分泌多少：唾液分泌得越多，酸度就越高。Chablis 或白蘇維濃會讓你分泌很多唾液。","Tannin: does your mouth feel dry, especially on your gums and teeth? Tannin is mostly something you feel rather than taste, and you will meet it in red wines. A red Bordeaux leaves your mouth gripped and dry; a Beaujolais barely does. Alcohol: how warming does the wine feel? Most wines sit between eleven and a half and fourteen percent, but a Châteauneuf-du-Pape feels noticeably warmer than a light White Zinfandel.":"單寧：你的口腔有沒有乾澀感，尤其是牙齦和牙齒？單寧主要是感覺到，而不是嚐到，而且會出現在紅酒中。波爾多紅酒會讓口腔緊澀乾燥；Beaujolais 則幾乎不會。酒精：這款酒帶來多少溫熱感？大多數葡萄酒在百分之十一點五到百分之十四之間，但 Châteauneuf-du-Pape 的溫熱感明顯比輕盈的 White Zinfandel 強。","Body: how mouth-filling is the wine? Imagine sipping water, then fruit juice, then a smoothie: each one fills your mouth a little more. A light-bodied wine, such as a Pinot Grigio, feels delicate; a full-bodied one, such as a Californian Cabernet Sauvignon, feels viscous and fills the mouth. Finally, the flavours: use the same three families as on the nose, fruit, oak and other. Often you will confirm what you smelled, and sometimes you will find something new.":"酒體：這款酒在口中有多飽滿？想像先喝水，再喝果汁，再喝果昔：每一種都讓口腔更飽滿一些。酒體輕盈的葡萄酒，例如灰皮諾，感覺細緻；酒體飽滿的葡萄酒，例如加州卡本內蘇維濃，感覺濃稠、充滿口腔。最後是風味：使用和聞香時相同的三大類，水果、橡木和其他。你常會確認先前聞到的香氣，有時也會發現新的。","Let's put it together with a quick example, in plain words. For a Chablis, the note might read: appearance, white. Nose, apple and lemon, no oak. Palate, dry, high acidity, no tannin, medium alcohol, light to medium body, with flavours of apple and lemon. For a Beaujolais: red; raspberry and red cherry; dry, high acidity, low tannin, light body. Short, clear and always in the same order.":"我們用一個簡短的例子，以簡單的文字把這些整合起來。以 Chablis 來說，筆記可以這樣寫：外觀，白色。香氣，蘋果和檸檬，沒有橡木。口感，不甜，高酸度，沒有單寧，酒精中等，酒體輕盈至中等，帶有蘋果和檸檬風味。以 Beaujolais 來說：紅色；覆盆子和紅櫻桃；不甜，高酸度，低單寧，酒體輕盈。簡短、清楚，而且永遠依照相同的順序。","Here is a tip: treat the three stages like a pilot's checklist before take-off. Look, smell, taste, always in that order, and never skip a line. A good way to practise is to taste wines in contrasting pairs: an unoaked Sauvignon Blanc beside an oaked Chardonnay, or a Pinot Noir beside a Cabernet Sauvignon. The differences jump out, and the vocabulary sticks.":"這裡有個訣竅：把這三個階段當成飛行員起飛前的檢查表。看、聞、嚐，永遠依照這個順序，絕不跳過任何一行。有個很好的練習方法，是把對比鮮明的葡萄酒兩兩一起品飲：不經橡木桶的白蘇維濃配經橡木桶的夏多內，或是黑皮諾配卡本內蘇維濃。差異會一目了然，詞彙也記得牢。","One last word about alcohol and health. Enjoyed in moderation, alcohol is not regarded as harmful to health. But drinking too much can seriously affect behaviour, sometimes in dangerous ways; for some people alcohol can be highly addictive, and in excess it harms both short and long-term health. Many governments and public health bodies publish guidelines on low-risk drinking, and they vary from country to country, so check the ones where you live.":"最後談談酒精與健康。適量飲用時，酒精不被視為對健康有害。但飲酒過量會嚴重影響行為，有時甚至造成危險；對某些人來說，酒精可能有高度成癮性，過量飲用則會損害短期和長期的健康。許多政府和公共衛生機構都公布了低風險飲酒的指引，各國不盡相同，請查閱你所在地的指引。","Before the quiz, remember three things. First, prepare well: no distracting smells, a white surface, a glass with a wide bowl that narrows at the top, and a clean palate. Second, follow the same three stages every time: appearance, which is the colour, white, rosé or red; nose, with aromas of fruit, oak and other; and palate. Third, on the palate assess sweetness, acidity that makes your mouth water, tannin that dries it, alcohol and body, then the flavours, again sorted into fruit, oak and other.":"測驗之前，記住三件事。第一，做好準備：沒有干擾的氣味、白色的表面、杯身寬而向上收窄的酒杯，以及乾淨的口腔。第二，每次都依照相同的三個階段：外觀，也就是顏色，白、粉紅或紅；香氣，分為水果、橡木和其他；以及口感。第三，在口感階段評估甜度、讓你分泌唾液的酸度、讓口腔乾澀的單寧、酒精和酒體，然後是風味，同樣分為水果、橡木和其他。"});(window.TWG_I18N_F=window.TWG_I18N_F||{})["zh-hant/l1"]=1;
